{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.330109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5e81a5de658d16210e9cefc9c2bac5ef1c4f311d5990309dccb2a22e31a2a67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 5 (Small-noise equalization and corrected lower crossover) of arXiv:2608.30374, 'Compact and Infinite-Order Error Analysis\\ for Null-Space SVD Estimation'] Let \(h_\star=\|H\|_2\) and \(\zeta=\sigma/h_\star\).  Assume that the
ordered expected risks may be expanded through sixth order and that their
maximizing and minimizing branches are unique and do not switch near zero.
Then
\begin{equation}
    \varepsilon_{\mathrm{gen},i}^{\mathrm{ord}}(\sigma)
      =h_\star^2\zeta^2
        \left(a+b_i\zeta^2+c_i\zeta^4+O(\zeta^6)\right),
    \qquad
    \boxed{a=1+\frac{n}{\tau-n-1}},

\end{equation}
and every branch has the same leading coefficient \(a\).  Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \varepsilon_{\mathrm{gen},i}^{\mathrm{ord}}(\sigma)
   =\left(1+\frac{n}{\tau-n-1}\right)\sigma^2+O(\sigma^4).}

\end{equation}
The first rank-dependent contribution is contained in the
\(O(\sigma^4)\) term.  If
\(i_+=\arg\max_i b_i\), \(i_-=\arg\min_i b_i\), and
\(\bar b=q_0^{-1}\sum_i b_i\), then
\begin{equation}
    \Delta_{\mathrm{rank}}(\sigma)
       =C_2\zeta^2+C_4\zeta^4+O(\zeta^6),

\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
    C_2&=\frac{b_{i_+}-b_{i_-}}{a\sqrt{q_0}},
       \\
    C_4&=\frac{1}{\sqrt{q_0}}
       \left[
       \frac{c_{i_+}-c_{i_-}}{a}
       -\frac{\bar b(b_{i_+}-b_{i_-})}{a^2}
       \right].

\end{align}
If \(C_2>0\), then, for sufficiently small \(\delta_{\mathrm{vis}}\) such
that the discriminant below is nonnegative and the positive root remains in
this expansion and no-switch neighborhood, the fourth-order corrected lower
crossover is
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
    \sigma_{\mathrm{lo}}(\delta_{\mathrm{vis}})
      \simeq h_\star
       \left(
       \frac{2\delta_{\mathrm{vis}}}
       {C_2+\sqrt{C_2^2+4C_4\delta_{\mathrm{vis}}}}
       \right)^{1/2}.}

\end{equation}
For \(C_4=0\), this reduces to
\(h_\star\sqrt{\delta_{\mathrm{vis}}/C_2}\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.625433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5e81a8a271d7450d1d372521633044b2a5e27496d80452596f6cbb7a071609f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Chordal meander Matrix of arXiv:2506.01306, 'Asymptotic of Coulomb gas integral, Temperley-Lieb type algebras and pure partition functi'] Let $LP(n,m)$ be the set of chordal link patterns on $n$ boundary points, consisting of $m$ non-crossing pairings of $n$ points on the real line. The \emph{meander matrix} $\mathcal{M}_{\kappa}(\alpha,\beta)$ is the Gram matrix associated with the bilinear form
\[ \langle \alpha , \beta \rangle_{n,m}
\]
where $\alpha, \beta \in LP(n,m)$, $\delta = n(\kappa)=-2\cos(\frac{4\pi}{\kappa})$ is a loop weight parameter.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.397308+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5e8a1b9a45618b2561beae9a42eb5720ad209cd40ceb55133fd5271ebf8d705","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 46 ({\cite[Theorem~6.2) of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] {zhan2019two}}]

Let $v_-, w_-, w_+, v_+ \in \BR$ with $v_- < w_- < w_+ < v_+$ be such that $0 \in [v_-, v_+]$. Let $(\eta_+,\eta_-)$ be a bichordal SLE$_4$ in $\BH$ with link pattern $\{\{w_+, v_+\}, \{w_-, v_-\}\}$. Then, there exists a universal constant $C \in (0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation*}
    \BP[\text{both } \eta_+ \text{ and } \eta_- \text{ exit } B_L(0)] \leq C L^{-4} G_1(w_-, w_+; v_-, v_+) \left(1 + C((v_+ - v_-) / L)^{5/6}\right)
\end{equation*}
for all $L > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5ea7560569e2f4781c28804b23b2e6129f71d3e7a6b9c5dae80a2e70e3023cd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:uniform-profile-tail of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:uniform-profile-tail}
We say that the random field satisfies \(({\rm PT})_p\) if, for every
\(a>0\),
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \sup_{x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1)}
 \mathbb P\{\left\lverth_N^J(x)\right\rvert\ge a\}
 \le-\frac{a^2}{2}.
\end{equation}
This asymptotic one-profile tail rate, rather than a moment-generating
function bound, is the exact probabilistic input used by the
sparse-profile upper bounds.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.866252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5eac1b997e185ba625dbfe8a3c18e184c35c7a80ae80b6711fcf46c97fdbfba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 24 of arXiv:2605.21638, 'Markov renewal theory for transfer operators and point processes on the line'] For every measurable function $F\colon \mathbf{N} \rightarrow \R$,
