{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.991337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6023dfcbbe7138a14a8cc495bf73c7a09fe77b9cd5491c18abe7b4d1cbe30cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Linearized backward equation) of arXiv:2604.00937, 'Infinite Horizon Optimal Control of Forward-Backward Stochastic Volterra Equations with De'] The processes $(\dot{Y},\dot{Z},\dot{K})$ satisfy
\begin{align*}
\dot{Y}(t) &= \int_t^\infty \Bigg[ \frac{\partial g}{\partial x}(t,s)\dot{X}(s) + \frac{\partial g}{\partial x_1}(t,s)\dot{X}_1(s) + \frac{\partial g}{\partial y}(t,s)\dot{Y}(s) \\
&\quad + \frac{\partial g}{\partial z}(t,s)\dot{Z}(t,s) + \langle \nabla_k g(t,s),\dot{K}(t,s,\cdot) \rangle + \frac{\partial g}{\partial u}(t,s)\beta(s) \Bigg] ds \\
&\quad - \int_t^\infty \dot{Z}(t,s) dB(s) - \int_t^\infty \int_{\mathbb{R}_0} \dot{K}(t,s,e) \tilde{N}(ds,de).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.416448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6070495278bc20289925c5f21dc131ef942531b37b69e3bf36ddaa9a5eeb5c0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2605.16072, 'Stochastic integration \\with respect to a L\'evy basis'] Let $\Theta\colon \RR \to L_P^0(\Omega;\R)$ be an infinitely divisible random measure. 
