{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.386004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b60c995c3f59d4138d02be14356684018e84b8701e5227dabd3f9fb824770cc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 38 of arXiv:2609.03962, '$L^p$ isomorphisms for the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and their application'] Let $n\ge2$, $s\in(0,2)$, $p\in(1,\infty)$, and let $f\in L^p(\R^n)^n$ and $g\in V_{s,p}$, i.e.
