{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.263066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6359ed551ea193c7b65de7c209029f0d5ebcc5c773db7a5f39b5a847c922e53","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_bound_EEplus of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $k \geq 1$ and any $x_1, \dots , x_k \in \Omega_{\delta}$, 
