{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b63bdf8d0d0e7a2a3e773d85408bd4a42caa152e95445772b6523dca0b000f88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop edge-weight-locality of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $d=d^{{\mathrm {res}}}$. Suppose that $V,V_1,V_2\in\mathfrak{C}$ are such that $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V} = (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_1}) \cup (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_2})$ and $(\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_1}) \cap (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_2}) = \{a,b\}$. There exists a countable set $\mathcal{Z}_V=\{z_1,z_2,\ldots\} \subseteq \mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ that contains $a,b$, is dense with respect to $d^{{\mathrm {path}}}_{\overline{V}}$, and such that the following holds for sufficiently large~$m$. Let $A = \{z_1,\ldots,z_m\}$, $A_1 = A \cap \overline{V_1}$, $A_2 = A \cap \overline{V_2}$, and let $w$ (resp.\ $w_1$, $w_2$) be the weight function associated with $\mathfrak{d}_V(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A}$ (resp.\ $\mathfrak{d}_{V_1}(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A_1}$, $\mathfrak{d}_{V_2}(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A_2}$). Then
\begin{itemize}
    \item $w(x,y)=w_1(x,y)$ for each $x,y\in A_1$;
    \item $w(x,y)=w_2(x,y)$ for each $x,y\in A_2$;
    \item $w(x,y)=0$ for each $x\in A_1 \setminus \{a,b\}$, $y\in A_2 \setminus \{a,b\}$;
    \item $w(a,b)=0$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.586891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b63e71fe5384e1091190066e7f261385cc214966a09a2a4834303241bfb1b567","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Caputo fractional derivative) of arXiv:2608.25164, 'A time-fractional Kalman filter'] Let $\alpha>0$ and let $n=\lceil\alpha\rceil$. The Caputo derivative is
defined by
\begin{align}
D_C^\alpha f(t)
&=I^{n-\alpha}f^{(n)}(t)\nonumber\\
&=\frac{1}{\Gamma(n-\alpha)}
  \int_0^t(t-s)^{n-\alpha-1}f^{(n)}(s)ds,
  \qquad n-1<\alpha<n,
\end{align}
while $D_C^n f=f^{(n)}$ when $\alpha=n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.871570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b63fcae1b9c799a572d3e315755f6372f870b39f19e6b8dfaad9e39e99300ce9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:monotonicity of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] A set $T \subset \reals^d\times\reals^d$ is cyclically monotone if,  for every integer $n \geqslant 1$ and all $(x_1,y_1),\ldots,(x_n,y_n) \in T$ with $y_{n+1} := y_1$, we have 
\begin{equation}

    \sum_{i=1}^n \langle{x_i,y_i}\rangle \geqslant \sum_{i=1}^n \inpr{x_i,y_{i+1}}.
\end{equation}
If (rel:cyclical_mononicity of the paper) holds for $n=2$, then $T$ is monotone.
The set $T$ is maximal (cyclically) monotone if it is not contained in a larger subset of $\reals^d\times\reals^d$ that is also (cyclically) monotone.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.354453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b641a7e3becca9eae1710929a9c6ff58a0065dd337c1b414375a0ed834af4783","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(X, X_1,X_2,\dots\) be an i.i.d.\ family of \(\Z\)-valued, irreducible, aperiodic random variables satisfying~\eqref{eq:conditions_steps}. Let \(a_*,b_*\) be defined as in~\eqref{eq:dual_allowed_slopes}, and \(a_*<a<b<b_*\). Let \(h\in C^2([0,1])\) be a non-negative concave function with \(h''<0\), \(\mathrm{Image}(h')\subset H_X'([a,b])\), and \(h(0)=0\). Define
    \begin{equation*}
        h_n(k) = nh(k/n),\quad k=0,\dots, n.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, there are \(c_+\geq c_- >0, n_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\),
    \begin{equation*}
        e^{-c_+n^{1/3}}
        \leq
        e^{n\int_{0}^1 I(h'(s))ds} P\bigl(S\geq h_n, S_n = \lceil h_n(n)\rceil\bigr)
        \leq
        e^{-c_-n^{1/3}},
    \end{equation*}
    where \(S_0=0\), \(S_k=S_{k-1}+X_k\) and \(I(x) = \sup_{\lambda} \bigl(\lambda x - H(x)\bigr)\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.699601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6428a7553ff71ca496d2f24fa57fb57ed10368bea7aba23c32fa8856437a330","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] Let $n\ge3$, let $\Sigma\subset\mathbb R^n$ be a connected embedded $C^2$ hypersurface, and let $D_t$ have positive pair-sum-nonresonant weights. Put $N=\binom n2$. The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $D_t\Sigma$ is minimal for every $t>0$;
\item $D_{t_1}\Sigma,\ldots,D_{t_N}\Sigma$ are minimal for some $N$ distinct positive numbers $t_1,\ldots,t_N$;
\item $\Sigma$ is a connected open subset of an affine hyperplane.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.308778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b643655a8247cf30e52483250bdbed3a90a7990001372261ded4c2419d4c972a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] For any $H\in (0,\frac12)$, there exists a constant  $c_H>0$ depending on $H$ such that for any $x\in\mathbb{R}$,
