where $\mathfrak{T}=\mathfrak{T}(n,M,g;T)$ is a constant depending only on $n,M,g$ and on the constant $T$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.635885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6598ce552b86800679931bc1b7965fa93399f838aa5122a34df65dc46c58ec8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: character bound finite level general with M sigma with extra assumption more than r for I alpha of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $r\geq 0$. As $n\to \infty$, uniformly over all $\lambda \vdash n$ such that $\lambda_1 = n-r$ and every $\sigma \in {\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n$ such that $I(\alpha) >r$, we have
