{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.436176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b65e98f31c3aaa7933aa40c367ba8417189df96353c2efba8887fa9ec13e04b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:approx-C4 of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let \( \mu, \nu \in \Lambda_2(\mathbb{R}^d) \), and suppose \( \varphi, \psi \in C^2_2(\mathbb{R}^d) \) satisfy the quadratic growth condition \( |\varphi(x)|, |\psi(x)| \le C |x|^2 \) for some \( C \ge 0 \), along with \( \varphi \oplus \psi \le c_2 \). Then there exists a family \( \{(\varphi_\varepsilon, \psi_\varepsilon)\}_{\varepsilon > 0} \) such that for all \( \varepsilon > 0 \), the following hold:
