{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b68c05bda9d8a745f540eb77ff8df70fa5e6139afab593f99a55b54ccef74716","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 4 (Generalized form of the $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem) of arXiv:2603.25536, 'The $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem revisited'] Suppose $F: \mathbb{R}^N \to \mathbb{R}$ is smooth and jointly convex (i.e., it has a positive semi-definite Hessian). Then the integral
