{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.252031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6de3ece14bd2bf8b152ba44e9dce74f131033d59ef62c171fc834e78ffcbb03","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 70 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] The following holds if the constant $L$ entering \Cref{yy} is chosen to be sufficiently large. Let the constants $A,B,R$ satisfy
			\begin{eqnarray}

