{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.789656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6ff0a993e5b3401b536efce42b78f9571a168e801e4f7ca208b9e860b62bbc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teo T: Survival of arXiv:2606.10165, 'The frog model with death and drift on free products of complete graphs'] Let $\beta = \frac{1-\alpha}{\Delta-1}$ and assume $m \geq 2$ and $d \geq 2$ are fixed integers. We define the functions

{\allowdisplaybreaks
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
\phi(r)&= -d(m-1)r^2 + 2d(m-1)r,\\[4pt] 
A(\alpha, p) &= 
\frac{
1 - \beta p (m-2)-\sqrt{[1 - \beta p (m-2)]^2 - 4 \alpha \beta p^2 d (m-1)
}}{2 \beta p d (m-1)},\\[10pt]
\gamma(\alpha, p) &= 1 - \beta p \, [d (m-1) A(\alpha, p) + m - 3],\\[10pt]
\mathscr{Q}(\alpha, p) &= -\alpha p \, [\gamma(\alpha, p) + \beta p (m-2)],\\[10pt]
\mathscr{R}(\alpha, p) &= \gamma(\alpha, p) \, [1 - \beta p (d-1) (m-1) A(\alpha, p)] - \beta p^2 (\alpha + \beta) (m-2),\\[10pt]
\mathscr{S}(\alpha, p) &= -\beta p \, [\gamma(\alpha, p) + \beta p (m-2)],\\[10pt]
B(\alpha, p) &= \frac{-\mathscr{R}(\alpha, p) + \sqrt{\mathscr{R}(\alpha, p)^2-4 \, \mathscr{Q}(\alpha, p) \, \mathscr{S}(\alpha, p)}}{2 \, \mathscr{Q}(\alpha, p)}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}}

Then, \(\FM{\mathbb{D}_{m,d}}{\alpha,p}\) survives with positive probability for  $(\alpha, p)$ such that $\phi(B(\alpha, p))> 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

