{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.741287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b759fd1d0c2838435ce3d50875213b8a2ed2a4e26ab3d167a41c675754c8e449","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition-connetion-BW-RWRE of arXiv:2507.19222, 'Convergence of the KMP model to the KPZ equation'] Assume that, at discrete-time $n_{0}\in \mathbb{Z}$, we have $\eta(n_{0},x)+\eta(n_{0},x+1)=\mathsf{p}_{n_{0}}(x)$ for all $x\in\mathbb{Z}$. 
		Then, for all $n\in \mathbb{Z}$ such that $n\geqslant n_{0}$, we have 
