{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.764200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7b1e89f355f9b314db7252c7e5d0d9a8a4ec9f03136b39dd29603d91167025e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Evaluation of $\eps(\pi\otimes\tilde\chi)$) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $\pi$ be as usual and $\chi\notin E$. Then if $\pi_p=\pi(\tilde\mu_1, \tilde\mu_2)$, we have
