{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.461322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7fcf4b160080b8333f78b610c2f9ff7b77870ce143ea6c5c05c7f4ea29cd79b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem comparison-result of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Fix $T > 0$ and assume $f,g: \mathbb{D}([0,T], \mathcal{M}) \to [0,\infty]$ satisfy for all $x \in \mathcal{M}$:
    \begin{gather}
        \mathbb{E}[f(\{X_s^x\}_{s \leq T})] \leq \mathbb{E}[g(\{X_s^x\}_{s \leq T})] \,,
    \\

        \limsup_{t \to \infty} \mathbb{E}\Big[\frac{1}{t}\int_0^t f(\{X_r^x\}_{s\leq r \leq s+T})^2 + g(\{X_s^x\}_{s \leq r \leq s+T})^2ds\Big] < \infty \,.
    \end{gather}
    Then
    \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t}\int_0^t f(\{X_r^x\}_{s\leq r \leq s+T})ds \leq \limsup_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t}\int_0^t g(\{X_r^x\}_{s\leq r \leq s+T})ds \,.
    \end{equation}

    Furthermore, if $f$ has the form $f(\phi) = \int_0^T \hat f(\phi(s))ds$ where $\hat f: \mathcal{M} \to [0,\infty]$, $g_2: \mathbb{D}([0,T],\mathcal{M}) \to [0,\infty)$ satisfies $g(\phi) \leq \frac{T}{2}\hat f(\phi(0)) + g_2(\phi)$, and (equation eq-compare-var of the paper) also holds with $g$ replaced by $g_2$, then
    $$\limsup_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t}\int_0^t \hat f(X_s^x)ds \leq \frac{2}{T}\limsup_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t}\int_0^t g_2(\{X_r^x\}_{s\leq r \leq s+T})ds \,.$$","status":"unverified"}

