{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.295316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8020c84d63008d79d118753f6190475ceedeafb7125f28f746ae171ee267de6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Lipschitz_width of arXiv:2609.03129, 'A Closed-Form Formula for Consistent Lipschitz Regression on Metric Spaces with Sparse Neu'] {petrova2023lipschitz}}]

Let $(\mathcal{X},\|\cdot\|_{\mathcal{X}})$ be a Banach space, let
$\mathcal K\subseteq \mathcal{X}$ be bounded, let $n\in\mathbb N_+$, and let
$\gamma\ge 0$.  
For each fixed norm $\|\cdot\|_{Y_n}$ on $\mathbb{R}^n$; the $\|\cdot\|_{Y_n}$-Lipschitz width of $\mathcal{K}$ is defined\footnote{We denote the  closed unit ball
$
    B_{Y_n}
\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \{y\in\mathbb{R}^n:\|y\|_{Y_n}\le 1\}
$ if a normed space $(\mathbb{R}^n,\|\cdot\|_{Y_n})$.}~
by
\begin{equation}

    d^\gamma(\mathcal K,Y_n)_{\mathcal{X}}
\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \inf_{\Phi}
        \sup_{f\in\mathcal K}
            \inf_{y\in B_{Y_n}}
                \|f-\Phi(y)\|_{\mathcal{X}},
\end{equation}
where the outer infimum in~(equation eq:def_LipWidth of the paper) is taken over all $\gamma$-Lipchitz maps
$
    \Phi:B_{Y_n}\to\mathcal{X}
$.
The $n$-th Lipschitz width of $\mathcal K$ is obtained by further minimizing over all norms $\|\cdot\|_{Y_n}$ on $\mathbb{R}^n$; i.e.\
\begin{equation}

    d^\gamma_n(\mathcal K)_{\mathcal{X}}
\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \inf\big\{
        d^\gamma(\mathcal K,Y_n)_{\mathcal{X}}
    :
    \,
        \|\cdot\|_{Y_n} 
            \text{ a norm on } 
        \mathbb{R}^n
    \big\}
.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.535549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8031425600cc8502e2789fb152ae98b537352381a3c401d27b20e7ee3f44f83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2608.06646, 'Three-dimensional stochastic wave equation with non-Lipschitz coefficients'] Let $f(u)=|u|^{-\beta}$ be the Riesz kernel with $0<\beta<3$. For all positive parameters $a,b$ such that $a+b=3-\beta$, the following statements hold.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For all $u,\xi\in\mathbb{R}^3$ and $h\in\mathbb{R}$,
    \begin{align}
        f(u+h\xi)-f(u)
        =  |h| ^b \int_{\mathbb{R}^3} |u-hw|^{a-3}
        \bigl(|w+\xi|^{\,b-3}-|w|^{\,b-3}\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}w .
    \end{align}

    \item If, in addition, $|\xi|=1$, then
    \begin{align}
        \bigl|f(u+h\xi)+f(u-h\xi)-2f(u)\bigr|
        \le  |h| ^b \int_{\mathbb{R}^3}& |u-hw|^{a-3}\\
        &\notag \times \bigl||w+\xi|^{\,b-3}+|w-\xi|^{\,b-3}-2|w|^{\,b-3}\bigr|\,\mathrm{d}w .
    \end{align}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

