{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.585639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b82ab6b06f45260fbb5ecc9ef157452a973b6574d5df0c11817923832a4ed40e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm.Moment of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p\geq 1$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\zeta,x\geq 0$,
