{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.708839+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b83c9af8d1323b9e669194fd6f5dc197802ac1b2e408245071bbc826feb936d6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def reflection of arXiv:2605.30017, 'Conditional Probability Spaces and the Structure of Agreement\footnote{We thank Emiliano C'] Fix an agent $i = A, B$.  We say $i$ satisfies \textbf{certainty reflection} if for every event $E$, every number $q \in [0,1]$, and every state $\omega$:
\begin{equation}
p^i_{m_i(\omega)}(E) = q  \,\,\, \text{implies} \,\,\, p^i_{m_i(\omega)}\bigl(\{\omega^\prime \in \Omega : p^i_{m_i(\omega^\prime)}(E) = q\}\bigr) = 1.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.408734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b83ddac3f91b29943ace1029ce200c8d81b9f9345a6a0d93eba37dc31b5d1bf6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop twist-height of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Let $S = \left(\begin{smallmatrix}0&-1\\1&1\end{smallmatrix}\right)$. We have
\begin{equation*}
	S^{-1}\rho_z(l_{1,m}^{tw})S = \begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\ -z & 1\end{pmatrix} \ \ \ \ \ S^{-1}\rho_z(l_{2,m}^{tw})S = -\begin{pmatrix}1&4-2z\\0&1\end{pmatrix} \ \ \ \ \ S^{-1}P_zS = S^{-1}T_zS = \begin{pmatrix}1 & -z \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*}
In particular, the central signs are $(+1, -1)$, and the transverse parameters are $(-z, 4-2z)$. Let $\widetilde\rho_z$ be a meridian-normalized lift to $\widetilde{PSL}_2(\mathbb R)$. Then
\begin{equation*}
	\mathrm{trans}(\widetilde\rho_z(l_{1,m}^{tw})) = 0 \ \ \ \ \ \mathrm{trans}(\widetilde\rho_z(l_{2,m}^{tw})) = 1
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.358902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b83e35e23461bc80592b5668c0e1535f722cf7a82c5f30f4af5b03ad70f5708f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Poincar\'e inequality) of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] Let $d \ge 1$ be an integer and let $U \subset \Rd$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain.
		Then there exists $C = C(d, \operatorname{diam} U) < \infty$ such that for every $\eps \in (0,1)$ and every $h \colon \eps\Zd \to \R$ with $h = 0$ on $\eps\Zd \setminus U$,
		\begin{equation}

			\|h\|_{L^2(U^\eps)}^2
			\le C \|h\|_{H^1_{\mathrm{crit}}(U^\eps)}^2\,.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.033879+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8401dd9868de943eebb96fbce87d97f2e4c7cd5fc261650de6d6a57c7396c6a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:siteperc_dom_ZIM of arXiv:2607.29409, 'The Zombie Infection Model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph of bounded degree.
