\\  &f|_{[0,T] \times D(A)} \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times D(A), L(V,D(A^3))).
\end{align}
Then for every $\xi \in D(A^2)$ there exists a unique mild solution $$(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \beta}([0,T],W)$$ to the RPDE \eqref{RPDE} with $Y_0 = \xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.887944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b858d456a57386ada53bfdcf4be12559f2573ef4b6267273701159a004d2f710","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem123 of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] Let $k\geq 1$ be an integer.
