{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.441451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8617e1c1f18ad07ce2c903979560cefc7a7088c0dfe6dabd1b77c4a34bcaced","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:tail_bound of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Under the assumption of Theorem (thm:main_thm of the paper), if $x>0$ and $x^2 t_N N^{-\frac{1}{3}}< c_0$ for some small absolute constant, then there exist constants $c, C>0$, such that
