Here, we allow the laws $\pi_i = \Law(\bm{\xi_i})$ to be non-identical (e.g., to accommodate deterministic initial data with $\Omega = [N]$), provided they satisfy the averaging condition $\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N \pi_i = \pi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

