{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.965935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b89b08774d18944f6e7b0720a4a8f5c1854ed6168b297bed0a6b3d90fe83d9b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Gaussian Hamming-Lipschitz Concentration}


    Let $X \sim \mathcal N(\mu, \Sigma)$ on $\R^n$ with $\Sigma \in \R^{n \times n}$. Assume $f : \R^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property with constants $c = (c_1,...,c_n)\T$. Then, with $\kappa^\star(\Sigma) := \eigmax{D^{1/2} \Sigma D^{1/2}}$ where $D := \diagonal{\Sigma\inv}$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \P\Parent{|f(X) - \E[f(X)]| \geq t} 
        \leq 2\exp\Parent{-\frac{2t^2}{\kappa^\star(\Sigma) \twonorm{c}^2}}
        \quad \text{for all $t > 0$}. 
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.826695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b89c6b3594c3fc1062a18ee19de199cb73c42444c6ea439b386afbb24bcd2685","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 39 (Reduced covariance negative moments) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Set
\[
    C_{t,r}^{\delta,\mathsf O}
