{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.259673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8cc32a161c69ca250c6b4115768d0198ecae2c521173324a570e194b4fda9b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:rho-closed of arXiv:2609.02544, 'A finiteness theorem for geodesic Leech wheels'] Let $w\ge10$ and set
\[
  \lambda_w=\frac{14(w-1)}{36w-25}.
\]
Then $\ell=\mu(w)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
  (1+\lambda_w^2)\ell^2-(5+\lambda_w)\ell+6-4w\le0.
\end{equation}
Relaxing $\lambda_w\ge\tfrac38$ in (equation eq:rho-sharp of the paper) gives
\begin{equation}
  73\ell^2-344\ell+384-256w\le0,
\end{equation}
and hence the closed form
\begin{equation}
  \mu(w)<\frac{15}{8}\sqrt w+\frac{12}{5}.
\end{equation}
Moreover (equation eq:rho-closed of the paper) holds for every $w\ge1$.","status":"unverified"}

