{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.613431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b954bc0fec78346f66e21e49501cb2f3f44a0981bb9c384c6f72c414b0fc049a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2506.09333, 'On the Dimension-Free Concentration of Simple Tensors via Matrix Deviation'] Let $X$ be a mean-zero subgaussian random vector with covariance matrix $\Sigma$ and $X_1,\ldots,X_N$ be i.i.d. copies of $X$. Then, for any integer $p\ge 2$, we have
