{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.897672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b96c51720637026a8311d76503a340963ade46f662428c7b77c59c89eeaeb773","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 64 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Set~$D_p=p_0-p_\infty$,~$D_q=q_0-q_\infty$, and~$D=p_0+p_\infty-q_0-q_\infty$. Then, for~$j=1,\dots,4$ and~$q\in \mathcal R$, 
