{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.043719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b976890e1fa379b1806ef59d61eb03d9de1ee4e51957cef68ec1fc76d33004f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition 2.1 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Assume  that (equation 1.2 of the paper) holds. Then a pair of nonnegative functions
\begin{equation*}
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&u\in C^{0}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty)), \\
&v\in C^{0}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\cap C^{2,1}(\overline{\Omega}\times(0,\infty)),\\
&w\in C^{0}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\cap C^{2,1}(\overline{\Omega}\times(0,\infty))\\
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation*}
such that
\begin{align}
  u^2 \in L^{1}_{loc}([0,\infty); W^{1,1}(\Omega))\quad \hbox{and}\quad u^2\nabla v \in L^{1}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times
  [0,\infty);\mathbb{R}^3)
\end{align}
 will be called a continuous weak solution of (equation 1.1 of the paper) if
\begin{align}
    -\int_{0}^{\infty}\!\int_{\Omega}u\varphi_t-\int_{\Omega}u_0\varphi(\cdot,0)=
    &-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\infty} \!\int_{\Omega}
     v \nabla u^2 \cdot\nabla\varphi 
     +\int_{0}^{\infty}\!\int_{\Omega}u^{2}v\nabla v\cdot \nabla \varphi
     +\ell\int_{0}^{\infty}\!\int_{\Omega}vw\varphi
\end{align}
for all
 $\varphi \in C_0^{\infty}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))$
 fulfilling $\frac{\partial \varphi}{\partial \nu}=0$ on $\partial\Omega\times(0,\infty)$, and if
\begin{align}
\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}v\varphi_t+\int_{\Omega}v_0\varphi(\cdot,0)=\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}\nabla
v\cdot\nabla\varphi+\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}vw\varphi
\end{align}
for any $\varphi \in C_0^{\infty}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))$, as well as
\begin{equation}
    \int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}w\varphi_t+\int_{\Omega}w_0\varphi(\cdot,0)=\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}\nabla
w\cdot\nabla\varphi-\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}w\varphi+\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{\Omega}u\varphi
\end{equation}
for all $\varphi\in C_0^{\infty}(\overline{\Omega}\times[0,\infty))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.265880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b979b77764a13092ed804254d7c219d3c3b08c44f9f705ea38fff071f35bad1e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S31L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] Fix $p, \eta, M \in (0, \infty)$ and $\delta_1 \in (0,1/2)$. There exist $N_1 \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\delta > 0$, depending on $p, \eta, M, \delta_1$, such that the following holds. If $n \geq N_1$, $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$ are such that $x \leq y$ and $|x| \leq M n^{1/2}$, $|y - pn| \leq M n^{1/2}$, $t \in [\delta_1, 1-\delta_1]$, and $a \in \mathbb{R}$, we have
