{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.357092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b98a906e7d312ee4d17fb17beb53682619ee972a09cb75e71c1b1fc2e8612918","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:convergence_covariance of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $B_1,B_2$ and $B$ be balls in ${\mathbb R}^d$ such that $B_1\cup B_2\subseteq B$, and $B$ has radius $\leq 1/2$. Then there exist constants $C,\gamma>0$ such that, for all $N\geq 1$, $\delta\in (0,1]$, and $F\in L^2(B_1\times B_2;{\mathbb R}^{d\times d})$ such that $\nabla_x F\in L^2(B_1\times B_2)$, it holds that 
