{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.185522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9aa23c5e7a30b0ccfc45711a0e94748b6811d00aae11cca326c71c4ae553d31","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Distance to equilibrium of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] The \red[distance to equilibrium] at time $t\ge 0$ is 
