When any $($therefore, all$\,)$ of  
(equation 6.16 of the paper)--(equation 6.16c of the paper) hold, then   so does (equation 6.15 of the paper)   with $\, d_N \equiv \delta_N\,$  as in   (equation 6.6 of the paper), and $\,\pi_N^\star( \varepsilon) \equiv \pi_N ( \varepsilon) $ as in  (equation 6.9' of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

