{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.053055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba1ba33d79e425850741b4539dd7615af9c82d75bd393ad78046f02392af38c0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Uniform off-axis scalar bounds) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $K\Subset(b,\infty)$ be a compact interval.  For $\theta\ge0$, set
\[
 T_\theta(\zeta):=
 \frac1{1-\theta^2d(\zeta)}
 \begin{pmatrix}
