{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.930926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba1eadce4de0b55a124d0e9ae11484a063e23e4c61cdbeb74e3fe7f21db050f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 (Scaling limit of the leftmost positive subtree of $T^k$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] Let $\alpha$ be the unique solution in the interval $(1/2,1)$ to the equation in~\eqref{eq:eq-to-defn-alpha} and recall that $\gamma-1\stackrel{\eqref{eq:gamma-alpha-rel}}{=} \frac{1}{2\alpha}\in (1/2,1)$. 
