{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.088984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba2ade648c39280150dc2966fdf69c118fbebba440da5a3c68a92339594c6049","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:strong-regularity-condition of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] ),d_{\text{BL},1})\)}]
	A subset \(\mathcal{K}\subset (\mathcal{P}_{\nu}(\mathcal{X}\times [0,1]),d_{\text{BL},1})\) is relatively compact if and only if the following properties hold:
	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
		\item \(\mathcal{K}\) is tight. 
