{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.756167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba72ef2879f7d533698d94907ff607b55bf20e155010c27a55cacd7692944c86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 54 ({\cite{C70}*{Theorem 2}}) of arXiv:2609.03836, 'Koszul Orlik--Solomon Algebras from Non-supersolvable Arrangements'] A collection $\Fc$ of subsets (called ``blocks'') of the ground set of a matroid $M$ of rank $r$ is the set of rank $r$ flats of an erection of $M$ if and only if 
