{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.048603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba74d221abf00a6a3fe70a48860901d044c99f9dc51449d1c5309030dfe3e9fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Exact separation at fixed levels and windows) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Assume \cref{ass:global-noise,ass:edge,ass:real-SLL} and weighted compatibility on a neighborhood of a fixed $z_0>b$.  Set $\vartheta_0=d(z_0)^{-1/2}$.  If, for some fixed $\gamma>0$,
