{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.476433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba7a7b5c072f5ad2f7b6548248696ac62b27d9e8155541aa0330f4e1e7a113c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 80 (Equivalent exterior and Fredholm spectral gauges) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $B\in\Sch_2(E)$ be skew-adjoint, let
$a_1\ge a_2\ge\cdots$ be its positive skew singular values, and let
$0<\rho<2$.  Define
\begin{align}

 \mathfrak F_\rho(B)
 &:=\sup_{N\ge1}(N!)^{1/(\rho N)}
   \left(
    \frac{2^N}{N!}\|\alpha_B^{\wedge N}\|
   \right)^{1/N},\\
 M_\rho(B)
 &:=\sup_{x>0}x^{-\rho/2}\log\mathscr D_B(x),
 \qquad
 \mathscr D_B(x):=\prod_{j\ge1}(1+xa_j^2).
\end{align}
Then
\begin{equation}

 c_\rho\|B\|_{\Sch_{\rho,\infty}}
 \le \mathfrak F_\rho(B)
 \le C_\rho\|B\|_{\Sch_{\rho,\infty}},
\end{equation}
and, with $W_\rho:=\sup_jj^{1/\rho}a_j$,
\begin{equation}

 M_\rho(B)\le C_\rho W_\rho^\rho,
 \qquad
 W_\rho\le(\log2)^{-1/\rho}M_\rho(B)^{1/\rho}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}

 B\in\Sch_{\rho,\infty}
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 \mathfrak F_\rho(B)<\infty
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 M_\rho(B)<\infty.
\end{equation}
Thus the weak-Schatten scale is equivalently encoded by factorial exterior
powers or by the positive-axis growth of the Fredholm product. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.949526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba7a9334c532b77e9f25395a47064a2247b4bd0f0c9729b642163910b63466da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Euler-Lagrange equations for the height function in 2D of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Suppose that $h$ is the limit shape height function for $(R,b)$. Then $h$ is the unique solution to the PDE
