{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.208337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba94173763b2710c1e07ffbdcf221513fa3c75caf0bd91dd060bd3a8eb75a130","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.03771, '\vspace{-5ex}\bfseries\scshape{Local law and delocalization for the Sachdev--Ye--Kitaev mo'] Let $\varepsilon\in(0,\frac{1}{2})$ and $q$ be even such that $2\leqslant q\leqslant N^{\frac{1}{2}-\varepsilon}$. Let $H_q$ be the Hamiltonian defined in \eqref{eq:sykhamil}, and let $\psi_j$ be the eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues $\lambda_j$.
