{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.731159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba9de6fb3443fbc3775f02939ff0a568c6ed7c1d4f7f36fb6161414c3361d30c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem asymptotic_normality_smaller_degrees of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m\in\mathbb{N}$ and a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$ is satisfied for  $I_{\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}}=\lfloor n^{\varepsilon}\rfloor$  and $0<\varepsilon<\eta<1-1/((m+1)\log\theta)$ in Parts~(item:hI of the paper) and~(item:Jn of the paper). Let $(i_n^\mathrm{a})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ and $(i_n^\mathrm{f})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be integer-valued sequences such that $i_n^\square\to-\infty$ and $i_n^\square=o(\log n)$ for $\square\in\{\mathrm{a},\mathrm{f}\}$, and let $Z_1$ and $Z_2$ be two i.i.d.\ standard normal random variables. Then,
