{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.632771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba9fbabd8b3c7801865355abf9d1c998b0839d3806f743a50cb5482475162249","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition \cite{lawler80selfavoiding} of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Two-sided LERW $\hat\eta$ satisfies the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item the law $\hat\eta$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the law of $\eta$;
	\item $T^k\eta$ converges weakly to $\hat\eta$ as $k\rightarrow\infty$;
	\item $\hat\eta$ is stationary with respect to $T$, i.e., $T\hat\eta\stackrel{d}{=}\hat\eta$;
	\item $\eta$ and $\hat\eta$ are ergodic with respect to $T$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.961349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baa3d5661bf21d21f4ce699188e0c5a237b22f52e21230775e760870cd4f8761","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 (Intrinsic Taylor expansion) of arXiv:2608.12225, 'Higher-order variation and\\ pathwise It\^o calculus on manifolds'] Let $p\geq1$, $f\in C^p(M)$, and let $K\subset M$ be compact. For
$(x,y)\in {\mathcal U}\cap K^2$, we have
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
    f(y)-f(x)
    &=
    \sum_{k=1}^p
    \frac1{k!}
    (\nabla^{(k)}f)_x
    \bigl(e_\nabla(x,y)^{\otimes k}\bigr)
    +
    R_{p,f}(x,y),

\end{split}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
    |R_{p,f}(x,y)|
    \leq
    \omega_{f,K}(|e_\nabla(x,y)|)
    |e_\nabla(x,y)|^p,\qquad \omega_{f,K}(r)\longrightarrow0
    \qquad\text{as }r\downarrow0.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.816935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baa6b7e2976d97982125d83ce18b0449377b47fd35f450fdb759787f159a907e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cond-lem of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $\{ \mathbf{X} _n\}$ be an adapted sequence of $\mathcal{S}_d$-valued random matrices with conditional means $ \mathbb E  ( \mathbf{X} _n | \mathcal{F}_{n-1}) =  \mathbf{M} _n$. Further, suppose there is a predictable and integrable sequence of $\mathcal{S}_d$-valued random matrices $\{ \widehat  \mathbf{X} _n \}$ such that $\lambda_{\min}( \mathbf{X} _n - \widehat  \mathbf{X} _n ) \geqslant -1$. Let
\begin{equation}
      \mathbf{E} _n =  \exp(\gamma_n( \mathbf{X} _n - \widehat{ \mathbf{X} }_n)  - \psi_{\mathrm{E}}(\gamma_n) ( \mathbf{X} _n - \widehat{ \mathbf{X} }_n)^2) ,\quad  \mathbf{F} _n = \exp(\gamma_n ( \mathbf{M} _n - \widehat{ \mathbf{X} }_n)  ),
\end{equation}
where $\{ \gamma_n \}$ are predictable $(0,1)$-valued scalars. Then,
\begin{equation}
     \mathbb E  ( \mathbf{E} _n|\mathcal{F}_{n-1}) \preceq  \mathbf{F} _{n}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.734400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baa87bb0ac880d7d903b45a72083abae08a0a6b2c0db444048be1a02fd2519bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sobolev of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] On the unit sphere $\mathbb S^{N-1}$, for any $g \in W^1_2(\mathbb S^{N-1})$, we have the Sobolev inequality
    \begin{align*}
        \left\lVertg\right\rVert_q^2\leq \frac{q-2}{N-1} \left\lVert\nabla g\right\rVert_2^2+\left\lVertg\right\rVert_2^2\,,
    \end{align*}
    where $q=\frac{2(N-1)}{N-3}$.    
    Switching to $\mathbf{S}_N$, for any $f\in W^1_2(\mathbf{S}_N)$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \left\lVertf\right\rVert_q^2\leq \frac{N(q-2)}{N-1} \left\lVert\nabla f\right\rVert_2^2+\left\lVertf\right\rVert_2^2\,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.847546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baab58696f47e8c8897d1ae84449a3f354e08d5da62f874d9147754a67923797","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the: characterization of subsequential limits of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] The following property holds with probability one:
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_0^t \angled{\bar r\left(\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s\right) h_g^x + h_g^y}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}ds < \infty \quad \text{for all} \quad t \geq 0.
	\end{equation*}
	Furthermore, for all $t \geq 0$ and $\varphi \in C_c^1(\mathbbm{R}_+^3)$, we have:
	\begin{align*}
		\angled{\varphi_t}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_t} &= \angled{\varphi_0}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_0} + \lambda_0 \int_0^t \varphi_s(0, 0)ds - \int_0^t \angled{\varphi_s\left[\bar r(\bar \boldsymbol{\mu}_s)h_g^x + h_g^y\right]}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}ds \\
		&+ \int_0^t \angled{\partial_t\varphi_s + \bar r\left(\bar \boldsymbol{\mu}_s\right)\partial_x\varphi_s + \partial_y\varphi_s}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}ds.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

