{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.475817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb495bbd39f084704a0e0fd63daac0190cefc128b862241fbf53a087e91d934a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:laplacian-general of arXiv:2505.02685, 'On the Spectral Expansion of Monotone Subsets of the Hypercube'] The \emph{directed Laplacian operator} of $G$ is the operator $\mathscr{L}^- = \mathscr{L}^-_{G} : L^2(V) \to
    L^2(V)$ given by
    \begin{equation}
