      Furthermore, if $(\widetilde{\tau}_n)$ is also an FS for $\mathbb{C}$, then $H_{\bullet}A=X$ where $X$ is given by
      \begin{equation*}
      X=\left((H_0A_0)I_{\llbracket{0}\rrbracket}+\sum\limits_{n=1}^{{+\infty}}
      (H^{\widetilde{\tau}_n}.A^{\widetilde{\tau}_n})I_{\rrbracket{\widetilde{\tau}_{n-1},\widetilde{\tau}_n}
      \rrbracket}\right)\mathfrak{I}_\mathbb{C},\quad \widetilde{\tau}_0=0.
      \end{equation*}
      In this case, we say that the expression of \eqref{HA-expression0} is independent of the choice of FS $(\tau_n)$ for $\mathbb{C}$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.683729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb70e48e1d72619ea8990865d0facfeae9f14b05b83ecdcf5fab67b036588b77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 of arXiv:2609.03777, '2609.03777'] Let $N,r\in\ZZ_{>0}$. For $\tau\in C$ and $\mu_1,\mu_2\in\Lambda_\tau$ with $\mu_1\ordN\mu_2$ and $\mu_1\succ\mu_2$, we have
