{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.300587+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb7e29c7310379ac16c44c94b9c318b8d1814310144ce1a3b684fad45e40d988","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:potential-single of arXiv:2602.19192, 'Bakry--\'Emery Curvature of the Fractional Laplacian\\ via Fractional Brownian Covariance'] For $f(x) = \cos x$ and $V(x) = -\omega^2\cos x$:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\Gamma_{L,2}(f,f)(x)}{\Gamma(f,f)(x)}
  = \frac{1 + \alpha^2\cos 2x + \tfrac{\omega^2}{2}(\cos x + \beta\cos 3x)}
         {1 + \alpha\cos 2x},
\end{equation}
where
$\alpha(\gamma) = 1 - 2^{\gamma-1}$ and
$\beta(\gamma) = (2^{\gamma+1} - 3^\gamma - 1)/2$.
At $\gamma = 1$: $\alpha = \beta = 0$, giving
$\Gamma_{L,2}/\Gamma = 1 + \frac{\omega^2}{2}\cos x$
with minimum $1 - \omega^2/2$ at $x = \pi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.609111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb7f5a04836322d502a58127aa8421cd1c7b5a9517c290655cfb0655efe2e5c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:T1-T2 of arXiv:2604.04922, 'Elephant random walk on the infinite dihedral group $\mathbb{Z}_2 * \mathbb{Z}_2$'] Define
\begin{align}
    T_{1, n, q} &:= \sum_{k = 1}^n \frac{H(k,q) I(k, q)}{k^2} \cdot \int_0^1 \frac{u^{k+q-1} (1-u)^{1 - q}}{1 + u} \, du, \\ 
    T_{2, n, q} &:= \int_0^1 \frac{u^{n + q} (1 - u)^{-q}}{1 + u}\, du \sum_{k = 1}^n (-1)^{n - k} \frac{H(k, q) I(k, q)}{k^2},
\end{align}
where $H(k, q)$ is as in (equation eq:H_defn of the paper) and
\begin{equation}
    I(k, q) := \bigg(\int_0^1 u^{k + q - 1} (1 - u)^{-q} \, du\bigg)^{-1} = \frac{\Gamma(k + 1)}{\Gamma(k + q)\Gamma(1 - q)}.
\end{equation}
Then for any $n \ge 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}[\tilde{Z}_{n + 1}^2] = T_{1, n, q} + 2 \, T_{2, n, q}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

