\end{array}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.905591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bba0c15254136624fb6a10a1dbd58cd271bc968c6014084efa1b2ff8e2be25a6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2607.17177, '2607.17177'] For any $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_T>0$ such that, for any $N\in\N^+$ and $y_T\in\mathcal H$, the solution $y$ of equation \eqref{oseen adjoint} satisfies
