{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.022227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bba4770290b76f1a0077d2c447ef06f7fe3c5e492af21d5396769a396d53642d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (\cite{voiculescu2000lectures,voiculescu_analogues_1999,gao2008}) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Let $\{U_t\}_{t\ge0}$ be a family of self-adjoint operators in $\widetilde{\mathscr A}$.
For each $t\ge0$, define von Neumann subalgebras
\begin{equation*}
\mathscr B_{\le t}:=W^*(U_s:0\le s\le t),\qquad
\mathscr B_{\ge t}:=W^*(U_s:s\ge t),\qquad
\mathscr B_{=t}:=W^*(U_t).
\end{equation*}
We say that $\{U_t\}_{t\ge0}$ is a \emph{free Markov process} if, for every $t\ge0$, $\mathscr B_{\le t}$ and $\mathscr B_{\ge t}$ are $\mathscr B_{=t}$-free.","status":"unverified"}

