{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.101898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbb63bb16fab696068119eab98480845ec84796f55aca889a9b3b4c7a7624bc7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:equivalent_Gcausal of arXiv:2608.13716, 'Graph Causal Optimal Transport \\ and Wasserstein Distances'] Suppose $G$ is a DAG, $\mu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{X}}$, $\nu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{Y}}$, and $\pi \in \couplings{\mu}{\nu}$. Then the following are equivalent:

