{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbcdabed08d7cfe8fd871029a2aa4b95a25f4f6686910caab6dacc4eccdabad6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] For every integer $q\geq0$, the function $h_q$ in~\cref{eq:hq-definition} satisfies
