{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbd6db5e88aaba902ea0f8e1428ac3e54301bc96565acf8b9b1a44a80457be9e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 99 (Theorem 1 in \cite{MP05}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] For $u,v \in V(G)$, let $q_t(u,v)$ be the $t$-step transition kernel of the lazy random walk on $(G, \weight)$. 
