{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.006806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbe8832157018dafcacb50b01509454bb3754f0244f15c91e0841117daa566b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition B4z of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] For $N$ large enough, we can find an $s_1>0$ such that for any $s$ with $s_1\le s\le \frac{2\tilde{\mu}_{n,N}}{3\tilde{\sigma}_{N,n}}$ and $z$ around $z_1$,
