{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.907063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbfbe1eb3607e89b22a00ef1099a6dae8130da95c53d54322f9280e1350af536","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:local-extinction of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] Let $\mathscr{Z}^\vartheta_t(A)$ be the mass of the Critical 2D SHF with (without loss of generality)
