{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.687723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc03ee58a3518586d79085f1459e3f24ec7d8522abd3e447d0f3b6444fb0beac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Straight signature line) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $E$ be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space, denote its norm by $\norm{\cdot}_E$, and let $0\neq v\in E$.
Then
\[
\mathcal{A}_v=\set{\e^{tv}:t\in\R}
\]
is a closed geodesic line in $(\Sl(E),d_\infty)$, and
\begin{equation}
d_\infty(\e^{sv},\e^{tv})=\abs{t-s}\,\norm{v}_E
\qquad (s,t\in\R).
\end{equation}
If $a\in\Sl(E)$ and $g=a\e^v a^{-1}$, then
\[
\mathcal{A}=a\mathcal{A}_v
 =\set{a\e^{tv}:t\in\R}
\]
is a closed convex geodesic line, invariant under left multiplication by $g$, and
\begin{equation}
g\,a\e^{tv}=a\e^{(t+1)v}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.812681+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc05937335566276fbbb24513d0598410c3402164126f477bef10461363236d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:mellinbeta of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] The Mellin transform of the function
    \begin{align*}
        h(t) = \frac{1}{(1+t^2)^{a}}, \quad a>0,
    \end{align*}
    is absolutely convergent for $0< \re(z)<a$ and it is given by
    \begin{align}
        M[h,z] = \frac{\Gamma\left(\frac{z}{2}\right)\Gamma\left(\frac{a-z}{2}\right)}{2\Gamma\left(\frac{a}{2}\right)}.
