  The index set has cardinality $|\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon,\epsilon_1}(c)|\leq \kappa^{2n}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc109f4d3a8ae8a47524d80419b8effb2c864302ca9817a9f7ecea4798f7a611","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 (Universality of general functionals over triangulable spaces) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $M \subset \RR^D$ be an admissibly triangulable space and let $f: M \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a good density. Let $\func_n$ be a functional that satisfies the conditions (1)--(7). Then there exists a real number $\overline{\func}^*$ so that the  following holds independently of $M$ and $f$:
