{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.897443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc3dcff598a39cf6fda1e2e6c64b9776ba76b650e609d9c9aea6f0de94338678","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 37 (Polynomial reformulation of Theorem~\ref{main_thm}) of arXiv:2606.19115, 'Finite free perpetuities'] Fix $\kappa\in\N$ and $\mathcal{I}\subset\{1,\dots,\kappa\}$. Let $(p_n^{[j]})_{n \in \N, 1 \le j \le \kappa}$ be a family of polynomials such that $p_n^{[j]} \in \mathcal{P}_n(\R_{\ge 0})$ for all $1\le j\le\kappa$. Assume that 
