{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.712657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc438e4797425e99373b761ea147e859f3085d2a9eb5aac51e102c90f211df94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:power_law_dev of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $\alpha>1$. Consider the one-dimensional random band matrix $H$  in definition (defmodel of the paper) with Gaussian entries and the bandwidth $W \ll N^{1-\frac{1}{3\alpha}}$. There exist absolute constants $C_1, C_2, C_3,C_4 > 0$,  when   $y>C_4$ and $W$ satisfy the constraint $y^{\frac{\alpha}{4\alpha-2}} W^{\frac{3\alpha}{3\alpha-1}} \le C_3 N$, then
