{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.970363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc6207888f8bce1c9ca3b03690dc1ac2e48a339450ea633c89d002a8e8a7e36f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 25 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] There exists $c_{c}=c_{c}(d,m)>0$ such that for any $\Ga>0$, $R>0$, for $\mathcal{C}$ as defined in \eqref{e.regdefs} and $\mathcal{S}$ as defined in \eqref{e.bbSdef},  
