{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.769814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc626c8e565ae4170c8d0a08aa1971bc7fecc52333b4078ca7157e429add6cf8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop number of components of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Let $(X_n)_{n \geq 1}$ be a sequence of random finite $d$-dimensional simplicial complexes that converges locally weakly in probability to a random $(d-1)$-rooted simplicial complex $(X, o) \sim \mu$. Let $C_n$ denote the number of $d$-dimensional connected components in $X_n$. Then, it holds that
\[  \tag{2.2.1}
