{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.056180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc7d2a5959c5855c9fd807798ca53e8f2d9b2dd59ccf1c628f9001ddafa895d2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 (Sphere quadratic forms) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $w$ be uniform on the unit sphere of $\F^N$, and let $D$ be deterministic Hermitian with $\norm D_{\op}\le M$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left(\left|w^*Dw-\frac1N\tr D\right|>t\right)
 \le 2\exp\left(-cN\min\left(\frac{t^2}{M^2},\frac tM\right)\right)
\end{equation}
for all $t>0$.  In particular the Gaussian form $2\exp(-cNt^2/M^2)$ holds for $0<t\le M$, and on any range $t\le CM$ the two exponents agree up to the constant $c$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.643835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc7de441cb021db1113e1d8208f30083cafb45ba4fa21f88a7507b683e03963d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (\citet{EloOurs}) of arXiv:2605.24445, 'Matrix concentration inequalities for time-inhomogeneous Markov chains'] \label[lemma]{lem:elo_fixed_environment_curvature}
