{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.072390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc83cf6f64781203081bb6df92b0b6b6fea4ff1111d43b4a133e3ac48bf07ac0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 26 of arXiv:2606.01832, 'MA(1) processes with uniform innovations conditioned to stay positive in the non-expanding'] In the orange region, for any $0\le m\le p$, it holds
    \begin{align*}
        \hat{P}_{a,y,\theta}(z)=\sum_{i=0}^mc_{m,i}(\theta,a,z)H_i(y),~~~~~y\in A_m,
    \end{align*}
   with radius of convergence $|z|<\frac{1}{\lambda}$ and recursive definitions
    \begin{align*}
   c_{0,0}&\coloneqq c_{0,0}(\theta,a,z)\coloneqq \frac{1}{1-zF(z)},
        \\c_{m,i}&\coloneqq c_{m,i}(\theta,a,z)\coloneqq \frac{-z\theta^i}{a+1}c_{m-1,i-1},~~~~~1\le i\le m,~~~~\text{and}
