{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.382372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc8d8d17b1d4dc1aa4318b875ca24e9960fc52160c138df6fcb9fd33fa656f8a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main-LK of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}\in\mathcal{G}_2^\Lambda(\mathbb R^d)$ be in the global form, and $\mathcal{A}^\bullet,\mathcal{B}^\bullet$, $\bullet\in\{\nabla,\Delta,J\}$ be the drift, diffusion,  and jump part of $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}$ respectively. It holds for all $x,y\in \mathbb R^d$: 
