{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.820346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc9962e032fbc22b69e6e7fb2847c269125c70f1d46c4a539a0d80d72a6edcdd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop sub-halfin-whitt-mixing-integral-lambda of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\pi_{n,t}, \nu_n$ be the queue length distribution at time $t$ and the steady state distribution of the continuous-time $M/M/n$ system with unit service rate respectively and let $\{\lambda_n\}$ be a sequence of integer arrival rates ($\lambda_n \in \Z$) such that $\lambda_n \geq 0, n-\lambda_n \geq 1, \frac{\log\br{n-\lambda_n}}{\log n} \in (1/2,1)$ and
