{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.789656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcb3c63e6c9768d7672fbbd03c3b48831c5cb5a588f29ed66955ca86ef88e65f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:relu-switching-distance of arXiv:2608.22910, 'A Commutator Framework for Selective Spectral Alignment in Deep Neural Networks'] For every \(s,t\),
\begin{equation}
\|D_\ell(\cdot,t)-D_\ell(\cdot,s)\|_{
\mathrm L^2(\mu;F)}^2
