{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.821906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcc04ab8a4ffd01cf1621c8c51a56a42292fc90e96d01ddc68650825143665f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ordered-group-shadow of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Let $\Gamma$ be any linearly ordered abelian group, let
$A=(a_0<\cdots<a_{k-1})\subset\Gamma$, where $k\geq2$, and let
$h\in\mathbb Z_{\geq1}$.  Write
$r=r_h^\Gamma(A)$ and $d=k-1-r$.  There are integers
\[
 0=b_0<b_1<\cdots<b_{k-1}
\]
such that, for every $1\leq j\leq h$ and $u,v\in\mathcal U_{j,k}$,
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{sgn}_{\Gamma}\!\left(\sum_i(u_i-v_i)a_i\right)
 =\operatorname{sgn}\!\left(\sum_i(u_i-v_i)b_i\right),
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 b_{k-1}
 \leq d h^{d-1}\prod_{i=1}^{r}p_i^\Gamma(A)
 \leq(k-1-r)h^{k-2},
\end{equation}
with the empty product understood as one.  For fixed $k$, the universal
$h$-exponent $k-2$ is optimal, already for subsets of $\mathbb Z$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.768322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcc1458aa14e7990038d238ba1736b498f384781866736d595cc8ff638a62302","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Step2 of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $(Z,d,\mathfrak{m})$ be as in (Setting of the paper), and let us assume it verifies the global Sobolev inequality (equation eqn:GlobalSobolev of the paper), and the Ricci lower bound (equation eqn:RicciControl of the paper) in (assumptions of the paper). Let $f\in W^{1,2}(Z,d,\mathfrak{m})$ verify $\Delta f= -\lambda f$ for some $\lambda\geqslant 0$. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that 
