{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.970946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcd80762cd6dba5b01f1d7b4b48ec6b668c1deecc807bf9599d9a8a9cf301664","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:R1b of arXiv:2509.17319, 'Non-directed polymers in random environments with range penalties: the high-dimensional ca'] Let $\alpha\in(\frac{d}{2},2)$ (in particular $d=2,3$) and $(\zeta,\gamma)\in R_1$ (see Figure (diagram2 of the paper)). Then $(S_n)_{0\leq n \leq N}$ has end-to-end fluctuations of order $N^{\xi}$ under ${\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} _N$ with $\xi=\frac12$ and we have the following scaling limits for ${\ensuremath{\mathbf Z}} _N$.

\noindent{\rm (i)} If $\zeta\in(1,\gamma+\frac{d(\alpha-1)}{2\alpha})$, then
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{h_N{\ensuremath{\mathbf E}} [|{\ensuremath{\mathcal R}} _N|]}\log{\ensuremath{\mathbf Z}} _N\overset{{\ensuremath{\mathbbm P}} }{\longrightarrow}-1.
\end{equation}

