{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.631451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcf1354bebbe72eb5ab52da8a46659c80394e1ffeb5d78dc1cc959fab1493b17","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$, $\psi$ be its generator, $\vartheta \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$, $A \in \mathcal{A}$ be the corresponding Pickands dependence function, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$. Then the following equation holds for every $t \in (0,1)$:
