{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.410024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd2569758294579eb10ed1ccd0452979947f1c2a69d35b181844d5fa9a833c72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:qtaylor of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] There exists a constant $C > 0$ so that 
    \begin{align*}
        &\left| \mathbb{E}[s_{Q_n'((\tilde{X}_n)_{ab})}(z)] - \mathbb{E}[s_{Q_n'((\tilde{Y}_n)_{ab})}(z)] \right| \\
        &\qquad\leq C \frac{(A_n)_{ab}}{\varepsilon n K_n}   \left( \mathbb{E}[( X_n)^2_{ab}\chi_{ \{|(X_n)_{ab}| > \varepsilon \sqrt{K_n} \} }] + \mathbb{E}[( Y_n)^2_{ab}\chi_{ \{|(Y_n)_{ab}| > \varepsilon \sqrt{K_n} \} }] \right) \\
        &\qquad\qquad + C \frac{(A_n)_{ab}}{ n K_n} \varepsilon \left( \mathbb{E}[|(X_n)_{ab}|^2] + \mathbb{E}[|(Y_n)_{ab}|^2] \right),
