{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.632675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd59fb5f52cf60d3be35ac4141268bd47947356552b27f83ab867a29bbd8f2f6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Recursive derivation of the W_k coefficient of arXiv:2603.10738, 'Pairwise Negative Correlation for Uniform Spanning\\ Subgraphs of the Complete Graph'] For $r\;\geqslant\; 3$, 
	define ${\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _1(r)$ and ${\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _2(r)$ as follows:
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbf{C}_1(r) = \sum_{j=1}^{r-2} 9j(r-1-j) \chi_{j} \chi_{r-1-j},
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbf{C}_2(r) = \sum_{j=1}^{r-2} \Big( 3j(3(r-1-j)-1)\chi_{j} \tilde{\chi}_{r-1-j} + 3(r-1-j)(3j-1)\tilde{\chi}_{j} \chi_{r-1-j} \Big).
	\end{equation}
	For simplicity, we denote ${\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _1={\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _1(k)$ and ${\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _2={\ensuremath{\mathbf C}} _2(k)$. 
