{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.106963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd72765525920d18683e2a49272a0ff2109a6bc39b7ff26233acdd9e198cebc7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition DEF34 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $(\widehat{{\mathscr E}},\widehat{{\mathscr F}})$ be another Dirichlet form on $L^2(\widehat{E},\widehat{m})$ with $\text{supp}[\widehat{m}]=\widehat E$.  The Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ is called \emph{quasi-homeomorphic} to $(\widehat{{\mathscr E}},\widehat{{\mathscr F}})$ if there exists an ${\mathscr E}$-nest $\{F_n:n\geq 1\}$, an $\widehat{{\mathscr E}}$-nest $\{\widehat{F}_n: n\geq 1\}$ and a map $j:\bigcup_{n\geq 1}F_n\rightarrow \bigcup_{n\geq 1}\widehat{F}_n$ such that 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] $j$ is a topological homeomorphism from $F_n$ to $\widehat{F}_n$ for each $n\geq 1$.
\item[(2)] $\widehat{m}=m\circ j^{-1}$.
\item[(3)] $(\widehat{{\mathscr E}},\widehat{{\mathscr F}})=j({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$,  the image Dirichlet form of $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ under $j$. 
\end{itemize}
Such a map $j$ is called a \emph{quasi-homeomorphism} from $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ to $(\widehat{{\mathscr E}},\widehat{{\mathscr F}})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.404003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd739f499796a6be2fffcb5e641130e7970252d00ac54b164b04107d44f26d67","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm tcl of arXiv:2412.06480, 'A SIR epidemic model on a refining spatial grid \\ II-Central limit theorem'] For $3/2<\gamma <2$, as $\varepsilon \to 0$, $\{\mathscr{Y}_{\varepsilon}(t)\; , \;  0\le t\le T \}_{0<\varepsilon<1} \Longrightarrow \{\mathscr{Y}(t)\; , \;  0\le t\le T \}$ in $C\big([0,T]\, ; \,  (\mathrm{H}^{-\gamma})^3\big)\cap  L^2\big(0,T; (\mathrm{H}^{-1})^3\big)$, where the limit $\mathscr{Y}$ is solution of the following system of SPDEs : for all $\varphi \in \mathrm{H}^{1}$
	\begin{equation}
