{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.758866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bdb733ae3a8e5d1b4579c1e2e14f0bc6a975f9b7c429270c051db202be046315","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:green-hilbert-schmidt of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The inclusion $\Omega_{\rm Fr}\subseteq\Omega_{\rm HS}$ holds.  For every
$x\in\Omega_{\rm HS}$, the operator $G_x$ is positive, self-adjoint,
and Hilbert--Schmidt, with
\begin{equation}
 \|G_x\|_{\rm HS}^2
 =\iint_{D^2}G_D(z,w)^2\,M_x(dz)M_x(dw)<\infty.
\end{equation}
For all $\theta,\eta\in L^2(M_x)$,
\begin{align}
 \iint_{D^2}|G_D(z,w)\theta(z)\eta(w)|\,M_x(dz)M_x(dw)
 &\le \|G_x\|_{\mathrm{HS}}\|\theta\|_2\|\eta\|_2,              \\
 I_D(\theta M_x,\eta M_x)
 &=\langle\theta,G_x\eta\rangle_{L^2(M_x)},                       \\
 |I_D(\theta M_x,\eta M_x)|
 &\le \|G_x\|_{\mathrm{HS}}\|\theta\|_2\|\eta\|_2.            
\end{align}
Consequently, $\theta M_x\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D)$ for every $\theta\in L^2(M_x)$, and
\begin{equation}
 \theta\ne0
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \langle\theta,G_x\theta\rangle_{L^2(M_x)}
 =I_D(\theta M_x)>0.
\end{equation}
In particular, $\kerG_x=\{0\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.933904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bdbada32f46b74c00d1019683a8142928fb5ded55d47d130f8e92e2d32a8838d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $\langle G_n \rangle$ be an exhaustion of $\Z^d$ and let $\nu^\infty$ be the MSF measure on $\Z^d$. Then 
