{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.614195+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bde43c112082e11faaff8ac81667277e48a5487e409aad0ebc869e4ccdf02e2c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:expressionsForG>0 of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let the functions $G_D^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, k}(\cdot, \cdot)$ be as defined in Definition (EHI:d:GkDef of the paper). Then for all $x, y \in D$,
