{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.298052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bdeb70dbf90294eb6b981b2ceda88939ef5e0bc598733adc7f5f4fbf276a3603","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: bound the difference of times of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] Let $0\le k\le\min\{v_2,w_2\}$. On the event that $E_{\rightarrow}(\lambda^-; -v, k\mathbf{e}_2)$ and $E_{\uparrow}(\lambda^+; -v, -k\mathbf{e}_2)$ occur, it holds that
