{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.328603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be0e66d86f41368e57b9bfa76e71efe29c72627c5630301b99e601cec01c59d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:properties_extrapolated_spaces of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $A$ be a positive, invertible, and self-adjoint operator on a Hilbert space $X$. Let $(\mathscr{X}^A_\sigma)_{\sigma\in{\mathbb R}}$ be the scale of Hilbert spaces defined in (equation eq:extrapolated_space1 of the paper)-(equation eq:extrapolated_space2 of the paper). 
Then the following assertions hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item {\rm (Extrapolated operator)}
For each $\sigma <0$ (resp.\ $\sigma>0$), the operator $A$ uniquely extends (resp.\ restricts) to a positive, invertible, and self-adjoint operator $A_\sigma$ on $\mathscr{X}^A_{\sigma}$ with domain $\mathsf{D}(A_\sigma)=\mathscr{X}_{1+\sigma}^A$. 

\item {\rm (Interpolation)}
For $\sigma_0,\sigma_1\in {\mathbb R}$ and $\theta\in (0,1)$, 
$$
\mathscr{X}_{\sigma}^A = [\mathscr{X}_{\sigma_0}^A ,\mathscr{X}_{\sigma_1}^A]_{\theta} \quad \text{ where }\quad \sigma=(1-\theta)\sigma_0+\theta\sigma_1.
$$
\item {\rm (Duality)} For each $\sigma \geq 0$, it holds that $
 \mathscr{X}_{-\sigma}^{A}
 =(\mathscr{X}_{\sigma}^{A})^*
$ and
$$
\langle x^*,x\rangle_{-\sigma,\sigma}^{A}
= ((A^{-\sigma})_{-\sigma} x^*,A^{\sigma}x)_{X} \ \text{ for all }\ x^*\in \mathscr{X}^A_{-\sigma}, \ x\in \mathscr{X}^A_{\sigma}.
$$
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

