{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.751449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be3402502427c1394cef9bae4f2bddd1ee49210d3c76555afdb81d49d5edfee9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:equiv_weak of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $v:(0,T)\to L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and let also $\sigma$, $b$ be as in (equation eq:sig_b_deg_den of the paper) and $\nu \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. If either
