{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.622682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be3a41205ddfc057d26e60700c80606ce786d6bf1d0cdef8c79d532d6ece4ba9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:PE of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X \in \mathcal{I}(d, r_0)$, and let $T$ be a random variable with Exponential($\lambda$) distribution, independent of $X$. For all $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $r>0$, we have each of the following:
