{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.369627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be6fa595313291f45896bc30c17380c710365bb27d0ca0d51ced8fd5da19442f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:davies329 of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] If $D \subseteq \bR^d$ is a bounded region with the extension property, then the Neumann heat kernel $p^r_\eta(1, x, y)$ satisfies, for any $\delta > 0$, and some constant $c_{\delta, D}$,
