{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.446812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be71e3fe67a3064e9e858e72c72a6245937331f9cae103fa41babaf95a6a63a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm finite N master loop equation of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] {cao2023random};} \textsc{$\mathrm{U}(N)$ master loop equation for finite $N$}]
Let $s = \{\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n\}$ be a string. Fix a specific edge $\mathbf{e}$ on $s$. Then \begin{align*}
	\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s) =&\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s') - \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s') \\
	&+ \upbeta\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s') - \upbeta \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda, N, \upbeta}(s')\\
	&+ \frac{1}{N^2}\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{M}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s') - \frac{1}{N^2}\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{M}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\Lambda,N, \upbeta}(s').
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

