{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.587913+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be986d1f05a25e2a593919fb60636d1249eb9b80a09651893acd97f4e7671e38","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor lambda_conv of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $1<p<2$  and let  $\mathsf{P}_i\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with  finite free energy $\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$, and $\Pi_i:= \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_i)$ for  $i=0,1$. Assume that the function $f^{p/(p-2)}$  (cf. assumption (assumption1 of the paper)) is convex on $[0,\infty)$ and  $\int f^{p/(p-2)}( \mathsf{s}_1)\Pi_i(d \mathsf{s})<\infty$ for $i=0,1$. Then $ \mathscr W_p(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)<\infty$ and 
