 where  $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ is the $\mathscr W_p-$optimal coupling from  Theorem (thm:interaction_gain of the paper), $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$ and  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.288709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be9b3c67eb10f63ad59ca2c4d61dfb3094baeb167ad798b2c38419f216a49166","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] If $X$ is an affine process on $S$, then for all $0 \leq T' \leq T$, there exist
