{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.748361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_beb4f910d96c009b9fcd8879edda97dca0a1409528bdc252ad93586e995fb336","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Multiplicative heat flow preserves positive/unitary zeros) of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] Let $P_n(x)\in \C[x]$ be a polynomial of degree $n\in \N$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)]  The positive case: If  all roots of $P_n$ are in $[0,\infty)$, then for every $s\geq 0$ all roots of the polynomials $\eee^{- \frac s{2} ((x \partial_x)^2- n x \partial_x) } P_n$ are also in $[0,\infty)$.
\item[(b)] The unitary case: If  all roots of $P_n$ are located  on the unit circle $\{|z|=1\}$, then for every $s\leq 0$ all roots of the polynomials $\eee^{- \frac s{2} ((x \partial_x)^2- n x \partial_x) } P_n$ are located on the unit circle.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.737323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_beb5c4addfcd4f07137b3038713a81124eb0b912cc6316d646a09f699c7ff179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2506.10476, 'Construction of ergodic \textsc{idla} forests in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] {(Global upper bound)}

