{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.385114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bec4a4ab374d3cf4893d0a62d5d00a177603b146cf6a18633e1ee2202d490f36","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2607.28004, 'Folding representations of reflected diffusions'] Consider an absolutely continuous function $\sigma: I \to (0,\infty)$ as in \eqref{eq:sigma_abs_cont}, and the strictly increasing function $g:I \to [0,\infty)$ of \eqref{eq:g}. Then there exists a unique pair $(f,\nu)$, with $f:I \to I$ of class $C^1(I)$ and $\nu \in (0,\infty)$, which satisfies \eqref{eq:nonlinear_ODE_nu} as well as 
