{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.077784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bee8bfc849b2f6088465f24fbd17bfb45472f884a5e4e16bcf4bdb7a35612460","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:change-patial-int of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Let $(Y,\mathcal Y,\mu)$ be a measurable  space with $\mu:\mathcal Y\to[0,\infty]$. Let $f$ be a complex-valued function defined on
