{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.743632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_beea4b09945dd4130898d3bffdbbbb7e0c8a856cef90cfd0ce82e300aa532e61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem cor022404-26 of arXiv:2606.07353, 'The Gaussian structure of a perturbed KPZ'] Under the assumption (equation V00 of the paper), {$\nu_V$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\nu$, i.e.,}  there exists a unique $\bar
