{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.384738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_beec9e18a96798710a1468f4c521957ab15d7b31946f0978124f9416e12673bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Levy_Coupling of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mu,\nu\in\Lambda(\mathbb R^d)$ be two Lévy measures on $\mathbb{R}^d$. A \emph{Lévy coupling} between $\mu,\nu$ is a Lévy measure $\gamma$ on $\mathbb{R}^{2d}$ such that for all measurable sets $E\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ that \emph{does not contain a neighbourhood of $0$}, it holds
