{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.168782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf67506825ca396fbcda0eb8b28cc6b851a491c762e5cc981051a615d6b39e66","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Stability of the Mild Solution) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. For a fixed penalization parameter $\varepsilon > 0$, let $u_{\varepsilon, 1}$ and $u_{\varepsilon, 2}$ be the respective mild solutions of \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized} driven by the problem data triplets $(f_1, \Phi_1, \Psi_1)$ and $(f_2, \Phi_2, \Psi_2)$. Then there exists a constant $C_T > 0$ such that:
