{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.636653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf75f3d28f0ef138b73b36224b15777c07abee7ba19c4a486c6ea1268c170dd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $\eps > 0$. Then, there exists $C = C(\eps,P,\G)$ such that 
