	for some constants $C_1, L>0$ and $K \in \mathbb{N}_+$. Recall the definition of $\| \cdot \|_{2,n}$ in \eqref{L2discnorm}. It holds
	\begin{align*}
\forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad		\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ \widehat{b}_n \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )    F_x(\eta_r^n)  \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq 2 C_1 (t-s)^{2} n \frac{(\widehat{b}_n)^2 K}{L^{2}} \| \nabla H \|^{2}_{2,n}.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.302450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf82ffbe9704f3864b0014583a5333709507ef4c7a61697fb8debee4a7b5f352","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 26 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Recall $\mathcal K$ from \eqref{kdef}. For $   \varsigma_N \in \R^d$, define the function $\boldsymbol u_{   \varsigma_N}: \R^d \to \R$ by 
