{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.040943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf83e5a4291925f067073ede88dd9b16d445fac1fea51cd55d788cbc724f5896","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tightmodulifactorization of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] The subset $\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathrm{tight}}_{g,n,p}(\mathbf{L},\mathbf{K})^{[\Gamma']_{g,n+p}}(\mathbf{x})\subset \mathcal{M}_{g,n+p}(\mathbf{L},\mathbf{K})^{\Gamma'}(\mathbf{x})$ is invariant under the torus action (twisting along the curves $\gamma_1',\ldots,\gamma_k'$) and the image under the symplectomorphism (equation eq:cuttingsymplectomorphism of the paper) of its quotient space $\hat{\mathcal{M}}^{\mathrm{tight}}_{g,n,p}(\mathbf{L},\mathbf{K})^{[\Gamma']_{g,n+p}*}(\mathbf{x})$ is 
