{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.616653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf855e38f50a279e0c71d17d3b8dca35630b747c846325229f180d088605374f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 141 (Basic properties of the flow map of $\newuL$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\newuL$ be the null vectorfield defined in \eqref{E:DOUBLENULLEIKONALFUNCTIONNORMALIZEDNULLVECTORFIELDS}, and recall that $\flowmapofnewularg{\Delta s}$ is the flow map of $\newuL$ (see Theorem\,\ref{T:CONSTRUCTIONOFTHEINGOINGEIKONALFUNCTIONCONTRACTIONMAPPING}). 

