{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:10.026815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf9c5db58766aec9c257775b9eab3842b0a5cb1b258428cc131a6e1303bf778d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem fixed-size-family-counts of arXiv:2607.21428, 'Subcritical percolation and network archaeology on random recursive tree substrate network'] Recall that \(W_{n,i}=|\mathcal{B}_{n,i}|\) are the ranked retained-tree blob
		sizes.  The following estimates hold.
		\begin{enumeratea}
			\item Let \(N_k(t)\) be the number of type families of size \(k\) at Yule
			time \(t\).  Then, for each fixed \(k\geqslant1\),
			\[
			\frac{N_k(t)}{Y(t)}
			\to
			q_k
			:=
			\frac{1-p}{p}B\left(k,1+\frac1p\right)
			\qquad\text{a.s.},
			\]
			where \(B(\cdot,\cdot)\) is the Beta function.  If
			\(N_{n,k}:=\#\{i:W_{n,i}=k\}\), then \(N_{n,k}/n\to q_k\) almost surely.
			\item For every fixed \(r>0\),
			\begin{equation}

				\sum_i W_{n,i}^r
				=
				\begin{cases}
					O_{\mathbb P}(n), & pr<1,\\
					O_{\mathbb P}(n\log n), & pr=1,\\
					O_{\mathbb P}(n^{pr}), & pr>1.
				\end{cases}
			\end{equation}
			In particular, for every \(\eta>0\),
			\[
			\sum_i W_{n,i}^r
			=
			O_{\mathbb P}\left(n^{\max\{1,rp\}+\eta}\right).
			\]
			\item For every \(\eta\in(0,1/p)\),
			\begin{equation}

				\sup_{x\geqslant1}
				\frac{x^{1/p-\eta}}{n}
				\#\{i:W_{n,i}\geqslant x\}
				=O_{\mathbb P}(1).
			\end{equation}
			\item If \(pr>1\), then the ranked \(r\)-mass is uniformly tight at scale
			\(n^{pr}\): for every \(\varepsilon>0\),
			\begin{equation}

				\lim_{L\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}
				\mathbb P\left(
				n^{-pr}\sum_{i>L}W_{n,i}^r>\varepsilon
				\right)=0.
			\end{equation}
		\end{enumeratea}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.567023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf9d1ce35365641e28cc901f12214420ff6b07ac70d2c2d152e7c31df8875038","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 21 (Finite-time KSD propagation of chaos) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target},
