{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.360004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfaecdb167115183bd67366613c6801d15358ff1ec499f5db7c4ab363a6e5ed4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:d+2 of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] For every $d\geq 2$ there exists a constant $c=c(d)$ such that, for every fixed $\varepsilon>0$
