{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.299921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfb6a07f85c6ae395386f5a966c2befa205bff4d44267a4e3ef1d5b387c49410","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:CO of arXiv:2601.09976, 'Stochastic Calculus as Operator Factorization:\\ An Operator--Covariant Derivative and Uni'] Let $X$ be a square-integrable process with natural filtration $(\mathcal{F}_t^X)_{t \in [0,T]}$, energy space~$\mathcal{H}_X$, stochastic integral~$\delta_X$, predictable projection~$\Pi_X$, and operator--covariant derivative $D_X = \delta_X^*$. Assume:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item \textup{Centered integrals:} $\mathbb{E}[\delta_X(u)] = 0$ for all $u \in \mathcal{H}_X$.
\item \textup{Isometry on predictable processes:} $\mathbb{E}[|\delta_X(u)|^2] = \|u\|_{\mathcal{H}_X}^2$ for predictable $u \in \mathcal{H}_X$.
\item \textup{Representation property:} Every $\mathcal{F}_T^X$-measurable $\tilde{F} \in L^2(\Omega)$ with $\mathbb{E}[\tilde{F}] = 0$ can be written as $\tilde{F} = \delta_X(v)$ for some predictable $v \in \mathcal{H}_X$.
\end{enumerate}
Then for all $\mathcal{F}_T^X$-measurable $F \in L^2(\Omega)$:
\begin{equation}
F \;=\; \mathbb{E}[F] + \delta_X(\Pi_X D_X F) \;=\; \mathbb{E}[F] + \int_0^T (\Pi_X D_X F)_t\, dX_t.
\end{equation}
Equivalently, the operator identity $(\mathrm{Id} - \mathbb{E}) = \delta_X \circ \Pi_X \circ D_X$ holds on $L^2(\Omega, \mathcal{F}_T^X, P)$.","status":"unverified"}

