{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.444183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfc5ade76c44ad58826c4f40bc97b2e5638c2abe017d57deb60c431e13ce0dbc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor:Pn_chebyshev of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] For every integer \(n\ge1\),   \(\mathcal P_n\) defined  in (equation def:Pn of the paper) can be expressed in terms of Chebyshev polynomials of first kind as  
