\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.309260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfdf4362f2e9153134a666a95517b5ab66c964dd8d8ea1f51d03eb4aeb5cf280","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:2.6 of arXiv:2412.09850, 'Averaging principles for time-inhomogeneous multi-scale SDEs via nonautonomous Poisson equ'] Suppose that Assumption {\rm(A1 of the paper)} holds. Then, $\{\mu^x_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{R}}$ is an evolution system of measures for the semigroup $\{P^x_{s,t}\}_{t\geqslant s}$, i.e., for any $t\ge s$, $x\in \mathbb{R}^n$ and $\varphi\in C_b(\mathbb{R}^m)$,
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^m}P^x_{s,t} \varphi(y)\,\mu^x_s(dy)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^m}\varphi(y)\,\mu^x_t(dy).
\end{equation}  Moreover, there is a constant $C>0$ such that for any $t\ge s$, $x\in \mathbb{R}^n$, $y\in \mathbb{R}^m$ and Lipschitz continuous function $\phi$ on $\mathbb{R}^m$,
\begin{equation}
 \left|P^x_{s,t} \phi(y)-\int_{\mathbb{R}^m}\phi(z)\,\mu^x_t(dz) \right|\leqslant C {\rm Lip}(\phi)(1+|x|+|y|)e^{-\int^t_s\alpha(u)\,du},
\end{equation}
where ${\rm Lip}(\phi):=\sup_{x\neq y}|\phi(x)-\phi(y)|/|x-y|$.
Furthermore, if $\{\nu^x_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{R}}$ is another evolution system of measures for $\{P^x_{s,t}\}_{t\geqslant s}$ and satisfies that for all $x\in \mathbb{R}^n$,
$$
\sup_{t\in\mathbb{R}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^m}\,|z|\,\nu^x_t(dz)<\infty,
$$
then $\nu^x_t=\mu^x_t$ for all  $t\in\mathbb{R}$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}^n$.","status":"unverified"}

