{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.714418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c01393c3a7c3e8dcc877c6a3caa4a9b102db893c811cdc8e4bd8811b817ae2cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 49 (Two-parameter Banach-valued time lift) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $B$ be a separable Banach space and
$\Delta_T=\{(t,s):0\le s\le t\le T\}$, equipped with the Euclidean metric.
Let $X:\Delta_T\to L^{p_0}(\Omega;B)$ satisfy, for some $p_0\ge2$ and
$\theta>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{u\in\Delta_T}\|X(u)\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega;B)}\le A,
 \qquad
 \|X(u)-X(v)\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega;B)}\le B_0|u-v|^\theta.
\end{equation}
If $p_0\theta>2$, then $X$ has a $B$-valued continuous modification and,
for every $2\le p\le p_0$,
\begin{equation}
 \|X\|_{L^p(\Omega;C(\Delta_T;B))}
 \lesssim_{T,p_0,\theta}A+B_0.
