{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:31.002666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c01e77cd42bf74c9594bc1d8eebbc0fdfc39274a92087e7a30871216eff01afb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 62 (All-degree canonical Gaussian factor and raw-register maximality) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] The series \eqref{all:eq:4.7}--\eqref{all:eq:4.8} converge in $L^2$ and
