{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.280676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c030c962a153949bcb5abeb5f48e618241832e09213ced3cfcf2128cd17d17bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:cond of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] Let $\alpha \in [0,d)$, and let $f$ be an SGF on $\mathbb{R}^d$ or $\mathbb{Z}^d$ satisfying one of the conditions~(item:1 of the paper), (item:2 of the paper), (item:3 of the paper) and (item:4 of the paper) in Theorem~(t: univ pro of the paper). Then:
