{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.696450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0328ed73c92a9156a4214f7950635d35491882ba3458f06ebe0389682882738","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: tree-reduct of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Let $S$ be an undirected, binary branching tree with $\ell+1$ leaves: all non-leaf vertices in $S$ have degree three. Suppose the admissible $\psi$ map the leaves to $v,w_1,\ldots,w_\ell\in \mathbb{Z}^d$, where $|w_i-w_j|\ge \epsilon n$ and $|w_i|\le \epsilon^{-1} n$.

Then
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{val}(S)\le C(\epsilon,k) n^{(4-d)(\ell-1)}\sum_{i=1}^\ell \langle v-w_i\rangle^{-d+2}.
\end{equation}
In particular, if 
\[|v-w_i|\ge \epsilon n, \quad i=1,\ldots,\ell\]
then
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{val}(S)\le Cn^{(4-d)\ell-2}.
\end{equation}
\begin{proof}
    This is a straightforward induction using Proposition (prop: contract of the paper) to contract all internal vertices.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.832071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0331ef38e53803cc98fcbccde43457791a11228a7eb8a11c6f01d6f572b0ca7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tailbound_onepoint of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] As $y \to \infty$, we have
