{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.274826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c039d9bb6c0d0d2415ec04268f1a749ff438f4260907086c2a5848ac1b20ed0d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 (Weak geodesic convexity) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Let $\bX_0 = \bG^{a_0, L_0}, \bX_1 = \bG^{a_1, L_1} \in \cFG$, where $(a_0, L_0), (a_1, L_1) \in \bR^{Nd} \times \mathscr{L}(N, d)$. Given $Q \in \mathscr{Q}(L_0, L_1)$, define $\hat{L}_1 = L_1 Q \in \mathscr{L}(N, d)$. For $u \in [0, 1]$, let $\hat{\bX}_u = \bG^{\hat{a}_u, \hat{L}_u} \in \cFG$, where
\begin{equation} 
\hat{a}_u = (1 - u) a_0 + u a_1 \quad \text{and} \quad \hat{L}_u = L_0 + u (\hat{L}_1 - L_0).
\end{equation}
Then $\AW_2(\bX_0, \hat{\bX}_0) = \AW_2(\bX_1, \hat{\bX}_1) = 0$ and
\begin{equation} 
\AW_2(\hat{\bX}_u, \hat{\bX}_v) = |u - v| \AW_2(\hat{\bX}_0, \hat{\bX}_1), \quad u, v \in [0, 1].
