{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.666193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0546c14c503560f7c44fdd578231776ff57b52a6205c6745b647e0b652e3be5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:entropic_stability of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let (ass:differentiability of the paper) hold and $\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu},\,\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\mu}$  be the unique optimizers in (equation EOT of the paper) for the set of marginals $(\rho,\nu)$ and $(\rho,\mu)$. If there exists $\Lambda>0$ such that 
