{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.994962+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c05b4090eebc686c53fca19e1ed5f034ae9df0117e44b63cf01c1fe6755f8ff6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 33 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] For any fixed integer $N\geq0$ the following factorization holds on any alphabet $(w_1,\dots,w_N)$:
