{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.403878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c074580bf14da1dcd340252fe5f7fe5b1c5b0014ad3ea61fa160fab012bd2a35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convbar of arXiv:2412.06480, 'A SIR epidemic model on a refining spatial grid \\ II-Central limit theorem'] The process $\{\, \left(\overline{u}_\varepsilon(t),\overline{v}_\varepsilon(t), \overline{w}_\varepsilon(t)\right), 0\le t\le T, \; \; 0<\varepsilon<1\, \}\Rightarrow \{\, (\overline{u}(t),\overline{v}(t), \overline{w}(t)), 0\le t\le T\, \}$ in 
	$L^2\big(0,T; (L^2)^3\big)\cap C([0,T];(\mathrm{H}^{-1})^3)$, where the limit $\{\,\left(\overline{u}(t),\overline{v}(t), \overline{w}(t)\right), 0\le t\le T\,\}$ is the unique solution of  the following  system of parabolic PDEs
	\begin{equation}
	\left\{ 
	\begin{aligned} 
	\dfrac{d\overline{u}}{dt}(t) &=  \mu_S\,\Delta \overline{u} (t)-f(t)\overline{u}(t)-g(t)\overline{v}(t)-f(t)u(t)-g(t)v(t)\\
	\dfrac{d\overline{v}}{dt}(t) &=  \mu_I\,\Delta \overline{v}(t)+ f(t)\overline{u}(t)+g(t)\overline{v}(t)+f(t)u(t)+g(t)v(t)-\alpha\left(v(t)+\overline{v}(t\right)
	\\
	\dfrac{d\overline{w}}{dt}(t) &=  \mu_R\,\Delta \overline{w}(t)+ \alpha\left(v(t)+\overline{v}(t)\right)
	\\ 
	\overline{u}(0)&=\overline{v}(0)=\overline{w}(0)=0.
	\end{aligned}
	\right. 
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.027140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c07a16f2d2f4c1947ddab3041122d4e6d7b8b292aec862c543fb5f04c18714a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2608.15616, '\textbf{Compact Support Property of Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift}'] For any $x_0\in\R$, there exists a unique nonnegative solution to \eqref{eq:initial_trace} such that 
