{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.679959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c07b5d828dc4ed4928afb4d0363cae7fa60c30a88f1884a6e999a23d13a1ba35","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 36 (Restarted It\^o signature response topology) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] For $z\in\mathsf Z_{\eta;\mathfrak I,1}(H)$ with cocycle chart $(x,A,q)$,
define its restarted step-two It\^o signature response by
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal J_\tau z=(x,V),\qquad
 V_{s,t}:=A_{s,t}+\frac12\bigl(x_{s,t}^{\otimes2}-q_{s,t}\bigr).
\end{equation}
Let $\mathsf R_\tau^{\rm sig}:=\mathcal J_\tau
(\mathsf Z_{\eta;\mathfrak I,1}(H))$.  On this image set
\begin{align}
 \mathfrak q(x,V)_{s,t}
 &:=x_{s,t}^{\otimes2}-V_{s,t}-V_{s,t}^*,
 \\
 d_\tau^{\rm sig}\bigl((x,V),(\widetilde x,\widetilde V)\bigr)
 &:=|x-\widetilde x|_{\eta;H}
   +|\Anti(V-\widetilde V)|_{2\eta;\mathfrak I}
   +|\mathfrak q(x,V)-\mathfrak q(\widetilde x,\widetilde V)|_{2\eta;\mathcal S_1}.

\end{align}
Stopping is inherited from the restarted two-index response.  We call this
the \emph{split signature topology}: it records precisely the skew second
level and the symmetric It\^o defect, rather than forcing one norm on the
whole second level.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.405097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c07c6e52528478a9f9bef44c8288dcf48fc662bb15c07b3324f830302b862506","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop-rw-end of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $X : [0,\infty) \to \mathcal V\mathcal G\cup \{\infty\}$ be the continuous time random walk on $\mathcal G$ reflected off of $\infty$ as in Theorem~(thm-cont-time-walk of the paper). Almost surely, for each $t\in [0,\infty)$ such that $X_t =\infty$, there is a unique end $\omega_t$ of $\mathcal G$ such that the following is true. 
