{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.061030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c085cddcaf0b338c31e16eaeb3e174b09f2d043a8f0eee026eb8ba93639447da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:4.6-site of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $G = (V, E)$ be a finite subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ containing $0$. For $n \in \mathbb N:=\{0,1,2,\ldots\}$ and $x \in V$ we denote $L_n(x) = \Lambda_n(x) \cap V$ and $\partial L_n(x) = \partial \Lambda_n(x) \cap V$. Let $\mu$ be an increasing measure on $\{0, 1\}^V$. For all $n \in \mathbb N^*$ we have
  \begin{equation}
    \sum\limits_{x \in V} \mathrm{Cov}(\mathbf 1_{0 \leftrightarrow \partial L_n}, \omega(x)) \geqslant \frac n 2 \mu(0 \leftrightarrow \partial L_n)(1 - \mu(0 \leftrightarrow \partial L_n)) \min\limits_{y \in L_n} \frac {\mu(\omega(y) = 1)} {\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n-1} \mu(y \leftrightarrow \partial L_k(y))}.

  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.650404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0883d0ef192627476e0ae6394b6bf2531cf0f1d624337169d849b3bd817e07b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lin-SDE of arXiv:2608.19198, 'Probabilistic Representation and Convergence of Gromov-Wasserstein Gradient Flows'] Let $(A_t)_{t \in [0,\infty)}$ be the solution of the matrix ODE (equation eq:IVP of the paper). The IGW gradient flow $(\rho_t)_{t \in [0,\infty)}$ agrees with the unique time-marginal flow of the linear SDE
\begin{equation}
    dX_t = -\frac14\big(A_t^{-1}+A_t^{-2}\big)X_t\,dt + A_t^{-1/2}\,dW_t, \quad
    X_0\sim \rho_0,
\end{equation}
where $(W_t)_{t \in [0,\infty)}$ is a standard Brownian motion in $\mathbb{R}^d$ independent of $X_0$. That is, $\rho_t=\mathrm{Law}(X_t)$ for all $t \in [0,\infty)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

