{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.980955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c08e5d39fa44f310839497b851778220b71bad0458cd5533931ac3505d287cfa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:truncated_expectation_diff_ineq_at_doubling_scales of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] If $\alpha<d$ then there exists a positive constant $C$ such that
