for every $0<\beta\leq \beta_c$ and $r,m\geq 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.544851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c08f57393178f825ab8291c2012a3ac121a091c20ed465178721cd67db369f48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Minimizer of upper bounded expectation of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Let $h: \mathbb{R} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ be a function defined as
\begin{equation*}
    h(t):=e^{-t\delta_0|\gamma|}(f(\beta)e^{t}+1)^{1+d|\gamma|}
\end{equation*}
for all $t\in \mathbb{R}$. If $\beta$ is small enough, $h$ possesses a unique minimizer 
