{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.822080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0a353eae3e0d5ba81adba1c00b5763457176cbb402fed203bc400119f109e06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: metatheorem remainder2 of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Assume that $\Upsilon_\tau$ is globally Lipschitz continuous for all $\tau\in{\mathcal T}^{\leq N}$. 
	Then for all $\tau_0\in{\mathcal T}^{\le N}$ there exists a function $H_{z_1z_2}(\cdot;\tau_0):{\mathcal F}^{\le N-|\tau_0|} \to\mathbb{R}^n\otimes(\mathbb{R}^n)^\ast$ such that
