{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.721167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0a825471865a259d633f85d121f7c27ede7393adc7ea2222537d6dd1a0fc119","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.01190, 'Rough differential equations on manifolds via natural bundles'] Let $m,n\in\Nsf$, $p\in [1,3)$, $x\in C^{p-\mathrm{var}}([S,T],\Rsf^n)$, and let $f_\alpha^i:\Rsf^m\to\Rsf$ (for $i\in\llbracket 1, m \rrbracket$ and $\alpha\in\llbracket 1,n \rrbracket$) be smooth functions. Let also $Y_S\in\Rsf^m$. Consider the system of controlled differential equations
	\begin{equation}

		\d{Y}^i  = f_{\alpha}^i(Y)\d{x}^\alpha, 
			\quad 
		Y^i(S) = Y_S^i,
	\end{equation}
for $i\in \llbracket 1, m \rrbracket$. Given a rough path lift $(X^\tau)$ of function $x$ (see \autoref{ex:natural-lift}), we say that a function $Y: [S,T]\to\Rsf^m$ is a \emph{Davie solution} to problem~\eqref{eq:ode} if $Y(S) = Y_S$ and if there exists a constant $C\in (0,\infty)$ such that the inequality
	\begin{equation}

		\left|
			Y^i(t) - Y^i(s) 
			- f_\alpha^i(Y(s)) X^{\ta}(s,t) 
			- \left(
				\frac{\partial f_\beta^i}{\partial y^j}f_\alpha^j
			  \right)
			(Y(s)) X^{\tc} (s,t)
		\right| 
		\leq C\omega(s,t)^\frac{3}{p}
	\end{equation}
holds for every $i\in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket$ and $(s,t)\in \Delta [S,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.939297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0a874c8f87a13f8506182f7ca7d06c5356418d5c7a253a1c23c7a0a3998c15f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.4 of arXiv:2412.05709, 'Incipient infinite clusters and volume growth for Gaussian free fields and loop soups on m'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exists $C>0$ such that for any $u\ge C$, $n\ge 1$, $m\ge un^{1\boxdot \frac{d-4}{2}}$, $h\in [0,m^{-d^{5}}]$, and any $\diamond\in \{\mathbf{N},\mathbf{x},\mathbf{T}\}$ with $\diamond \ge m^{d^5}$, 
		\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P}\big(\mathsf{H}_h^{\diamond}[n,m] \big):=	\mathbb{P}\big(\mathsf{H}_h^{\diamond} , \widetilde{ \mathcal{L}}_{1/2}[n,m]\neq \emptyset  \big)\lesssim u^{-1}\mathbb{P}\big(\mathsf{H}_h^{\diamond}  \big). 
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.356262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0a8934611a4afbb7186b50ea71bba50827d7272d7dd85e76948d69ad461c21a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:um of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Suppose $\mathbb{E}[(X(t)-X(s))^2]^{1/2} \asymp \varphi(|t-s|)$ for all $t,s \in I$, where $\varphi$ is non-decreasing, continuous and regularly varying at 0 of index $\theta \in [0\,,1]$ with

    \begin{align}
        \int_0^h \frac{\varphi(r) \, {\rm d} r}{r \sqrt{\log(1/r)}} \lesssim \varphi(h) \sqrt{\log(1/h)} = o(1) \quad \text{as $h \to 0^+$.}
    \end{align}
    If there exist $C_0>0$, $\rho >0$, $a_0>0$, and $h_0 \in (0\,,1]$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \Var(X(t)-X(s)|X(t')-X(s')) \ge C_0 \Var(X(t)-X(s))
    \end{align}
    uniformly for all $h \in (0\,,h_0]$ and for all $t,s,t',s' \in I$ with $|t-s| \le h$, $|t'-s'| \le h$ and $|s-s'| \ge a_0 h^\rho$, then
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{h\to0^+}\sup_{t,s \in I: 0<|t-s| \le h} \frac{|X(t)-X(s)|}{\varphi(|t-s|) \sqrt{\log(1/|t-s|)}} = K_1 \quad \text{a.s.}
    \end{align}
    where $0<K_1<\infty$ is a constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.326976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0accd63f4f7783a324957bc79f52975aae65ebea3f17d99527fd1e81856f7b7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:intersection-Brownian-multigraph of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] Let $g\in\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$, $m\geq1$, and
$\boldsymbol x\in\mathbb R_{>0}^m$.  For the unstable pairs $(0,1)$ and
$(0,2)$, interpret $F_{g,m}$ by
(equation eq:unstable-intersection-conventions of the paper).  Then
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  F_{g,m}(\boldsymbol x)
  =
  \frac{(\pi/2)^{m/2}}
  {(g+m-1)!\sqrt{x_1\cdots x_m}}
  \sum_{\boldsymbol\ell\in
  \mathfrak A_{m,g+m-1}^{\mathrm{conn}}}
  \mathfrak I_{\boldsymbol\ell}(\boldsymbol x).
  }

\end{equation}

Equivalently, let $M=(m_{pq})_{1\leq p\leq q\leq m}$ range over connected
multigraphs on the labeled vertex set $[m]$, with loops allowed and with
unlabeled edge copies, where $m_{pq}$ is the multiplicity of the edge
$\{p,q\}$. Suppose that $b_1(M)=g$.  Define $\mathfrak I_M$ to be
$\mathfrak I_{\boldsymbol\ell}$ for any labeling of the edge copies with
these multiplicities.  Permutation symmetry of the jump-pair variables
makes this independent of the chosen labeling.  Then
\begin{equation}
  F_{g,m}(\boldsymbol x)
  =
  \frac{(\pi/2)^{m/2}}{\sqrt{x_1\cdots x_m}}
  \sum_{\substack{M\text{ connected on }[m]\\ b_1(M)=g}}
  \frac{\mathfrak I_M(\boldsymbol x)}
  {\prod_{p\leq q}m_{pq}!}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.788762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0af0214246389106ab71a5223b0e0234cfa0ff5940c290441324612c9ddb7a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] We have
