and $P_\tau h \rightarrow h$ in $L^2(\mathbf{N} \times \WW)$ as $\tau \rightarrow 1$. Moreover, for $w,z \in \WW$ and all $p \geq 1$,
\begin{align*}
    \E |P_\tau h(\eta,w)|^p \leq \E |h(\eta,w)|^p\\
    \intertext{and}
    \E |D_zP_\tau h(\eta,w)|^p \leq \E |D_zh(\eta,w)|^p.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.354303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0af78c32eb36fc10b16414fed91a4390de781472e7799aa97aa5d80d9b5f199","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For all graphs $G=(V,(c_{xy})_{x,y\in V})$,  and site weights $\alpha=(\alpha_x)_{x\in V}$, $\omega=(\omega_x)_{x\in V}$ with $\omega\neq 0$, we have
