{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:39:18.537756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0cab04d7ff07275c5c8e780c693809b2670493bffe4b9fa252dcfa2d1189161","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 of arXiv:2609.02327, 'On the counting function of square-full numbers'] We assume the strong Riemann hypothesis. For any $x\geqslant x_0$, where $x_0$ is sufficiently large, there are effective complex constant $c_{\{\gamma /6 \}}$ such that the asymptotic formula
