{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.639467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0d8fcf17eddc7b09cc30ec6f79f902468f3fba7d18e80a5ff4a7c2632430281","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Theorem:DualOperator-L* of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume $L$ is a jump-diffusion operator given by (equation ReferenceGenerator of the paper) with coefficients satisfying the Assumptions \textup{(Assumptions-(C) of the paper)}. Then, the $L^2([0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n)$-adjoint operator $L^*: C^{\infty}_0 \to C^{\infty}_b$ is well defined, and for every $f\in C_c^\infty([0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n)$ and $(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
     L^*f(t,x)&:= -\nabla \cdot (bf) (t,x)+\frac{1}{2} \sum_{i,j}\frac{\partial^2[(\sigma\sigma^T)_{ij}f]}{\partial x_i \partial x_j}(t,x) \\
    &\;+\int_{\mathbb{R}^\ell} \left[\det \nabla\phi_{t,z}^{-1}(x)f(t,\phi_{t,z}^{-1}(x))-f(t,x) +\mathbbm{1}_{|z|\leq 1}\nabla\cdot (\gamma f)(t,x,z) \right]\nu(dz),
