\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.298101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0e6004cd16332b6927bb235e8d7695ef92f3648f937f80ad321e99e836c327a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:relative-entropy:bound of arXiv:2605.16904, 'Positive-rate PCA and IPS with stationary Bernoulli measures are rapidly forgetful \footno'] Let $\lambda=\lambda_q$  be a Bernoulli measure with strictly positive marginal $q\colon\Sigma\to(0,1)$.
