{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.236462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0ff51908cded17b922ba3bb27d397fd09460a9ca46d86a229a4b0d2706b3e84","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 78 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Affine flow $\Psi(Cone\ A, M)$]
Given $M \subset H_0$ and $Cone\ A \in CONE(H_0)$. $\Psi(Cone\ A\, M)$ is the regular flow on $M$ defined by
\begin{equation*}
\Psi(Cone\ A, M) := \Psi_{Cone\ A}|_{M} \quad  \in FLOW(M)
\end{equation*}
(Corollary \ref{cor_flow_on_M}). $\Psi(Cone\ A, M)$ is called an \textit{affine} flow on $M$. $Cone\ A$ is called the \textit{tangent cone associated with the flow}.","status":"unverified"}

