    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.675192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c14e0073563315fef14f5af24180a48d026020b379301c4b09fc5ff259ef9994","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2609.00245, 'Higher-order Gaussian bounds for maximally subelliptic boundary value problems'] For every \(\alpha\), there exists \(C_\alpha\geq 1\) such that, for every \((\xi,\delta)\in \CompactZero\times (0,\delta_0]\) and every \(\left( -\opL, \xi, \delta \right)\)-heat function \(u:(-1/2,1/2)\rightarrow \DomainLinfty\), the following statements hold.
