{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.558110+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1636e717d488f78ff058f4d182d02f73ef043f4133ccee6d221aec3c9647df1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defs 19 (Conditional absolute continuity) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] Let $\QP$ be a Borel probability on~$\U=\U(\R^n)$ and $\mssm_r$ be the Lebesgue measure restricted on $B_r=B_r(0)=\{x \in \R^n: |x|<r\}$.
