    |f(t,x,z_1)-f(t,x,z_2)|+\sum_{j=1}^{d} |q_j(t,x,z_1)-q_j(t,x,z_2)| \le C |z_1-z_2|,
  \end{equation*}
  and assume that the remaining conditions in Theorem \ref{th:purejump} hold, then there exists a unique global solution to \eqref{e:de-solution2} with the following property
