{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.749164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c174c6212e167cfec926d64cb24eed25f070e6c060a3b4c0a99bc147b6646110","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma local12 of arXiv:2507.20324, 'Non-existence of several random fractals in Brownian motion and Brownian loop soup'] For $d=2,3$, let $W_{i}$, $i=1,2,3$, be independent Brownian excursions from $\mathcal{C}_{0}$ to $\mathcal{C}_{n}$. Let $E_{1}$ denote the event that $W_{1}\cap(W_{2}\cup W_{3})=\varnothing$. Let $E_{i,j}$ be the event that $W_{i}$ returns to $\mathcal{C}_{jL}$ after hitting $\mathcal{C}_{(j+1)L}$. Then there exists $c$, such that for any integer $j\leq[n/L]-1$, and $i=1,2,3$,
