{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.356022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1fbc5e019ad0e7aa2ec786f329ac7c454f3f5301ea8f72be2cb5c892b30c3f3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] Assume that  $\alpha < d \le 2\alpha$ and $\mu \in \mathcal{K}_{\infty}$. 
