{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.202505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2183aa4692672927f891a1ec2154acd2976c573f91b0fbd9c965539a5da12ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 (Boundary identification) of arXiv:2608.03575, '2608.03575'] Assume the unimodular ADT $(G,\rho,\Theta)$ is simple, one-ended, tame, and RCP-hyperbolic, and that (Z1), (Z3), (Z4), and (Z2') hold. Assume further that $\mathbb{E}[\deg_{G}(\rho)^{3}]<\infty$. Let $(X_{n})_{n\ge0}$ be the simple random walk on $G$ started from $\rho$, then almost surely:
