{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.705396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c265aaf0dfb40e610c860868c7165c15ad3d2b5231394c0b2f7233e4b5852ae0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP:gglimit of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Let $g$ be a real-valued, smooth, compactly supported function with $\textup{dist}(\supp g, x_0)>0$, where $x_0\in \mathbb{T}_L$. Then, we have
\begin{align}
&\frac{ \mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0}}  \Big[  e^{i\langle \Re h^\perp, g_L \rangle+it^{+}\langle \gamma_L,g \rangle  }  e^{\bar {\mathcal{E}}(h^\perp, t^{+}) } e^{c_0(t^+)^2+b(h^\perp)t^+}  , \,D_L, \, B_K  \Big]}{ \mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0}}  \Big[ e^{\bar {\mathcal{E}}(h^\perp, t^{+}) } e^{c_0(t^+)^2+b(h^\perp)t^+}  , \,D_L, \, B_K  \Big] }=e^{-\frac{1}{2}\|g\|^2_{L^2}}(1+o_L(1)) \\
&\frac{ \mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0}}  \Big[  e^{i\langle \Im h^\perp, g_L \rangle }  e^{\bar {\mathcal{E}}(h^\perp, t^{+}) } e^{c_0(t^+)^2+b(h^\perp)t^+}    , \,D_L, \, B_K  \Big]}{ \mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0}}  \Big[ e^{\bar {\mathcal{E}}(h^\perp, t^{+}) } e^{c_0(t^+)^2+b(h^\perp)t^+}, \,D_L, \, B_K  \Big] }=e^{-\frac{1}{2}\|g\|^2_{L^2}}(1+o_L(1)),
\end{align}

\noindent
as $L\to \infty $, uniformly in $x_0 \in \mathbb{T}_{L}$ and $\theta \in [0,2\pi]$, where $g_L(x)=L^{-1/2}g(L^{-1}x)$ and $t^{+}$ is given in (equation eqn: t-oot of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.556205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c26697d615a858d50e965bc541e4b29e8c35c4c8856ac0dc4c2ced8609e9b291","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 43 (Type II blow-up limits split along $\mathcal{V}' \oplus \mathcal{H}'$) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Suppose the singularity at $T$ is of Type II. 

	{(i) The limit splits along} $\mathcal{V}' \oplus \mathcal{H}'$\emph{.} The distributions subconverge to complementary orthogonal distributions $\mathcal{V}'_\infty$ (rank $2 m + 2$) and $\mathcal{H}'_\infty$ (rank $2 n'$, where $n' := \sum_{k \geq 2} n_k$) whose O'Neill tensors vanish: both are parallel, and by the de Rham decomposition theorem the universal cover splits isometrically and holomorphically, for each $t$,

	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{M}_\infty \;=\; \Phi \times Y \,, \qquad \widetilde{g}_\infty (t) \;=\; g^\Phi (t) \,\oplus\, g^Y (t) \,, \qquad \dim_{\mathbb{R}} \Phi \;=\; 2 m + 2 \,,
	\end{equation}

	with each factor a complete eternal Kähler--Ricci flow.\\

	{(ii) The} $\mathcal{H}'$\emph{-factor is flat.} $( Y, g^Y (t) )$ is flat and static, hence $Y = \mathbb{C}^{n'}$, being simply connected; all curvature is carried by the fiber factor, $| \mathrm{Rm}_{g^\Phi} | \leq 1$ with equality at $( x_\infty, 0 )$, so $\Phi$ is nonflat.\\

	{(iv) The fiber factor is a limit of Calabi fibers.} Under \eqref{eq:typeII-splitting}, $\Phi$ is the leaf of $\mathcal{V}'_\infty$ through $x_\infty$: the pointed limit of the rescaled totally geodesic fibers $\big( ( \widehat{\pi}' )^{-1} \big( \widehat{\pi}' ( x_j ) \big), \, g_j (t) \big)$ --- each a Calabi-symmetric Kähler metric on $\mathbb{CP}^{m+1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.762465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2688f27f614f42d492fecb5df4899b5039f6450fab97d9a78bd8f975b01301e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:lbm-response-transversality of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The measures $\eta_{n_1}^x,\ldots,\eta_{n_N}^x$ are linearly independent.
