{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.402072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c26d95878167ccf6866faed70cd1a6aa71d7c74126a65a62b4819c8b069a8e6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2605.15386, 'The non-central gamma sum and difference distributions: exact distribution and asymptotic '] 1. Suppose that $\lambda_1=0$ and $\alpha_1=n$ is a positive integer. Then, for $x>0$, 
\begin{align}
f_{X_1-X_2}(x)=\frac{\beta_1^{-n}\beta_2^{-\alpha_2}}{(n-1)!}\bigg(\frac{1}{\beta_1}+\frac{1}{\beta_2}\bigg)^{-\alpha_2}x^{n-1}\exp\bigg(-\frac{x}{\beta_1}-\frac{\lambda_2\beta_2}{\beta_1+\beta_2}\bigg)\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{u_k(n,\alpha_2,\beta_1,\beta_2,\lambda_2)}{x^k},    
\end{align}  
where $u_0(n,\alpha_2,\beta_1,\beta_2,\lambda_2)=1$ and, for $1\leq k\leq n-1$,
\begin{align*}
u_k(n,\alpha_2,\beta_1,\beta_2,\lambda_2)&=(-1)^k(1-n)_k\bigg(\frac{1}{\beta_1}+\frac{1}{\beta_2}\bigg)^{-k}L_k^{(\alpha_2-1)}\bigg(-\frac{\lambda_2\beta_1}{\beta_1+\beta_2}\bigg).
\end{align*}
2. Suppose that $\lambda_2=0$ and $\alpha_2=n$ is a positive integer. Then, for $x<0$, 
\begin{align}
f_{X_1-X_2}(x)=\frac{\beta_1^{-\alpha_1}\beta_2^{-n}}{(n-1)!}\bigg(\frac{1}{\beta_1}+\frac{1}{\beta_2}\bigg)^{-\alpha_1}|x|^{n-1}\exp\bigg(\frac{x}{\beta_2}-\frac{\lambda_1\beta_1}{\beta_1+\beta_2}\bigg)\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{u_k(n,\alpha_1,\beta_2,\beta_1,\lambda_1)}{|x|^k}.    
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.715013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c26df2d164a44ece95ab57e4a0b7b51cd024a08d433a4d12b20dc5adbed98535","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollary_repl_lemma_ave of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] For any function $H \in C^{1,2}( {\Omega_T})$and for every $\delta > 0$, it holds that
