{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.999808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c282fa46c6872f00163b79b05748e94b1b314fdb365ccccd8422c396a29a90b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $t=-1$ and $F\in\mathcal{HP}_{T,-1}$ extendable. Let $M_+$ and $M_-$ as above. Then,  for $\alpha\in\mathbb C\setminus i\mathbb R$,
