{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.333876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2a7867ab06e7d001ba3bc08805bec817f88996955d52f927241285ef5d9c48a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Let $G(t)=G+te_1e_1^*$ where $t>1$ and $G$ is a complex Ginibre matrix with entries of variance $1/N$. Let $\lambda_1$ be the outlier eigenvalue of $G(t)$. Then 
