{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.965623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2a7b9e5b22b17f72ef8e2576f4d6abf061f26824b4d77d1fdc980c127e7d62a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:L_b of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] Assume that $b$ satisfies (equation eq:global_appx of the paper). Then, for $s < t$ and $x,y \in \mathbb{R}$,
