{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.674422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2ce47cd41a929511fca140e8e7bb119fdd9ad46b3a98ea2e9c16efe39d6f4ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 20 of arXiv:2607.11076, 'Smoluchowski-Kramers Approximation for Stochastic Differential Equations driven by Fractio'] Suppose that assumptions \textbf{(A1)}--\textbf{(A4)} hold and \(\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \frac{\mu(\varepsilon)}{{\varepsilon}^H} = 0\). Then \(\{\eta^{\varepsilon}(t)\}_{\varepsilon > 0}\) satisfies a large deviation principle on \(C([0,T];\mathbb{R}^d)\) with speed \(\lambda^{-2}(\varepsilon)\) and rate function \(\tilde{I}\) given by:

