    holds for every increasing convex function $\Phi: \mathbb{R}^{+} \xrightarrow{} \mathbb{R}^{+}$ such that $\Phi(0) = 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.347766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2e2180e55d1bf12178a1fc618da18d74f4f98fbda8a54f70dc6374da5227ddc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:escape of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $A$ be an $s \times M$ matrix with independent $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$ entries and let $T$ be a nonempty compact subset of the unit sphere of $\mathbb{R}^M$.  Then for every $t > 0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left\{
\inf_{x \in T} \|A x\|_2 \;\le\; \mathbb{E}\|g_s\|_2 - w(T) - t
\right\}
\le e^{-t^2/2} ,
\qquad g_s \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I_s).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.521535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2e33b1fbe3e41c262152bd348fc880ecf484333c823292379a912ad14e6878f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:PTASEP-H4 of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The dressed observable satisfies the mixed diamond
equation
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\bigl(q\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}+\mathbf{1}}^{-1}
+ p\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{2},
\mathbf{n}}^{-1}\bigr)
\mathcal{M}_{t+2, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}+\mathbf{1}} \\
&\qquad - \mathcal{M}_{t, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}}^{-1}
\bigl(q\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
