{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.992890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2fa9f357c676a7d22cdf0a09abab0f5f0e351e34f9ad5e2e3f032bce46c9a66","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:square-constrained-bonds of arXiv:2608.23545, 'Eulerian walkers on $\Z^2$ have range exponent $2/3$'] There are constants $c,C>0$ such that the following holds for every $x\in\mathbb Z^2$
