where the density profile $f$ satisfies the comparison conditions in Definition~(ass:ft of the paper) with respect to the $\alpha$-stable density $f_{\alpha}$. 
Under the same assumptions on the Markov chains $([N], P_N)$ and $([N], \widetilde{P}_N)$ as in Theorem~(prop:super_4 of the paper), the scaling limits of the correlation measures established in Theorem~(thm:convergence_proof of the paper) ($\alpha$-stable case) also hold for the matrix $X$. In particular, a new tricritical point process emerges at the critical bandwidth and critical external source, as described in Theorem~(thm:triple_critical_convergence of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.514347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c30d818bb80944aa53f925d0b8333ca086da8a3eb86fb4eea01f203a4c626797","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Schur's lemma) of arXiv:2608.30602, '2608.30602'] If $T$ has an admissible kernel, then it is bounded on 
