{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.282715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c32eaee8785afe92be920565d66804921b5e160a16e62ac306c98add122a7037","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 (Sign-barrier) of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] There exists a constant $\eps = \varepsilon_{1}>0$, and constants $C>0$, $T_{0}>0$ sufficiently large, only depending on $\Mcc$, with the following property. Let $T>T_{0}$, $\eta\in [1,T]$, $r>0$ satisfy either (a) $\frac{C}{T}<r<\frac{1}{C} \cdot \frac{1}{T^{\frac{d}{d+1}}}$ and $\eta> C(rT)^{d-1}$, or (b) $\Mcc=\Sc^{d}$, and $\frac{C}{T}<r < \frac{1}{C\sqrt{T}}$. Then, for every $x\in\Mcc$, there exists an element $h=h_{x,r}\in\Hc$ of the RKHS of norm
\begin{equation}

