{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.288811+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c34ff24d08e07ec86b2c1870fff8f08369a04f2aa45623e0f1dce7fd3834e96d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop of arXiv:2411.04802, 'Dynkin ghost games with asymmetry and consolation'] If $\gamma_2$ is a $\Gamma^2-$randomised stopping time and $\tau$ is a stopping time, then
\begin{equation}
    J_1(x;\tau,\gamma_2)= \mathbb E_x\left[e^{-r\tau}(1-p_1\Gamma^2_{\tau})g_1(X_\tau)+p_1\int_{[0,\tau]} e^{-rt}V^{h_1}(X_t)\,d\Gamma^2_t\right].
    \end{equation}
Similarly, if $\gamma_1$ is a $\Gamma^1-$randomised stopping time, then 
\begin{equation}
    J_2(x;\gamma_1,\tau)=\mathbb E_x\left[e^{-r\tau}(1-p_2\Gamma^1_{\tau-})g_2(X_\tau)+p_2\int_{[0,\tau)} e^{-rt}V^{h_2}(X_t)\,d\Gamma^1_t\right].
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.899040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c357b1af9df929d3c59b68e6827775aa154f9665953885bf6ebfef4b5310cc07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm MeasureTheorem of arXiv:2607.19037, 'Semiclassical analysis for Yang--Mills \\ random connections on compact surfaces'] For $\alpha<\frac{1}{2}$, $p\geqslant 1$, $s<0$, and $\ell$ small enough, there exists a $\mathcal{B}_{\mathsf{YM}}^{\alpha,p,s,\ell}$-valued random variable $A^\mathsf{Free}_{\mathcal{S},\sigma}$ such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item The solution $(U_\varepsilon(1))_{\varepsilon>0}$ at time $1$  of the $\epsilon$-mollification of the SDE defining the holonomy along level curves:
        \[\mathrm{d} U_\varepsilon=U_\varepsilon \mathrm{d} W_\varepsilon, U_\varepsilon(0)=1_G, \,\ W_\varepsilon(t):= \int_{\mathbb{R}} \chi_\varepsilon(t-r)\left(\int_0^r
        \gamma^*A^\mathsf{Free}_{\mathcal{S},\sigma} \right) \mathrm{d} r \]
        converges a.s., when $\varepsilon\rightarrow 0^+$, to a random variable $\mathsf{Hol}_{\gamma}\big (A^\mathsf{Free}_{\mathcal{S},\sigma}\big )$  measurable w.r.t. $A^\mathsf{Free}_{\mathcal{S},\sigma}$.
        \item The family of random variables $\big(\mathsf{Hol}_{\{f=r\}}(A^\mathsf{Free}_{\mathcal{S},\sigma})\big)_{a_{2g}\leqslant r\leqslant \max f}$ is a Markov process.
        \item The law of $\mathsf{Hol}_{\{f=r\}}$ is given by 
        \begin{equation*}
\mathbb{P}\big[\mathsf{Hol}_{\{f=r\}}\big(A^{\mathsf{Free}}_{S,\sigma}\big)\in \mathrm{d} g \big]= \sum_{\rho\in \widehat{G}}  \exp\Big(-\sigma\big(\Sigma_{\leqslant r}\big) c_2(\rho)\Big)  \dim(V_\rho)^{1-2g} \chi_\rho(g) \,\mathrm{d} g=:Z_{\Sigma_{\leqslant r}, \sigma},
\end{equation*}
where $Z_{\Sigma,\sigma}$ is the Yang--Mills partition function of the surface $\Sigma$ equipped with area form $\sigma$.
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.217565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c35b051b666fd57847228a01154847c59351c7ade1fa3e841418394dcc1c684a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:martprelim of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Suppose Assumption (assump:initdiff of the paper) holds.
For all $\varepsilon > 0$, $t \in [0,\infty)$, and $ \varphi \in \mathcal{D}(\mathbb{R})$, the following equalities hold:
\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
\mathcal{M}_t^\varepsilon(\varphi) & := \langle \tilde{\mathcal{E}}_t^{\theta,\varepsilon}, \varphi \rangle - \langle \tilde{\mathcal{E}}_0^{\theta,\varepsilon}, \varphi \rangle - \frac{1}{2} \int_0^t \langle \tilde{\mathcal{E}}_s^{\theta,\varepsilon},\varphi'' \rangle ds \\
& = -(1-e^{-\sigma\varepsilon^{1/4}})\sum_{i \in \mathbb{Z}} \int_0^t \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon(s,Y_i^\varepsilon(s))(p_{\varepsilon^{1/2\theta}} * \varphi)(Y_i^\varepsilon(s))dB_i^\varepsilon(s),
\end{split}
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
& \mathcal{W}_t^\varepsilon(\varphi) := \mathcal{M}_t^\varepsilon(\varphi)^2 - (1-e^{-\sigma\varepsilon^{1/4}})^2\int_0^t \left( \sum_{i \in \mathbb{Z}} \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon(s,Y_i^\varepsilon(s))^2(p_{\varepsilon^{1/2\theta}} * \varphi)(Y_i^\varepsilon(s))^2  \right) ds \\
& = 2(1-e^{-\sigma\varepsilon^{1/4}})^2\sum_{i \in \mathbb{Z}} \int_0^t \Bigg( \sum_{j \in \mathbb{Z}} \int_0^s \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon(u,Y_i^\varepsilon(u)) \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon(s,\tilde{X}_j^\varepsilon(s)) \\
& \hspace{2in}(p_{\varepsilon^{1/2\theta}} * \varphi)(Y_i^\varepsilon(u))(p_{\varepsilon^{1/2\theta}} * \varphi)(Y_j^\varepsilon(s)) dB_j^\varepsilon(u) \Bigg) dB_i^\varepsilon(s).
\end{split}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.051292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c35de0814ee8e1e3e093999dd0a48d4729c900b3bfbeedc1695d7bce3e77d1e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $\tau\in[0,T]$, $\beta\in\mathbb R$, and $\gamma\in(0,1]$. Then there exists a linear map
\[
\mathcal I_\tau^{\mathrm d}: \mathcal A^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^2;B_\beta) \to C([0,\tau];B_\beta),
\]
obtained from a dyadic recursion on $\mathcal D^\tau$ and continuous extension to $[0,\tau]$, such that, for every $A\in \mathcal A^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^2;B_\beta)$, $\mathcal I_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)_0=0$. If we define the dyadic remainder $\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A):=A-\delta\mathcal I_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)$, then
$
\delta \mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)=\delta A.
$
Moreover, if $\gamma\in(0,1)$, then
\begin{equation}

\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)\in C^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^2;B_\beta)\ \text{\, and \, }\ \|\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)\|_{\gamma,\beta;\tau}\le C_\gamma\|\delta A\|_{\gamma,\beta;\tau};
\end{equation}
if $\gamma=1$, then
\begin{equation}

\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)\in C_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_\tau^2;B_\beta)\ \text{\, and \, }\ \|\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)\|_{1,\log;\tau,\beta}\le C_{T}\|\delta A\|_{1,\beta;\tau}.
\end{equation}
while, for every $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$, $\|\mathcal R_\tau^{\mathrm d}(A)\|_{1-\varepsilon,\beta;\tau}\le C_{\varepsilon,T}\|\delta A\|_{1,\beta;\tau}$. Here the constants can be chosen independently of $\tau\in[0,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.789022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c360b000461ce55f8ed95236a2e68ef62ed70010dfe51c3ecbf6e3a6bd97c259","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem E.g., Lemma 2.8 of~\cite{MaTo} of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Starting from a domain $\Lambda$ with boundary conditions $\tau$, if we change the boundary conditions on a subset $\Delta \subset \partial \Lambda$ of size $|\Delta|$ to get boundary conditions $\tau^{\Delta}$, then 
    \begin{align*}
        t_{\textsc{mix}}(\Lambda, \tau) \le  4\beta |E(\Lambda)|\log 2\cdot e^{4\beta |\Delta|}\cdot  t_{\textsc{mix}}(\Lambda, \tau^\Delta)
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.028144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3627c5969fab13e5ae50e16a8cf05d803d797d07e63a0604bd4937c7b9cefe1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2-l03 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Recall the definition of $M^{p,\ell}_{k,x}$ introduced in
(equation 2-06b of the paper). There exists a finite constant ${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$,
uniformly bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{equation*}
\begin{gathered}
\sum_{k=1}^d \sum_{x\in{\mathbb T}_N^d}  M^{p, \ell}_{k,x} (\eta)^2
\;\le\; {\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N) \, s_d(\ell)\, \frac{K}{N^2}\, 
\sum_{x\in{\mathbb T}_N^d}  H^{(\ell)}_{1,x} (\eta)^2 \;, 
\\
\frac{\sqrt{K}}{N}\,
