        \chi(\pi_{t,1},\nu_1) \leq e^{- (\sqrt{\mu}-\sqrt{\lambda})^2 t} \chi(\pi_{0,1},\nu_1) \, \forall t \geq 0.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.482911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c394ab1627dc96d2a1f22d70acbe0db7dbb2e5d93f1fa05986ad5f5c45a1f729","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Association bound) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] For the continuous symmetric innovations considered here, $x \geq 0$, and $n \geq 1$,
