{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.205048+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3c9c4ae36e01acec8e028ef52f72a3911d1e25c2956fa3c377392b623da133d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 2 of arXiv:2604.27205, 'An Analysis of the Diaconis-Holmes-Neal Markov Chain Sampler Under Generalized Unimodal Un'] Suppose $P(s)$ and $Q(s)$ are probabilities on a finite space $S$. The \underline{variation} \underline{distance} between $P$ and $Q$ is given by
