{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.892737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3ea133e41872250620320f29cf3c7ed6fad1c3d67a883428303c924ca16c501","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$\cT_N$ and  $\cO_N$ denote the perfect t-embedding and its associated origami map of the Aztec diamond of size~$\ell N$ with $(1\times\ell)$-periodic weights described above. Let~$(\xi,\eta)$ be a point in the liquid region~$\mathcal F_R$ of the Aztec diamond. Then
