{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.689412+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c41b1fa3e9be538c872d0090a51a9751d88031f648bfaafe45ee642ab62eb5a8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2607.29534, 'Expected signatures via partial integration, coordinate change and symmetrization'] Let $p\geq 1$ and let $(E,d)$ be a metric space. For a path
$X:[s,t]\to E$, $0\leq s<t$, its $p$-variation over $[s,t]$ is defined by
\begin{equation}
    \Vert X \Vert_{p\text{-var};[s,t]}
    :=
        \sup_{\mathcal{P} \in \mathcal D([s,t])}
        \left(\sum_{[u,v] \in \mathcal{P}}
        d(X_{u},X_{v})^p
    \right)^{1/p},
\end{equation}
where the supremum is taken over all finite partitions
$\mathcal D([s,t])=\{s=t_0<t_1<\cdots<t_n=t\}$ of $[s,t]$.
We denote by $C^{p\text{-var}}([s,t],E)$ the space of all continuous paths
$X:[s,t]\to E$ such that
$\Vert X\Vert_{p\text{-var};[s,t]}<\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.822900+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c41bffeae24f19a4c82e4e61d0879b08d36b6cfdb913f7e9b8c943293471abe8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Lem: delta Z of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Let $Z$ satisfy (equation eq: sol Davie branched of the paper) and $Z^{[N+1]}$ be as in (equation Eq: Z remainders of the paper). Then
