{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.685689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4223e7247d8d0291a4dd6f0b55b1c93d91e79f55a9fb3dfb7dfa5aecc123899","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm t:1.1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let $\widecheck{{\mathbf t}}_N$ be defined via the relation:
\begin{equation}

\sqrt{\widecheck{{\mathbf t}}_N} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}} \log N - \frac{1}{4 \sqrt{\pi}} \log \log N \,.
\end{equation}
Then, there exist random variables $\widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_{\rm D}$ and $\widecheck{{\mathbf X}}_{\rm D}$, defined on the same probability space and take values in $\mathbb{R}$ and ${\rm D}$ respectively, such that
\begin{equation}

\Big(\frac{\widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_N/|{\rm D}_N| - \widecheck{{\mathbf t}}_N}{\log N}
\,,\,\, \frac{\widecheck{{\mathbf X}}_N}{N}\Big)
	\underset{N \to \infty}\Longrightarrow \, \big(\widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_{\rm D},\, \widecheck{{\mathbf X}}_{\rm D}\big) \,.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

