{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c42360bcd6bc4c8e68c4823154aea551a25aba79da6c7ffb2e47813677e272bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem asympforl of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma > 0$ is small enough then, for any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \tfrac{1}{2}$ sufficiently small (depending only on $\gamma$)  we have that, for all $k$ sufficiently large and $T \in [2k,{\rm e}^{\tfrac{1}{2}k^\gamma}]$,
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P} \Big( \Big\{ \sqrt{\widehat{T}_{(v)}(1)} = u\Big\} \setminus \mathcal L^{\eta,[1,T-1]}_{(v)} \Big)=r_{k,T}(\widehat{u},\widehat{v})(1+o_k(1))
	\end{equation} holds uniformly over all $u \in \mathcal R^{\eta'}_k(1)$ and $v \in \mathcal R^{\eta'}_k(T)$, where $r_{k,T}$ is as in (equation eq:funcfg of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990538+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c42764f665246a63b58563be90ec1a9c5f8054f351ca15f72738a3f1db28aded","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 96 (Edge expansion and expander graphs) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] The edge expansion $h_G$ of a graph is defined as
    \begin{equation*}
        h_G := \min_{1 \leq |S| \leq n/2} h_G(S) = \min_{1 \leq |S| \leq n/2} \frac{|E(S,S^c)|}{|E(S,V)|},
    \end{equation*}
    where $E(A,B)$ denotes all edges between vertex sets $A$ and $B$.
    Given $b > 0$, we say a graph $G$ on $n$ vertices is a $b$-{\em expander} if
\begin{equation}
	h_G =  \min_{1 \leq |S| \leq n/2} \frac{|E(S,S^c)|}{|E(S,V)|} \geq b, 
\end{equation}
or equivalently if
\begin{equation*}
    |E(S,S^c)| \geq b \min \big\{ |E(S,V)|, |E(S^c, V)| \big\} \quad \forall S \subseteq V.
\end{equation*}
We further say that $(G_n)_{n \geq 1}$ is a sequence of $b$-expander graphs if each $G_n$ is a $b$-expander on $n$ vertices.","status":"unverified"}

