{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.442438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c44e24434afdc7d8724381c800d1a68631b124f61b470dbc54ee9fa37e64f292","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm theorem local bounded of arXiv:2504.19942, 'The edge-averaging process on graphs \\ with random initial opinions'] Suppose that the initial opinions $\{f_0(v)\}_{v \in V}$ are i.i.d.\ and take values in $[-1,1]$. Fix $o\in V$. Then for every $t\ge 0$   and $\varepsilon <1$, we have 
   \begin{equation}
    \mathbb P \big( |f_t(o)-\mu |\ge \varepsilon  \big) \le 3 \exp \Big( -\frac{\varepsilon ^2 \sqrt{t_*}}{12} \Big)\,,
\end{equation}
where  $t_*:=\min(t,|V|^2)$ (so $t_*=t$ if $V$ is infinite). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.982399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c44e9715b773cf590beb8f18554fde38419c009494de849c33b25cbdc5d3d619","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 16 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] If
