{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.831931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c46125a499d2aadca1d6c0ffd78273d1febaeb517d2e6d707383e83a97914ac7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3 of arXiv:2506.12145, 'Functional central limit theorem for dependent models with finite memory'] We have, as $n \to \infty$,
\[\left\{\sqrt{n}\left(\frac{S_{\lfloor nt\rfloor}^M}{\lfloor nt\rfloor} - \frac{q}{1-r+q}\right) \ , \ t\geq 0 \right\} \overset{d}{\longrightarrow} \left\{W_t \ , \ t\geq 0\right\},\]
