{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c46ab60672324be12de5e04240abea49cf34dfb3968b459cbb7723030c0ba583","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Effective Independence of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For indices $i,j$ with $|\lambda_i - \lambda_j| \geq N^{-2/3+\delta}$ for some $\delta > 0$:
