{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.518381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c48282bf54df573310e5a0d86ea078a4c0bab6a32a5865b088f1a59cbfbff6ba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:main.mu.version.star of arXiv:2601.12677, 'Stable and Fréchet limit theorem for subgraph functionals in the hyperbolic random geometr'] $(i)$ If $\frac{1}{2} (k-1)<\alpha< k-1$, then as $n\to\infty$, 
