{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.876187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c487bf972398672449b2d93fad409bfe8370e34d9e93f72cf5066774c64157b2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Finite-length inverse-system duality) of arXiv:2609.02449, 'Finite Directional Coefficient Modules over Euler Fibers of $A$-Hypergeometric Systems'] Let $N$ be a finite-length $S$-module satisfying $\Supp_{S}(N)\subset\{\mathfrak{m}\}$.
