{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.321109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4b2fe0c2bfc575e3225bed884fdf6fee32544e881b872cfe7f555f3cc96a690","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Gordin decomposition) of arXiv:2607.04943, '\textbf{Approximation of Random Differential Equations Driven by Physical Brownian Motion '] Let $(Y_n)_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}$ be a strictly stationary sequence, $\mathcal{G}_n:=\sigma(Y_k:k\leq n)$. Assume that
		\begin{equation}
