{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:55.077987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4b3e16611843a617344b1f9b71d28a8924be83917fcebb9516a42085c952414","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:fik-is-mostly-intuitionistic of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] {balbiani_natural_2024}}]  \leavevmode
  (1) $\textbf{FIK}$ enjoys DP.
  (2) $\textbf{FIK} + \varphi \lor \neg \varphi = \textbf{K}$.\\
  (3) $\textbf{FIK} \nvdash \textsf{Dual}_\Box$ and $\textbf{FIK} \nvdash \textsf{Dual}_\Diamond$.
  \begin{proof}
    (1) It is easily proven by a semantical argument, similarly to Proposition (prop:ik-enjoys-dp of the paper).
    (2) As $\textbf{WK} \vdash \Box \varphi \to \neg \Diamond \neg \varphi$,
    it suffices to show that $\textbf{FIK} + \varphi \lor \neg \varphi \vdash \neg \Diamond \neg \varphi \to \Box \varphi$ (see Proposition (prop:ik-plus-em-is-k of the paper)).
    The following derivation proves it:
    \begin{center}
      \scalebox{0.75}{
        \AxiomC{$ $}
        \UnaryInfC{$\bot \to \Box \varphi$}
        \UnaryInfC{$(\Diamond \neg \varphi \to \bot) \to (\Diamond \neg \varphi \to \Box \varphi)$}

        \AxiomC{$ $}
        \UnaryInfC{$\neg \varphi \lor \varphi$}
        \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{M}_\Box$, $\textsf{N}_\Box$}}
        \UnaryInfC{$\Box(\neg \varphi \lor \varphi)$}

        \AxiomC{$ $}
        \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{wCD}$}}
        \UnaryInfC{$\Box(\neg \varphi \lor \varphi) \to ((\Diamond \neg \varphi \to \Box \varphi) \to \Box \varphi)$}

        \RightLabel{\scriptsize{MP}}
        \BinaryInfC{$(\Diamond \neg \varphi \to \Box \varphi) \to \Box \varphi$}

        \RightLabel{\scriptsize{Syll.}}
        \BinaryInfC{$(\Diamond \neg \varphi \to \bot) \to \Box \varphi$}
        \UnaryInfC{$\neg \Diamond \neg \varphi \to \Box \varphi$}
        \DisplayProof
      }
    \end{center}
    (3) Follows from Proposition (prop:ik-non-duality of the paper) and $\textbf{FIK} \subsetneq \textbf{IK}$.
  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:21:28.696972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4b539ae69105a2b555dbf719294a5696a30d754df472860ad735808e7b2dedf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:concave-entropy-dec of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] {anari2024trickle}}]

