{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.836387+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4f363b8761581b00afbb5d9328312a00dbe69030e3e337a401285bff6b08363","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Poisson point process) of arXiv:2604.11434, 'Maxima of stationary systems of randomly time-changed L\'evy particles'] Let $(\mathcal{X}_{}, \mathcal{C}, \mu)$ be a measure space satisfying $\{x\}\in \mathcal{C}$ for all $x\in \mathcal{X}$ and $\mu(\mathcal{X})=\infty$.
  A random collection $\{U^{(i)}\}_{i\in\NN}
  $ of points in $\mathcal{X}$ is called Poisson point process having intensity measure $\mu$ if for every $m\in\NN$ and corresponding disjoint sets $C_1,\ldots,C_m \in \mathcal{C}$ and non-negative (including $+\infty$) integers $r_1,\ldots,r_m $ it holds that
  \begin{align*}
    \PP
    \left[
    \sum_{i\in\NN}
    \ind\{U^{(i)}\in C_j\}
           \
    =
    \
    r_j
    \qquad\text{for all}\
    j\in \{1,\ldots,m\}
    \right]
    \ = \
    \prod_{j=1}^m
    p(\mu(C_j),r_j)
    \,,
  \end{align*}
  where
  \begin{align*}
    p(\lambda,k)
    \ = \
    \begin{cases}
      \frac{\lambda^k \exp(-\lambda)}{k!}
      &\qquad\text{if}\qquad \lambda <\infty\quad \text{and}\quad  k<\infty\,,\\
      1
      &\qquad\text{if}\qquad \lambda =\infty\quad \text{and}\quad  k=\infty
      \qquad\text{or}\qquad \lambda =0 \quad \text{and}\quad  k=0\,,
      \\
      0&\qquad\text{elsewhere}.
    \end{cases}
  \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.854422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4f4697997fbfabd725a9dabefb99943c816f4b3ab6f0a4dcfd3c2ef47d3794e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Uniform Ginibre power bound) of arXiv:2608.20998, 'Free-Probability Kernels for Zero-Rollout Hyperparameter Selection in Reservoir Computing'] Let
\[
A_n
=
(1-\alpha)I_n
+
