{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.890566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c508039581f40a2b530a25837735abbea2e6b329d356c798ddc96e0be60abb6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm masterthm_TCS of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Let $T \in (\mathbb R^d)^{\otimes r}$ be a symmetric random jointly Gaussian tensor with $\mathbb E[T] = 0$ as in (equation eq:Tasgaussianseries_TCS of the paper), and $2 \leq p < \infty$. Then, 
