{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.885204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c53ce8e988142d064e44ba6089a576ef78ce4a86bd8e4f0ac1502c248aa767e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:c_2 of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] There exists a constant $C > 0$ such that for all $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t > 0$ with $tN \in \mathbb{N}$,  

