{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.863817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c551e90f117f8549626805f683cccec31bee1caef012b0ed617eed128ca75730","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 14 (Convergence of root-neighbourhood tree distribution) of arXiv:2605.21459, 'Network evolution with self-reinforcement'] For every $\bt \in \bbT$ and $r \in \bN$,
\begin{equation}

