{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.243057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5c123a5a488f3e8b31917285572ce0f595ed69bae5e735203225fc0075318c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2605.25762, 'Brownian Convergence of Planar Domains and Stability of the Planar Skorokhod Embedding Pro'] Let $(x^{[n]}_{k})_{0\leq k\leq n}$ be a mesh such that $\max_{1\le k\le n}(x_{k}-x_{k-1})\underset{n\rightarrow+\infty}{\longrightarrow}0$.
