{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.650649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5c5f712a9ab0c4b1522f3a9de7b3a88bc1ada8f73ec54c7d4f9803da85d497c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:gauss of arXiv:2608.19198, 'Probabilistic Representation and Convergence of Gromov-Wasserstein Gradient Flows'] If $\rho_0$ is Gaussian, then $\rho_t$ is Gaussian for every
