{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.572052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5c6dae18093d07ea13c84336877a9e0e0b233b2b2605408b586451d354f0bad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Stein.solutions.Wishart of arXiv:2606.04859, 'Stein's method for the Wishart distribution'] Let $\alpha > 3d-3$ and $\Sigma\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d$ be given. Let $(\mathfrak{W}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the Wishart process in (equation eq:Wishart.process of the paper) with transition semigroup $(\mathcal{P}^{\mathcal{W}}_t)_{t\geq 0}$, extended generator $\mathcal{A}^{\mathcal{W}}$ given by (equation eq:Wishart.process.generator of the paper), and stationary limiting distribution $\xi = \mathcal{W}_d(\alpha, \Sigma)$ from Proposition~(prop:extension.Luk.1994.Lemma.2.4 of the paper). Let $h\in C_b^d(\mathcal{S}_{++}^d)$ be real-valued. Since $\mathcal{S}_{++}^d$ is convex, $h$ is bounded and Lipschitz; let $[h]_1$ denote its minimum Lipschitz constant with respect to the Frobenius norm. Set
\[
M_{1, \Sigma}^{\mathcal{D}}(h)
 \vcentcolon= \sup_{t\geq 1} \sup_{X\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d} \sup_{\substack{U\in \mathcal{S}^d\\ \|U\|_F = 1}} \big|\langle U, \mathcal{D}\rangle_F \, h_t(X)\big|,
\qquad \langle U, \mathcal{D}\rangle_F \vcentcolon= \sum_{i,j = 1}^d U_{ij} \, \mathcal{D}_{ij}.
\]
Then $M_{1, \Sigma}^{\mathcal{D}}(h) < \infty$, and the following hold. The function
\begin{equation}
f_h(W) \vcentcolon= -\int_0^{\infty}\Big\{\mathcal{P}^{\mathcal{W}}_t h(W)-\mathsf{E}[h(\mathfrak{W}_{\infty})]\Big\} \, \mathrm{d} t
\end{equation}
is well defined for every $W\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d$ and solves the Wishart Stein equation
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{A}^{\mathcal{W}} f_h(W) = h(W) - \mathsf{E}[h(\mathfrak{W}_{\infty})], \qquad W\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d,
\end{equation}
where $\mathfrak{W}_{\infty}\sim \mathcal{W}_d(\alpha, \Sigma)$. Moreover, if $\mathfrak{V}\sim \mathcal{W}_d(\alpha, I_d)$, then
\begin{equation}
|f_h(W)| \leq 2\|h\|_{\infty} + \frac{1}{2} \left\{\frac{M_{1, \Sigma}^{\mathcal{D}}(h)}{1 - e^{-2}} \, \|\Sigma^{-1/2}W\Sigma^{-1/2}\|_F + [h]_1 \, \|\Sigma\|_2 \, \mathsf{E}[\|\mathfrak{V}\|_F]\right\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.688640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5c7b62c14d0bba3154ba4f377e211f308fde5037f745204dbee09af1881efed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 65 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] A strong preparation map is a linear map $R:T\to T$ such that for every decorated trees $\sigma, \tau$, one has
