{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.436619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5f74b9a335872d10cc4e20c5d17661b0d90a80a4e8512b48b1f1159228e4d39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.07275, 'Some probabilistic properties and time-changed versions of a renewal process based on Mitt'] The bivariate distribution of $\{\hat{N}_{\alpha}(t)\}_{t\ge0}$, $0<\alpha\le 1$ is given by
		\begin{align*}
			\mathrm{Pr}&\{\hat{N}_{\alpha}(s)=l,\hat{N}_{\alpha}(t)=m\}\nonumber\\
			&=\lambda^{2m}\int_0^s u^{2\alpha l - 1} E^{2l}_{\alpha,2\alpha l}(-\lambda u^\alpha) \int_{s-u}^{t-u} v^{2\alpha - 1} E^2_{\alpha,2\alpha}(-\lambda v^\alpha) \times  \\
			& \ \ \Big((t-u-v)^{\alpha (2m-2l-2)} E^{2(m-l)-1}_{\alpha,1+2\alpha (m-l-1)}(-\lambda(t-u-v)^{\alpha})\\
			&\ \ +\lambda(t-v-u-\xi)^{\alpha}
			(t-u-v)^{\alpha(2m-2l-1)}E^{2(m-l)}_{\alpha,\alpha+1 +2\alpha (m-l-1)}(-\lambda(t-u-v)^{\alpha})\Big) \mathrm{d}v \ \mathrm{d}u.
