{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.955187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c637af60c5ad7d572ac2f6acdfd6d1df1ff17d688135b787032c8bfc6aa27e2d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Suppose $d>2$ is odd so that $d+1=2n$ for and integer  $n>1$. Let $R_1$ be the first Riesz transform on $\R^d$.  Consider the Cotlar matrix $\BH_{2n}$ given in \eqref{HilbertMatrix}.  Then the projection of the Cotlar martingale transform $\BH_{2n}*M_t^f$ is $R_1f$. That is,   
