{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.035288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c642abddec25371e7e10173bce7ad5bf482b7fd2cd33e18f9ae4ff54e1ca90b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2.7 of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] {wom}}}]
	Let $m$ be a positive integer and $f(z) = \sum_{n=0}^ \infty a(n)q^n \in  M_k(\Gamma_0(N), \chi ).$ The Hecke operator $T_m$ acts on $f(z)$ by 
	\begin{align}
		f(z)\mid {T_m} := \sum_{n=0}^\infty \bigg( \sum_{d\mid gcd(n,m)} \chi (d) d^{k-1}a \bigg(\frac{nm}{d^2} \bigg) \bigg)q^n.
	\end{align}
	In particular, if $m=p$ is a prime, then 
	\begin{align}
		f(z)\mid {T_p} := \sum_{n=0}^\infty \bigg( a(pn)+ \chi (p) p^{k-1}a \bigg(\frac{n}{p} \bigg) \bigg)q^n.
	\end{align}
	We adopt the convention that $a(n/p)=0$ whenever $p\nmid n$.","status":"unverified"}

