{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.130586+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c662e50bf6cc82f318b3abcb7d39ed6eb187b4f33daae8be85bd12bb3b770465","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:I[sigma,G] of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] For any $\varepsilon \in \{-1,1\}^{2q}$ and $\sigma \in \Sigma(q)$ as defined in (equation b4 of the paper), let $G_\varepsilon$ be the function defined in (equation lambda,T of the paper) and $\mathcal{I}[\sigma; \varepsilon, G_\varepsilon]$ be as defined in (equation I[sigma,G] of the paper).
