{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.368624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c66ac1671619fb271439b729a36b56c12c92e46f20e65d587c2f1fd05e0a7805","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 31 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] For each $l\geqslant 1$, we define the \textit{Taylor approximation function} \( F_l : \mathfrak{g}^{(l)} \times \mathbb{R}^N \to \mathbb{R}^N \) of order \( l \) associated with the RDE \eqref{density1} by
\begin{equation}
F_l(u,x) := \sum_{\alpha \in \mathcal{A}_1(l)} V_{(\alpha)}(x) \cdot (\exp u)^\alpha, \quad (u,x) \in \mathfrak{g}^{(l)} \times \mathbb{R}^N,
\end{equation}
where the exponential function is defined on \( T^{(l)} \) by \eqref{(2.6)} and \( (\exp u)^\alpha \) is the coefficient of \( \exp u \) with respect to the tensor basis element \( e_{(\alpha)} \). We  say that \( u \in \mathfrak{g}^{(l)} \) \emph{joins \( x \) to \( y \) in the sense of Taylor approximation} if \( y = x + F_l(u,x) \).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.225173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c66cce8539334f0af5e519d62fd7caab9af79a1d8ee4e59478c4dca6eef0efdc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop RW/RI to independent RI coupling of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] Let $\delta > 0$. Assume that $R \in [1, \frac{N}{1+\delta}]$ and $\boldsymbol{F} \subset \mathbb{T}_N$ (resp.\ $F \subset Q(0,N)$) is $(1+\delta)R$-well separated. Then for every $u>0$, $\rho \in (0,1)$, there exists a probability measure $\widetilde{\mathsf{P}}$ (resp.\ $\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}$) extending $\mathsf{P}$ (resp.\ $\mathbb{P}$) and carrying independent random interlacements $\left(\mathcal{I}^{(x),u(1\pm\rho)}\right)_{x\in F}$ with the same law as $\mathcal{I}^{u(1\pm\rho)}$, such that
    \begin{multline}

        \widetilde{\mathsf{P}}\Big(\mathcal{I}^{(x), u(1-\rho)} \cap Q_R(x) \subset X[0, uN^d] \cap Q_R(\boldsymbol{x}) \subset \mathcal{I}^{(x), u(1+\rho)} \cap Q_R(x) \text{\quad for all } x \in F \Big) \\
        \geq 1-C|F|R^{2d}\lceil uR^{d-2}\rceil \exp\Big(-c\rho\sqrt{uR^{d-2}}\Big), 
    \end{multline}
    resp.
    \begin{multline}

        \widetilde{\mathbb{P}}\Big(\mathcal{I}^{(x), u(1-\rho)} \cap Q_R(x) \subset \mathcal{I}^u \cap Q_R(\boldsymbol{x}) \subset \mathcal{I}^{(x), u(1+\rho)} \cap Q_R(x) \text{\quad for all } x \in F \Big) \geq \\
        1-C|F|R^{2d}\exp\big(-c\rho^2 uR^{d-2}\big)
    \end{multline}
    for some constants $c,C \in (0, \infty)$ depending only on $\delta$ and $d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.124579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c66e1a95944013ed3180eaf23a48ccd8f82349a9d0d47e6412c266d342789376","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] Let $W\in C^1(\T)$, with $W>0$ on $\T$. Suppose $h\in C^3(\T)$ is a
non-trivial real-valued periodic solution of
