then $W\in C^1(\T)$, $W\geq 0$ on $\T$, and $h$ is a solution of equation \eqref{fine19}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.753286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c671b5cf5968845d881726c3bd699ac784db9ac6169894d491c37ef015455b6b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition kbasicfn of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] The basic function $\phi_{s_B,q}^k$ corresponding to the $k$-th symmetric power representation $\sigma_k$ of $\text{GL}_2(\mathbb{C})$ is given by
