{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.306295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6838408673dc3a02048a9ed7234effbc797a6c7c5fd0e3acd2756c9dc7682bc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2606.24167, '\bf On the stability of rarefaction for stochastic viscous conservation law'] There exists a positive increasing $\mathcal F_t$-adapted stochastic process $\widetilde C_2(t,\omega)$   and constant $c=c(\alpha^*,\sigma,u_\pm,\mathfrak M)>0$, such that
    \bae
	\left\|\phi(t)\right\|^{2} + \int_0^t\left\| \phi_{x} \right\|^2 d s \leq \left\|\phi_0\right\|^{2}+ C\ln(1+t)+\widetilde C_2(t,\omega), \quad {\rm{a.s.}}
    \eae
    with the limit  $\widetilde C_2(\omega):=\displaystyle\lim_{t\rightarrow\infty}\widetilde C_2(t,\omega)$ has exponential moment, i.e., $\mathbb E e^{c \tilde C_2(\omega)}<\infty.$

    Moreover, for any $p>4$, there exists a positive increasing $\mathcal F_t$-adapted stochastic process $\widetilde C_p(t,\omega)$ and constant $c_p=c_p(\alpha^*,\sigma,u_\pm,\mathfrak M,\|\phi_0\|,\|\phi_0\|_p)>0$, such that
    \baee
\| \phi(t) \|_ {p} ^p  \leq C (2+t)^{\frac{-p+3}{4}}\widetilde C_{p}(t,\omega),\quad {\rm{a.s.}}
    \eaee
    where the limit  $\widetilde C_p(\omega):=\displaystyle\lim_{t\rightarrow\infty}\widetilde C_p(t,\omega)$ satisfies $\mathbb E \exp\big\{c_p \widetilde C_{p}(\omega)^{\frac{2}{p}}\big\}<\infty.$","status":"unverified"}

