{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.163672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c719cb3e04fd35cd115dc5907f2e58b008db1408b49b59841e91f271f2897f6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (A uniform exponential envelope) of arXiv:2606.29530, 'Cutoff profiles for colored top-\texorpdfstring{$m$}{m}-to-random shuffles with growing bl'] Fix \(p\ge1\), and assume $\lambda_n=nq_n^{k_n}$ is bounded. Then, for all sufficiently large $n$ and every integer $u\ge0$,
