{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.015617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c71ad3693689eaf5d0a22ec7159049c2e05b072dff610f9ef356210a0be15c63","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 40 (Gaussian concentration implies quantitative blowing-up, \cite{CMRU}) of arXiv:2602.14618, 'Finitary coding and Gaussian concentration\\ for random fields'] \leavevmode\\
Let $Y$ be an ergodic random field with law $\nu$, and assume $Y$ satisfies the Gaussian concentration bound \eqref{def-GCB} with constant $C$. Then $Y$ has the blowing-up property. More precisely, for any 
$\Lambda\Subset\Z^d$ and any $E\subseteq B^\Lambda$ with $\nu(E)>0$,
\begin{equation}
\nu([E]_\varepsilon)\ \ge\ 1-\exp\!\left[-\,\frac{|\Lambda|}{2C}\left(\,\varepsilon-\sqrt{\frac{2C}{|\Lambda|}\,\log\frac{1}{\nu(E)}}\,\right)^{\!2}\,\right],
\end{equation}
whenever $\displaystyle \varepsilon>\sqrt{\frac{2C}{|\Lambda|}\,\log\frac{1}{\nu(E)}}$\,. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.169282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c71e45475e84a9352534dfa8efaa310686b7c0020f8c292fb763fc0b5e39ba36","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Pathwise Bound) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumption \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. Define the cumulative control process $A_s := \int_t^s \gamma_r \, \mathrm{d}r$. For any progressively measurable control $\gamma \in \mathcal{V}_\varepsilon$ (Definition \ref{def:randomized_control}), the following pathwise integral bound holds $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.:
