{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.332841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c72a568b64c2250f599a05a3484e631f0f4631d3ad6253ee4afe24669b8ad5e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2609.03959, 'The combinatorial Hopf algebra of signed graphs'] In the CHA of graphs ($\mathcal{G},\zeta$), let $\zeta_x$ be the deformation of $\zeta$ defined by $\zeta_x(G) = x^{|E|}$ for $G = (V,E)$ a graph. Then
