{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.224743+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c72afa4a79eb8abfe215862ae1ebdd1ab61053dcbbc4bdd97413676bcd131bb6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 64 (Root finding in $\bC^{(3)}_{\alpha,\delta,\eps}(1)$) of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] Let $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\delta>0$ be such that $\alpha+\delta<1-\frac{1}{2\log 2}$. Fix $\eps\in (0,\gamma)$. Consider observing the graph $\bC^{(3)}_{\alpha,\delta,\eps}(1)$ without vertex labels, and fix $\varepsilon>0$. It is possible to construct a confidence set $K=K(\varepsilon)\subset V\left(\bC^{(3)}_{\alpha,\delta,\eps}(1)\right)$ not depending on $n$ such that 
