{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.232724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c735534da5bc745d2b9c1b07bca778f9c7df3f1995e1e31b45fe7664c1f45cfc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2512.10199, 'Explicit correlation functions for the six-vertex model in the free-fermion regime'] Let $x^1,\dots,x^k \in \midedge_n$ and let $y^1,\ldots,y^k$ be suitable neighbouring mid-edges, so that $y^i - x^i \in \{(0,0), e^1, e^2, e^3\}$ for each $i$.  Then
        \begin{equation} 
              P_n\left[\bigcap_{i=1}^k \{\orho(x^i) = y^i\} \right] =  \prod_{i = 1}^{k} K_{(0,0)}(x^i,y^i) \sum_{\theta \in \{0,1\}^2 } \frac{C_\theta \det(K_\theta)}{Z^{\gen}_n} q_\theta \det_{i,j = 1}^{k} K_\theta^{-1} (y^i,x^j),
