{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.162310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c75fa81793b71f9c20050dfdabad1f8a9d870e2b1bf1d9d49db0c2556fcf6af4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_SmoothingOperators of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] There is a family of smoothing operators $\paren{S_\varepsilon : \varepsilon \in (0,1) }$ on $L^2\Gamma\paren{NZ{\backslash} Z, \mathring S \otimes \mathring{\mathfrak l}}$ such that
  for every
  $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, \ 
  $\phi \in L^2\Gamma\paren{U{\backslash} Z, \mathring S \otimes \mathring{\mathfrak l}}$, and
  $k,\ell \in {\mathbf{N}}_0$ with $k \geqslant \ell$,
  \begin{align}

    \Abs{S_\varepsilon\phi}_{\mathring K^k}
    &\lesssim_{k,\ell}
      \varepsilon^{-k+\ell}
      \Abs{\phi}_{\mathring K^\ell}, \\


    \Abs{(S_\varepsilon-\mathbf{1})\phi}_{\mathring K^\ell}
    &\lesssim_{k,\ell}
      \varepsilon^{k-\ell}
      \Abs{\phi}_{\mathring K^k}, \\


    \varepsilon\Abs{\partial_\varepsilon S_\varepsilon\phi}_{\mathring K^k}
    &\lesssim_{k,\ell}
      \varepsilon^{-k+\ell} \Abs{\phi}_{\mathring K^\ell}, \quad\text{and} \\


    \varepsilon\Abs{\partial_\varepsilon S_\varepsilon\phi}_{\mathring K^\ell}
    &\lesssim_{k,\ell}
      \varepsilon^{k-\ell} \Abs{\phi}_{\mathring K^k}.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7616e99113aa8a29e0096a3206c8dcafba4684c673b599d0bba0592b3c5d3a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 50 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_{+,0}$ is a regular right edge for $\Pi_0$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. With high probability, the critical point $\zeta_{t,N}$ exists uniquely in the $t^2$-neighbourhood of $E_{+,0}$. Moreover,
