\(\Phi(s_n)-\Phi(r_n)\to y\), then
\(\Psi(s_n)-\Psi(r_n)\to y\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.964211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7cffba6a78d2200f314919ec769bf6b60fbfb808523c9b58d670896e77589ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Oques 30 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] Analyze the continuity of the phase transition, analogous to Theorem~\ref{thm:phase_transition}, for 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item the variance of $T_n$, which we conjecture fixing $\alpha=1$ it occurs at $c=1/2$, see Remark~\ref{rem:scaling};
        \item the distributional limit for $T_n$;
        \item means of other subgraphs, such as cycles or cliques of fixed size.
