			\hat{N}_{\alpha}(t)\overset{d}{=}\hat{N}(T_{2\alpha}(t)),\ \ t > 0,
		\end{equation}
		where the process $\{\hat{N}(t)\}_{t\ge0}$ is independent with $\{T_{2\alpha}(t)\}_{t > 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.061809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7e9f17603c2f8d14a40f79ba88713fcacbf7f65a43c05425c00051ad39fc39b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] We say that $\mu_{\ast }$ is a $(\psi ,p)$-stationary measure if for every $
		\mu \in \mathcal{P}_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})$ and every $k\in \mathbb{N}$ 
