{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.223854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7ffb86559fe44c43842d08e00691e3610cbe4bfb02225557b576bb8e04e3833","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 55 of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] Let $\alpha+\delta<1-\frac{1}{2\log 2}$, where $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\delta>0$. Then, there is a coupling between $\cT_n, G$ and i.i.d.\ random binomial subsets $S_1,S_2,\dots$  such that
