{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.099254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c829c67f53e00f7f59ab27ae7159c44affd6934620a3ca97578bfb97b18209e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:BE of arXiv:2412.08502, 'Berry-Esseen inequality for random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Assume $\mathbb{E} X_1 = 0, \mathbb{E} |X_1|^2 = \sigma^2$ and $\mathbb{E} |X_1|^3 < \infty$. 
Then there exists an absolute constant $A$ such that
\begin{align}

