            \Big(\mathcal X(-1)\,,\,\mathcal X(1)\Big)=\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\mathcal X^1(-1)-\min\{0,\mathcal X^1(2)+1\} \,,\, \mathcal X^1(2)-\min\{0,\mathcal X^1(2)+1\} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright).
            \end{equation}
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.789019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8465c95a3e07c50ec24dc61a74927adc198f0222bb023d6e8f43bb2b4bb2a15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.00183, '2609.00183'] There exist $A,R_0>0$ depending only on $n$, $\sigma_j$, the constant in \cite[(29)--(33)]{dm}, and the Lipschitz constant of $u$ on $B_{\sigma_j}(0)$, such that for all $x\in B_{\sigma_j/2}(0)$, the functions 
        \[r\mapsto I_{\phi,v}(x,r), \qquad r\mapsto I^v(x,r),\] 
