        \[r\mapsto e^{Ar}(\BDOrd_{\phi,v}(x, r)+Ar^2):=\Ord_{\phi,v}(x,r)\] are nondecreasing for $r< R_0 \leq \sigma_j/4$. Thus, the \textbf{frequency pinching} \[W_s^r(x,v):=\Ord_{\phi,v}(x,r)-\Ord_{\phi,v}(x,s)\] is a nonnegative function on $B_{\sigma_j/2}(0)$ for $0<s\leq r\leq R_0 \leq \sigma_j/4$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8471f76ca3205d81f2812d224cb6b002d59e15271d1391cc5d6b2905294c613","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 12 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d=4$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
