{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.223221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c884607faa71e7ccccd10bd61acaaf5873c39c67f6399f80ac0e42450172d240","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Averaging of observables along the fast coadjoint leaves) of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] For any smooth observable function $G: \su(N)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, any $T\geq 0$ we have
