{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.984242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8b5630fa23b85a2a0d72603f88361fcca4f4c1f6cd8308df70ce66dde9ba0bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma: estimate for g^2 if sv is in 0 1 of arXiv:2607.27472, 'The stochastic Keller--Segel system in critical spaces'] Assume (equation Eq_standard of the paper) and  (equation Eq_pc1_new of the paper)--(equation Eq_pc5_new of the paper) and that $g^2$ satisfies Assumption (Ass_noise of the paper)~(equation Aii of the paper).
			If $s_v \in (0,1]$, then for every $\eta >0$
