{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.236961+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8d796deae791aa180febf1d17bd1dbb8da807d42c13a643f9c3a815bcc82447","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 82 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [$\prod_{i \in I} CONE(S_i)$]
Given $M \subset H_0$ and its open covering 
\begin{equation*}
V=\{S_i \subset M \ |\ i \in I \}.
\end{equation*}
 $\prod_{i \in I} CONE(S_i)$ is the collection of all formal products of tangent cones on $S_i \subset M$ ($i \in I$), i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
\prod_{i \in I} CONE(S_i):=\left\{ \prod_{i \in I} (Cone\ A_i, S_i)\  |\ (Cone\ A_i, S_i) \in CONE(S_i) \ (i \in I)\right\}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

