{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.885013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8e6f1f6a043aa41903129dc0e79b07cdd99ad8e2c953ca64251bf1f019c1756","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:detailed balance reactions of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] A chemical system  $(\Omega, \mathcal R,  \mathcal R_s , \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ satisfies the property of detailed balance if there exists a  $f_s  \in \mathcal P (\mathbb N^M ) $ that is  such that 
