{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.828857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c926729a7a655de0ab0af0f234cabe0a5ee6b604dca1230094a49a548c17ecd9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.13235, 'Mixing Properties of Random Laguerre Tessellations'] Let $\ppp$ be a stationary marked point process on $\rd \times \R$ such that it is \as non-empty. Then for any $x \in \rd$ and any $a > 0$, we have
