{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.829056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c926fe2c0e2304e31edea5ec7b4f332313786feec73ae5a5552c6e42625727d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.10705, '#1'] Let $F \in \mathscr{C}^{0,1}_l([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)$, be differentiable in the direction of a Lipschitz and boundedness-preserving $\gamma$. Then $F \in \mathscr{C}^{1,1}_l([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)$, and
