\noindent (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.811677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c927b6db863155b609e4c593513e7c6fb6ae7920d611edf36d9a16ea5c1fdb4b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Theorem 7.1 of arXiv:2609.03411, 'Adjacent vertex distinguishing total chromatic number of graph products'] {\em Let $G$ and $H$ be two total colorable connected graphs. Let $k_{1}$ and $k_{2}$ be the vertex covering
