{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.924600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c930761f92daf299419a0e8507b5e6bb1ccc72b2b9220b29984ba84e91e5c965","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_loop_measure_crossing of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For $d\ge 3$, there exist $C,c>0$ such that for $N\ge 1$ and $A\subset \widetilde{B}(cN)$, 
