(\boldsymbol{\tau}_\ell-\boldsymbol{\tau}_{\ell+1}) \mathbf H(\mathbf Q_\ell)/2 \right)\mathbf I_{\beta,\vec\mathbf k}[\vec \mathbf p, \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H] \Bigg| <
C_2\mathbf F[\vec\mathbf p, \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H]\mathbf{Err}[\vec\mathbf p, \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H].
\end{multline*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.784726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c93e917464e53b37bfcc26e7779194968ccaeb83eb54a8f27090db418a890ede","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 42 (Hypercontractivity of the Ornstein--Uhlenbeck semigroup) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For $p>1$ and $t>0$, let 
