{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.290750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9620eca02c2a97ec96650e730522a96d023c662186cb5680ce9ee43eb17fef6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_Portenko of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] [Efimenko-Portenko (1989), see~[Port94]]

	We consider the setting of Lemma~(thm_Altmeyer of the paper). 
	For all $t>0 $, 

	$\sum_{i=1}^{[nt]} \indicb{\hfprocess{X}{}{i-1}\hfprocess{X}{}{i}<0}$
	converges in law to some discrete random variable $Z_t $
	with values in $\IN_0 $, i.e., there exists $(b_k(t);\; k\in \IN_0,\, t\ge 0) $ such that $\Prob_0 \left( Z_t = k \right) = b_k(t) $, for all $k\in \IN_0 $.
	The probabilities $(b_k(t);\; k\in \IN_0,\, t\ge 0) $ are defined via their Laplace transforms 
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}
			\int_{0}^{\infty} \lambda e^{-\lambda t} b_k(t) \,\mathrm{d} t &= 
			\frac{A_{\lambda}}{1/\rho^{2} + A_{\lambda}}
			\left( \frac{1/\rho^{2}}{1/\rho^{2}+A_{\lambda}} \right)^{k},
			& \forall &k\in \IN_0,
			& \forall & t\ge 0,  
		\end{aligned}
	\end{equation}
	with $A_{\lambda}= \sqrt{\lambda} \left( \sqrt \lambda + \sqrt{2}/\rho \right) $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.957713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c964de8b8c1829309a9355dfa3ae8ac3115f5270365c996246e74421af9513e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:zero-first-moment of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[lemma]{thm:centered-product}
Let $R$ be an $m\times m$ correlation matrix and let $X\sim\mathcal N(0,R)$.  For
each $i$, let $f_i:\mathbb R\to[0,\infty)$ be bounded and log-concave, with positive
Gaussian integral, and suppose that
\begin{equation}
  \int_{\mathbb R}z f_i(z)\,d\gamma_1(z)=0.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\prod_{i=1}^m f_i(X_i)
  \geq \prod_{i=1}^m \mathbb E f_i(X_i)
  =\prod_{i=1}^m\int_{\mathbb R}f_i\,d\gamma_1.
\end{equation}
The covariance matrix $R$ may be singular. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.778204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c96b0fbcfd2ddc626fb2764d6b40cd49ed3595cf17be785073ef72f160539254","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop::one_arm_bd of arXiv:2411.01467, 'Conformal covariance of connection probabilities \\ in the 2D critical FK-Ising model'] Let $u_1^a$ and $u_2^a$ be the southwest and southeast corners of the box $\Box_2^a$, respectively. Let $u_3^a=\partial \Box_2^a\cap \{\mathfrak{i} y: y>0\}$. Consider the critical FK-Ising model on $(\Box_2^a;u_1^a, u_2^a)$ with Dobrushin boundary conditions and denote by $\mathbb{P}_*^a$ the corresponding measure. Then there exists a universal constant $C_9$ such that 
