{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.902280+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c96df0056b4a1ceb8d456437c7ae63a77704ce1495370eecc2dcdb5b482befec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma epslowerbound of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Assume that the linear measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^m$ satisfies the NSP of order~$r$ with constant $ \eta_r < 1 $.
	Moreover, assume that $\mathbf{X}_\star$ has rank~$r$.
