{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.504035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c99d9dfe69b09e2207753248d7e8d1da1304f7c659c7b51d3259992c8f769057","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma induction-statement of arXiv:2607.22480, 'Distinguishability threshold for random geometric graphs'] Assume that $H\in \mathcal{E}$. Then for every $0\leq s\leq n-1$,
{\relscale{0.95}\begin{align*}
