{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.658883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca124849c0a5fc42dc44a9c2e30615573002fb5fe5c4e1d929ba41f354ae2212","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] For $1\leq p\leq\infty, k \geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\|\nabla^{k}(S_{0}u)\|_{L^{p}(\R^{d})}\lesssim \|S_{0}u\|_{L^{p}(\R^{d})},\\
&\|\nabla^{k}(\Delta_{j}u)\|_{L^{p}(\R^{d})} \sim 2^{kj}\|\Delta_{j}u\|_{L^{p}(\R^{d})}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}
For $1<p<q<\infty, k\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\|\nabla^{k}(S_{0}u)\|_{L^{\infty}(\R^{d})}\lesssim \|S_{0}u\|_{L^{p,\infty}(\R^{d})},\\
&\|\nabla^{k}(S_{0}u)\|_{L^{q,1}(\R^{d})}\lesssim \|S_{0}u\|_{L^{p,\infty}(\R^{d})},\\
&\|\nabla^{k}(\Delta_{j}u)\|_{L^{\infty}(\R^{d})}\lesssim 2^{(k+\frac{d}{p})j}\|\Delta_{j}u\|_{L^{p,\infty}(\R^{d})},\\
&\|\nabla^{k}(\Delta_{j}u)\|_{L^{q,1}(\R^{d})}\lesssim 2^{(k+\frac{d}{p}-\frac{d}{q})j}\|\Delta_{j}u\|_{L^{p,\infty}(\R^{d})}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.679181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca140db9186998d8bc865f42d1e602786b4808661778ba022e9c635cd5d92292","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:CE1_old of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] {ChenLubetzky25}}]
    Fix $n\geq 1$. Let $V\subset \mathbb Z^2$ be a connected domain, and consider the \ensuremath{\mathbb Z\textsc{gff}}\xspace model $\pi_{V;F}^{\xi}$ with a floor at~0 imposed only on a subset $F \subset V$, and boundary conditions $\xi$ that are $H+1-n$ on a $*$-connected path in $\partial_{\mathtt v} V$ and $H-n$ elsewhere so that they induce a unique disagreement polymer $(\gamma,\{D_i\},\{h_i\})$ in $V\cup \partial_{\mathtt v} V$ that contains boundary disagreements. Then for $\beta\geq \beta_0$, the law of this unique disagreement polymer $\gamma$ is given by 
		\begin{align}
			\pi^{\eta}_{V;F}(\gamma) =\frac1{Z_{V;F}^\eta} \exp\Big(-{\ensuremath{\mathscr E}}_\beta(\gamma) + \mathfrak{I}_V(\gamma)
			\Big)\prod_{i\geq 0}{\widehat\pi}_{D_i^\circ}^{h_i}\big(\phi_x \geq 0,\, \forall x \in D_i^{\circ}\cap F\big)\,,
		\end{align}
		for $Z_{V;F}^\eta = Z_{V;F}^\eta(\beta,n)$ 
        and $\mathfrak{I}_V$ from (eq:IU(gamma)-def of the paper) featuring a decoration function $\Phi$ as per (def:disagree-polymer-len-energy-decor of the paper).

		Moreover, if we further have $|F| \leq L e^{\kappa\sqrt{\log L}}$ and $|\partial F|\leq L^{1-\delta}$ for fixed $\kappa>0$ and $0<\delta<\frac13$, denote by $D_0$ and $D_1$ the regions of $\gamma$ containing the boundary vertices of $V$ at heights $H+1-n$ and $H-n$, respectively, and let
		\begin{align*} E:=\left\{|\gamma|\leq L^{1-\delta}\,,\;
			\;|F| - |D_0 \cap F| - |D_1 \cap F| \leq L^{1-\delta}\right\}\,,\end{align*}
		then the following holds
		for all $\beta\geq \beta_0$. The probability distribution given~by 
		\begin{equation}
        \mathfrak{p}_{V;F}^{\eta}(\gamma) := 
		\frac1{\widetilde{Z}^\eta_{V;F}} \exp\bigg(-{\ensuremath{\mathscr E}}_\beta(\gamma) + \frac{|D_0\cap F|}{N_n}+ \mathfrak{I}_V(\gamma)\bigg)\prod_{i \geq 2}{\widehat\pi}_{D_i^\circ}^{h_i}(\phi_x \geq 0,\, \forall x \in D_i^{\circ} \cap F)
		\end{equation}
        for $\gamma\in E$, 
		with $N_n$ from (eq:Nn-def of the paper) and $\widetilde{Z}^\eta_{V;F}$ a normalizer, satisfies that for every $\gamma\in E$,
		\begin{align}
			\pi^\eta_{V;F}(\gamma \mid E) =(1+o(1))\mathfrak{p}_{V;F}^{\eta}(\gamma)\,.
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.548013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca16ce355ca217fa0f6a90e85b08d4fcde329403bc4b4ed6ef6ba5d11c22c373","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] Let $\emprashomonset$, $\rretailset$, and $x$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assume:rashomon} for parameters $\sigma, \rashlexpctparam > 0$. Let $\rlocaltestmat =  \{\rlocaltest_{j}: j \in [\nogaussianpts]\}$ be a random set of perturbations of $x$, distributed $\iid \Unif(\ltwohsphere(x,\sigma))$, and $\ensmretset(\retailset,\localtestmat)$ be the ensemble model defined in \ref{def: local ensemble}.
Define
\begin{align}
   \lallavg(x) = \abs*{\ensmretset(\rretailset,\rlocaltestmat) - \frac{1}{2}}.
\end{align}
Then for any $\slackgap > 0$, 
    \begin{align}
    \prob_{\rretailset,\rlocaltestmat}*{
        \abs*{  \lallavg(x) - \explallavg(x)}
    \ge \slackgap }
    \le 2\exp\parens*{ \frac{-S\slackgap^2}{8\eta^2\sigma^{2}} } +
        2\exp\parens*{ \frac{-\Nretail\slackgap^2}{8\rashlexpctparam^2} }.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.715445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca17e2b8650185d1b11b33f14771e426bcfc530f6c5a366b4fc4d4d6b69c5896","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Strong levelwise variation contact) of arXiv:2608.06393, 'Intrinsic Tangential Hadamard Differentiability of Rough-BSDE Solution Maps'] Fix $\mathbf x\in WG\Omega_p(E)$. Let $\varepsilon_n\to0$ with
$\varepsilon_n\neq0$, let
$\tau_n=(h_n,\kappa_n)\to\tau=(h,\kappa)$ in
$\mathbb T_{\mathbf x}^p$, and let
$\mathbf x_n=(1,x_n,\mathbb x_n)\in WG\Omega_p(E)$. We say that
$\mathbf x_n$ has strong levelwise variation contact with
$(\varepsilon_n,\tau_n)$ at $\mathbf x$ if
\begin{equation}
 \|x_n-x-\varepsilon_n h_n\|_{p\text{-var}}
 +\|\mathbb x_n-\mathbb x-\varepsilon_n\kappa_n\|_{q\text{-var};2}
 =o(|\varepsilon_n|).
\end{equation}
Such a sequence is called an admissible secant at $\mathbf x$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.225292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca1b3d524c89cda538d032b74bf78cc2a8c5337cbfd1df1aec117c9979e59ad5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] If
