{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.812987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca1cd07a06c19c272a5239ca9ff13cf74f02d73d2f244f6737d4a1ee5045718a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:graphic of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] For every spanning forest \(F\), every square minor of \(B_F\) belongs to \(\{0,+1,-1\}\). In particular, if \(|S|=s-1\),
