{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.475177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca217c475c54f3fc9196bc1979a6da741c442a128784f64dc7226465aa4b2300","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 ({Hinrichs--Kolb--Wachtel \cite{HKW2020}}) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] Symmetric $\alpha$-stable innovations satisfy the hypotheses of \cite[Theorem~1]{HKW2020}. Specifically, $\EE[\log{(1+|\xi_{1}|)}] < \infty$, $\EE[(\xi_{1}^{+})^{\delta}] < \infty$ for every $0 < \delta < \alpha$, and $\PP(\xi_{1} > 0)\PP(\xi_{1} < 0) > 0$. Then the following holds:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item The limit
\begin{equation}

\Lambda(a,\alpha) \deq
-\lim_{n \to \infty}\,\frac{1}{n}\log{Q_{n}(x;a,\alpha,\sigma)}
\end{equation}
exists in $(0,\infty)$ and is the same for every fixed starting point $x > 0$.
\item Writing $\pi$ for the stationary law of \eqref{eq:ar1},
