= \Lambda(a,\alpha).
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.293757+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca2345cc0e03bf54828154e593f9ca3ac17d3f3f8b5c03641529cab714ed1aa6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:vax of arXiv:2411.05369, 'Stochastic games of parental vaccination decision making and bounded rationality'] If $\bar{I}(t)\xrightarrow[]{t\to\infty} I_0$, then $x(t)$ has an almost sure logistic stable equilibrium at $0$ and $1$ under the following conditions:
