{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.593209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca333331c73d6981cea24175703ecd64c31b901c9e7c7595775c1bd2d9c4ca28","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eigenvalues distinct k_i of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] Let $\Sigma_n $ be as in ((Eq: Kov.matrix Laengen Potenz Funktional of the paper)) in the subcritical regime for $n\geq2$ with respect to the vector of distinct $k_i$-simplices $(\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k_1}^{(\alpha_1)},  \ldots,\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k_n}^{(\alpha_n)})$. Then the following statements hold:
