{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.363996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca6af5dafc8d98deb45dc723c7fb196acf3f75c9e17b05ba2737a5761fc079b7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] Let \(K>0\). There exist \(n_0\geq 0, K_0\geq 0, c\in (0,+\infty)\) such that, with the notations above, for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(x,x'\in \R^2\), \(y\in x+\Z^2\), \(y'\in x'+\Z^2\) with \(y_1-x_1= n\), \(|x_2|,|x_2'|,|y_2|,|y_2'|\leq \sqrt{n}\), \(x_2-x_2' \geq K_0\), \(y_2-y_2' \geq K_0\), \(|x_1-x_1'|\leq 10\), \(|y_1-y_1'|\leq 10\)
	\begin{equation*}
		P_{x,x'}\Big( \HitEvent_{y,y'},\, \bigcap_{x_1\leq k\leq y_1-1}\big\{\rmd(\DiaEnv\cap \slab_{k,k+1},  \DiaEnv'\cap \slab_{k,k+1}) > K+ \rmd(k,\{x_1,y_1\})^{1/6}\big\}\Big)
		\geq
		\frac{c}{n^2},
	\end{equation*}where \(\DiaEnv = \DiaEnv(S_0,\dots, S_{T_y})\), \(\DiaEnv'=\DiaEnv(S_0',\dots, S_{T_{y'}'}')\), and \(\rmd(\varnothing, A) = +\infty\) by convention.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.279480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca6e423673a6e1c872babd5141c185943e5c0cd900c0a6c40518cf4474c9985a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi eq:assumptioninticonditionK of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $R_{0} \in [0,R_{\max}]$ be a random variable. Let $(\nu^{K}_{0})_{K \geq 1}$ be a sequence of random variables in $\mathcal{M}_{P}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$, such that
    \begin{align}
    \underset{K \geq 1}{\mathrm{sup}} \bigg( \dfrac{1}{K} \hspace{0.1 cm} \mathbb{E}\left(\langle \nu^{K}_{0},1+\mathrm{Id}+\omega \rangle\right) \bigg) < + \infty.

    \end{align}
We use the Poisson point measures $\mathcal{N}$ and $\mathcal{N}'$ of Section~(sec:construction of the paper), independent from $R_{0}$ and $(\nu^{K}_{0})_{K \geq 1}$. For every $K \geq 1$, the renormalized process $(\mu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t})_{t \geq 0}$ with initial condition $(\mu^{K}_{0},R_{0})$, is given for every $t \geq 0$ by $\mu^{K}_{t} := \dfrac{\nu^{K}_{t}}{K}$ and

\begin{align*}
    (\nu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t}) = &  \hspace{0.1 cm}X^{K}_{t}(\nu^{K}_{0},R_{0})  \\  & +  \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathcal{U} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} } \mathbb{1}_{\{u \in V^{K}_{s-} \}} \mathbb{1}_{\{h \leq b\left(\xi^{u,K}_{s-}\right)\}}}  [ X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-} + \delta_{x_{0}} + \delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}-x_{0}} -\delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}},R^{K}_{s})  \\
    &  \hspace{3 cm} - X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-},R^{K}_{s}) ] \mathcal{N}(\mathrm{d}s,\mathrm{d}u,\mathrm{d}h)  \\
     & + 
    \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathcal{U} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} } \mathbb{1}_{\{ u \in V^{K}_{s-}\}} \mathbb{1}_{\{h \leq d\left(\xi^{u,K}_{s-}\right)\}} [X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-} - \delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}},R^{K}_{s})}  \\ 
    & \hspace{3 cm} - X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-},R^{K}_{s}) ] \mathcal{N}'(\mathrm{d}s,\mathrm{d}u,\mathrm{d}h), 
\end{align*}
where for all $t \geq 0$, $V^{K}_{t}$ is the set containing alive individuals at time $t$, and $\xi^{u,K}_{t}$ are individual energies, defined and actualized over time with the same conventions as in Section~(sec:construction of the paper), simply replacing the flow $X$ by $X^{K}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.639221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca70fbf4efba17a26cd370e2ded9b882cef4c6aea487ea8314b0bbbfbe1ae4ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P^hk strong conv to hatP of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Suppose that Assumption \textup{(Assumption:Hypo of the paper)} holds for $\set{P_{s,t}(x,\cdot):0\leq s\leq t\leq T,x\in\mathbb{R}^n}$ the transition distribution  under the strong Markov reference measure $\mathbf{R}$. Let $\mathbf{P},\hat\mathbf{P}$ be the same as in Lemma (lem:from bR to bP of the paper) and $g_k,f_k$, $k\geq1$ be as in Lemma (lem:f_k,g_k approximation convergence of the paper). For every $k\geq 1$, we define 
\begin{equation}
    h_k(t,x):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^n}g_k(y)P_{t,T}(x,dy)\text{ for }(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n,
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{P}^{h_k}:=\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ X_0\in A_k \right\}}}{r_k}\frac{h_k(T,X_T)}{h_k(0,X_0)}\mathbf{P},
\end{equation}
where $A_k:=\set{x\in\mathbb{R}^n:h_k(0,x)>0}$ and $r_k:=\rho_0(A_k)$. 
Then $\set{\mathbf{P}^{h_k}}_{k \geq 1}$ is a sequence of $h$-transforms by harmonic functions, and  $\mathbf{P}^{h_k}$ converges to $\hat\mathbf{P}$ in the strong topology in the sense that \[\lim_{k\to\infty}\sup_{A\in\mathcal F}|\mathbf{P}^{h_k}(A)-\hat{\mathbf{P}}(A)|=0.\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.863521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca728c4c2a001f18bd15adb17c9076c3ead4698ce347d7d8a2367a6b761677a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2607.16502, 'Asymptotic Behavior of Path Functionals for Vector-Valued Gaussian Processes at High Level'] For the process \(\bm W-\bm d\) appearing in conditions~\ref{F2}--\ref{F3},
    if \( G_i : \R \to \R \), \( i = 1, \dots, d \), are
