Moreover, fix $N\geqslant1$, $\text{${\boldsymbol{\tau}}$}\in\widehat\mathcal{T}$, $k\in[p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})]$, and $(\text{${\boldsymbol{\sigma}}$},n,f\pi,\rho)\in\text{$\mathrm{Ind}$}({\boldsymbol{\tau}})$. Then, for any collection $(\psi_q)_{q\in[|\rho|]}$ of functions such that, for every $q\in[|\rho|]$, $\psi_q\in\mathcal{D}'(\R^{p({\boldsymbol{\lambda}}_q)}\times\R^{\mathfrak{s}({\boldsymbol{\lambda}}_q)})$,  
