{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.367435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cad28e1c9dab0312cce8773bb758745a6d8452b8162446c6741e7012910c9a99","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2411.13419, 'Forest Fire Model on $\Z_{+}$ with Delays'] Let $c\le 1$. Assume that either 
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(a)] $\Delta_x\le c/x$ \ for all large $x$, or
    \item[(b)] for some $C>0$ we have $|\Delta_x|\le C$ for all~$x$,  $\sum_x Var(\Delta_x)<\infty$, $\left|\sum_x \left[\mathbb{E}\Delta_x-\frac{c}x\right]\right|<\infty$.
\end{itemize}
Then the infinite fire does not occur a.s. i.e., $\mathbb{P}(n_k<\infty\text{ for all }k )=1$.
\\[2mm]
Conversely, if $c>1$, and either 
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(c)] $\Delta_x> c/x$ \ for all large $x$, or
    \item[(d)] $\mathbb{E} \Delta_x=\frac {c+o(1)}x$  and $\displaystyle \mathbb{P}\left(\lim_{x\to\infty}\, |\Delta_x|\sqrt{x}=0\right)=1$.
\end{itemize}
Then the infinite fire occurs a.s.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.993721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cad3458487dd3b8e3294442c8317adec42f7c86b1550cb8144c3eeafd282c186","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem d<1 acyclic of arXiv:2412.01086, 'Spectral radii of sparse non-Hermitian random matrices'] {rrw20}}] 
