{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.618229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cafcb1a353a9dd1000102dad27ec323061aeffa0d6cc1c473e47f7d7d10a0512","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 74 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c,C',c'$ such that for all $\delta>0$, all $n$ and all $m$ satisfying $m\leq n^{1-3\delta/2}$, we have
  \begin{align}

        &\PP(\exists x: |x|\in [(1+m)^{2/3}n^\delta, n^{2/3}], |T_{(m+x,m)}^{\n}+x- T_{(m,m)}^{\n}|\geq H_{x,m}/4)\nonumber\\
    &\leq C\exp(-c \min_{|x|\in [(1+m)^{2/3}n^\delta,n^{2/3}]}(\frac{H_{x,m}}{\sqrt{|x|}})^2)\leq C'e^{-c'n^{\delta}}.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.313517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cafe6d4d1416e631ea5c3684a1f286f3c194fab8786e4ddeacf5489aa145e636","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 41 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] Suppose $d \ge 1$, $q > 1$, and $0 < \gamma$ such that $d(q-1) < 2q$ and $\gamma \le \frac{2q}{d(q-1)}$. Then the variational problem
    \[
    \rho_{d, q, \gamma} = \sup \{ \| \xi \|_q^{\gamma} - \mathcal{I}(\xi) : \xi \in \widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1}(\mathbb{R}^d) \} = \left(\frac{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}{2q} \right) \left( \frac{\gamma d(q-1)}{q} \right)^{\frac{\gamma d(q-1)}{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}} \kappa_{d, q}^{\frac{4\gamma q}{2q - \gamma d(q-1)}}
    \]
    has a unique solution, which is an element of $\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}_{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.337874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cafeb0be1e70983becd02d302f3253558c254110bc3047feaa9d29c7ffd5ebf9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $D$ be regular for $A$, $\mathpzc{l}(D)<+\infty$, and $f\in \BB_b(D)\cap C^2_{loc}(D)$. The problem
		\begin{align}
			\begin{cases}
				\phi(\partial_t) \big(U(x,t)-U(x,0)\big)=-\Lpsi U(x,t), & x\in D,\,t>0,\\
				U(x,t)=0,& x\in D^c,\, t>0,\\
				U(x,0)=f(x),& x\in D.
			\end{cases}
		\end{align}
		has a pointwise solution $U(x,t)\coloneqq \EE^xf(X^D(t))$. 

		In particular, if $f\equiv \1$, the solution is 
		$U(x,t)=\mathds{P}^x(\tau_D>t)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.627334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb02955c2f348767c2a08513c33a3e104407c56d01cd1e390d9487bd88f45793","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2511.22162, 'Landau Hamiltonian with Gaussian white noise potential and the asymptotics of its bottom o'] Given an open box $B$, $\bA \in \ccA$ and $q \in \ccM$, the strongly continuous semigroup $(P_t^B(\bA, q))_{t > 0}$ admits a unique generator $\Phi^B(\bA, q)$ with a dense domain $\cD(\Phi^B(\bA, q)) \subset L^2(B)$, defined by
	\begin{equ}
		\Phi^B(\bA, q) f = -\left.\frac{\dd}{\dd t} P_t^B(\bA, q) f\right|_{t = 0}, \quad \cD(\Phi^B(\bA, q)) := \{f\in L^2(B) \text{ for which the derivative exists}\}.
	\end{equ}

	In particular, $\Phi^B(\bA, q)$ is self-adjoint and its spectrum is contained in $(-\omega^B(\bA, q), \infty)$ with $\omega^B(\bA, q)$ given in Corollary (cor:P_t-bounded of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.860979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb03629e8c0f062b2477d9c27b40de3716eac28dcd6538f8bd25c3d999ca66c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Atheo 1 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $f$, $\sigma$ be sufficiently smooth functions and $\xi$ satisfying Assumptions \ref{Ass:Half_Step} and \ref{Aspt_new}. Let $\delta,h$ be small. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that
