{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.820345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb12838e14f5e8a32e140c2fd6653581e6c0958e7ed88fe5b47c4aaed41822f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2506.13587, 'Non-exchangeable mean-field theory for adaptive weights: propagation of dissociatedness and graphon sampling l' (conj environment).] Adopt the setting of Theorem~(thm:empirical_data_stability), but for $k \in \mathbb{N}$, assume the $N_k$-particle system $\bm{\mathcal{Y}}^{(k)}(t) = ((\bm{X}^{(k)}_{i}(t))_{i \in [N_k]}, (\bm{W}^{(k)}_{i,j}(t))_{i,j \in [N_k]})$ evolves according to the SDE system (eqn:decay_SDEs) with $\epsilon = 1$. 
