{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.221135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb2c47130b30d5e6db663110324b5d2d4cd08b07643255773482c87d0fcdc52f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: 445 of arXiv:2607.05848, 'Mesoscopic eigenvalue statistics for correlated random matrices'] We define the matrix $V=(V_{ij})$ by setting
\begin{equation}
	V_{ij}\equiv V_{ij}(z,w) \coloneqq \sum_{b} \big( \mathcal{B}_{z,w}^{-1}\mathcal{C}_{M,\widetilde{M}}\mathcal{S}[E^{jb}] \big)_{ib}.
