{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.342512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb52ffa629631f0aa6113daebcc4412c4894a895b4a7569e4c8890e5d7b9f3ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:conv of arXiv:2605.05904, 'Schr\"odinger's problem with constraints'] Suppose Assumptions~(a:main of the paper),(ass:f of the paper) and  (a:feps of the paper) hold. 
As $\eps\to0$, the solutions of the Schr\"odinger problems $\mathcal{S}_E(\mu_0,\mu_1^\eps)$
