{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.675700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb6841fb37918d02951a8ac726a6bef0eb8a2b51b7d8b8387e09b558d87e8fff","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma bound2 of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Let $a,b\in \mathbb{R}$ and $M=2b+a-2(1+a+|a|)$. For every progressively measurable process $\varphi\in L^\infty(0,T;H^{2b+a})$, define 
