{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.610140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb842a68cc58cbc9b7e0efbafdc714b4ad6e35d7f5e795e77ed68fbad12696b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Fourier_PF of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] Let $\Sigma_{g,n}$ be a compact connected oriented surface and let ${\mathbb{G}}=(V,E,F)$ be a topological map embedded in $\Sigma_{g,n}$, with every boundary component carried by ${\mathbb{G}}$. Let $(Q_t)$ be a family of central continuous probability densities and assume the graph-level spectral summability condition
