{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.764107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb8738a3174db46b98f8cf03bb479b1863a06db5af316541dafb0bdd376261fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] For $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $G$ a Gibbs kernel defined on some partition $(\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \KL{\widetilde{\pi}_\alpha}(Q_\alpha\ \|\ \widetilde{\Pi}_\alpha) = (1-\alpha)\KL{\pi} (G\| \Pi) + \alpha \KL{\pi}(P \| \Pi). 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.360588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb89a3d627d4404fc4e21137c69a70162dd810e274f2453c326c0dabb4820fd0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] For every $0\leq p < \widehat{\mf q}$, the $0-$level set of $\ms J^{(p)}$ is the
convex hull of the $(p+1)-$order metastable states. That is,
\begin{equation*}
\left\{\mu\in \mss P(\bb T): \ms J^{(p)}(\mu) = 0\right\}\,=\, \mss P_{\mc M_{p+1}}.
