{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.981727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb8b53276b1d463f829874bb262ed69a152946a8bf8db93141f4f98e489daa5f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Propo lem: c_k of arXiv:2606.15339, 'Uniform integrability of the distance to the nearest leaf in random trees'] Let $(\mathcal{T}_n)_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of size-conditioned simply generated trees of type~I, II or~III, and set $c_k := \mathbf{P}(\partial(\hat{\mathcal{T}}) \geq k)$. Then $c_0 = c_1 = 1$ and, for every $k \geq 1$,
	\begin{align}
		c_k = \prod_{j=1}^{k-1} G'(F_j(1))\,.
	\end{align}
	For types~I and~II this admits the closed form
	\begin{align}
		c_k = {F_k'(1)}/{m}\,, \qquad \text{ for every } k \geq 1\,,
	\end{align}
	so that $c_k = F_k'(1)$ when $m = 1$ (type~I) and $c_k = F_k'(1)/m$ when $0 < m < 1$ (type~II). In type~III the limit $\hat{\mathcal{T}}$ is the infinite star, and hence $c_k = 1$, for any $k \leq 1$ and $c_k = 0$, for any $k \geq 2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.299468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb8bd367fdfadc09aac150595ce25b8b46e35e28ea445cb4a90461917b282f4b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Information identity, ceiling, and comparison invariance) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] For every metric probability space,
\begin{equation}
  \log 3-\Htri(P,\metric)
  =I\{L_V(X);V\},

\end{equation}
and hence
\begin{equation}
  0\le \Htri(P,\metric)\le\log 3.
\end{equation}
Equality in the upper bound holds if and only if $q(V)=(1/3,1/3,1/3)$ almost surely. Moreover, the value is unchanged when every dissimilarity is transformed by a common strictly increasing function; in particular, it is invariant to global metric rescaling.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.748866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb95d27cff87759fe337ffd6000a5ece58346b46949cf7043815dd13598474eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 22 (Brownian functional limit in the finite-variance regime, see~{\cite[Theorem 7.4.1.) of arXiv:2607.28865, 'First-Passage Percolation on Spread-out line graphs: Microscopic Regime'] {whitt02}}]
Assume that $\ell\ge 2$ is fixed, $\go$ is not deterministic, and $\E\sfP_1^2 + \E\sfT_1^2 + \E\sfH_1^2 < \infty$. By Proposition~\ref{prop:k-moment}, this integrability condition holds if either Assumption~\textnormal{A.\ref{ass:A1}} holds (\ie\ $\E\go^2 < \infty$), or Assumption~\textnormal{A.\ref{ass:A2}} holds with $\gc > 2/\lc$. Then, in the Skorokhod space $D([0,\infty),\dR^{2+\ell})$ equipped with the $J_1$ topology, the centered joint skeleton process converges to a $(2+\ell)$-dimensional Brownian motion:
\[
    \left(
    \frac1{\sqrt n}
    \begin{pmatrix}
        S_{\sfN(nt)}^{\sfT}-nt\cdot \mu_{\sfT}/\mu_{\sfP}\\[2mm]
        S_{\sfN(nt)}^{\sfH}-nt\cdot \mu_{\sfH}/\mu_{\sfP}\\[2mm]
        \mvS_{\sfN(nt)}^{\sfJ}-nt\cdot \mvmu_{\sfJ}/\mu_{\sfP}
    \end{pmatrix}
    \right)_{t\ge 0}
    \Longrightarrow
    (\vB_t)_{t\ge0},
\]
where $\vB_\cdot$ is a centered $(2+\ell)$-dimensional Brownian motion with covariance function $\cov(\vB_s,\vB_t) = \min\{s,t\}\cdot \Sigma$, and $\Sigma$ is the $(2+\ell)$-dimensional covariance matrix from Corollary~\ref{cor:geo-stat}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.699079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb9c6693fcf800caa408d5ac55e93436c899bcbb8f640e7f0ca9b59442a4feee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 (Convergence of partially defined random variables) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $(S,d)$ be a separable metric space, let $G\in\mathcal F$, and let
$(A_n,X_n)_{n\ge1}$ consist of events $A_n\in\mathcal F$ and strongly
measurable $S$-valued random variables $X_n$.  For a strongly measurable
$S$-valued random variable $X$, we say that $(A_n,X_n)$ converges to $X$ in
probability on $G$ if, for every $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\bigl(G\cap(A_n^c\cup\{d(X_n,X)>\varepsilon\})\bigr)
 \longrightarrow0.
\end{equation}
The values assigned to $X_n$ on $A_n^c$ do not affect this notion.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.759718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb9c75862e86a977879cf08c81bd84b5502f589398a6f7c4c7dac0370f1af3b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thm:workhorse-lemma of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $(\xi_k)_{k\in\mathds{N}}$ be a sequence of independent nonnegative (finite) random variables.
