{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.501799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbb5111e5468df737575a03a7057f048770498ec559fa249ecb307f57cd3f0df","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 42 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For $X \in \calc^{\alpha}([0,T], V)$, $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W)$ and $f \in C_b^2(W, \bar{W})$ we have
