{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.223343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbc4d5688be6a16caad2ee371fd57422244cc0a19ec132ce24f6d445f39a72a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] For any bounded smooth function $G: \su(N)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, any $t>0$ we have, as $\varepsilon\rightarrow 0$ and then $\delta \rightarrow 0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{E}_{\Omega_0^{\varepsilon,\delta}=\Omega_0} \int_0^{t\wedge \tau^{\varepsilon,\delta}} G(\Omega_s^{\varepsilon,\delta})ds \rightarrow \mathbf{E}_{Z_0=\pi(\Omega_0)} \int_0^{t\wedge \tau} \overline{G}(Z_s)ds \ .
\end{equation}
where $\overline{G}(z)=\displaystyle{\int_{\mathcal{O}^*(z)}}G(\Omega)dm_z(\Omega)$ is defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:AveragingLeafwiseCoAdjointsuN})}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.977087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbc504b116e71f0d362c78ad347c06acb322969892e6a6890434330d9d00726c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] Let $m \in \{1,\dots,n-1\}$, $T \in\cT_m$, $r_0,\dots,r_m \in \N$.
