{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.978498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbf5d5eb9c2636241047c935f7ffeb31586e00ffe89bf186cbc066b464717d15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.11389, 'Instability of a nonlinear oscillator with small friction and small additive noise'] Suppose $h > 0$.  We have
  \begin{align*}
  T(h) & =  4(1-2m^2)^{1/2} K(m), \\
  G_1(h) & =  -\frac{T'(h)}{T(h)} =  \left( \frac{1}{m(1-2m^2)}-\frac{E(m)}{m(1-m^2)K(m)} 
     \right) \frac{dm}{dh}> 0,  \\[1ex]
  G_2(h)  & =  \sigma^2\left(\frac{8}{15}h + \left(\frac{7}{15}+ \frac{12}{5}h\right)\left((1+4h)^{1/2}\left(\frac{2E(m)}{K(m)} -1\right) - 1\right) \right)
     \end{align*}
where
 $$m^2 = \frac{1}{2}\left( 1 - \frac{1}{\sqrt{4h+1}}\right)
 $$
and $K(m)$ and $E(m)$ denote the complete elliptic integrals of the
first and second kind (see \cite[Sect.\ 22.7]{WW62}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

