{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.726384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc11db917c46e9bbab5e180063f6b37007c87feec8a4f2eb8dc5f469eaa3e619","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2.2 of arXiv:2604.19294, 'On the maxima of Littlewood polynomials on $[-1,1]$'] There exists a function $w\colon\mathbb{R}\to[0,1]$ such that $\operatorname{supp}(w)\subset[-1/2,1/2]$, $w(x)=1$ for $x\in[-1/4,1/4]$, and
