{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.958506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc156d644bf8a28cfc8bb76d970d742d0767c0a024b0dbe4c74670d59d1a9315","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (Abstract transfer to roots) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] Assume that, for every $D\subset V$, every $x\in D$ and every $t\geq0$, it follows that:
