{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.721954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc28b727285c04663f7e0caafbbdbba7799b4b0dd6eb4b5021aacbb9ee4162e5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main-1 of arXiv:2609.02769, 'Divergence-Free Approximation in Sobolev and Lebesgue Spaces on general unbounded domains '] Let $\Omega=\mathbb{R}^d$ and $\boldsymbol{y}\in\mathbb{V}\cap\mathbb{L}^p_{\sigma}$. Then, there exists a sequence $\{\boldsymbol{y}_n\}_{n\geq1}$ in $\mathbb{C}_{0,\sigma}^{\infty}(\Omega)$ such that 
