{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.975743+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc2f98523e3904ebf64e45c633670b93662aff8196253bc0c0fe93682e9a3941","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 20 (Threshold for monotonicity and FKG property) of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite graph with coupling constants $J$. Then for any $p\leq p(J)$, $\en_J$ has the $p$--weak FKG property and for any $J_2\geq J_1\geq J$, $\en_{J_1}\domi_{p}\en_{J_2}$.

	Furthermore, take $n\in \mathbb N$, $J\in (\R^+)^{n}$, and $p\in (0,1]^{n+1}$ such that 
\begin{align}
	\sum_{k=1}^n\frac{p_k-p(J)_k}{p_k}>1.
\end{align} Then, there exists a graph $G$ with $n+1$ edges with coupling constants $J_G$ that satisfies the following:
\begin{itemize}
	\item If we number the edges of $G$, $J_G$ restricted to its first $n$ edges is equal to $J$.
	\item Its energy field does not satisfy the $p$--weak FKG property.
	\item There is $J'_G\geq J_G$ such that $\en_{J'_G}$ does not $p$--weakly dominate $\en_{J_G}$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.627742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc326a24eeeeeabd86b0bbd203330d97f1295a8df0b8d97a68dbe24cde592c7c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Combinatorial discrepancy) of arXiv:2605.13107, 'Discrepancy and Fisher information'] Let $v_1,\dots,v_n \in \R^d$ be any fixed vectors, and let $\e_1,\ldots, \e_n$ be independent Rademacher random variables. Then there exists an online algorithm that discards some terms $\e_j v_j$ so that, for each $k$,
