{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.964173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccae8f382b6183b88a370dc1c6c6ed86a2e27df0ee3f4b5038e746814fb87405","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Entropy}

    Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$. For an integrable $f : \R^n \to [0, \infty)$ \st{} $\int_{\R^n} f\abs{\log(f)}d\nu < \infty$, 
