{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.857822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccc6f1084677dde8582f87dcd3c12258b7616d15c9ba07cea4de3f5b206a76fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ch5-t30 of arXiv:2410.23995, 'Sample path properties of parabolic SPDEs with non constant coefficients'] We assume that $({\bf H_\Lambda})$, $({\bf \bar{H}_\Gamma})$, $({\bf H_L})$ and $({\bf H_I})$ hold.
Let $(u(t, x), \, (t,x)\in[0,T]\times D)$ be the solution of (equation 5.1 of the paper) given in Theorem (ch5-t2 of the paper). Then
for every $p\in[2,\infty[$, $\gamma_1\in \left]0,\frac{1-\eta}{2}\right [$ and $\gamma_2\in\, ]0,1-\eta[$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for all $s,t\in[0,T]$, $x,y\in D$,
\begin{equation}

 E\left(|u(t,x) - u(s,y)|^p\right) \le C\left(|t-s|^{\gamma_1 p} + |x-y|^{\gamma_2 p}\right) + |I_0(t,x)-I_0(s,y)|^p.
\end{equation}
As a consequence, for $\gamma_1 \in \left]0,\frac{1-\eta}{2}\right [$ and $\gamma_2\in\, ]0,1-\eta[$, there is a version of $(u(t, x) - I_0(t, x), \, (t, x) \in [0, T] \times D)$ with  locally H\"older continuous sample paths with exponents $(\gamma_1, \gamma_2)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.372490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cccabc390a41229e1890e3c88a069c0bfd6f0090cb92f641651e72af3d9870b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] We denote by $P(k)$ the set of partitions of $\{1,\ldots,k\}$, with these partitions $\pi\in P(k)$ being most conveniently being drawn as diagrams,
