{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.916023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccd44ec40c2d89d6583c3d61434288f2992893b427c4879d0ff8e627c28993eb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] We define $\Xi$ to be the random set 
    \[
    \{\xi \in \mathbb{R}: W^{\xi -}(p;q) \neq W^{\xi +}(p;q) \quad\text{for some }p,q \in \mathbb{R}^2\}
    \]
