{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328006+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cce495cc4cfb13e0e8babd393e5fea156609f23e3114ace9a4a2092843833eed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Horizontal perimeter of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For a measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$, its \emph{horizontal perimeter} is defined by
\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)=\sup\left\{\int_{\Omega}\sum_{i=1}^{d} X_i \rho_i: \|\sum_{i=1}^d \rho^2_i\|_\infty\leqslant 1, \rho_i\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb G)\right\},
\end{align*}
where $\{X_1, \ldots, X_{d}\}$ is an orthonormal frame in $V_1$. A measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is called a \emph{Caccioppoli set} if $\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.312271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cce66a6aa42ef6779a4ff030bd2800bf0a09697fc9dfb024a85c524d70c48515","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma guided-diffusion-u-v of arXiv:2608.29507, 'Denoising as Projection: Constrained Optimization with Gradient-Guided Diffusion'] Define
    \begin{align}
        u_t:= Ax_t, \qquad v_t := A^{\perp} x_t
    \end{align}
    then (equation eq:guided-diffusion of the paper) with Assumption (assump:linear of the paper) would give the following update
    \begin{align*}
        v_{t-1} &= \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} v_t\\
        u_{t-1} &= u_t - (1-\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t})(I + \sigma_t^2\Sigma^{-1})^{-1}(\sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1} u_t + \eta_t A \nabla f(x_t)) 
    \end{align*}
    \begin{proof}
        From Lemma (lemma:pi-t of the paper), $\widehat\pi_t(x) = A^\top (I + \sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1})^{-1}Ax$, hence
        \begin{align*}
            v_{t-1} &= A^{\perp} x_{t-1} = A^{\perp}\left(\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} x_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)\widehat\pi_t(x_t -\eta_t \nabla f(x_t))\right)\\
            &= A^{\perp}\left(\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} x_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)A^\top (I + \sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1})^{-1}A(x_t -\eta_t \nabla f(x_t))\right)\\
            &= \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}A^{\perp} x_t =\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} v_t\\
            u_{t-1} &= A x_{t-1} = A\left(\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} x_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)\widehat\pi_t(x_t -\eta_t \nabla f(x_t))\right)\\
            &= A\left(\frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} x_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)A^\top (I + \sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1})^{-1}A(x_t -\eta_t \nabla f(x_t))\right)\\
            &= \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t} u_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)(I + \sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1})^{-1} (u_t - \eta_tA\nabla f(x_t))\\
            & = u_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)\left(-u_t + (I + \sigma_t^2 \Sigma^{-1})^{-1} (u_t - \eta_tA\nabla f(x_t))\right)\\
            & = u_t + \left(1- \frac{\sigma_{t-1}}{\sigma_t}\right)(I + \sigma_t^2\Sigma^{-1})^{-1} (-\sigma_t^2\Sigma^{-1}u_t -\eta_t A\nabla f(x_t) )
        \end{align*}
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.267742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cce6f3f6d665bcdd51df894ef3b11d922e4380de770583e3c8aaec2cae6b082d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff 4 (Extended Carre du Champ operator) of arXiv:2604.20435, 'Stochastic Extinction with Relaxed Boundedness Conditions'] Let $A\subset M$ be an open invariant set. Define $\mathcal D^{ext}_2(A)$ be set of all continuous $f : A \to \R$ such that there exist continuous functions $\Lom f : A \to \R$ and $\Gamma f : A \to [0, \infty)$ such that $M^f_t(x)$ \begin{equation}
