{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.389797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccf0b96bf6dbc4173e212ec4e05fc78ad5bd028fdf46b2e4abde112c7652c896","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-time-finite of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] There exists a function $\mathfrak w_* : \mathcal V\mathcal G\to (0,\infty)$ such that if $\mathfrak w(x) \geq \mathfrak w_*(x)$ for all but finitely many $x \in \mathcal V\mathcal G$, then the following is true. 
