{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.971747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccf2ae847ff5eb55e4dda7f1353620801affc8753d28a384a14b4b59be5fa7f8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:skew_gt_patterns of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] For $\mu \in \Sig_n, \lambda \in \Sig_{n+k}$, we define $\GT_P(\lambda/\mu)$ to be the set of sequences of interlacing signatures $\mu = \lambda^{(0)} \prec_P \lambda^{(1)} \prec_P \cdots \prec_P \lambda^{(k)}= \lambda$. 

For $\lambda,\nu \in \Sig_n$, we define $\GT_{Q,k}(\lambda/\nu)$ to be the set of sequences of length $n$ interlacing signatures $\nu = \lambda^{(0)} \prec_Q \lambda^{(1)} \prec_Q \cdots \prec_Q \lambda^{(k)}=\lambda$. We refer to elements of either $\GT_P$ or $\GT_{Q,k}$ as \emph{Gelfand-Tsetlin patterns}.

For $T \in \GT_P(\lambda/\mu)$ with $\len(\lambda) = \len(\mu)+k$, set $\psi(T) := \prod_{i=1}^{k} \psi_{\lambda^{(i)}/\lambda^{(i-1)}}$. For $T \in \GT_{Q,k}(\lambda/\nu)$, set $\varphi(T) := \prod_{i=1}^{k} \varphi_{\lambda^{(i)}/\lambda^{(i-1)}}$. In both cases, let $wt(T) := (|\lambda^{(1)}|-|\lambda^{(0)}|,\ldots,|\lambda^{(k)}|-|\lambda^{(k-1)}|) \in \mathbb{Z}^k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.385098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccf4b20cc4f5ae80f8488177af86a0b63b9d688626376612daf2bbbbfc446734","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] Let $\rho\geq 1$ and $b\geq 2$ be integers. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] the numbers $C_b^\rho(n)$ of $\rho$-color $b$-ary partitions 
of $n$, and 
\item[(b)] the numbers $Y_n$ of compositions of $n$ into $\rho$ parts
