{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.281772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccff0ac16397112ed4450fc32377449ec7bf83071b62ff5f57d318614c585232","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] For every $r>1$ there exists a sequence of smooth functions $f_{j}:\R^{2}\rightarrow\R$ with the following properties as $j \to \infty$:
