{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.169935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccff374e39f42f40be76c821e626175650c2695b266b75ef17ec0fb9aa780dcc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:transport-cover of arXiv:2609.00399, 'Shannon's problem on the monotonicity of entropy and a Conjecture of Tao'] Let $0\leq L<\infty$.  Assume that $q$ is finitely supported and
