{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.751656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd109099319789de88f331010a4571246605d452ded98f6b127e40f6d8203d0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:exact-dimension-support-mass-witnesses of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Let \(\beta>A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\), let \(\Lambda\) be the block-count exponent in Lemma~(lem:biggins-chernoff-block-count-exponent of the paper), and let \(C\) be a nonnegative random variable with \(0<C<\infty\) almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\). Then, almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\),
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)=\Lambda(1-\beta).
\end{equation*}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)
=
\inf_{q\ge0}
\left\{
1+\log_2\mathbb E(W^q)-q(1-\beta)
\right\},
\end{equation*}
where \(W^0=\mathbf 1_{\{W>0\}}\), and the value inside the infimum is interpreted as \(+\infty\) whenever \(\mathbb E(W^q)=+\infty\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.771087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd1415f064d5574cf26e53386e299e54070e3a8a6d3ffdcb8262ddf31fcd9044","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 4 ({\cite[\S7) of arXiv:2608.30513, 'Brieskorn spheres bound orbit spaces of torus manifolds'] {ga-04}}]
		Let $M$ be a smooth $n$-dimensional manifold with corners, and let $\mathcal{C}$ be a finite collection of locally closed, connected, smooth submanifolds (without boundary) in $M$ with $M=\bigsqcup\limits_{X\in \mathcal{C}} X$.
		The collection $\mathcal{C}$ is called a \emph{(smooth) conical stratification} of $M$ if either $n=0$, or the following hold:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(C1)] There is a unique stratum of maximal dimension $n$ in $\mathcal{C}$; for each $X\in\mathcal{C}$, $\overline{X}\setminus X$ is a union of elements in $\mathcal{C}$; every boundary hypersurface of $M$ is a union of elements in $\mathcal{C}$; this equips $\mathcal{C}$ with the partial order $X<Y\Leftrightarrow X\subset \overline{Y}$;

			\item[(C2)] Every $\overline{X}\in\mathcal{C}$ is admissible.
			Let $l(X):=S_{N}\subseteq M$ (using intersection with a sphere of small radius) for any $X\in\mathcal{C}$.
			For $X,Y\in \mathcal{C}$, $X<Y$, let $l(X,Y):=l(X)\cap Y$.

			\item[(C3)] For all $X\in \mathcal{C}$, $x\in X$ with the respective neighbourhoods $D(X,x)$ one has:
			\begin{itemize}
				\item $\overline{Y}\cap D(X,x)=\varnothing$ for $Y\in \mathcal{C}$ unless $X\leq Y$;
				\item $\mathcal{C}(X):=\lb l(X,Y)\mid X<Y\in\mathcal{C}\rb$ is a smooth conical stratification of $l(X)$, and its product with the trivial stratification on $D_{T}$ is the induced by $\mathcal{C}$ stratification on $D(X,x)$.
			\end{itemize} 
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.330479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd183c5a50bb8a4547d8f3a58297a596393de24cd3e694c26c3fdfcb5a6ef1d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 7 (Equal--ranked--equal profile) of arXiv:2608.30374, 'Compact and Infinite-Order Error Analysis\\ for Null-Space SVD Estimation'] Under the assumptions of the two propositions,
