{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.662936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd2c2b8932f2ca1c65221e0161b1eebc230fce9450098341ed7805085382b3a9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmaMoment of arXiv:2604.06012, 'Large fringe trees for random trees with given vertex degrees'] Let $\mathbf{n}$ and ${\mathbf{m}}$ be two degree statistics and let
$\mathcal{T}_{\mathbf{n}} \in {\rm Unif}(\mathbb{T}_{\mathbf{n}})$. 
Then, for every  $q \in \mathbb{N}$, 
we have
\begin{align} 
\operatorname{\mathbb E{}}[(N_{{\mathbf{m}}}(\mathcal{T}_{\mathbf{n}}))_{q}] = |\mathbb{T}_{{\mathbf{m}}}|^{q} \frac{|\mathbf{n}|}{(|\mathbf{n}|)_{q|{\mathbf{m}}|-q+1}} \prod_{i\geq 0} (n(i))_{qm(i)},
