{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.557360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd6cb20cce4f6bade8f3fcb19054015cb54f47100e788890cb42eaa95ec431f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 ({Thm.~\ref{t:WC}, \ref{p:PBE}, \ref{t:DFH}}) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] Suppose~\ref{ass:CE}, ~\ref{ass:ConditionalClos} and Assumption~\ref{ia:AP}.  
\begin{enumerate}[{\rm (a)}]

\item   $(${\bf  $\mssW_{p, \mssd_\U}$-contraction}$)$ Let $1 \le p <\infty$.  {Then, $\mcT_t^{\U, \QP} \nu$ is well-defined for $\nu \in \overline{\mcP_{\Theta}}^{\mssW_{p, \mssd_\U}}$. Furthermore, for $\nu, \sigma \in \overline{\mcP_{\Theta}}^{\mssW_{p, \mssd_\U}}$,}

