{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T07:38:10+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7f42fa6cce70728b6f738f882eb1c9265b6470f11903f06083059a131ed96a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4.5 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
\begin{align}

\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t;x,y)=p_t(x-y)\mbf E_B\left[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^{x,y}_t)>t\}}\exp\left(-\ka\int_0^t\xi_\eps\big(B^{x,y}_t(r)\big)\d r\right)\right],\qquad x,y\in D,
\end{align}
where we assume that $B^{x,y}_t$ and $\xi_\eps$ are independent, and we use $\mbf E_B$ to
denote the (conditional) expectation with respect to the randomness in $B$ only.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:35:59.927756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd7ffa204b911e9845e88c360f922479c247c784791976b794df9d216143c342","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 57 of arXiv:2608.26084, 'Localic Esakia Duality\\via Conic Frames'] For a localic relation~$R$ on a locale~$X$, its \emph{internal (down) cone} is defined as the function
