{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.061787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd8135fe9fa5fe9bb2007f7e5b9ae049227f667dd75f0420917f599e6d82c83b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Fractional Brownian motion of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] Let $H\in (0,1)$. Fractional Brownian motion with Hurst index $H$ is a real-valued Gaussian process $(Z_H(t))_{t\in [0,\infty)}$, where Hurst index, $H\in (0,1)$, such that $Z_H(0)=0$ almost surely and \\
\begin{align}
    E[Z_H(t)Z_H(s)]=\frac{1}{2}\{t^{2H}+s^{2H}-|t-s|^{2H}\},
\end{align}
for all $t,s\geq 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.871022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd836b7ebd7aa8393c5446c95110b6fb08d6f8dcbbdc274c4cc2090a3e9282ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Constant alternating regret for polyhedral OLO of arXiv:2608.24731, 'Optimal Alternating Regret for Online Learning and Games\thanks{Authors are alphabetically'] \label[corollary]{cor:polytope}
Let $\mathcal X=\operatorname{conv}\{\boldsymbol{v}_1,\ldots,\boldsymbol{v}_N\}$ be a  polytope. Consider  linear losses $f_t(\boldsymbol{x})=\langle \boldsymbol{c}_t,\boldsymbol{x}\rangle$, with $f_t(\boldsymbol{x})\in[-1,1]$ for every $\boldsymbol{x}\in\+X$. Running (alg:main of the paper) with $\mu$ being the uniform distribution on $\{\boldsymbol{v}_1,\ldots,\boldsymbol{v}_N\}$ gives
\[
  \max_{\boldsymbol{u}\in\mathcal X}\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(\boldsymbol{u})\le8\log N.
\]
In particular, for $\mathcal X=\Delta_d$ and $\boldsymbol{c}_t\in[-1,1]^d$, (alg:main of the paper) coincides with (alg:variance hedge of the paper) and recovers the bound $8\log d$.","status":"unverified"}

