 for any bounded $\F_t$-measurable functional $F_t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.806561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd86deab767a29ee00826769dab5701bbaafb04a31429395e6ebb6c1b6823ecc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:4th-power-I2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the term $\mathcal{I}_2$ be defined in equation (equation E:LLn-4th-power of the paper). Then, for the solutions $\Phi(x,y)$ and $\Xi(x,y)$ of Poisson equations (equation E:I2-Poisson-Eq of the paper), we have the following representation of $\mathcal{I}_2:$
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
 \mathcal{I}_2 & =   \int_0^t e^{2\alpha s} (X_s^\varepsilon- \bar{X}_s) \mathscr{L}_y \Phi(X_s^\varepsilon, Y_s^\eta) \thinspace ds \\
&  = \eta e^{2 \alpha t} (X_t^\varepsilon- \bar{X}_t)\Phi(X_t^\varepsilon, Y_t^\eta)  - \eta \int_0^t 2 \alpha e^{2 \alpha s} (X_s^\varepsilon- \bar{X}_s)\Phi(X_s^\varepsilon, Y_s^\eta) \thinspace ds \\
