{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.169701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd8edec4897bb116c85dff16bc0652eb14a7f4cc66580e5bd8a3111aadde7fb1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 (Global Maximality of $u_\varepsilon$) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. If $Z:[0,T]\times H\to \mathbb{R}$ is a mild sub-solution of the variational inequality in the sense of Definition \ref{def:mild_subsolutions}, then for any penalization parameter $\varepsilon > 0$, the unique mild solution $u_\varepsilon$ to the penalized backward equation \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized} satisfies:
