{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.852364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd9d9331b3f3da4aa9e2b48612497049b345e49cac3bad0df440b48d7ef2a4c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def bousfield-lattice of arXiv:2608.26876, 'Local Bousfield classes via homological support'] Let $\cat T$ be a well generated tensor-triangulated category. The set of homological Bousfield classes $\BL(\cat T)$ is a complete lattice when ordered by reverse inclusion:
	\[
	  \mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\le \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\ \Longleftrightarrow\ \mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\supseteq \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}.
	\]
	The top and bottom elements are $\mathinner{\left\langle \unit \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}=\{0\}$ and $\mathinner{\left\langle 0 \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}=\cat T$ respectively. The join is given by
	\begin{equation}
		\bigvee\SETT{\mathinner{\left\langle A_i \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}}{i \in I} = 
		\big\langle\hspace{-0.2ex}
		\coprod\nolimits_{i \in I} \hspace{-0.2ex}A_i \big\rangle_*
	\end{equation}
	and the meet is given by 
	\begin{equation}
		\bigwedge\SETT{\mathinner{\left\langle A_i \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}}{i\in I} = \bigvee\SETT{\mathinner{\left\langle X \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}}{\mathinner{\left\langle X \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \le \mathinner{\left\langle A_i \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \text{ for all } i \in I}.
	\end{equation}
	In general, the meet operation $\mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \meet \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}$ is different from $\mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \otimes \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \coloneqq \mathinner{\left\langle A \otimes B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}$ although we always have $\mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \otimes \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\leq \mathinner{\left\langle A \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \meet \mathinner{\left\langle B \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}$. For example, the Brown--Comenetz dual of the sphere $I\in {\mathscr{S}p}$ satisfies $I \otimes I = 0$; see [HoveyPalmieri99]. Hence $\mathinner{\left\langle I \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}\otimes \mathinner{\left\langle I \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} = \mathinner{\left\langle 0 \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}$ but $\mathinner{\left\langle I \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *} \meet \mathinner{\left\langle I \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}=\mathinner{\left\langle I \right\rangle}_{\mkern-2mu *}$ in $\BL({\mathscr{S}p})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.901845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd9e1b0b087a5550520f31c4abe32bfcd621e601b5e5caec3fe631f5e44fc7ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] Let $g\in\cp_{2,2}$ satisfying the following assumptions:
