{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.747523+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cda04d16c6fdbe7739db4259e84308609faa38edcc9795062e20fb6308bebf4b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma pmf of x+y of arXiv:2603.09008, 'On the statistics of random-to-top shuffles'] Let $X\sim\operatorname{Poisson}(a)$ and let $Y$ be geometric with $P(Y=k)=a(1-a)^k$. Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are independent. Then, we have 
