\ge
\Pr\mleft(\eta(A)\ge\eta_0\mright)
-\sqbrac{3n\lg\frac{3R}{\eta_0} + 3\lg\frac{2\eta_0}{\tau_0}}
\cdot\frac{\E\vol\Lambda_\varepsilon(A)}{\tau_0\cdot\varepsilon^2}
-\Pr\mleft(\left\|A\right\|>R\mright).}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.076230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cda937f846db612179c5bfe653bafb40d2a3050cbc47bc736db2b7d5c97b9a88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:reg-hat-V of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Assume the conditions of Lemma (le:sLND-hat-U of the paper) hold. Then the 
Gaussian random field $\{\hat V_t(x), x\in\mathbb{R}^d\} $ is well-defined and there exists a finite constant $C > 0$ such that 
for all $t >0$ and  $x,y\in\mathbb{R}^d$ with $|x-y|\le e^{-1}$,   
  \begin{equation*}
    \begin{split}
       &\mathbb E\left[ \big|\hat V_t(x)-\hat V_t(y)\big|^2 \right] \\
         &\qquad\le
    \begin{cases}
      C\:t^{2H_0+2\gamma-2}\times|x-y|^{2\alpha-2d+2H}, & \mbox{if } 0<\alpha-d+H<1, \\
       C\:t^{2H_0+2\gamma-2}\times|x-y|^2 \log\left(|x-y|^{-1}\right), & \mbox{if } \alpha-d+H=1, \\
      C\:t^{2\beta+2\gamma+2H_0-2-\frac{\beta(2d-2H+2)}{\alpha}}\times|x-y|^2, & \mbox{if } \alpha-d+H>1.
    \end{cases}
    \end{split}
  \end{equation*}
Consequently, the function $x\mapsto \hat V_t(x)$ is smoother than $x\mapsto \hat U_t(x)$ on $\mathbb{R}^d$.","status":"unverified"}

