{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.505030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdc6a8d3a5d83293fc4b59be20dfe05fff19cf5717692f11af63789e4aa7e2cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm.zador of arXiv:2505.15283, 'Quantization of Probability Distributions via Divide-and-Conquer: Convergence and Error Pr'] Suppose ${\mathbb{E}}[|X|^{1+\delta}]<\infty$ for some $\delta>0$ and assume that the distribution of $X$, denoted by $\mu$, is absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure with density $f$. 
