    where $\sum_{i=1}^5\epsilon_i=0$. \qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.573591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdd2c568ed82da60acbe3d252b796027aeabebfdf0f09f239b5978f0d768455c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2606.14564, 'Upper tails for irregular graphs \\ beyond the mean-field regime'] Suppose that $p \ll 1$ and let $G \subseteq K_n$ be a graph with $O(f \log(1/p))$ edges.
  Suppose further that either $\eps_H = \infty$ or $\eps_H < \infty$ and $p \gg n^{-1/\Delta - \eps_H} (\log(1/p))^K$ for some large constant $K$ that depends only on $H$.
  Then
  \begin{equation*}
    \Ex_G[X]-\Ex[X] \leq \sum_{J\in \cJ} \frac{|\Emb(J,H)|}{|\Aut(H)|} \cdot N(J,G)\cdot n^{v_H-v_J}p^{e_H-e_J}+o(n^{v_H}p^{e_H}).
  \end{equation*}
  Furthermore, if $p \le n^{-1/\Delta-\Omega(1)}$, then
  \[
    \Ex_G[X]-\Ex[X] \leq \sum_{J\in \cJ^*} \frac{|\Emb(J,H)|}{|\Aut(H)|} \cdot N(J,G)\cdot n^{v_H-v_J}p^{e_H-e_J}+o(n^{v_H}p^{e_H}).
  \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.370421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdd4f9efcb07c0b0b4e60eabab82951a593fd3c1d57f90ab91266152498c7572","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def: HeightOffset of arXiv:2411.13465, 'Height-offset variables and pinning at infinity for gradient Gibbs measures on trees'] A function $H: \Omega \rightarrow \mathbb{R} \cup \{\pm \infty\}$ is called a \underline{height-offset variable} for a gradient Gibbs measure $\nu$ iff it fulfills the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}[a)]
\item For all $a \in \mathbb{Z}$ we have $H(\tau_{-a}(\omega))= H(\omega)+a$ for all $\omega \in \Omega$;
\item $H$ is measurable with respect to the tail-$\sigma$-algebra $\mathcal{T}$ on $\Omega$;
\item $\nu( \vert H \circ\sigma^{x,s}  \vert <\infty)=1$ for some site $x\in V$ and some 
integer height $s\in \mathbb{Z}$.

\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.963299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdd683c1cdf75de18ecd8b4cf993a04f49b4c679cde3fd3a53988f01a70cae6c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:function_G of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C \in \mathcal{C}_{ar}^d$ be an Archimedean copula and $\psi$ and $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d}$ be its corresponding generator and Williamson measure, respectively. Then
