    holds for every $z > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.633273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdd8fe47079486045db22edcf26154606372677d242da29c01a3774c3c9fa2cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2506.17061, 'Non-uniform bounds for non-normal approximation via Stein's method with applications to th'] Let $z\ge 5$ and $|u| \le 100$. Then
