{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.849471+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdf00fc46e93da56cf5b3e3a820f11f69b6610d46e85a9bb2ef201d62e998355","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let $A \in \mathcal{M}_{n,m}(\mathbb{R})$. Then $B = A^+$ if and only if	
						\begin{enumerate}		
							\item  $ABA = A$,\\[-4ex]
							\item $BAB = B$,\\[-4ex]
							\item $(AB)^\top = AB$,\\[-4ex]
							\item $(BA)^\top = BA$.		
						\end{enumerate}
						Furthermore, $A^+$ always exists and is unique (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.896256+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdf01a2e2602076f89d9a3cc672148ec0c7b5e415286783c3dc1d4ee0ee3d024","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 46 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$w=w_{\ell x'+i',2y'+j'}$ and~$b=b_{\ell x+i,2y+j}$ be non-boundary vertices in the reduced Aztec diamond. 

The Coulomb gauge functions~$\mathcal F^\bullet$ and~$\mathcal F^\circ$ defined in Proposition~\ref{prop:FG} are given by
\begin{equation*}
 \mathcal F^\bullet(b)=
\frac{1}{2\pi\i}\int_{\tilde \Gamma}\left(f(z)Q(z,w)
  \prod_{m=1}^{2i}\phi_m(z)\right)_{j+1}(z-1)^{\ell N}\frac{w^{x-N}}{z^{y}}\frac{\d z}{z},
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation}
\mathcal F^\circ(w)
=\frac{1}{2\pi\i}\int_{\tilde \Gamma}\left(\left(\prod_{m=1}^{2i'+1}\phi_m(z)\right)^{-1}Q(z,w)
  g(z)
  \right)_{j'+1} \frac{z^{y'}}{(z-1)^{\ell N}w^{x'-N}}\d z,
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}
f(z)=\sqrt{a+\i}\left(-\frac{\i\alpha_1}{z-1}
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & -\alpha_1^{-1}
\end{pmatrix}
-\frac{\beta_\ell a}{z-1}
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & \beta_\ell^{-1}
\end{pmatrix}
\right)
=\frac{\sqrt{a+\i}\left(\i-a\right)}{z-1}
\begin{pmatrix}
\i\sqrt{\alpha_1\beta_\ell} & 1
\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
g(z)=\sqrt{a-\i}\left(\frac{\i}{\sqrt{\alpha_1\beta_\ell}}\frac{1}{z}
\begin{pmatrix}
 1 \\
 0
\end{pmatrix}
+
\begin{pmatrix}
  0 \\
  1
\end{pmatrix}
\right)
\end{equation}

and~$\tilde \Gamma=\tilde \Gamma_s$ is as in Lemma~\ref{lem:bdry_bulk}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.352532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdf384cf93aaeffa1c3bfdfd525b51902b945e8d75e5e3f147cc4782fc2066d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2607.27932, '2607.27932'] For $\underline{H}_0$ and $\mathcal M_0$ as in Theorem \ref{thm:main1}, and for any $N$ large enough, $1\le i\le N$ and $\delta>0$, it holds that
	\begin{equation*}
