{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.047015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce3278daf4cf1e30592e7d66d26724db16341da4f911094d58d8d13726c80c9c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] Suppose $\sup_{ f \in \mathcal F } ||f||_{\infty} < \infty$ and, for each $n$, there exists:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item A partition
		\(\mathcal P_n=\{B_1,\ldots,B_{M_n}\}\) of \(N_n\), with
		\(\max_m |B_m|\le q_n\), and an associated \(r_n\)-coloring,
		\item A  finite partition of \(\mathcal F\), \(T_{L_{n}}\)
	\end{itemize}
	such that for some $a,b$
	\begin{align}
		\left( \frac{
			\sqrt{ K_{r_{n}}}	}{\sqrt n}  \max_{m\in[M_n]}\Gamma_p(B_m)    \right)   2^{\frac{\lceil a L_{n} \rceil}{2}}  \to 0 ~and~	\left(  \frac{K_{r_{n}}  q_n}{n}
		+	\bar{\tau}_{\operatorname{cone} \Pi[T_{L_{n}}]  ,G_n}
		\left( 	\mathcal P_{n}, 	\mathcal C_{r_{n}}[\mathcal P_{n} ] \right)    \right)   2^{\lceil b L_{n} \rceil}   \to 0, 	
	\end{align}
	and
	\begin{align}
		\frac{1}{n}
		\sum_{i\in N_n}
		\mathbb E 	\left[  \sup_{C\in T_{L_n}} D_C(Z_i) \right] \to 0,

	\end{align}
	as $n \to \infty$. Then \(  (\mathcal F,G_{n}) \) is graph Glivenko--Cantelli, i.e.,
	\begin{align}
		\sup_{f\in\mathcal F}
		\left| \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i \in N_{n}} \{ f(Z_{i}) - \mathbb E[f(Z_{i})]   \}  \right|
		=
		o_{\mathbb P}(1).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.675353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce35341ad244321602f92c5afdb0b21bc49d53ab746625285b8a2bcf06e4c92e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Delay blow up-NS of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Let $\frac{1}{4}\leq a<\frac{1}{2}<2b+a$ and $\nu>0$. Fix $R_0>0$ and $0<\epsilon<1$, then there exists $N_0=N_0(\nu,R_0,\epsilon)$, such that for all $N>N_0$ and initial data $u_0$ satisfying 
