    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.185837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce7dbb4d69da05d5332bd01ed1f3df4f72374d98dc100d65718fe2109f903643","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:trel of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] There is a number $\lambda>0$, called the \red[spectral gap], such that
