{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.776194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce7fe4d36ac62729c574edcc34c360fc2c36a3e69877dc4660c289afde951e20","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 32 of arXiv:2608.26816, '\textbf{On the existence of maximal foliations in general relativity}'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{maxfol}, if the following holds at time $t=0$ for some $k\geq 2$:   
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{i=0}^{k}||\nabla^i \bar{R}m||^2_{L^2(M_0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}||\nabla^i h ||^2_{L^2(M_0)}< \infty,
\end{equation}

then there exists  $\Lambda_k>0$ depending only  on the initial data $(g_0,h_0)$ such that   for any $t>0$, we have 
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 \sum_{i=0}^{k}||\nabla^i \bar{R}m||^2_{L^2(M_t)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}||\nabla^i h ||^2_{L^2(M_t)} \leq \Lambda_k.
 \end{split}
 \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.385261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce80204ad8651c8b3854535d01c0f6edb44dac1f9a0b9b24dc3601bee6d20963","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] Let $b\geq 2$ and $\rho\geq 1$ be integers. Then the sequence
