         \mathsf{S}^2,\quad k\in \IZ.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.988628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce99f56a928bcf1729079b85d47da2d2f986a0b75bdc5f48bcc04751a0e9e16a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:herm_pieri of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] For any $\nu \in \Sig_n, \mu \in \Sig_{n-1}$ and $D$ large enough so that all $n$-tuples below are valid signatures, 
    \begin{equation}
        c_{(D,0[n-1]),\nu}^{\her,(2D+|\nu|-|\mu|,\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{n-1})}(t) = \sum_{\kappa \in \Sig_{n-1}} P_{\nu/\kappa}(1;-t)Q_{\mu/\kappa}(-1;-t),
    \end{equation}
    where $c_{\mu,\nu}^{\her,\lambda}(t)$ is as defined in (equation eq:def_herm_lr of the paper) {\color{green} \sf $\clubsuit$ Roger's comment: [when that's in a def environment, change eqref to ref to def]}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.208906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce9a89263995b566817adc4d63519742dc6a0cb9f26fa3bcaa5dff1cc2cbbb16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.13677, 'Asymptotically complete free-energy dissipation: \\ a coarse MLSI holds at any positive te'] \label[lemma]{lemma:computation_flip_density}
    Suppose \(\sigma(\mu) < \infty\), or even just \(\mu \ll \mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1}\) (or, equivalently, \(\mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1} \ll \mu\)).
    Then, for \(\mu\)-a.e. \(\eta\) and all \(x \in \Lambda_n\), we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\d \mu_{\Lambda_n \vert \Lambda_n^c}(\cdot \vert \eta) }{\d (\mu_{\Lambda_n \vert \Lambda_n^c}(\cdot \vert \eta) \circ \mathrm{flip}_x^{-1})}(\eta_{\Lambda_n})
        = \frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}(\mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1})}(\theta_{x}\eta),
    \end{align*} where \(\theta_x\) means translation by \(x\), i.e., \((\theta_x \eta)_y = \eta_{y+x}\) for all \(y \in \Z^d\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.507260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce9b369563626300df6a2d7563fcb91dd3233f09e1edd4b0a35a4ba060116326","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 (decay of the $A$-tensor and of the base curvature) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Let $A$ denote the O'Neill tensor of the extended submersion $\widehat{\pi} : \widehat{M} \to N$ of \S\ref{subsec:oneill} (including its symmetric part, i.e. the full second fundamental form of the splitting $T\widehat{M} = \mathcal{V} \oplus \mathcal{H}$; recall $T \equiv 0$ by Proposition \ref{prop:2.5}). Then there is $C = C ( g_0, T )$ with

	\begin{equation}
		\big| A \big|^2_{g(t)} \;\leq\; \frac{C}{T - t} \qquad \text{on } \widehat{M} \times [0, T) \,,
	\end{equation}

	and the same bound holds for the sectional curvatures of horizontal planes of $g(t)$ and for those of the evolving base metric $\check{g}_t = \sum_i f_i^2\, g_i$. Consequently, along the Type II rescaling,

	\begin{equation}
		\big| A \big|^2_{g_j(t)} \;=\; K_j^{-1}\, \big| A \big|^2_{g ( t_j + K_j^{-1} t )} \;\leq\; \frac{C}{K_j ( T - t_j ) - t} \;\longrightarrow\; 0 \qquad ( j \to \infty ) \,,
	\end{equation}

	locally uniformly in $t \in \mathbb{R}$, and likewise for the rescaled horizontal and base sectional curvatures: a Type II blow-up sees a flat base and an integrable, totally geodesic horizontal distribution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.078016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce9c672eb5c8e809739cea0ff30d8dbee08273fe61db599642b6f9e194554a28","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 33 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] For every $\ell\in\NN$, every $\vec{r}\in\NN^\ell$, we have 
