{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.633390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ced3294c84efd653e44fb185e660c785a4a47862e2054086c42d9175d9f7bbc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:d3-general of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let $\ell\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $0\leq u_1\leq\ldots\leq u_{\ell}$. There exists a coupling of $(n^{-1/\beta}\eta(n\cdot))_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ and $\gamma$ such that $(n^{-1/\beta}\eta(n\cdot))_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ converges almost surely to $\gamma$ in $(\mathcal{C},\chi)$ and for all $u_i$,
