    \qquad
    F_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}
    =
    \lim_{L\to\infty}F_{\xi,d,n,L}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}
\]
exists, the other exists as well, and
\[
    F_{\xi,d}^{\mathrm{post}}
    =
    F_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}
    +
    D_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{post}}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.703225+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ced9e9cfba64caa4fe0df8e17fa6d6fd7ba97c0b6801b328ce66a71ef5bbba74","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th_hydrodynamics of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] {(Hydrodynamic Limit)}
Let $\gamma: [0,1] \rightarrow [0,1]$  {be a measurable function and $(\nu_N)_{N \geq 1}$ a }sequence of probability measures on $\Omega_N$ which are associated to the initial profile $\gamma$. Then,  {for every $G \in C([0,1])$, every $t \in [0,T]$ and every $\delta > 0$,}
