{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.880228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cede1b741fdfa3691222f99a933aa40cffeca221e1297cb370c267a5b98bf98b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.02478, 'Improved Weyl bounds on short intervals'] Under the hypotheses of \cref{prop:orbit-collision}, let $x\ne y$ satisfy \eqref{eq:centre-collision}, and put $h=x-y$.  Then, if $\delta=\delta(k)$ is sufficiently small, there are integers $r,v_2,\ldots,v_k$ such that
