{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.118651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cedf4b0be9a075522082e04fdd6cd9cfd148bcec05f54242d86a4720adbb571f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Let~$\hat\epsilon, \eta, a$ be as in Lemma~\ref{l:lyapunov}.  Then, for all~$\epsilon \le \hat\epsilon$ and all~$h$ satisfying~$0<h/\epsilon^2 \le \eta$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \gap(\hat P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})}) \geq 2^{-4} \gap(\bar P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})})\,.
    \end{equation}
    Here, $\bar P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})}$ denotes the restriction of the chain $\bar P_{h,\epsilon}$ to $B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})$, where $\bar P_{h,\epsilon}$ is Metropolis random walk with step size~$h$ and the normal stationary distribution~$N(m_1, \epsilon D^2 U(m_1)^{-1})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.353669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cee4100f2a16c0e185c6e29a822647a68a3e81930b6b85d0a930a16eeabf46c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.vnupperbound of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $p > 4$, there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that for all $n \in {\mathbb N}$, $k_0 \in \{0,1,\dots,n\}$, and $\bm{x} \in {\mathbb R}^n$, we have
