        \mathcal{V}^n(k_0,\bm{x}) \leq \mathcal{U}_p(k_0/n, m_{\bm{x}}^n) + C_p n^{\frac{1}{2p} - \frac{1}{4}}.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.288704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cee451e42d17a92cc0226de842afbd6d962d09935a484dece25e3bb1a2a98306","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem qh1 of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $q>1$, there exists a positive constant $\widehat{C}_0$ which does not depend on $\Delta$ such that, for any $t>0$, 
\begin{align}

	\mathbb{E} \left[\left|\widehat{X}_{\underline{t}}\right|^q\right] \le 4 ^{q-1}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[|\widehat{X}_t|^q\right] +\widehat{C}_0 \right).
