{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.371576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cee8121ca9eaac0a83fb2890164581ff70b09c315d542c17227464b4218d7093","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] Let $\phi:\R^d\to\R$ be a $C^{1}$ function such that 
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item $\Omega=\phi^{-1}(0,\infty)$ is pre-compact,
			\item $|\nabla\phi|$ is bounded away from $0$ in a neighborhood of $\partial\Omega$. 
		\end{enumerate}
		For any $r>0$, define $\Omega_r=\phi^{-1}(r,\infty)$. Then, 
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{r\to 0}\mathcal{H}^{d-1}(\partial\Omega_r)=\mathcal{H}^{d-1}(\partial\Omega)
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.724482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceec619eec494f12508d7b39682e8b5fe7a9db012a1d5d05e3bf8bb9fc95fd47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem4new of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Fix $T >0$,  $\lambda=(\lambda_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}_0}$, and  $\mu\in \mathcal B$ such that
$$(\lambda_0\mu_0,\lambda_1\mu_1,\lambda_2\mu_2,\ldots)\in \mathcal{S}^*.$$
Assume that
$$\mathcal A (\lambda_k\frac{(\cdot)^k}{k!})(x)=\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})+\beta_k\lambda_k\frac {x^k}{k!}$$
for some $\beta_{kj}\in \mathbb R_+$ and $\beta_k\in \mathbb R$ such that $\sup_{k\geq 0}\beta_k^+<\infty$ and $\lim_{j\to\infty}\beta_{kj}=0$ for each $k\in \mathbb{N}_0$. 
If for all $x\in (-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)$ the sequence 
\begin{equation}
\Big(\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!},\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})\Big)_{k\in\mathbb{N}_0}
\end{equation}
lies in the bounded pointwise closure of 
\begin{equation*}
\Big\{\Big(\mathbf{a}_k,\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\mathbf{a}_j-\mathbf{a}_k)\Big)_{k\in \mathbb{N}_0}\colon \mathbf{a}=(\mathbf{a}_k)_{k=0}^N,\quad N\in \mathbb{N}\Big\},
\end{equation*}
then the linear ODE given by (equation eq:ODE sequence space holomorphic of the paper) admits a solution $({\bf c}(t))_{t\in[0,T]}$ satisfying (equation eq: ODE pointwise of the paper) for each $x\in S$ of the form  ${\bf c}_k(t)=\lambda_k\mu_k(t)$ for some $\mu_k(t)\geq0$. If $\beta_k\leq 0$ for each $k$, then  $\sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k(t)\leq \sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.563685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceefcaf4a54c0b4498ac0fbd6ec8e31d53bf639007c566c9cf6c7e7453c71ab3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (The $m$th-order Santal\'o inequality on $\R^n$) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Fix $Q\in\conbodo[m].$ Let $K\subset \R^n$ be a compact set of positive volume such that $K$ or $K^\circ$ has center of mass at the origin. Then,
  \begin{equation}
  \Vol(K^{\star,Q})\vol(K)^m \leq \vol(\B)^m \Vol((B_2^n)^{\star,Q}).

\end{equation}
There is equality if and only if $K=E$ for some centered ellipsoid $E\subset\R^n$ up to removal of null sets. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.980206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef0c7d8e07cb6fc9759bcfeb4272fe79a5ccd070635881dfd512a862da6927c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eqn|CatsAndDogs of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] If $n$ and $k$ are non-negative integers, and $A$ an integer such that $n+A\in[0,k+n]$, the following holds
\begin{eqnarray}
\sum_{i=\max\{0,A\}}^{\min\{k,n+A\}} \binom ki\cdot\binom{n}{n+A-i}&=&\binom{n+k}{n+A}. 
\end{eqnarray}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.776011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef17bc8767d4faf1ecd75f5a0a58aecb650beae6d293a8b2a6ee91580f43b50","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $(\XX,\norm{\cdot})$ be a quasi-normed space with modulus of concavity $C_2 \ge 1$.
    Assume that $\SC$ satisfies {\ConditionZetaTextAlphaC{(\alpha,C_0)}} for some constants $\alpha, C_0>0$.
    Let $s\ge0$, $t\in \RR$ (with $t>0$ if $s=0$), and let $c_1>0$. 
    Let $(\SC_n)_{n\in\NN}$ be a sequence of finite $2^{-n}$-separated subsets $\SC_n \subset \SC$,
    and let $n_0\in \NN$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \num\SC_n \ge \exp\bigl( c_1 \cdot 2^{ns}n^{t}\bigr)
        \quad \text{for all $n\ge n_0$.}

    \end{equation}
    Then the measure $\mu$ given in \cref{definition_measure_SC_n} satisfies the following:
    There exist $r_0>0$ and $c>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \om{\mu}\bigl(\ball(x,r)\bigr) 
        \le \exp\biggl( - c  
        \cdot \Bigl(\frac{1}{r}\Bigr)^{s} \cdot \Bigl( \log_2 \Bigl(\frac{1}{r}\Bigr)\Bigr)^{t-\alpha s}\biggr)

    \end{equation}
    for all $r\in (0,r_0)$ and all $x\in \XX$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.608486+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef3d0fe6682d1e6b34f6743ebfed3de4cb8c9e166813ec76faaa5e584321de0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2609.00884, 'The weakness of typicality'] \label[theorem]{thm:gl-genericity}
For every~$n \geq 1$, the following class is co-meager:
