	\end{equ}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.706195+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef9951e88dc8ef513a61f1a667888b96f9b4756deb5bad12d850a5432f5897e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Revesz of arXiv:2604.10214, 'Large deviations for maximum local time of simple random walk in dimensions \texorpdfstrin'] There exists a constant $C_d>0$ such that
\begin{align}
{\mathbb P}\big(x\in S[0,\infty)\big)=\frac{C_d+o(1)}{\left\lvert x \right\rvert^{d-2}},
\qquad \text{as }\left\lvert x \right\rvert\to\infty.
