{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.320037+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf01dc58d7e5bfba0fbc869314a49c5180aef5414d6aa4b9fc70f36d6ffae677","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 4 of arXiv:2506.21087, 'Quasi-Stationary Distributions of Interacting Dynamical Systems and their approximation'] Assume \ref{condhzero}, \ref{condhun}, \ref{condhdeux} and \ref{condhtrois}. Assume  that  $(\mu_n)_{n\ge1}$ is $a.s.$ tight on ${\cal P}(\MM)$ and that $(\gamma_n)$ satisfies \eqref{hyp:pas}. Then,
