{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.923485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf3587018d2464704d0bb16dfc97d7abeb6fec7bc796b7452c1b7d661589a22b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2412.02087, 'The spectral distribution of random graphs with given degree sequences'] Suppose $p^3 \ll D$, $1\leq i\leq p$, and  $S\subseteq [i-1]$ is an arbitrary subset. Then, the following bound on the Fourier coefficient can be achieved
