{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.339891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf49cb2208a0b051682e283c305a5bcd1b9dcd8b0f30c867cd0ce02785de2d28","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propoAiry: any q potential of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Let $K_q$ be the fundamental solution of (equation eqAiry: Airy PDE with q of the paper). There exist numerical constants $\varepsilon_\star,\mathcal{E}_\star,\Lambda_\star>0$ with the following properties.

