{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.961415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf526a886d26691968192744884443e019f1c993b81f81fecd95629185e76db3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 ({\cite{BollobasRiordan,EggemannNoble,SubgraphsPAM}}) of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] Let $m\ge2$ be a fixed integer and $\delta> -m$ be a fixed real number. Let $T_n$ be the number of triangles in $\pam(m,\delta)$. Then
