{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.794658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf6c7c2e1f9e2232f738d7ec027f4e01c5efa9544784fa2a5bdc32084d8d75e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.10051, 'Ergodicity of the voter model with dynamic anti-voter bonds'] Fix an arbitrary $k \in \N$, a graph~$G$ and a function~$Q$ satisfying~\eqref{Q_def_adoption_rw}. Then, the voter model with dynamic anti-voter bonds $(\eta_t,\zeta_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with adoption rate~$Q$ and environment parameters~$p$ and~$\mathsf v$, and the Markov chain~$(\mathbf Y_t,\mathbf i_t,A_t,B_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with matrix rate~$Q_\mathrm{crw}(p,\mathsf v,k,Q)$ are dual with respect to the function~$D = D_k:\Omega \times \mathcal S_k \to \R$ defined as
