{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.211098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cffb08888a4b13b1602eed4abd74e7b98244385bdc9725e55f2f01e20b8d0899","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2604.27485, 'On large deviation principles for general random processes \footnote{Research supported by'] In the general case, the l.d.p.\ always implies the l.l.d.p. Con\-versely, let the following condition be met: for any $N>0$ there exists a $v>0$ such that 
