	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d002224e4f9a16032eb0361e1cebf4cfc43ed0c72868e797a2e2dbc2c0956591","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition error4d of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $R'_{n-1,N}(s)$ and $R'_{n,N-1}(s)$ be the error terms given in (equation a4D of the paper), then
