{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.745700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0042e970e3fdd677260b34d5ca57b5c60232682f3218fedaf5a6e46aa98e2ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn GibbsDefinition of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] Let $N \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{\infty\}$. We say that a line ensemble $\mathcal{L}\in \mathrm{C}(\llbracket 1, N \rrbracket)$ satisfies the Gibbs resampling property with respect to the law of the $\mathsf{A}$-bridge if for all $\llbracket \ell,\ell+k-1 \rrbracket \subset \llbracket 1, N \rrbracket$ with $\ell, k \ge 1$ and any $[a,b]\in \mathbb{R}_+$ we have
\begin{equation}
\mathsf{Law}\left(\mathcal{L}|_{\llbracket \ell,\ell+k-1 \rrbracket \times [a,b]}|\mathscr{F}_{\mathrm{ext}}\left(\llbracket \ell, \ell+k-1 \rrbracket \times (a,b) \right)\right)=\mathbf{P}_{\mathrm{avoid}}^{a,b;\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y};u,l},\ \ \textnormal{ almost surely,}
\end{equation}
where the external sigma-algebra $\mathscr{F}_{\mathrm{ext}}\left(\llbracket \ell, \ell+k-1 \rrbracket \times (a,b) \right)$ is defined as
\begin{equation}
\mathscr{F}_{\mathrm{ext}}\left(\llbracket \ell, \ell+k-1 \rrbracket \times (a,b) \right)= \sigma\left(\mathcal{L}_j(t);(j,t)\notin \llbracket \ell, \ell+k-1 \rrbracket\times (a,b)\right), 
\end{equation}
and the (random) boundary data $\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},u,l$ given by,
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{x}=\left(\mathcal{L}_\ell(a),\mathcal{L}_{\ell+1}(a),\dots,\mathcal{L}_{k+\ell-1}(a)\right), \  \mathbf{y}=\left(\mathcal{L}_{\ell}(b),\mathcal{L}_{\ell+1}(b),\dots,\mathcal{L}_{k+\ell-1}(b)\right), \ u=\mathcal{L}_{\ell-1},  \ l=\mathcal{L}_{\ell+k},
\end{align*}
with the convention $\mathcal{L}_{0}\equiv \infty$, $\mathcal{L}_{N+1}\equiv -\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d004953ce7f14c09eef204c1bb95f68ea2b5bbae27f86a4e71fea63fc0d5951b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem le:Lp_concentration of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $p\in \mathbf{N}^*$. There exists some constant $C = C(p)$ such that for any $j, N \geq 1$ and $t > 0$\,, we have
