{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.399766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d02cff6d571b65c0ce9788edc8bc0f317dde77e84a3316f84fda3fe53b82350f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 9 of arXiv:2608.31054, 'Revisiting Picard's proof of the Picard--Weber--Weck selection theorem'] Let $\Omega\subseteq \R^d$ be a global Lipschitz domain and $\Phi\colon Q\to \Omega$ be an admissible transformation. Writing $J_\Phi := \Grad(\Phi)$ and $\tilde{u} := u \circ \Phi$, the following assertions hold.

    (a)
    Let $  u \in H_0(\Rot;\Omega)$. Then 
    $J_\Phi^\top \widetilde{  u} \in H_0(\Rot;Q)$ and
    \begin{equation*}
        \Rotcirc_Q{(J_\Phi^\top \widetilde{  u})} 
        =  J_\Phi^\top\,\widetilde{\Rotcirc_\Omega   u}\,J_\Phi =: ( J_\Phi^\top \otimes J_\Phi^\top )\widetilde{\Rotcirc_\Omega   u}.
    \end{equation*}

    (b)  Let $  u \in H(\div;\Omega)$. Then $(\adjugate J_\Phi) \widetilde{  u} \in H(\div;Q)$ and
    \begin{align*}
        \div_Q{( (\adjugate J_\Phi) \widetilde{  u})} 
        = (\det{J_\Phi})\widetilde{\div_\Omega   u}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.188227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d035d53bd1999872ed5a48de1aacd20bcf214645927fd1ff71c9be10672a0221","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Rank-one perturbations preserve the product condition but destroy cutoff of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] Consider a model $(T_n)_{n\ge 1}$ which exhibits cutoff, and choose $(\theta_n)_{n\ge 1}$  in $(0,1)$ so that
\begin{eqnarray*}
\frac{1}{{\rm t}_{\textsc{mix}}^{(n)}} \ \ll \ {\theta_n} \ \ll \ \lambda_n.
\end{eqnarray*}
Then, the model $(\widetilde{T}_n)_{n\ge 1}$ produced by the rank-one perturbation ((def:bias of the paper)) satisfies
\begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{\lambda}_n  \sim \ \lambda_n,& \quad\textrm{and}\quad & 
\widetilde{{\rm t}}^{(n)}_{\textsc{mix}}(\varepsilon) \ \sim \ \frac{1}{\theta_n}\log\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right).
\end{eqnarray*}
In particular, $(\widetilde{T}_n)_{n\ge 1}$ still satisfies the product condition, but fails to exhibit cutoff.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.187888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d039fd3e6a334d6b91e37195a4b169f5ee4873e0ec51ba87e6c0e52fb4aba1da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumption~\ref{assump-particles} hold with $p>d$ and $\gamma\in (\frac{d}{p}, 1)$. If $d=3$, assume further that $\frac{\gamma}{2} + \frac{3}{2}(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{p}) <1$.
Then there exists $C = C(T,A,k,\gamma,p,d)>0$ such that for any $q \geq 1$,

\begin{equation*}
\sup_{N\in\N^*}   e^{-C T \sigma_{N}^{-2}} \, \Big(\mathbb{E}\Big[\sup_{t\in[0,T]} \left\Vert  u^N_{t} \right\Vert _{\gamma,p}^{q}\Big]\Big)^\frac{1}{q}  <\infty.
