{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.664061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d095fad30a95590205ee89f7be31400afbb08c974e75df78adca142ba9ec9092","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem monotonie of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] $(a)$ For every $\xi\!\in U$, $v\!\in S(0,1)$, the mapping $(t^-_{\xi,v}, t^+_{\xi,v}) \owns t \mapsto \phi_{_F}(\xi, \xi+t v)$ is decreasing on $(t^-_{\xi,v},0]$ and increasing on $[0,t^+_{\xi,v})$.

