{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.875542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0c02920da987c9cda8c17ac628b81a25c3a82a56a544493747ae1e968b2ddad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_area of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Let $f\colon[a,b]\to\mathbb{R}$ be continuous and convex.
Assume $\partial^+f(a)=s_a<s_b=\partial^-f(b)$, where at least one of $s_a,s_b$ is finite.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]

