{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.280085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0dea002e545f40ed8b6da6512010272cb65a772db411287abfc9a22802a38ba","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi \textbf{Allometric form} of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] We say that $\omega \in \mathcal{C}^{1}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$ has an \hypertarget{alloform}{allometric form} if there exists $0 \leq \kappa_{1} \leq \kappa_{2}$ with
