{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.117958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1380d97dfcf651c8d369524e0d27668bf607d1e535a22fe831899e6c9dac0b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] For any sufficiently large~$a$, there exist $\hat\epsilon (a), \eta, \hat  \gamma,\lambda > 0$ such that for all~$\epsilon, h, \gamma$ with
