{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.335666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d15bffbfdb128013444956060f684ad44ca8c5c0cf2e2f0b50848aad43b66cc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-busemann-tail of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let ${\operatorname{XDP}} \in \{\operatorname{LDP} , \operatorname{SDP}\}$ and let $\mathcal X$ be the Busemann function, as in Theorem~(thm-busemann of the paper). 
\begin{enumerate}[label=(v\alph*),ref=(v\alph*)]
 \item If ${\operatorname{XDP}} = \operatorname{LDP}$, then there is a constant $c_1 > 0$ such that as $x\to\infty$, 
\begin{align} 
&\mathbbm P\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \mathcal X(1) - \mathcal X(0) \leq -x \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] = c_1 \, x^{-2/3} + o(x^{-2/3}) ,\notag\\
&\mathbbm P\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ |\mathcal X(0) - \mathcal X(-1)| \geq x \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] = 2c_1 \, x^{-2/3} + o(x^{-2/3}) .
\end{align} 
 \item If ${\operatorname{XDP}} = \operatorname{SDP}$, then there is a constant $c_2 > 0$ such that as $x\to\infty$,
\begin{align} 
&\mathbbm P\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \mathcal X(1) - \mathcal X(0) \geq   x \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] = c_2 \, x^{-4/3} + o(x^{-4/3}),\notag\\  
&\mathbbm P\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ |\mathcal X(0) - \mathcal X(-1)| \geq x \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] = 2c_2 \, x^{-4/3} + o(x^{-4/3}) .
\end{align}  
Moreover, in this case $\mathbbm E[\mathcal X(k) - \mathcal X(k-1)] = 0$ for all $k\in\mathbbm Z$.  
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

