{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.712556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d168dea03dd8dba45a3103ce168a6b59bd546c0809c5f5dbc8b7fb6bb3053c5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tensorization of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $\varepsilon_0 \in (0, 1)$ and $B \ge 1$. Let $X_1, \dots, X_m$ be independent
 random variables such that each $X_i$ satisfies
\begin{align*}
\textbf{P}\left(|X_i| \le \varepsilon\right) \le B\varepsilon \quad \text{for all } \varepsilon \ge \varepsilon_0.
\end{align*}
