{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.813027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d16a2c7405af616885f64086a4038abfe843c5b02de541d4db561d6445ad5c59","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:length-dl of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] For any $s<t$ and any continuous path $\pi:[s,t]\to \mathbb{R}$, we define the \emph{length} of $\pi$ by
    \begin{align*}
        \int_s^t d\mathcal{L}\circ \pi \coloneqq  
        \inf_{k\in \mathbb{N}}
        \inf_{s=s_0 < s_1 < \cdots < s_k = t}
        \sum_{i=0}^{k-1} \mathcal{L}(s_i, \pi(s_i); s_{i+1}, \pi(s_{i+1})). 
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

