{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.786937+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d16b126e4692804e08aa7a4afe316210d6412857c0c2acbfc3de1f8711721331","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:basic of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $Q \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ be an isometric involution transition matrix. For $L \in \mathcal{L}(\pi,Q)$, we then have
