{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.831323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d17daefa419d04e038b0ea6a5154a3b833467249b1f37181bda6fc6f9cd8e6fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:upper_bounds of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] For any relative deviation $\delta > 0$ and corresponding absolute deviation $\varepsilon = \rho\delta > 0$:
  \begin{equation}
  \begin{gathered}
    \mathbb{P}(\bar{X} \ge \rho(1+\delta)) \le \exp\braces*{ -n \frac{\rho}{\Gamma} \frac{\delta^2}{2 + 2\delta/3} }, \\
    \mathbb{P}(\bar{X} \ge \rho + \varepsilon) \le \exp\braces*{ -\frac{n}{\Gamma} \frac{\varepsilon^2}{2 \rho + 2\varepsilon/3} }.
