where $\chi_{R}$ is defined by (\ref{eq:ChiR}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.352153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1a81bcc35b935b7f422b20c913c63ef6226ead34adc1a8024eb11adc444aaec","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem_fourmoment of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] In addition to the hypothesis of Proposition (prop_estimatecarreduchamp_kthderivative of the paper), let us assume further that $X$ is a {chaotic} eigenfunction of chaos grade $q$. Then,   we have the pointwise estimate with respect to $x\in \mathbb{R}$ for the densities of $F=X+\alpha$ and $\mathcal{Z}$.
\begin{align}
     &\abs{p_F(x)-p_\mathcal{Z}(x)}\nonumber \\
     &\leq \E{\frac{1}{S_1^3}}^{1/2}\E{\autobracket*{LQ_1}^2}^{1/4}\mathcal{M}(q)^{1/4}+\E{ \brac{\frac{2b_2F+b_1+F-m}{S_1b(F)}}^2}^{1/2}\mathcal{M}(q)^{1/2}\nonumber\\
&\qquad +\brac{\E{\mathcal{U}_2(0,x,F)^2}^{1/2}+\E{\mathcal{U}_4(0,F)^2}^{1/2}+\E{\mathcal{U}_6(0,F)^2}^{1/2} }\frac{1}{q^2}\mathcal{M}(q)^{1/2}.  
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{M}(q)$ is defined at (equation def_Mq of the paper). 

Moreover,  for any integer $k$ such that $1\leq k\leq N$, we have
\begin{align}
      &\abs{p_F^{(k)}(x)-p_\mathcal{Z}^{(k)}(x)}\nonumber \\
      &\leq   \brac{\E{\mathcal{U}_2(k,x,F)^2}^{1/2}+\E{\mathcal{U}_4(k,F)^2}^{1/2}+\E{\mathcal{U}_6(k,F)^2}^{1/2} }\frac{1}{q^2} \mathcal{M}(q)^{1/2}
 \nonumber     \\
     &\qquad +\sum_{P_{k+1}}\E{\abs{\frac{c\brac{i_1,i_2,i_3,i_4,j_1,\ldots,j_{k+1},n_1,\ldots,n_{k+1}}{\prod_{r=1}^{k+1}S_{j_r}^{n_r} } F^{i_4}}{S_1^{i_2}b(F)^{i_3} }}^2 S_1}^{1/2} \nonumber\\ 
     &\qquad\quad  \qquad\quad \times \brac{\prod_{m=2}^{i_1-1}\mathbb{E}{\left[ \left\vert LQ_m \right\rvert^2 S_1\right]}^{\frac{1}{2^{i_1+1-m}}}}\mathbb{E}{\left[ (LQ_1)^2\right]}^{\frac{1}{2^{i_1-4}}}\mathcal{M}(q)^{\frac{1}{2^{i_1-4}}}\,,  

    \end{align}     
 where $P_{k+1}$ is the set of multi-indices specified in Proposition (prop_densitydecompose of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.048397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1a9c282f9574c5efdefc06f8fe82046141c6f02df66403d265552176c1d800b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Importedtheorem 8 (Spectral norm of a GOE, \protect{\cite[Thm.~4.4.3) of arXiv:2606.16018, 'A non-asymptotic bound on the TV distance between a \\Wishart matrix and an appropriately '] {vershynin2025high}}]

