{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.209485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1c868b70c99f61cc2e5decb181809246af862c8fab31353c574b677f35a83cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.03771, '\vspace{-5ex}\bfseries\scshape{Local law and delocalization for the Sachdev--Ye--Kitaev mo'] There exists $c>0$ such that for every $E\in\Rbb,$ $\eta\in(0,1],$ and $t>0$, we have for $\tau\in\{\text{Full},+,-\}$ 
