{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.298249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1d96da19aab49d9e5e80076811976d7534dc87145193828fa6ef275bc2fd75d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_estimation_SID of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] Let $\mathcal P_x =(\Omega, \bF, (\bF_t)_{t\ge 0}, \Prob_x)$ be a filtered probability space and let $X$ be an $(\bF_t)_{t\ge 0}$-adapted process solution to (equation eq_stickySDE of the paper) on $\mathcal P_x$. 
