{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1dc5426d5c32f6da5cfe11dec4f8b372fe767da011107dd4c189daed2cf1bae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Schur of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^n$ be convex. A continuously differentiable function $f:\Omega\to \mathbb{R}$ is Schur-convex if and only if for all $1\leq i, j,\leq n$, 
