    where we have set $B_k(\delta):= \{(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in D_{\delta}^k: \exists i \neq j, \vert x_i - x_j \vert \leq 4\delta \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.241971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1e830c033ae194c940baf310976b40a88c14fd91bba26dfebe682fa51e51285","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2605.25719, 'A note on convergence rate for reflected BSDEs with quadratic generators by penalization m'] Let assumptions $(A1^{'}),~(A2)$ and $(A3)$ be satisfied. Then for $n \geq 1$ and $i=1,\dots,n$, BSDE \eqref{num-PBSDE} has a unique solution $(Y_{t}^{n,i,\lambda},Z_{t}^{n,i,\lambda}) \in \mathcal{S}^{\infty,i}(\mathbb{R}) \times \mathcal{H}^{2,i}(\mathbb{R}^{d})$ and \eqref{e3} has a unique solution $(Y_{t}^{n,\lambda},Z_{t}^{n,\lambda}) \in \mathcal{S}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}) \times BMO$ and
