{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.545719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1f42f688a93d56e1efabc6230b905029802bfd48870df00b72ec18708c7e257","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: A.s. convergence emp. mean of bad vertices of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] For any thinned branch $(\Lambda^r_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ such that $\sum_{n=1}^\infty\frac{1}{|\Lambda^r_n|}<\infty$ and for $\mu_A$-almost every $\omega$, the following limit holds
