{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.346101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d224cd218036b1f280e68ec57d2dd29b90fbecd27930047e93f6939412f530b2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor fincor of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] For almost every measure $\mu_{\mathfrak{s},a}$ that belongs to the extremal decomposition of $\mu_\mathfrak{s}$, there exists some $r \in \mathbb R$ such that,
