{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.256793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d232bfabf9d73993f1b19d457ede634bccd2daec48b0b6bcf1f0bb29686fb2ab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Measure-theoretic upper expectation of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and $X:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ a measurable variable.
  Then we define
  \begin{align}
    \overline{\mathbb{E}} X &:= \sup_{P\in\Delta(\Omega)} \inf_{Z\in\mathrm{mdcl}(\mathcal{Z})} \mathbb{E}_P [X-Z]~,
  \end{align}
  and $\underline{\mathbb{E}} X := -\overline{\mathbb{E}}(-X)$.
  If $\mathbb{E}_P[X-Z]$ is not defined, we define it to be $\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.583580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2350ab7527d42fecaf3c643c16468ef7f40f8674cab99bd3bab971b9c3c44f9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi:interface of arXiv:2511.01851, 'Percolation on graphs of polynomial growth is local:\\analyticity, supercritical sharpness'] Let $\mathscr{I}\subset V$ be a finite set of vertices. We say that $\mathscr{I}$ is an \textit{interface} if it is $t$-coarse connected and either $o\in \mathscr{I}$ or $o$ lies in a finite connected components of $\mathscr{G}\setminus \mathscr{I}$. Let $\overline{\mathscr{I}}$ denote the set of vertices $x$ such that $d_{\mathscr{G}}(x,\mathscr{I})\leqslant 10N$. We say that an interface $\mathscr{I}$ \textit{occurs in $\omega$ at scale $N$} if
\begin{enumerate}
    \item every $x\in \mathscr{I}$ is bad,
    \item every $x\in V\setminus \mathscr{I}$ such that $d_{\mathscr{G}}(x,\mathscr{I})\leqslant t$ is good,
    \item the closed edges of $\overline{\mathscr{I}}$ form a bond-cutset between $o$ and $\infty$.
\end{enumerate}
When clear from context, we simply write that $\mathscr{I}$ occurs.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.775739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2352d16218985c3399752761e2328a444377212e50c89903a00f61fdbd9afcd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 of arXiv:2608.26816, '\textbf{On the existence of maximal foliations in general relativity}'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{maxfol},  there exists a positive  constant $C=C(\alpha_0,\alpha_1)$ such that the solution to the mean curvature flow  (\ref{mcf}) satisfies 
