{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.792619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2aee03b68b56b491b3ec80129fbe5be9fbe1f59b2bcbe1ec38ce77654e54f9c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p.ST of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Let $\Psi$ be a SHEF, $\gamma>0$ and define the set of $\gamma$-thick points as
    \begin{align*}
    T_\gamma:=\left \{(x,t): \gamma^+_x(t):=\limsup_{\varepsilon \to 0} \frac{ \Psi_\varepsilon(t,x)}{-\log(\varepsilon)}=\gamma\right \}.
