{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.903077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2b85f4bf517dbfd09d5ae8ca5444bed9098194c293e66e07ff604407a8443dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2608.29298, 'On Hypersurfaces of Space Forms that are Gradient Yamabe Solitons'] If the space form $\left(\overline{M}^n(C), \overline{g}\right)$ is simply connected and the isometric immersion $ \Sigma^{n-2}\hookrightarrow \overline{M}^n(C)$ is full then the equality for $\sup\limits_{\Sigma}\left|\Phi^{\Sigma}_{\overline{M}}\right|^2$ holds and is attained at some point of $\Sigma^{n-2}$ if, and only if, $\left(M^{n-1}, g\right)$ is isometric to either
