{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.319821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2c412f19501ddf50e7ccecc025209307dbf02913cca62bb758857b363309b02","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 1 of arXiv:2506.21087, 'Quasi-Stationary Distributions of Interacting Dynamical Systems and their approximation'] A probability $\nu\in{\cal P}(\MM)$ is called a Quasi-Stationary Distribution (QSD) for $(K_{\mu,\partial})_{\mu\in{\cal P}(\MM)}$ if $Y_0\sim\nu$ implies that
