Furthermore, $\mu_\ast$ has finite $V$-moments of order $\alpha$, and, in particular,
\begin{equation}
\int_{H} \|z\|^{\alpha}_V\,\mu_\ast(\mathrm{d} z)\le\frac{\|B\|^2_{L_2(U,H)}}{\delta_1}.
\end{equation}
Here, the constants are as in Hypotheses~(hyp:coerc of the paper),~(hyp:monotonicity of the paper),~(hyp:growth of the paper),~and~(hyp:quant of the paper), respectively.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.821742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2c6d25108afb484c5337f658d64d98adb875f7e9fbd049aad8805f325bd9d4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2604.10142, 'H\MakeLowercase{arnack inequality for} $p$\MakeLowercase{-harmonic functions: \\ improved '] There exist universal constants $\gamma,C_*>0$ such that the following holds. Let $u$ be a positive $p$-harmonic function on $B_R(0)\subset\Rd$   with $u(0)=1$.  
