{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.333382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2d15cd9df3240b3188e8f45373b2408cf39214f0c126f25b25665899da03a2e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-prelim-gap-est-time-after-2R of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Suppose that $\alpha > 1$ and
    \begin{equation}{}
        M \geq (\log n)^{100},\quad \delta \geq M^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\log n)^3, \quad (1-\delta)M \geq (\log n)^{12}, \quad 1-\delta > n^{-\frac{1}{\alpha+1}} \,.
    \end{equation}
    Define $\mathfrak F(M,\delta)$ to be the collection of $(M',\delta')$ such that
    \begin{align}
        &(M')^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\log n)^3 \leq \delta', \quad \left( 1-(\log n)^{-1} \right) M \leq M' \,;   \\
        &\min\left\{ \left( 1-(\log n)^{-3} \right) M(1-\delta), (\log n)^{20} \right\} \leq M'(1-\delta') \,;   \\
        & \left( 1-\frac{\delta}{\sqrt{\log n}} \right) (1-\delta)^\alpha \leq (1-\delta') \leq \left( 1+\frac{\delta}{\sqrt{\log n}} \right) (1-\delta)^{\alpha} \,.  
    \end{align}
    Given any $(\mathbf X_1,\ldots,\mathbf X_n) \in \overline{\Omega}_n(M,\delta)$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb P^\alpha_{n,\mathbf X}\left( (\mathbf X_1',\ldots,\mathbf X_n') \in \cup_{ (M',\delta') \in \mathfrak F(M,\delta) } \overline{\Omega}_n(M',\delta'), \mathcal L(\mathbf X')=\mathcal L(\mathbf X) \right) \geq 1-\frac{1}{\log n} \,.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.858242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2d367aeb39fb980837a109ba39b6403fe5e719254558894699fe18e72862f9f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm 9 of arXiv:2511.20875, 'Double $q$-Wigner Chaos and the Fourth Moment'] Let $0\le q \le 1$ and $ f \in H^{\otimes m},  g \in H^{\otimes n}$ be fully symmetric, and let $X=I_q(f)$ and $Y_k=I_q(g)$ be the $q$-Wigner integrals.
      We set $\| f\|_{\mathcal{F}_q(H)}=\sigma_X$ and $\| g\|_{\mathcal{F}_q(H)}=\sigma_Y$. Assume $m,n$ have opposite parities. Then, we have 
      \[\tau_q[(X+Y)^4]-(2+q^{m^2})\sigma_X^4-(2+q^{n^2})\sigma_Y^4 -(4+2q^{mn})\sigma_X^2\sigma_Y^2
      =\kappa_X+\kappa_Y +\kappa_{X,Y}
      \]
      where 
     \begin{align*}
         \kappa_X&=\tau_q(X^4)-(2+q^{m^2})\sigma_X^4\\
         \kappa_Y&=\tau_q(Y^4)-(2+q^{n^2})\sigma_Y^4\\
         \kappa_{X,Y}&=4\tau_q(X^2Y^2)+2\tau_q(XYXY)-(4+2q^{mn})\sigma_X^2\sigma_Y^2\\
         &=4\mathrm{cov}(X^2,Y^2)+2(\tau_q[XYXY]-q^{mn}\sigma_X^2\sigma_Y^2).
     \end{align*}
     Moreover, $\kappa_X,\kappa_Y,\kappa_{X,Y}\ge 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990215+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2de35461911d6f2f9f75ccf2363d2aad9e6873f2ee52f0e509031c4952e44da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 91 (Spatial Markov Property) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $(G, \weight)$ be a finite connected weighted graph and let $A, B\subset E$ be two disjoint sets of edges such that $\bP^\weight(A\subset \cT, B\cap \cT=\emptyset)>0$. Then for any set of edges $F\subset E$,
	\begin{equation*}
	    \bP^\weight_G (\cT = F \mid A\subset \cT, B\cap \cT =\emptyset) = \bP^{\weight}_{(G-B)/A}(\cT \cup A = F).
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.943942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2e000d282fe94f640cdb506fe4e5ad1491ff9a5da61582d88f48a70d9bd8d54","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mont of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$, for all $\xi \in \mathbb{R}$. Whenever $\xi \notin \Xi$ and $b \in \mathcal{F}^\xi$, we have that 
\begin{equation} 
b(y,t) - b(x,s) = W^{\xi}(x,s;y,t),  \quad \forall (x,s;y,t) \in \mathbb{R}^4.
\end{equation}
In general, for $\xi \in \mathbb{R}$ and $b \in \mathcal{F}^\xi$, $t \in \mathbb{R}$, and $x < y$, 
\begin{equation} 
W^{\xi -}(x,t;y,t) \le b(y,t) - b(x,t) \le W^{\xi +}(x,t;y,t).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.788913+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2e054b0d626865317151afe2cafa2e2bac3f2cd56b8f7b33161875f7918dd86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem pure-phase-decay-of-correlations of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Let $\pi_\infty^-$ be the infinite volume minus measure, and fix some finite sets $U,V$. For $\beta>\beta_0$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\pi_\infty^- (\sigma(V) \in \cdot) - \pi_\infty^-(\sigma(V) \in \cdot \mid \sigma(U)\equiv -1)\|_{{\textsc{tv}}}\le |U| e^{ - \beta d(U,V)}\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:15.264642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2e081d24f65fbe771349d7c20533fe239c4f018e02e3794a53981f8dc974e56","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[10 7 of arXiv:2607.12303, 'Marginal Stationary Distributions and Convergence Rates of Higher Order Markov Chains'] {\rm 
