{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.330349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d30043eb094dcda2c0b87a3f3dd256730cdb96bcf8734689d98ca79cd4275ce7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 (Large-noise equalization and upper crossover) of arXiv:2608.30374, 'Compact and Infinite-Order Error Analysis\\ for Null-Space SVD Estimation'] Assume additionally that \(\tau\geq m\), and that the ordered projector
expansion at inverse noise has an \(L^1\) remainder through fourth order.
Set \(\overline Z=Z/h_\star\), \(\overline B=B/h_\star^2\), and
\(t=\zeta^{-1}\).  Let
\begin{equation}
 \Pi_i(t)=\sum_{k\geq0}t^k\Pi_{i,k}^{(\infty)}

\end{equation}
be the ordered rank-one eigenprojector of
\((\cE+t\overline Z)(\cE+t\overline Z)^T\).  Then
\begin{equation}
 \varepsilon_{\mathrm{gen},i}^{\mathrm{ord}}(\sigma)
   =h_\star^2\left(
      \zeta^2+c_\infty+d_i^{(\infty)}\zeta^{-2}
      +O(\zeta^{-4})\right),

\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 c_\infty=\frac{\operatorname{tr}(\overline B)}{m}
   =\frac{\|H\|_F^2}{m h_\star^2},
 \qquad
 d_i^{(\infty)}=\operatorname{tr}\!\left(
   \overline B\,\mathbb E_{\mathrm{tr}}
      [\Pi_{i,2}^{(\infty)}]\right).

\end{equation}
In unscaled variables, the common leading law is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \varepsilon_{\mathrm{gen},i}^{\mathrm{ord}}(\sigma)
   =\sigma^2+\frac{\|H\|_F^2}{m}+O(\sigma^{-2}).}

\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \Delta_{\mathrm{rank}}(\sigma)
   =C_H\zeta^{-4}+O(\zeta^{-6}),
 \qquad
 C_H=\frac{\max_i d_i^{(\infty)}-\min_i d_i^{(\infty)}}
          {\sqrt{q_0}}.

\end{equation}
When \(C_H>0\), the leading upper visibility crossover is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \sigma_{\mathrm{hi}}(\delta_{\mathrm{vis}})
   \simeq h_\star
       \left(\frac{C_H}{\delta_{\mathrm{vis}}}\right)^{1/4}.}

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.933218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d304a36c9328f540d07dd79da4d457c3675c32b439e7b2b76e9d63806d99dd87","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_1.3 of arXiv:2412.05709, 'Incipient infinite clusters and volume growth for Gaussian free fields and loop soups on m'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$ and for any $\lambda\ge 1$, there exist constants $
