{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.605616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d370316f70bdf0da0dd2e4335ad395b4cdbb2cf889ebd59f514e76c5fbd39491","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SSL of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] [BDG-Levy] 
Let $(S,T)\in[0,1]^2$. Let $p\in[2,\infty)$.   Let
$(A_{s,t})_{(s,t)\in \Delta_{[S,T]}}$ be a family of ${\mathbb R}^d$-valued random variables in $L_p(\Omega)$
such that $A_{s,t}$ is $\mathcal{F}_t$-measurable for all $(s,t)\in \Delta_{[S,T]}$.   Let ${\mathcal G}\subset{\mathcal F}_S$ be an $\sigma$-algebra. Suppose that there exist constants $\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2>0$ and constants $K_1, K_2\in[0,\infty)$,  such that the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}[(1)]
   \item $\|A_{s,t}\|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathcal G}}\leqslant K_1|t-s|^{\frac{1}{2}+\epsilon_1}$, $(s,t)\in\Delta_{[S,T]}$,
   \item $\|{\mathbb E}^{s-(t-s)}\delta A_{s,u,t}\|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathcal G}}\leqslant K_2|t-s|^{1+\epsilon_2}$, $(s,t)\in\Delta_{[S,T]}$ and $u=\frac{s+t}{2}$,
   \item there exists a  process $\mathcal{A}:[S,T]\mapsto L^p(\Omega;{\mathbb R}^d)$  such that  for any $(s,t)\in [S,T]_\leqslant^2$ one has
   \begin{align}

       {\mathcal A}_t-{\mathcal A}_s=\lim_{m\rightarrow\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}A_{s+i\frac{t-s}{m},s+(i+1)\frac{t-s}{m}} \quad\text{ in probability}.
   \end{align}
\end{enumerate}
 Then there exists constants $\hat K_1,\hat K_2>0$ which depend only on $\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2,\epsilon_3, d,p$ so that for any $(s,t)\in[S,T]_{\leqslant}^2$,
  \begin{align}

       \|{\mathcal A}_{t}-{\mathcal A}_{s}\|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathcal G}}\leqslant K_1\hat K_1|t-s|^{\frac{1}{2}+\epsilon_1}+K_2\hat K_2|t-s|^{1+\epsilon_2}.
   \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.789048+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3720543bddfc048987e8d6d7c8e533befd0bfc54914a6ed3d4849483019060c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2604.00630, 'The contact process on a bipartite spatial network'] Let~$\pi=(\pi_0,\ldots,\pi_\ell)$ be a combinatorial path of length~$\ell$ with~$k$ distinct vertices; assume that~$\pi_\ell \notin\{\pi_0,\ldots,\pi_{\ell-1}\}$. Let~$T$ be the discovery tree of~$\pi$. Let~$\mathcal Q(\pi)$ be the probability that there exists an infection path in~$\mathcal G$ started at the root and having an ordered trace~$\Gamma$ satisfying the following properties:
\begin{itemize}
\item the combinatorial path associated to~$\Gamma$ is~$\pi$;
\item all vertices of~$\Gamma$ are blue.
\end{itemize}
Then,
	\[
		\mathcal Q(\pi) \le 
			(2\lambda^{a \wedge 1})^{(\ell-2k)\vee 0} \cdot F(T,\pi_0,\pi_\ell). 
	\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.365943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d37723ae6e9f92d3ed279817507cf3c9c7ac7f7595bf15b7a3a23232ed9cb0b2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm -1 of arXiv:2411.13403, 'Path weighting method for spot sensitivities and its variance reduction'] If $F(S)$ has generalised derivatives with at most
polynomial growth a.e., then the random variables 
\begin{equation}
\xi=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}}\Big(F(S)\Theta^{(1)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}Z_{1})-F(\hat{S})\Theta^{(1)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}\hat{Z}_{1})\Big),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\eta_{1}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}}\Big(F(S)\Lambda^{(1)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}Z_{1})-F(\hat{S})\Lambda^{(1)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}\hat{Z}_{1})\Big),
\end{equation}
have variance of order
\begin{align}
\mathrm{Var}(\xi) & =\mathrm{O}(1),\;(\Delta t_{1}\to0),\\
\mathrm{Var}(\eta_{1}) & =\mathrm{O}(1),\;(\Delta t_{1}\to0).
\end{align}
If, in addition, $F(S)$ has second order generalised derivatives
with at most polynomial growth a.e., then the random variable
\begin{equation}
\eta_{2}=\frac{1}{\Delta t_{1}}\Big(F(S)\Lambda^{(2)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}Z_{1})-2F(\bar{S})\Lambda^{(2)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}\bar{Z}_{1})+F(\hat{S})\Lambda^{(2)}(s,Z_{1},\sqrt{\Delta t_{1}}\hat{Z}_{1})\Big)
\end{equation}
has variance of order
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Var}(\eta_{1})=\mathrm{O}(1),\;(\Delta t_{1}\to0),
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:44.389765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d37a94b161c4fdff33c4e889cffdc049ac2e04288b496dc49081ad1cd2552cad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2609.02826, '2609.02826'] Let $\cG$ be an algebraic commutative group stack that is proper, flat, and
