{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.586212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3842e4d111fccc9f6a79866f79c09fff6869fea7e5a364a79f259bdde28e146","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Hamilton of arXiv:2609.00840, 'Kählerity of complete almost-Kähler gradient shrinking Ricci solitons'] [Hamilton [Hamilton:95]] 
	Let $(M^n,g,f)$ be an $n$-dimensional complete gradient shrinking Ricci soliton satisfying Eq. ((eq:soliton of the paper)). Then
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] $ R + \Delta_g f = n\lambda, $
		\smallskip
		\item[(ii)] $ \mathrm d R = 2Rc(\nabla f,\mathord\cdot),$
		\smallskip
		\item[(iii)] $ R + |\nabla f|^2 = 2\lambda f+C_0.$
	\end{itemize}
	Here $C_0$ is some constant and $\Delta_f=\Delta_g-\langle\nabla f,\nabla\mathord\cdot\rangle$ is the drift Laplacian. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.490636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3848f9a63b589cedf57ce3388b18079e26d49f7096b3e347b64c02483dc524d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Definition and triangularity of $\Gamma$) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $ (\pi^{(\n)} )_{\n\in\NN^{1+d}} \subset \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$ such that for all $\beta$ and $\n$ it holds that $\pi^{(\n)}_{ \beta} \neq 0$ implies $ |\n| < | \beta| $.
Then 
\begin{enumerate}
\item the map $ \Gamma :  \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!] \to  \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$ defined by 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Gamma z_{k}\coloneqq z_{k}\,, \quad 
\Gamma z_{\n}\coloneqq z_{\n}+ \pi^{(\n)}\,, \quad 
\Gamma 1\coloneqq 1\,, \quad \text{and}\quad 
\Gamma ( \pi_{1} \pi_{2}) = (\Gamma \pi_{1}) ( \Gamma \pi_{2})
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} 
for $\pi_1,\pi_2\in\RR[\![z_k,z_\n]\!]$
is well-defined on $\RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$, 

\item for all $\beta,\gamma$ it holds that $ (\Gamma - \mathrm{id})_{ \beta}^{ \gamma}
\neq 0$ implies $ | \gamma| <
| \beta| $ and $\langle\gamma\rangle<\langle\beta\rangle$, and

\item if $ (\pi^{(\n)} )_{\n\in\NN^{1+d}} $ is such that $ \pi^{(\n)}_{ \beta'} = 0$ for all non populated $\beta'$, then for all $\beta,\gamma$
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
(\Gamma - \mathrm{id})_{ \beta}^{ \gamma} \neq 0 \quad \implies \quad \gamma
\prec \beta\,.
