The $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. means as usual that we have a 
$\mathbb{P}$-full  set involved. 
Actually, one could make this $\mathbb{P}$-full set independent of $t$ and $\theta$ by Lemma (lem-transport-weak-2-(i) of the paper).
\end{trivlist}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.814324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3ae8168b58b20e5e8d4f4e675bd962313fa78a7a97ae603f316279212e13b3c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:eq norm of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Assume that $d\ge 3$, $s\in (1,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1/2)$, let $M_0$ be in $\dot{H}^{-s}$, fix $R>0$. Let $M$ be a solution to (equation eq:KK of the paper) (in the sense of (def:sol of the paper)) which is also in $L^2_{t,\omega}(\dot{H}^{-s+1-\alpha})$. Then we have
