{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.704042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3bd4a34f4dc50998c7d9bcf0298b00c54096882b83d5203eba35f32d0f7cebc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: BK-prob of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] There are constants $C$, $c>0$ such that, for $K$ large enough, we have 
