{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.100571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3ce552c8e3301bbdc5a16db81df056a0c95fd8b9769f93a8cddbaabace65d30","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LM42 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] The right process $X^G$ is $m|_{G}$-tight and is properly associated with the quasi-regular Dirichlet form given by
