{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.652792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4110acae5a55df0111314be10b4317dfdcbb2fb975797830f59d2aebed1ec7e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2607.24533, 'Colored Markov-Modulated Brownian Motion for Preemptive Workload Stacks'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{assump:intensity} and~\ref{assump:stability} hold, and fix a depleting color $\ell\in\mathcal C$. Let
$\vect m_\ell(y)=\int_0^\infty\vect G_\ell(y,x)\,\dd x$. Then
\begin{equation}

