{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.996425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d417fdd6f6d208fd58fc4852d90e27523cfdf700c9342d18801a6071161d7442","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 42 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $m$ be a fixed integer and let $M$ be a fixed $2m\times2m$-dimensional skew-symmetric matrix such that the minors 
    \[[M]_{k,\ell}, \quad \text{for } 2j-1\leq k,\ell\leq2m\]
    are invertible for all $1\leq j\leq m$. Then $M$ has a \emph{skew-Borel factorization} of the form
    \begin{equation}
        M = R_{2m} J_{2m} R_{2m}^T,
    \end{equation}
    where $R_{2m}$ is an upper-triangular $2m\times2m$-dimensional matrix which is uniquely determined up to setting $\left[R_{2m}\right]_{2j-1,2j}=0$ and $\left[R_{2m}\right]_{2j,2j}=1$ for each $1\leq j\leq m$. Also where
    \[J_{2m} = \diag\left\{\left[\begin{array}{cc}
			0 & 1\\
			-1 & 0
		\end{array}\right],\dots,\left[\begin{array}{cc}
			0 & 1\\
			-1 & 0
		\end{array}\right]\right\}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.969361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d41c93fee1d806d87158d2c20ef4f5d732de2d6035f197c681b508f6dd42ba82","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dense_discrete_measures of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] The following assertions hold:
