\item[(iii)] The family of absolutely continuous $d$-Williamson measures with full support is dense in $(\mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d},\tau_w)$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.290376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d41dd4d66773d17b33c142981fd8637c2ef0c6f4cb8d0efc425678a90bfbefdd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: r8 bound of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $\delta > 0$ sufficiently small, there exists $C_\delta > 0$ such that
