{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.842354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d427a93ba2614fef8e3015a2bab28cdd03c0fe30bf919a32b454d7aa93c12766","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:113 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c$ such that for all $n$, and all $\Delta,j,k,i$ satisfying $1\leq \Delta\leq 2\varepsilon n^{1/3}$, $|j|,|k|\leq 3\varepsilon n^{1/3}$ and $0\leq i\leq \Delta^3/4$, we have
