{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d43acc2e5e82e18857f5c6e2d0c2a960b794529ceab0dd9ced9cbbd7851ed499","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:incrementLambda of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$, any $0\le s<t\le T$ and any $\varepsilon >0$, the quadratic term defined in (equation eq:Lambda of the paper) satisfies
