{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.161090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4484b2c1c60e312e7379662b46aa2d81f475e78dffbd8b02a36f005db78c6d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Gini_comparison_special_case of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Let $a \in \mathbb N$ and $b \to \infty$. Then the equilibrium solution $({\bf p}^{a,\infty})^*$ of the mean-field system (equation eq:law_limit of the paper) with ${\bf p}(0) \in V_\mu$ satisfies the following Gini index comparison principle
