\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.708105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4919f996fc8b4e12e9119bd1c74ef71e92aad84c7b24b731648b7dade92b28b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:roleofFouriermodes of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Under the conditions of Theorem~(thm:NGlimit of the paper),  for $\vec{k} \in \mathbb{K}$,  as $N\rightarrow \infty$,
