{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.143328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4d7b483ce5825ecfb794897bc758799b7e4239ff49dfa75bf249af1a38266bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tail-rate of arXiv:2607.04620, 'The Exact Ville Identity\\ \large From the Absorbing Case to the General Law\\ with an App'] Let $S_n$ be a centered martingale with $\mathbb{E}[S_n^2]=n$, and let $T$ be a first-passage time with $L=\mathbb{E}[S_T\mathbf{1}(T<\infty)]$ finite as in (thm:conservation of the paper). Then, from the moment inequalities of [klass2026beyond], for every $p>1$,
\begin{equation}
  |L|^{p/(p-1)}
  \le
  \liminf_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{P}(T>n)
  \left(\mathbb{E}[|S_n|^p\mathbf{1}(T>n)]\right)^{1/(p-1)}.

\end{equation}
The case $p=2$, after dropping the indicator inside the moment, gives the cruder $\liminf_n n\mathbb{P}(T>n)\ge L^2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.648693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4daa926559842845fb6c8ea5179b267fcca197ca15c507ad22e644ec51a422d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition frechet_subdifferential of arXiv:2608.19198, 'Probabilistic Representation and Convergence of Gromov-Wasserstein Gradient Flows'] Given a proper and lower semicontinuous functional $\mathsf{F}:\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^d)\to\mathbb{R}\cup\{+\infty\}$ with $\mathrm{Dom}(\mathsf{F}) \coloneqq\{\mu\in\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^d):\mathsf{F}(\mu)<+\infty\} \subset\mathcal{P}_2^{\mathrm{ac}}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, its \textit{Fr\'echet subdifferential} $\partial\mathsf{F}(\mu)$ is the collection of all $\xi\in L^2(\mu;\mathbb{R}^d)$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathsf{F}(T_{\#}\mu)-\mathsf{F}(\mu)\geq\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \left\langle\xi(x),T(x)-x\right\rangle d\mu(x) +o(\|T-\id\|_{L^2(\mu;\mathbb{R}^d)})
    \end{align*}
    for any map $T \in L^2(\mu;\mathbb{R}^d)$. Any element $\xi\in\partial\mathsf{F}(\mu)$ is called a \textit{strong subdifferential}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.760242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4db1c3a78f2b9e210ce14c2feea2053ded99f5429a826a9ab7c38abb218a778","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 (Bound on the gradient) of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] Let $r\geq 2$ be an even integer, $q \in [1,\infty)$ and $f(X)=\mrm{Tr}\left(X^{r}\right)^q$ for all $X\in B_E(S_p^N)$. Then
