{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.271058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4df3bedbc8e6306277344d682efa00ab45db4752d52cbb378c0ed96598e0840","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_martingale_problem of arXiv:2512.21159, '\textsc{From multitype branching Brownian motions\\ to branching Markov additive processes'] For any $\theta\in (0,\bar{\theta})$, a function $\Phi_{\theta}\in \mathcal{T}_1$ is a travelling wave with speed $\rho_{\theta}=\frac{\lambda(\theta)}{\theta}$, if and only if 
