{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.866455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4e6ee577ab7e2a4fcefdd8b1f1a70fc333565ee65ee3a221f2e985456d88151","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 68 of arXiv:2608.26823, 'Evolutes, involutes and parallels of Legendre curves in hyperbolic and de Sitter 2-spaces '] Let $(\bgamma_T,\bgamma_T^d):I\rightarrow\Delta_5$ be a timelike Legendre curve  with curvature $(m_T,n_T)$.    $\widetilde{\mathcal{DP}}^\pm_{\widetilde{\lambda}_\pm} (\bgamma_T,\bgamma_T^d)$  and
