{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.397402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4fcf0ad8e42480fd46f9df7543d8467702b0e529033285e68ab0a7cde18db74","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition6.666 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix $B>0$, $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ and consider the random matrix $A_n\sim\operatorname{Sym}_n(\zeta)$. Fix any $\kappa>0$. Then, uniformly for all $\lambda\in[-(2-\kappa)\sqrt{n},(2-\kappa)\sqrt{n}]$, for any $\epsilon>0$,
    \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}(    \sigma_{min}(A_n-\lambda I_n)\leq\epsilon n^{-1/2})\leq c\epsilon+e^{-cn},
    \end{equation} where the constant $c>0$ depends only on $B$ and $\kappa$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.410569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d50170312f65b1b153a5be19b1e5198f39f2592deb22588a379a6d10ad4cff0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:modelcriterion of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Under the above hypotheses, the four-longitude decomposition is in positive parabolic normal form along one, and hence both, real half-branches if and only if $c_1c_2\alpha_1\alpha_2 < 0$. Moreover, for each real half-branch $B$, there is a sign $\sigma_B \in \{\pm 1\}$ such that its limiting height vector is 
\begin{equation*}
	(h_1, h_2, h_3, h_4) = \sigma_B(\eta_1, \mathrm{sgn}(c_1c_2)\eta_2, \eta_3, \mathrm{sgn}(c_1c_2)\eta_4)
\end{equation*}
Consequently, height-cancellation holds along one, and hence both, real half-branches if and only if $\eta_1+\eta_3 + \mathrm{sgn}(c_1c_2)(\eta_2 + \eta_4) = 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.127855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d504a1ebf0a8d1c1aad039f106fd1852123a5683db07789ab4d03f25aa575bc0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop identity of arXiv:2411.15954, 'A gradient model for the Bernstein polynomial basis'] Fixed $L\in\mathbb{N}$, it holds that 
    \begin{align}
    \mathbf{b}_{n,L}
    &=
    \sum_{\ell=n}^{L}
    (-1)^{\ell-n}
    \binom{L}{\ell}\binom{\ell}{n}
    \mathbf{p}_{\ell;L}
    &&\text{for each } 0\leq n\leq L
    ,
    \\
    \mathbf{p}_{\ell;L}
    &=\sum_{n=\ell}^L
    \frac{\binom{n}{\ell}}{\binom{L}{\ell}}
    \mathbf{b}_{n,L},
    &&\text{for each } 0\leq \ell\leq L

    \\
    \mathbf{b}_{n,L}(\eta)
    &\leq
    \binom{L}{n}
    \mathbf{p}_{n;L}(\eta),
    &&\text{for each } \eta\in\Omega_N
    .

    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.302296+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d50995405b1f1040683c1912d9f66829d2e56c0b7541763932740c8654859be2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2608.21787, 'Stability of extremal hyperplane projections of balls in $\ell_p^n(\R)$'] Let $Y_1$, $Y_2$ be i.i.d. square integrable random variables whose distribution is not a Dirac delta distribution. Let $a_1$, $a_2$, $b_1$, $b_2$, $s$ also be real numbers such that $s \ge 0$, $a_1^2 + a_2^2 = b_1^2 + b_2^2 = \sigma^2 > 0$ and $a_1^2 \ge b_1^2 \ge b_2^2 \ge a_2^2$. Then there exist positive constants $c$, $\eta$, depending only on the distribution of $Y_1$, such that
        \begin{align*}
            \E\sqrt{b_1^2Y_1^2 + b_2^2Y_2^2 + s} - \E\sqrt{a_1^2Y_1^2 + a_2^2Y_2^2 + s} \ge c\left(s + \eta\sigma^2\right)^{-\frac 3 2}\left(a_1^4 + a_2^4 - b_1^4 - b_2^4\right).
        \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.305081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d50b765005293fdf3b74e6720b575a039c93298e7cb3d3c1049f158860f2234e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local-lower of arXiv:2608.07410, 'Extreme least singular values of random row submatrices\\ with bounded-density subgaussian'] Let $\xi$ and $X$ be as in \hyperref[lem:marginal-density]{Lemma~\ref*{lem:marginal-density}}. There are constants $\eta,c_0>0$,
