{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.294280+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d54251455dfc6a75274aedbb4bdda5d434ae57e2aedfcdbeff0655b30956c441","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition tt of arXiv:2605.08624, 'On the sum-of-digits measures and Cusick's conjecture via stopped random walks'] Given $T \in \mathcal{T}$, define the stopping time $\tau_T$ recursively:
