{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.368342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d54b27233aee23c1433a6127a0902f332fde6f54dd2ab5d2a9e04c28c1b2077e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] There exist a constant $C > 0$ and a family of positive random variables $(\Psi^1_{s,t})_{0 \leqslant s < t}$, where the Malliavin-Sobolev norm of each $\Psi^1_{s,t}$ does not depend on $s$ or $t$, such that
