{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.981984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d58c2488c165ce837c21136f685c2b89be37732d1cd07a702a791673414bf33f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:fictitious_derivative_lower_bound of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] Suppose that $d=3\alpha$ and that the modified hydrodynamic condition does \emph{not} hold. There exist positive constants $c$ and $\lambda_0$ such that 
