{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.958961+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d597401f02c317d6f3ff336afea0322aac421d7b350bc9f8cb4585f373b0c905","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $\mathcal{Z}$ be a finite set of points with subset $\mathcal{D}\subseteq\mathcal{Z}$ and let $\mu$ be a conditional Pfaffian $L$-ensemble on $\mathcal{D}$ within $\mathbb{Z}$ as in Definition \ref{defn:cond pf L-ensemble}. Then $\mu$ is a Pfaffian point process on $\mathcal{D}$ whose correlation kernel is given by
	\begin{equation}
		K = J_\mathcal{D} + \left(J_\mathcal{D}+L\right)^{-1}\Big|_{\mathcal{D}\times\mathcal{D}},
	\end{equation}
	where the second term denotes the inverse of the matrix $J_\mathcal{D}+L$ indexed by $\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Z}$ restricted to $\mathcal{D}\times\mathcal{D}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.771147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d598964554905139e799bfc1ee8cb2fc2d6dd3d88f06efd518b3f069299edd65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lower-bound of arXiv:2608.04900, 'A Sharper Hoeffding Bound for Weighted Sums of Exchangeable Random Variables'] \begin{align*}
C_N^\star
\ge
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle \frac{N}{N-1}, & N \text{ even}, \\[0.8em]
\displaystyle \frac{N+1}{N}, & N \text{ odd}.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
In particular, $C_N^\star\ge 1+N^{-1}+c_{N}N^{-2}$ for a bounded sequence $(c_N)_{N\ge 2}$, where $c_N=N/(N-1)$ for even $N$ and $c_N=0$ for odd $N$. Thus the first-order coefficient $3/2$ in Theorem~(thm:main of the paper) can at best be reduced to $1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.994164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5a13342542738cf2f91625df5302b47ae6d5f0d8b75ba69675f5777ff074ccd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem rho bound of arXiv:2412.01086, 'Spectral radii of sparse non-Hermitian random matrices'] {k09}}] 
For an $n\times n$ matrix $A$ with $n>2$ and for $k\geq 1$,
\begin{align*}
C_n^{-\sigma_n(k)/k}\left( \frac{\| A\|^n}{\| A^n\|}\right)^{-\nu_n(k)/k}\| A^k\|^{1/k}\leq \rho (A)\leq \| A^k\|^{1/k},
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
C_n =n^{3n/2}, \quad \sigma_n(k) = \frac{(n-1)^3}{(n-2)^2}k^{\frac{\log (n-1)}{\log n}}, \quad \nu_n(k) =\frac{(n-1)^2}{n-2}k^{\frac{\log (n-1)}{\log n}}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.652945+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5a3458b5e9b6282bb12bd8c597eb6ca99b7f7a7cda87abe1a3be80a0f44cecc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2605.17155, '2605.17155'] Let \(d\geq 1\), and let \(f:\Nzero^d\to\R\) be almost periodic.  Then
