{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.632195+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5acaadb7acb4330cb6516d7f5e3746cde7f6b763421f9a9f4c5877864d94e14","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$ with $\mathrm{supp}(\gamma) = \left[\frac{1}{\varphi(0)},\infty\right)$, $\vartheta\in\mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$ and $C$ be the corresponding Archimax copula. Moreover, let $L$, $R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R_measure} with $L < R$. Then the following assertions hold:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[$(i)$] If $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}}^{abs}$, then $\mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}^{abs}) = \mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}).$
    \item[$(ii)$] If $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}}^{dis}$, then $\mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}^{dis}) = \mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}).$
    \item[$(iii)$] If $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}}^{sing}$, then $\mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}^{sing}) = \mathrm{supp}(\mu_{C}).$
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.354194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5acb56dba6259fba102d29a060af63d21aceacf979933fcf7bdd6e3d1c00b05","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:BEP of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For all graphs $G=(V,(c_{xy})_{x,y\in V})$ and site weights $\alpha=(\alpha_x)_{x\in V}$, we have
