{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.763850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5bff45c63b44ff39c7d7f26c7ab9db16733936d35baebd4360d97329febe42d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thm:count-lattice-points of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d,a\in\mathds{N}$, $\beta\in\mathds{R}$, and $p\in (0,\infty)$.
We have
\begin{equation*}
\sum_{m\in\mathds{Z}^d}\lr{1+\frac{\left\lVertm\right\rVert_\infty}{a}}^{\beta p}<\infty
\end{equation*}
if and only if $\beta< -\frac{d}{p}$, in which case $\sum_{m\in\mathds{Z}^d}\lr{1+\frac{\left\lVertm\right\rVert_\infty}{a}}^{\beta p}\asymp a^d$, with the implied constants only depending on $\beta$, $p$, and $d$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:44.393041+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5c05bc182921d5a40939221cba915cfb9cb0fb315342d02ed727363b2566b4f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 of arXiv:2609.02826, '2609.02826'] Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring with $2\in R^{\times}$.  Let $\cG$ be a
proper flat finitely presented algebraic commutative group stack over $R$, and
assume that $H:=\HHm(\cG)$ is finite flat.  Then $\Dual{\cG}$ is algebraic,
proper, flat, and finitely presented over $R$, with finite diagonal.  More
precisely, the canonical sequence dualizes to an exact sequence
