{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.035032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5fe3253eb8da4d152e5d3445a4b65fd93e53a5f79d63b19e1321e884ad3ee1f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2605.03100, 'Berry-Esseen bounds for multivariate martingale difference sequences in the Kolmogorov dis'] Let $\{\bm{X}_k\}_{k \in [n]}$ denote a martingale difference process in $\mathbb{R}^d$ that satisfies Assumptions \ref{as:fixed-variation} and \ref{as:finite-3rd-moment}. Then
