{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.146511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6438dfb980aa17466997ff55641000c2cec0cb80eb26590a7b5f614f2295e61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:1 of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] For each ${\bf p} \in \mathcal{A}$, let $C_0 = \sum_{n\geq 0} 2^n\,p_n < \infty$. Then
