{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.991107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d644c6b1fb3b9ea9b7331c595af7bc9cdb97f09e4b8cb39957e0efb7f3ba6be1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 104 (Subcritical) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $p= \frac{\lambda}{n}$ with $\lambda < 1$. Then there exists a constant $C(\lambda) > 0$ such that
