{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d64b34fc9eebf7bd07ea424fe4d98253e7d9498cc4feb944b0ac096fb9935f1b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 13 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] The family $\{\Phi_{0,\cdot,\sigma}^{\eps}u_0\}_{\eps\in(0,1]}$ of solutions of \eqref{e.080302} with time symbol $\sigma$ satisfies the Freidlin--Wentzell uniform LDP on $C([0,T];H)$ with rate function $I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}$ if the following two conditions hold for the law $\nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}$ of the solution $\Phi_{0,\cdot,\sigma}^{\eps}u_0$:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[(1)] For every $R>0$, $M\geq0$, and $\d,\d'>0$, there exists $\eps_0>0$ such that
        \begin{align*}
          \inf_{\|u_0\|\leq R}\inf_{\xi\in\{I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}\leq M\}}
          \left(
          \nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}\bigl(\Nc_{\d'}(\xi)\bigr)
          -e^{-(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}(\xi)+\d)/\eps}
          \right)\geq0,
          \qquad \forall \eps\in(0,\eps_0],
        \end{align*}
        where $\Nc_{\d'}(\xi)$ is the $\d'$-neighborhood of $\xi$ in $C([0,T];H)$.

        \item[(2)] For every $R>0$, $M\geq0$, and $\d,\d'>0$, there exists $\eps_0>0$ such that
        \begin{align*}
          \sup_{\|u_0\|\leq R}
          \nu_{u_0,\sigma}^{\eps}
          \left(C([0,T];H)\setminus\Nc_{\d'}(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma},M)\right)
          \leq e^{-(M-\d)/\eps},
          \qquad \forall \eps\in(0,\eps_0],
        \end{align*}
        where $\Nc_{\d'}(I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma},M)$ is the $\d'$-neighborhood of the level set $\{I_{u_0,T}^{\sigma}\leq M\}$.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.478731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d64ef7c9d091f1253cdb009f2c1d983dc124e41b0637e8a6f29109a1599ef74e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 103 (Covariance-admissible regularization) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Fix $m\ge1$ and a nondecreasing profile
$\mathfrak c:\mathbb D\to[1,\infty)$.  The family
$(\eta_{\nu,\cdot})_\nu$ is \emph{$m$-covariance-admissible with profile
$\mathfrak c$} if there are $J>d$ and constants $C_0,\ldots,C_m$ such
that, for every $0\le n\le m$, every $\nu,\mu$, and every dyadic $R$,
\begin{align}

 \max\bigg\{&\sup_x\int_M|\gamma_{\nu,\mu}(x,y)|^n
   R^d(1+Rd_g(x,y))^{-J}\,dV_g(y),\notag\\
 &\sup_y\int_M|\gamma_{\nu,\mu}(x,y)|^n
   R^d(1+Rd_g(x,y))^{-J}\,dV_g(x)\bigg\}
 \le C_n\mathfrak c(R)^n.
\end{align}
Define the order-$m$ mixed defect
\begin{equation}

 \varepsilon_{\nu,\mu}^{(m)}
 :=\|\gamma_{\nu,\nu}^m+\gamma_{\mu,\mu}^m
      -\gamma_{\nu,\mu}^m-\gamma_{\mu,\nu}^m\|_{L^1(M\times M)}.
\end{equation}
The family is \emph{ultraviolet Cauchy at order $m$} if
$\sup_{\nu,\mu\ge N}\varepsilon_{\nu,\mu}^{(m)}\to0$.  Two families are
jointly covariance-compatible if these conditions hold for their union in
one common Gaussian realization.","status":"unverified"}

