{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.504113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d64f35f9fe380e881c25f25a0b5fbe7a25d341476f43b46f327bf47c52c42cb9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (The viewing
angle) of arXiv:2608.06591, 'Random Triangles on Concentric Circles'] \protect\hypertarget{lem-omega}{}

Let \(\psi = \angle O P_i P_k\) and let
\(h = r_k \sin\omega = r_i \sin\psi\) be the distance from the center to
the line \(P_kP_i\). Then

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  if \(r_k \leq r_i\), the folded angle \(\min(\omega, \pi - \omega)\)
  is uniform on \((0, \pi/2)\);
\item
  if \(r_k \geq r_i\), the acute branch
  \(\psi_0 = \min(\psi, \pi - \psi)\) is uniform on \((0, \pi/2)\). (The
  line meets the circle twice, and \(\psi\) is obtuse at the far point,
  so \(\psi\) itself is not confined to \((0, \pi/2)\).)
\end{itemize}

In both cases \(h = \min(r_i, r_k)\sin\mu\) for a \(\mu\) uniform on
\((0, \pi/2)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.821651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d651b85122f3fba33de8fba20ff367fe7688432916f45235b214a7f0c6290ddc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 of arXiv:2604.10142, 'H\MakeLowercase{arnack inequality for} $p$\MakeLowercase{-harmonic functions: \\ improved '] Let $u$ be a positive $p$-harmonic function on $B_5(0)$. Then $u$ satisfies the Harnack inequality:
