{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.500802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6562a8a60892d4c67a3d05df75dc6425e09ece2e6907c939a9a20be1c197cab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Binomial collision kernel) of arXiv:2607.04467, 'Bernstein Functions at Work:\\ Coalescents, Copulas, and Subordination'] For every integer $n\ge2$ and $x,y\ge0$ with $x+y\le1$,
