{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.348086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6949c4a94ab5f57e97a23c85c7b6b05d5a8cfbdac1503e697c2589b385e75d1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:feature-edge of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $K \subset (0, 1/2)$ be compact and let $n = n(p)$ satisfy $n/p^2 \in K$ for all large $p$.  There are constants $0 < c_K \le C_K < \infty$ such that, with probability tending to one as $p \to \infty$,
\begin{equation}
c_K\, p^2\, I_d_n \;\preceq\; \mathcal{Q}_y \mathcal{Q}_y^* \;\preceq\; C_K\, p^2\, I_d_n .
\end{equation}
In particular, with probability tending to one,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{T \neq 0} \frac{\|\mathcal{Q}_y(T)\|_2}{\sqrt n\, \|T\|_{\mathrm{F}}} \le C_K' .
