Moreover, if $\mathcal{G}(T) = (\sqrt p \operatorname{Tr}(G_i T))_{i=1}^n$ with $G_i \stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim} \operatorname{GOE}(p)$, then $\|\mathcal{G}\|_{\mathrm{F} \to 2} \le C_K' \sqrt n$ with probability at least $1 - 2e^{-n/2}$.  All constants and all $o(1)$ probabilities are uniform over sequences with $n/p^2 \in K$.","status":"unverified"}

