{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.520855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6c39090b5dafc13ece107c708b4ba5fb87cdd8b31dbf5e71ffd732667545dbf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 (Best Euclidean pole) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] Let
\begin{equation}
 \overline C_X=\sup_{\|u\|=1}C_X(u).
