Moreover, \(\overline C_X\) is the smallest constant that can replace it in \eqref{eq:covariance-isotropic}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.137578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6c5846cbef9002e03d1a1075922420500bd949bf8254eccc1fa47c2d29ccc20","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 (Critical residual geometry) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] Let $d\ge2$ and let $A\in\R^{2d\times d}$ have orthonormal columns and
$\lVert a_i\rVert_2^2=1/2$ for every $i$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \frac{1-\rho_A}{4}
  \le \nu_A
  \le \frac{(1-\rho_A)(3+\rho_A)}{8}.}

\end{equation}
Moreover, the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=*]
\item $\nu_A=0$;
