{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.961755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6f610dca85e0f4569a8d9af21468923256fb821000c4d02161c76d64daa77a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] The dominating term in the centered-edge decomposition of $T_n$, as in~\eqref{term:central0}--\eqref{term:central3}, is of fluctuation order 
