{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.685802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7110644615bfcbb01994049b496cc6702301abf8ed505c56b4abf6320bc4c6c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm t:1.2i of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists a coupling between
$\eta_{\rm D}$ from~(equation e:1.10i of the paper), $\mathcal Z_{\rm D}$ from~(equation eq:deflqgm of the paper) and $\overline{h}_{\rm D}$ from~(equation e:1.7p of the paper), such that $\eta_{\rm D}$ and $\mathcal Z_{\rm D}$ 
