{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.027446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7205e03ba911877d64ef567d05f5ba51e5c465826f3d3217439ee9d7aa60dfd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem J2 of arXiv:2607.28167, 'Temporal properties of the stochastic fractional heat equation with rough dependence in sp'] For any  $T>0$,  $p>p_0$,  $\vartheta\le \vartheta_0$ and $\vartheta<\frac{1-2H}{\alpha}$,  there exists a finite positive constant  $c_{3,3}$, independent of  $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$, such that
