{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.422897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d73b79e68d67b1e2dec13f199c97660311cf4ade03c8126298f640197795b526","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-green-conv of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $\mathcal A\subset\mathcal V\mathcal G$ be finite and non-empty. Let $\{\mathcal G_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be an increasing family of connected subgraphs of $\mathcal G$ whose union is all of $\mathcal G$ such that $\mathcal A\subset\mathcal V\mathcal G_n$ for every $n\in\mathbbm N$. 
