{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.464618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d73d7e5c43693cbb29bd302ffd2ff30a3ed13ccea1fa01654af577da483006cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 43 (Useful identities for the first fundamental forms; \cite{abbrescia2022emergence}*{Lemma\,3.15}) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\smoothtorusproject$, 
