{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.275493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d75a02d426ae723ef8fca098b7d1e0d7dd3c89259f016d90197bf603dba56bc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.7 of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] [[tikhomirov2015limit], Lemma 12] We can find a universal constant $C_{(equation lemma3.7 of the paper)}>0$ so the following holds. Given $n,m\in\mathbb{N},n\geq m$, $\epsilon\in(0,1]$, a subset $S\subset\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$, and let $T\subset\mathbb{B}_2^n$ (the unit ball in $\ell_2^n$) be a subset of $m$-sparse vectors that satisfy 
\begin{equation}
\text{for each }y\in S\text{ we can find }x=x(y)\in T\text{ such that }y\chi_{\text{supp}x}=x.
\end{equation} Then we can find a set $\mathcal{N}\subset T$ with cardinality bounded by $(\frac{C_{(equation lemma3.7 of the paper)}n}{\epsilon m})^m$ so that given any $y\in S$ we can find $y'=y'(y)\in\mathcal{N}$ satisfying $\|y'-\chi_{\operatorname{supp}y'}y\|\leq\epsilon.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.031582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d75bcedcf100fadf276c68109aadfa93218f757370e3261682a06d1f64a0e14e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cole-hopf-plateau of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] Let $0\le s<t\le1$, assume $\zeta((s,t))=0$, and set $\alpha:=\zeta([0,s])$.  Then
		\[
		U(r,x):=\exp\{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(r,x)\}
		\]
		solves the backward heat equation on $[s,t]$,
		\[
		\partial_r U(r,x)+\frac12\xi''(r)\partial_{xx}U(r,x)=0 .
		\]
		Hence, with
		\[
		p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y)
		:=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi(\xi'(t)-\xi'(s))}}
		\exp\left\{-\frac{(y-x)^2}{2(\xi'(t)-\xi'(s))}\right\},
		\]
		we have
		\begin{equation}
			e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(s,x)}
			=\int_\mathbb{R} e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(t,y)}p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y)\,\mathrm{d} y .
		\end{equation}
		Equivalently, conditionally on $X_s=x$, the transition density of the Auffinger--Chen process on the plateau is
		\begin{equation}
			p_{s,t}(x,y)
			=\frac{e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(t,y)}}{e^{\alpha\Phi_\zeta(s,x)}}
			p^{\mathrm{BM}}_{s,t}(x,y).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.877914+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d75e31fbb2400cd6c3ab655883dc65e82461eab86087240a9cce9fbc3d462fad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.29501, 'Disorder Thresholds and Free Energy of Brownian Directed Polymers with\\ Product and Radia'] Let \(V:\R^d\to[0,\infty)\) be bounded and Borel measurable.  Then, for \(h\ge0\), the limit
\begin{equation}
  \lim_{T\to\infty}\frac1T
