as $n \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.347223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d77eb20014673b2af360390a3d95630d0e91b9dd9a0290ba3b3cd57f9c656c51","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $x_1,\dots,x_n \stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim} \mathcal{N}(0,I_d)$ and let $p(n,d) = \mathbb{P}\{\exists S \succeq 0 :\ x_i^{\top} S x_i = d \ \forall i\}$.
\begin{enumerate}
