{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.855321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d78753f6910bede5747d7b234def76cf020c8545f47bfa8a9d89f8fa9a941e3f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2605.20041, '\makeatletter \HRule \\[0.4cm] { \huge \bfseries Fourier Representations of Spectral Densi'] The two following assertions are equivalent:
\vspace{-\parskip}
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item Condition \ref{condition:longMemoryAutocovariances} is satisfied with $L_{1}$ quasi-monotone,
\item Condition \ref{condition:longMemorySpectralDensity} is satisfied with $L_{2}$ quasi-monotone.
\end{enumerate}
\vspace{-\parskip}
In addition, if one of these assertions is satisfied, the spectral measure of $(X_{t})_{t \in \mathbb{Z}}$ is absolutely continuous, and the Fourier series of its spectral density converges everywhere on $(0,\pi]$ and diverges to $+\infty$ at 0. Moreover, Condition \ref{condition:longMemorySpectralDensity} holds with $f$ the sum of the Fourier series of the spectral density, and we have $$L_{2}(x) \underset{x \to 0}{\sim} L_{1}\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\frac{1}{x}\right)\frac{1}{\pi}\Gamma(2d)\cos(d\pi),\,\text{and}~L_{1}(x) \underset{x \to +\infty}{\sim} L_{2}\hspace{-1.6pt}\left(\frac{1}{x}\right)2\Gamma(1-2d)\sin(d\pi).$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.106298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d78b694c5474be401544dae1b925c16697dfeaeb351c1aca6a561a05f7eee7de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma random-walk of arXiv:2505.04942, '\textbf{Randomized Routing to Remote Queues}'] Assume condition~(equation eq:rmk-inequality of the paper) holds. Then with probability 1,
