{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.118491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d79d0dce02aa569ccb30c2cbf05f2b80127fd5864ec884721bf9281862cc30bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: DHX input for specific rare event of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Recall that $u_i$ is the center of $\mathsf{B}_i$ and let $\bar{\partial}\mathsf{B}_i=\partial\mathsf{B}_i\cup\partial\Lambda_{M/2}(u_i)\cup \partial\Lambda_{M/4}(u_i)$. There exists a constant $c_5>0$ such that for any $1\le i\le n$, any external field $h\in\mathbb R^{\Lambda_N}$ and any set $I\subset \mathsf{B}_i$, we have  \begin{align}
