{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.340123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7a4c88a8b6b20a3a0d7cfb1a02fc72a5e2daa68c16c3553643f92b91ca7df25","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition BBM fixed splitting time, tail estimate of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$ and consider the same BBM as in Proposition~(proposition: aBBM exceeding probability of the paper). Recall that $\mathcal{N}_T$ is the index set of all particles at the terminal time $T$. There exist constants $C,c,c_1,c_2>0$ and thresholds $K_*,T_*>0$ such that, for all integers $N\geq1$ with $T=N\Delta t\geq T_*$, all $K_0\geq K_*$, all
	$n\in\mathbb{Z}_+$, and every deterministic subset $\Gamma\subset\mathcal{N}_T$,
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}
			&\mathbb{P}\Bigl(\exists\,v\in\Gamma\colon
			Y_T^{\alpha,v}\geq A(T)+K_0-n\Bigr)\\
