{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.877384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7beec3105e6813e7eea94b70f995ac0e8b02d070028fa2705c6f37d48f1774b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:heightone-singlecross of arXiv:2608.09368, 'A proof of Ross's conjecture for two-site moving-target search'] Let $H,L$ be a height-one pair and let
