{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.884020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7c25bee30d1abf4f2bd0cc8eae0208adb92732acd630dbbacc28c3acc8b88f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:central_lemma of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] For an inverse temperature $\beta$ sufficiently small, the following statements are true:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For all $\theta > 0$,	
