{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.889479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7eef61154dd814a681928454d9329c3c22aeb4604e77f7af249dd30a4c285ed","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:doblerpeccati of arXiv:2505.11389, '\bf The Poisson Multiplication Formula'] Fix $p\in [1,2]$. Suppose that $F$ is a $\sigma(\eta)$-measurable random variable such that $\mathbb{P}(|F|<\infty) = 1$ and that there exists $M\geq 1$ such that:
