{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.914983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7ef1e0513a8858950af8aa8986eb2baf182fd0163d5dc43dbc3aa8342523501","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma size_biasing_for_Poisson_zoo of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Let us assume that $\Gamma \leq \mathrm{Aut}(G)$ is a transitive and unimodular subgroup of automorphisms, $\nu_{o}$ is a $\Gamma$-rotation invariant measure on $\mathcal{H}_{o}$, $\nu$ is the measure on $Z$ induced from $\nu_{o}$ via (equation def:induced_measure_on_zoospace of the paper) and $\mathcal{X} = \sum_{i \in I} \delta_{(x,H)_i} \sim \mathcal{Q}_{\nu}^\lambda$. Given some $R \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{ + \infty \}$ and $x \in V(G)$, consider the restricted processes $\mathcal{X}^R := \mathcal{X} \mathds{1} \left[ Z^R \right]$ and $\mathcal{X}_x^R := \mathcal{X} \mathds{1} \left[ Z^R( \{ x \} ) \right]$. Then we have
