{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.292933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7f0c3b1d710c0a681d448a95fa53015a02d7842f6bb25994b9765f953512b23","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:metriccc of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] Provided the constant $\varepsilon>0$ was chosen sufficiently small and $n$ is sufficiently large, we have:
