{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.186453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7f778116f5bf22cd5a8ede478cd113f39b13c855ea2e79eec7bf10c0ef99687","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:cutoff of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] A model $(T_n)_{n\ge 1}$  exhibits a (worst-case)  \red[cutoff] if
\begin{eqnarray*}
\forall \varepsilon\in(0,1),\qquad \frac{{\rm t}_{\textsc{mix}}^{(n)}(1-\varepsilon)}{{\rm t}_{\textsc{mix}}^{(n)}(\varepsilon)} & \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{} &  1.
\end{eqnarray*}
Equivalently, the function $t\mapsto {\rm d}_{\textsc{tv}}^{(n)}(t)$, suitably rescaled,  approaches a step function as $n\to\infty$, i.e. there is a sequence of non-negative numbers $(\theta_n)_{n\ge 1}$ such that for any fixed $t\ge 0$, 
\begin{eqnarray*}
{\rm d}_{\textsc{tv}}^{(n)}(\theta_n t) & \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{} & \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
1 & \textrm{if }t<1\smallskip\\
0 & \textrm{if }t>1.
\end{array}
\right.
\end{eqnarray*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.775807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7f7e4a32bf2abd314a2dc5d07f041a2c9b2a5e5cd627e09a1a913bbcd1038e4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Cumulant expansion) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Let $X$ be a random variable such that $\expec{\e^{tX}}$ exists for all $t$ 
in an open interval $(-\delta,\delta)$, and write 
\begin{equation}

 \expec{\e^{tX}} = \sum_{n\geqs0} \mu_n\frac{t^n}{n!}\;, 
 \qquad 
 \mu_n = \expec{X^n}\;.
\end{equation} 
Then the \emph{cumulant expansion} of $X$ is given by 
\begin{equation}

 K_X(t) = \log\expec{\e^{tX}}
 = \sum_{n\geqs0} \kappa_n \frac{t^n}{n!}\;.
\end{equation} 
The coefficients $\mu_n$ are called \emph{moments} of $X$, while the 
$\kappa_n$ are called \emph{cumulants}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.662002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7fba3647dec14b31bdadb5ac9408d0abbbd863e68de1a344e8fa45ebcf5e685","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 (generalized moving-subspace bound) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] Let $(\rho,\Lambda)$ be a positive survival datum for
$(\mathsf G,\mathsf H,E,\ell,\Omega)$, and let $\tau<\Lambda$.  Write
\begin{equation}
 D_\rho=\dim\ran\rho,
 \qquad
 r_\rho=\rank K_\rho(o,o).

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \vartheta'(\mathfrak G_t(\tau))\leq
