{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.426407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8303f6852af0b44123c75dce598910f5d79cfc441f8275ed530e94e8ef68dd5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:singleCol of arXiv:2508.03577, 'Phase Transitions in a Particle Model\\ for the Self-Adaptive Response to Cancer Dynamics'] Let $\alpha>0$ and $0<p=1-q<1$. Let $\left(X_t\right)_{t\ge 0}$ be the continuous-time Markov process on $\left\{0,1,\ldots, M\right\}$ specified by the following transition rates $Q\colon \left\{0,\ldots,M\right\}^2\to\mathbb{R}$
