{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.958976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d849f17a85fcd8332a3e0d7394aa5a569e62e032f44eb1b49d0fe9876d15d3fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] If there exists a function $L$ slowly varying at infinity such that the random variable $Z$ satisfies
