{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.602149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d85c1bcf1abd66f5a48002e75773580546a65cd2805c7537072437e609efbaa0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lower of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] There exists an absolute constant $c_{-}>0$ such that, for every fixed $r>0$,
