{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.129049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d89a632ca4aabb9a1061111207cace19967383c25aaa73aabfc35fe7d5652699","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:BM of arXiv:2411.16058, 'Gaussian deconvolution on $\mathbb R^d$ \\ with application to self-repellent Brownian mot'] Let $d > 4$ and $\alpha$ be sufficiently small.
