{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.053729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8b22c4ae1f6dfb95f0c9d2118508ba49694b89ad88842bb5ebf7016d5e78bca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 44 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Fix an admissible scale-dependent selection rule $\mathsf s$ on a domain $\D^{\mathsf s}_{\gamma}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$.  Let $p\in[1,\infty)$.
If $0<\gamma<1$ and $H\in L^p\big(\Omega; \D^{\mathsf s}_{\gamma}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)\big)$, then $R^{\mathsf s}:=\hat\Lambda^{\mathsf s}_{S,\gamma,\alpha}H$ satisfies
