{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.720628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d925408e10e34fb8ad7ad78705c114dbea26a88a6a142dc1746b2de78faca4bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:poincare of arXiv:2609.02769, 'Divergence-Free Approximation in Sobolev and Lebesgue Spaces on general unbounded domains '] {Brezis-2011}, [Ern-2021]}]
		Let $\mathfrak{D}\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain and let
		\(1\le q<\infty\). Then there exists a constant
		$C=C(\mathfrak{D},q)>0$ such that
		\begin{align}
