{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.047624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d95c3d9a8958238e98d7cd1c5412dfe82719c862dd5c56771cd2a9874ab4c7d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma upper bound of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] There is a universal constant $C<\infty $ such that for all $n\geq 2$, $t\geq 0$ and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$,
