{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.888191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d960d10b7c76de2e30e5e2e9a491eeacf19250b32fb353046d8788ef673a03a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma estimate of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] Let $p\geq 2$ be such that $m_p<\infty$, and $\Phi=\{\Phi(t,x); t\geq 0, x\in\mathbb{R}\}$ be
