{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.505641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d961b4bed756e269d0d3466e00e106905cdc31eef7dfa3bff5f88f31645e6839","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 98 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\beta \in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2}]$ be an index, and let $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times W,D(A))$ and $f \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times W, L(V,D(A^2)))$ be mappings such that \eqref{f0-restriction} and \eqref{f-restriction} are fulfilled. Then the It\^{o}-Lyons map
