{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.348942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9908dcdab2a629475a671063d4aa28622d6a04afe38d428822e8c501e8954c3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:kurtz of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] The operator \fs{${\mathscr G}_{\hat\alpha,k}\coloneqq\Pi_k A_{\hat\alpha,k}|_{\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)}:\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)\to\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)$} is an infinitesimal generator  on $\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k) \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{\Xi_k}$. Moreover,  we have the following  convergence:
