{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.642239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9e3ed1816c4cd8832b2a4abc0391f8f2084ab4d6f8ffd400b2c8c512f3bdf2c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2607.28992, 'Minimal inversion of a permuton sample'] Let $\mu$ be a permuton which admits a piece-wise continuous and strictly positive density $f:[0,1]^2\rightarrow(0,\infty)$ continuous at $(0,0)$ and at $(1,1)$.
    Let $\minv_n^\mu$ be the minimal inversion of $n$ points distributed according to $\mu$, as defined in~\eqref{eq:main}.
    Then, the random variable $\minv_n^\mu$ satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        n^{-1/2}\minv_n^\mu
        \dconv\ray[2,\frac{f(0,0)+f(1,1)}{2}]
    \end{align*}
    as $n$ goes to infinity, where the convergence occurs in distribution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.728733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9e57795d21caa38d9d413ebe45cc6fa644dd3a4b18cbc146e20bdf9481a82e7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Let $(u,v)\in E$ be any edge of the graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximal degree $\Delta$. Assume that Assumption \ref{thiasssumptionnew} holds for the given $p_0\in(0,1)$, then we have, for any $m\geq 1$,
    \begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\mathbb{P}&\left(\sup_{\theta\in[0,\theta_*],\Lambda,\tau_0\in\Omega(\Lambda)}
\sum_{(wz)\in E}|\operatorname{Cor}_{(1-\theta)\otimes\mu^{\tau_0}}^{(2)}(uv,wz)|\geq \Delta m\right)\\&\leq \frac{2}{(1-e^{-\alpha_*})(1-e^{-2\alpha_*})}e^{2\gamma_*}e^{-\alpha_*m},\end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    where $\gamma_*:=\ln\frac{1-p_0}{p_0(\Delta-2)}$ and $\alpha_*=\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{(\Delta-2)^{\Delta-2}}{p_0(\Delta-1)^{\Delta-1}(1-p_0)^{\Delta-2}}.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.134456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9e67ae6f457e40e441010325b045ac9c00b595bc9cd5539da833351d259340c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 (Wall) of arXiv:2608.26698, 'Mapping class groups of simply connected closed spin 5-manifolds with no 2- and 3-torsion '] Let $M$ be a simply connected oriented $n$-manifold with $n \geq 5$, $D \subset M$ be an embedded $n$-disc. Then there is a commutative diagram of exact sequences \[\begin{tikzcd}
