{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.893348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da1f269003ab137c011a9ba56c141c11841eea8c38dca47b0547860501329827","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2412.04527, 'Critical Drift for Brownian Bees and a Reflected Brownian Motion Invariance Principle'] Fix $T>0$ and let $\Lambda_T$ be the set of continuous and strictly increasing bijections $[0,T]\to[0,T]$. Then for $X,Y\in \mathcal{D}([0,T],\mathbb{R})$
\begin{align*}
    d_T(X,Y)&:=\inf_{\lambda \in \Lambda_T}\left\{\sup_{t\in [0,T]}|t-\lambda(t)|\vee \sup_{t\in [0,T]}|X(t)-Y(\lambda(T))|\right\} 
\end{align*}
and for $X,Y\in \mathcal{D}([0,\infty),\mathbb{R})$
\begin{align*}
    d_\infty(X,Y)&:=\sum_{T\in\mathbb{N}}^\infty 2^{-T}(1\wedge d_T(\psi_T(X),\psi_T(Y))).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:44.380993+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da23279065073e5c4c6ea88bf9e99d492439877884d7fb13b9f589c5ca768700","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2609.02819, 'Adelic Points and Unramified Brauer Approximation for Classifying Stacks'] The image of the full localization map is exactly the full Brauer--Manin set:
