{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.685933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da282d8e637ff85477b6c4c8b96bd373ebe39b67d26e28a473c0b059d372fa56","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition \bf Ribbon graph of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $\Sigma$ be a compact surface with or without boundary. A (punctured) ribbon graph $\Upsilon$ with $s$ faces and perimeters $(m_1,\dots,m_s)$ is a quadruple $(\mathcal{V}(\Upsilon), \mathcal{E}(\Upsilon), \iota, \phi)$, where
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(1)] $(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$ is a graph;
    \item[(2)] $\iota: (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E}) \hookrightarrow \Sigma$ is an embedding;
    \item[(3)] $\phi: [s]=\{1,2,\ldots,s\} \to \mathcal{V}$ assigns a marked vertex to each face;
\end{enumerate}
such that
\begin{itemize}
    \item The boundary of the surface lies in the graph: $\partial \Sigma \subset \iota(\Upsilon)$;
    \item The complement $\Sigma \setminus \iota(\Upsilon) = \bigsqcup_{i=1}^{s} D_i$, where each $D_i$ is an oriented $m_i$-gon and $\phi(i) \in \partial D_i$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.658745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da2ae995abd80f8c9dcc06bcaaf126c91dde5c867d7c03d9d1f0ab3eac18c8eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm no_uniform_abs of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] There does not exist a sequence of (possibly randomized) $p$-blind rules~$(\pi_n)$ such that
