{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.309546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da2e9960e93a04bc0808d82a8bf09dbc8c0d9e099d605f063ad059a4992d85f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_irreducible:CPPdrift of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Assume $L$ is a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) with characteristic triplet $(\Sigma_L, \gamma_L, \nu_L)$ such that $\Sigma_L=0$ and $\nu_L$ has finite total mass, i.e. $L$ is a compound Poisson process, possibly with drift $\gamma_L^0 \in \mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$. Assume that the closed semigroup generated by
