{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.263422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da4fb9d1a049327bf696520414efbb7d83c3a4f4460d526ecc6d44e29f02f417","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem bt1 of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] For $d\geq 2$, there is a constant $c_2=c_2(d)>0 $ such that for all fixed $\varepsilon>0 $ and all sequences $\alpha=\alpha(n)$ 
it holds that
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{P}(\chi(G({n},\alpha)) > 2)=\begin{cases}
1 & \text{if }\alpha\geq (c_2+\varepsilon)\cdot n^{-1/d},\\
0 & \text{if }\alpha\leq (c_2-\varepsilon)\cdot n^{-1/d}.
\end{cases}
