{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.238928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da6c6b142f968636c7db811fc5bed6a08b0565ad0e3e40617d227497f4e13353","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2607.26564, 'Stochastic Scalar Conservation Laws on Moving Hypersurfaces'] Let Assumptions \ref{Assumption1} and \ref{Assumption2} hold. Then for every $u_0 \in H^{1,1}(\Gamma_0) \cap L^{\infty}(\Gamma_0)$, there exists a martingale entropy solution $({\Omega}^*,{\mathcal{F}}^*,\{{\mathcal{F}}_t^*\}_{t \in [0,T]},\mathbb{P}^*,u^*,B^*)$ to the stochastic conservation law \eqref{eq74} started from $u_0$. Moreover, $\mathbb{P}^*$-a.s.
\begin{equation}
\|u^*\|_{L^{\infty}(Q_T)} \leq e^{C^*}(1+ \| u_0 \|_{L^\infty(\Gamma_0)}),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{eqnarray*}
C^*&=& (T+1)(L_1+1)(1+\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\nabla_{\Gamma_t} \cdot v(t)\|_{L^{\infty}(\Gamma_t)} +\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|w^*(t)\|_{L^{\infty}(\Gamma_t)}  \nonumber\\
      & & + \sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\nabla_{\Gamma_t}w^*(t)\|_{L^{\infty}(\Gamma_t)} + \sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\Delta_{\Gamma_t}w^*(t)\|_{L^{\infty}(\Gamma_t)}  ),
\end{eqnarray*}
and $w^{*}(t,x) = \int_0^t \sigma(s, G(s, G^{-1}(t,x))) dB^{*}_s, \ (t,x) \in Q_T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.082954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da6cb77ed9029bdd4638347a508f05f24282354490cb86fa75ec6a04b0e61261","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SkotoFM of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] Let  $f_n$ ($n\geq 1$) and $f$ be functions in  $\mathcal{D}$. Suppose that $f_n$ converges to $f$ in $(\mathcal{D},d_{\mathrm{S}})$ and that \begin{align}
