{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.203860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da7068378e79f0e13ea68bf53dbbbd39654aa870798db425e5b0645776213aec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PropCarlo-Levy of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Let $d\in{\mathbb N}$, $H=L^2([0,1]^d)$ and $A$ be the realization of the Laplacian operator with Dirichlet boundary conditions. Assume that $\nu(H\backslash H_{1/4+\delta})=0$ and
\begin{equation}
\int_H {\left|z\right|}_\delta^2+{\left|z\right|}^4_{1/4+\delta}\nu(dz)<+\infty.
\end{equation}
The following two assertions hold true.
\begin{enumerate}
