\item Let $\delta>\frac{d-1}{4}$. Then $\{L_A(t)\}_{t\geq 0}$ is a càdlàg process in $C([0,1]^d)$ and
\[
{\mathbb E}\left[\sup_{t\in [0,T]}{\left\|L_A(t)\right\|}^q_{C([0,1]^d)}\right]<+\infty,\qquad T>0,\, q\in [1,4).
\]
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.352979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da706ca09c374db49f0aee1650d4a3efb5e5c40862911c637e92f217ccddabab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 19 (Theorem 3.1 of \cite{T2}) of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] For all $a\in \R$ and $t\ge 0$, it holds that
