{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.141272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da70f573ab748dddf78a3164d73fa97e939baf148146f4fbd5c17267e8c74f1f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 ({\cite[Lemma  3.1) of arXiv:2604.05861, '\LARGE Quantitative bounds for high dimensional entropic CLT'] {JB04}}]
	Let $Y_1,Y_2$ be independent $\R^d$-valued random vectors.
 Then 
	\begin{equation}
	\rho_{Y_1+Y_2}(Y_1+Y_2)=\E[\rho_{Y_1}(Y_1)\mid Y_1+Y_2]=\E[\rho_{Y_2}(Y_2)\mid Y_1+Y_2].
