{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.497282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da9e654939906389f751685397b6539da4ac22b3fa0e69619f66de19ecfcd5c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] Fix $T,\beta,\varepsilon>0$ and $0\le s<t\le T$. The map 
