{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.860114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_daa582d4b46aa41c36c963e090c56fd9bba5d0192b9de6ebcf904d40f14e1221","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] Let $k \in \N_0$, $F \in \bW^{k+1, p}$, and $\Delta_F^{-1} \in L^q(\Omega)$ for $p,q,r \in (1,\infty)$ satisfying $\frac{2k}{p} + \frac{k+1}{q} \leq \frac{1}{r}$. 
