{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.609041+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_daae2a17aa5680b6334bd3c6f2e77f26562ed1316567396544f537c7b0eb33a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] Fix $T\in\N$ and $m\in\N$. Assume $\Delta<\Delta_0$, where $\Delta_0$ is the constant in Theorem~\ref{thm:main}. Under the assumptions \textup{\textbf{(A1.3)}}, \textup{\textbf{(A2)}} and \textup{\textbf{(A3)}}, given any $m$ test functions $\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_m\in C^2(\T)$ and a function $\Psi\in C_b^3(\R^m)$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \left|\mathbb{E}\Psi\left(\langle\varphi_1,\eta_t^N\rangle,\dots,\langle\varphi_m,\eta_t^N\rangle\right)-\mathbb{E}\Psi\left(\langle\varphi_1,\eta_t\rangle,\dots,\langle\varphi_m,\eta_t\rangle\right)\right|\leq\frac{C\mathrm{e}^{Ct}}{\sqrt{N}},\quad t=0,\dots,T,
    \end{equation}
    where the constant $C>0$ depends on $\Delta,m,\|\Psi\|_{C_b^3},\|F\|_{C^2},\|h\|_{C^2}$ and $\|\varphi_i\|_{C^2}(1\leq i\leq m)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

