{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.314806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dad6dad1dc81255dec2b73a27940ed16b393e522271f8f377d5f150db9285dd0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 53 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] For all $y \in \T^d$ and $h>0$,
    \[\P_U\big(\text{there exists more than one solution to~\eqref{eq:main refreshing ODE 0} on } [0,h]\big) = 1.\]
    Further, for all $y \in \T^d$ and almost surely in $U$, for all $\ep>0$ sufficiently small
    \begin{equation}
