	\item \cite{KKSS} The inclusion $N^n \subseteq M^{n+2}$ is $n$-connected; or
	\item  $M^{n+2}$ admits a $\Z_p^2$ action such that $N^n$ is a fixed-point set component of a $\Z_p$ subgroup and such that there is a second $\Z_p$ subgroup whose fixed-point set component $N'$ has codimension  at most $\frac{n+1}{2}$;
