{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.889850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db8620aa58009dda31335301c72ef1e7c452445e6506bfbbfe8ed2b46fef7d30","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $x\in \mathbb{R}^m$ and let $y\in x^\perp$. Then we have:
