{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.994844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db948a3299b6dd64b61b1f245205162bd9e58ac05234a6fae66029f90dbf8848","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm T loc dim of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Almost surely under $\hat{P}_{\bm{\rho}}$, for every $t \in (0,\infty)$,
