{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.923090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dba6b5cc0fdac722753773a828792704f4628fb1222df44e59e189c5f6746811","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:disInt of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] On the event $\Omega_1$, the following holds  for every $\xi\in\Xi$. \vspace{2pt}\\ 
       \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
           \item  For every $t\in\mathbb{R}$, there exist bijections $\sigma_t^-: \mathfrak S_{t,\xi}^L \to \mathcal{T}^{\xi,-}$ and $\sigma_t^+: \mathfrak S_{t,\xi}^R \to \mathcal{T}^{\xi,+}$  such that, for any $x\in \mathfrak S^L_{t,\xi}$,  $\sigma_{(x,t)}^- :=\sigma_t^-(x)$ is the unique element of $\mathcal{T}^{\xi,-}$ satisfying   $\sigma_{(x,t)}^-(t) = x$, and for $x \in \mathfrak S_{t,\xi}^R$, $\sigma_{(x,t)}^+ :=\sigma_t^+(x)$ is the unique element of $\mathcal{T}^{\xi,+}$ satisfying  $\sigma_{(x,t)}^+(t) = x$.  
           \item  For any $x<y$ in $\mathfrak S^L_{t,\xi}$ (resp $\mathfrak S_{t,\xi}^R$), we have
           \begin{equation}
               \sigma_{(x,t)}^-(r)<\sigma_{(y,t)}^-(r), \quad\text{\rm(resp. $\sigma_{(x,t)}^+(r)<\sigma_{(y,t)}^+(r)$)} \qquad \forall r\in\mathbb{R}.
           \end{equation}
           In other words, leftmost (resp. rightmost) bi-infinite interfaces associated with different points in $\mathfrak S^L_{t,\xi}$ (resp. $\mathfrak S^R_{t,\xi}$) never meet. In particular, the elements in $\mathcal{T}^{\xi,\pm}$ are disjoint.  
       \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.203417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dba7c20f50d267e031f01bc9f29026a5fc68402664e7cf07e6010f374a06998e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] Let $\mu_0 \in \mathcal P_1(\S^{d-1})$ be the initial distribution, $\empmu_0$ be the empirical measure of \eqref{eq:dynamics_tokens} at initialization, sampled iid from $\mu_0$. Let $r_{d}(N)$ be the rate
