and
\begin{equation*}
  \lim_{n\to\infty}n^{\frac{2}{3}E}\sup_{\substack{|x|\le K\\t\in [T_1,T_2]}}\left| p(t,0,x)-p_n\left( t,0,\frac{\floor{nx}}{n} \right) \right|=0,
\end{equation*}
$P$-almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.656784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbb88883e9ac172f8511e5457d983d272d3993b0b8b412347ab486b791948226","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.01885, 'The Order of the Non-universal Tree of a Hilbert Space with Respect to the Haar Basis'] Let $T$ be a tree on a set $A$. An \textbf{infinite hand} in $T$ is a sequence $(s_n)_{n=0}^\infty\subseteq T$ with the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $(|s_n|)_{n=0}^\infty\subseteq\mathbb N$ is strictly monotone increasing.
\item There exists an element $s\in T$ with $s\sqsubset s_n$ for every $n$; the element of largest length which satisfies this property is called the \textbf{palm} of the infinite hand.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbb892c63d1716d37df3ca32bad4e7bdd79efdfe1a2383f8fc4e744f62335b65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:delta of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] Under any coupling between $\mathbf{X}$ and $\mathbf{Y}$, we have
\begin{align}
    \mleft|
        \operatorname{Cov}[X^i(0), X^j(t)]
    \mright|
    &\leqslant
    2 \sqrt{
        \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^i(0) (X^i(0) - Y^i(0)) \mright] \cdot
        \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^j(t) (X^j(t) - Y^j(t)) \mright]
    } \\

    &\qquad + \mathbb{E} \mleft[ Y^i(0) (X^j(t) - Y^j(t)) \mright]
        + \mathbb{E} \mleft[ (X^i(0) - Y^i(0)) Y^j(t) \mright] \\

    &\qquad + \mathbb{E}\mleft[Y^i(0)\mright] \mathbb{E}\mleft[ X^j(t) - Y^j(t) \mright]
    + \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^j(t) \mright] \mathbb{E} \mleft[ X^i(0) - Y^i(0) \mright].
\end{align}
Moreover, both factors appearing under the square root in (equation decom4631 of the paper) are nonnegative.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.427389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbbafe4c184a48dd9963dba60defade867be3bc1b7c8b013fb40f24d2a321583","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two-point-decompose of arXiv:2605.19419, 'Tail exponents of the three-dimensional uniform spanning tree and Abelian sandpile'] Suppose $4r<R$ and $x\in\partial B_R$, $y\in\partial B_r$. Suppose that $\gamma$ is an ILERW started from $0$. $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ are two independent SRWs started from $x$ and $y$. Write $P_{x,y}$ for their joint law. Let $E$ denote the intersection of the following events:
\begin{itemize}
\item[1.]\ $S_{1}$ hits $0$ and, writing $\tau_{1}$ for the first hitting time of $0$, $S_{1}[0,\tau_{1}]\cap\gamma=\{0\}$.
\item[2.]\ $S_{2}$ hits $\operatorname{LE}(S_1[0,\tau_1])$ before it intersects $\gamma$.
\end{itemize}
Then,
\begin{equation}
P_{x,y}(E)\gtrsim (\log r)^{-1}R^{-1-\alpha}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

