{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.997281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbc729eec0966fc2dc0843ba64c5518cf3e65dec5a91d4f6c5009de3363ef7e6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:GAP1 of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $Q\ge 2$ and let $\delta>0$. Then there exists $c>0$, depending only on $Q$, such that if $\phi \in \mathcal{C}_Q$ with $\phi(-\infty)=0$ and $\phi(\infty)=2\pi Q$ satisfies 
\begin{align}
\textup{dist}(\phi, \mathcal{M}^Q):=\inf_{\xi_1,\dots, \xi_Q \in \mathbb{R}} \| \phi-m_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k} \|_{L^2(\mathbb{R})} \ge \delta>0,

\end{align}

\noindent
then
\begin{align*}
E(\phi) \ge \inf_{\phi \in \mathcal{C}_Q } E(\phi)   +c \inf_{\xi_1,\dots, \xi_Q \in \mathbb{R}} \| \phi-m_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k} \|_{L^2(\mathbb{R})}^2 \ge \inf_{\phi \in \mathcal{C}_Q } E(\phi)+  c \delta^2.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.350783+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbc749c84012c10ac36d23e44d879db72ad1c323719f22621d3730287ed2285e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2511.07350, 'Decoupling of clusters in independent sets in a percolated hypercube'] There exists a universal constant $\gamma > 0$ such that for $p > \fr{1}{2} - \gamma$,
