{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.859292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1703dc7cc995841e21df001b7d3bcd6b456e11337f3c559177a1fa048e1f9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] Let $0<\theta<\frac{1}{2\gamma}$. Then, for any $\delta\in(0,1)$, $\beta\in(0,\frac12)$ and $K>0$, there exists a $T_{\delta,\beta,K}>0$, such that for all $T\geq T_{\delta,\beta,K}$ and any $x\in\R$, $y>0$ with
    \[\abs x\abs\leq T^{\beta/2}\quad\text{and}\quad \left|y-\theta T\right|\leq K\,T^\beta\]
    it holds
    \begin{equation*}
        (1-\delta)\,C_\theta\,A(T)\leq\P_x(Z_T\leq y)\leq (1+\delta)\,C_\theta\,A(T),
