{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1ab3a8b6f8f53abb021eaee690b6c19cc57edc20adc0f8f8872316d92e1156","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 ({Theorem 2.3 of \cite{MSS23}}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] For any $\alpha>0$, there exist $C, k, \gamma > 0$ such that if $(G, \weight)$ satisfies conditions \eqref{eq:Nbalanced}-\eqref{eq:Nescaping} with $\alpha$ and $D,\theta \leq n^{\gamma}$, then for any $\delta > n^{-\gamma}$,
