for all $t\ge 0$, implying that the first moment of the root distribution of $p(x,t)$ grows linearly in time.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.931038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc3f33bbdc3e49228c8c55a16c28505cd60aabba7ffca29fae3fdc2c49c46f89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:blsBis of arXiv:2602.04673, 'Brownian paths as loop-decorated SLEs'] Consider the couplings from Theorem~(th:bls of the paper).
