{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.222125+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc45dd6469e49e91ff677c545717e7bb2ec80778646b8899373dfcca97391d48","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 25 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] Let $D$ be an  open subset in $\R^d (d\geq 3)$ and  $R_0>0$.
Assume for each $x\in\R^d,$ $z\mapsto j(x, z)$ is positive and for each  $R\in (0, R_0)$ and $x_0\in\R^d,$
\begin{equation}
\inf_{z\in \R^d:  R/16\leq |z|<R/2} j(x_0, z)>0.
\end{equation}
Suppose  for each  $x_0\in\R^d, R\in (0, R_0)$ and $0<p<q\leq 1,$ there exists $c_1=c_1(x_0, R, p, q)>1$  such that  for any $x\in B(x_0, pR)$ and $y\in B(x_0, qR)^c,$
\begin{equation}
c_1^{-1}J(x_0, y)\leq J(x, y) \leq c_1J(x_0, y).
\end{equation}
Then  for each $z_0\in \partial D$ and $R\in (0, \tfrac{1}{16}R_0),$
there exists a constant  $C=C(z_0, R)\geq 1$   independent of the geometry of $D$ such that   for   any  nonnegative  regular harmonic functions $f$ and $g$
on $D\cap B(z_0, R)$   vanishing  on  $(D^c)^r\cap B(z_0, R),$
\begin{equation}
f(x)g(y)\leq Cf(y)g(x)  \quad \hbox{for } x, y\in D\cap B(z_0, R/32).
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if \eqref{e:4.27} and \eqref{e:4J} hold uniformly for $x_0\in\R^d,$
then BHP \eqref{e:Xb} holds with $C=C(R)\geq 1$ uniformly for $z_0\in \partial D$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc45e50d9deb88ddc2fba582be4e90e76d2f902640f451c6d0f0cbc3fbd5991d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma TSP-E-L-A-1 of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] Suppose $\left| {t - {t_0}} \right|{\left\| u \right\|_1} \lesssim 1$. Let $w{\left( t ,x \right)}$ be the solution of the transport equation
\begin{equation*}
\left\{ {\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}
