{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.727660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc60742db19f59a00edaf72c8a3804ce262e583a19f2376fd2f08a3365c49be1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:new of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $(u(t,\cdot))_{t>0} \subseteq  \mathcal P_* $ be a distributional solution to the FPE (equation eq:Main_FPE_our_paper of the paper) in the sense of (def:FPE-sol of the paper) with initial condition $\zeta \in \mathcal P$ and coefficients $(a, b): \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathcal P_* \to \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}^d$ for some $\mathcal P_* \subseteq \mathcal P_{\textup{ac}} $, and assume further (equation eq:integrability_our_paper of the paper). Let $f: \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathcal D(f) \to \mathbb{R} $ with $\mathcal D(f) \subseteq \mathcal P_{\textup{ac}}$ be as in (lem:many-PDEs_new of the paper),
        and assume further
        \begin{equation}
            \big[(t,x)\mapsto f(x,u(t,\cdot))\big] \in L^1_{\textup{loc}}(\mathbb{R}_+;W^{1,1}(\mathbb{R}^d)).
        \end{equation}
        Then there exists a weak solution $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ to 
        \begin{equation}
        \begin{dcases}
            dX_t = \left( b(X_t,u(t,\cdot)) + \frac{\nabla f(X_t,u(t,\cdot))}{u(t,X_t)} \right) dt + \sqrt{2}\left( a(X_t,u(t,\cdot)) + \frac{f(X_t,u(t,\cdot))}{u(t,X_t)} \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} dW_t, \\
            \mathcal{L}(X_t) = u(t,x)dx,\quad t>0,
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation}
    with $\mathcal{L}(X_0) = \zeta$, with the same convention for the coefficients on $\{u=0\}$ as in (lem:many-PDEs_new of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.741120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc60cbe82590b45fa9314d31102779adb332fd5c392e874eeccb36097564f0d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2605.14206, 'The clumsy coupon collector's problem'] Suppose words in $L_1.L_2$ have a \emph{unique factorisation}
