{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.903303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc65bfb76801f256b71ae5585ca69dabffbb8480c1e86eacbe34ccd2fa964d8a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:KPZ of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] \ 
Let $h^\varepsilon$ be the solution of the mollified 2D KPZ equation (equation eq:2DKPZ of the paper) with disorder strength $\beta_\varepsilon=(\hat\beta+o(1)) \sqrt{\frac{2\pi}{\log \frac{1}{\varepsilon}}}$ for some $\hat\beta\in (0,1)$. Then for any test function $\phi\in C_c(\mathbb{R}^2)$, we have
\begin{align}
