{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.496214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc66fa1e92e9c2a316c5c9a9c6b4bb3fe6064ecbaaa7d113b55bb5e4025f46ad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Let $u:\Omega_\tau\to\mathcal H$ be Borel and suppose that
\begin{align*}
 u\in\mathbb D^{1,p}(\mathcal H)
 \qquad\text{for every finite }p,
\end{align*}
where $\mathbb D^{1,p}(\mathcal H)$ is the usual Malliavin Sobolev space \cite{Bogachev10}.
Define
\begin{align*}
 \mathbf u(\omega)(t)=\int_0^t u(\omega)_r\,\dd r,
 \qquad
 T_u(\omega)=\omega+\mathbf u(\omega).
\end{align*}
Suppose moreover that, for some $d\ge0$,
\begin{align}
 \|u\|_{\mathcal H}\le Cd,\qquad
 \|D_{\mathcal H}u\|_{\HS}\le Cd,\qquad
 \|D_{\mathcal H}u\|_{\rm op}\le\frac12
\end{align}
$\mathbf P$-almost surely. Then $(T_u)_\#\mathbf P\sim\mathbf P$
and
\begin{align*}
 \operatorname{Ent}\bigl((T_u)_\#\mathbf P\mid\mathbf P\bigr)
 \le C_{\rm Ram}d^2,
\end{align*}
where $\operatorname{Ent}(\cdot\mid\cdot)$ denotes relative entropy and
$C_{\rm Ram}$ depends only on the fixed constant $C$ in
\eqref{eq:Ramer-small}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.084291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc697364f130a0d4f03f08b643599b12aa13068200278304c58ddd6cd455d582","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary InverseGammaU of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] Let $S$ be a random variable with an inverse Gamma distribution of parameters $\alpha$ and $\beta$ given by $\alpha=\frac{d+2}{2}$, $\beta=\frac{|m|^2}{4}$. Let $B_t$ be the standard $d$-dimensional Brownian motion. Then, for $m\in\mathbb{Z}^d$, with $m\ne 0$,
