    All the above constants are only dependent on $\lambda, \mu, C$ and $\alpha$. Their closed forms are given in (equation eq: constants for L-p norm of the paper) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.035351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc72dae5b29423d183514d787c353083e67c4e3b050b5dda0434f74bf3e90631","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition dhe of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] {wom}}}] 
	A modular form $f(z)\in M_k(\Gamma_0(N), \chi)$ is called a Hecke eigenform if for every $m\ge 2$ there is a complex number $\lambda(m)$ for which
	\begin{align}
		f(z)\mid T_m=\lambda(m)f(z).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

