{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.659248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc8a516c3d1e5f9f84a201d18d73ff20ab8108a79b76b840c66407bf0b74433e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Scalability of random matrices) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Let $(\r,\c)$ be an $m\times n$ $\delta$-smooth margin and let $\X$ be an $m\times n$ nonnegative random matrix with independent entries. Denoting $p_{0}=\max_{i,j} \P(\X_{ij}=0)$,
