{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.367734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc97b5817fe856ac9636dc74c93aba438bdf001ba2cb9a06eeab9eb68b80a0f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:IBP-with-cutoff of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $s\in[0,1]$, $a>0$, $d,d_1, k\in\mathbb{N}$, $\chi'\in\mathrm{Cut}_{d_1}$,

and $h\in\mathcal{C}^k({\mathbb{R}}^d)$. 

There exists $p^*=p^*(k)\in[1,\infty)$ and $k^*=k^*(k)\in\mathbb{N}$ such that the following hold.
Let $\mathcal{X}$, $\mathcal{Y}$ be ${\mathbb{R}}^d$-valued random variables, $\mathcal{Z}$ be an ${\mathbb{R}}^{d_1}$-valued random variable, all three belonging to $\mathbb{D}_s^{k^*,p^*}$, and $\Gamma,\mu$ be  $(0,\infty)$-valued random variables such that $\mu$ is $\mathcal{F}_s$-measurable and one has
$\mathbb{E}_s^B\Gamma^{-p^*}\leq \mu^{p^*}$ almost surely

and on the event $\{|\mathcal{Z}|\leq 2^{k}a\}$ one has 
\begin{equ}
    \mathcal{M}_s:=\big(\scal{D_{\mathcal{H}^\perp_s} \mathcal{X}^i,D_{\mathcal{H}^\perp_s} \mathcal{X}^j}_{\mathcal{H}_s^{\perp}}\big)_{i,j=1,\ldots,d}\succeq \Gamma\, \mathrm{id}.
\end{equ}




Then 
there exists a constant $N=N(k,d,d_1,a,\chi')$ such that for any $i_1,\ldots,i_k\in\{1,\ldots,d\}$ one has almost surely
    \begin{equs}
