			L^{\Phi}(Q\times \Omega )$-weak $\digamma\,\Sigma $, where $\varrho $ denote the
			canonical mapping of $\mathfrak{X}^{\Phi}_{A}$ into $\mathcal{X}^{\Phi}_{A}$, and the
			function $\varrho (u)$ is defined by $\varrho (u)\equiv \varrho
			(u(x,\omega,\cdot ))$ for a.e. $(x,\omega )\in Q\times \Omega $;

			\item[(ii)] $\left\| u^{\varepsilon }\right\| _{L^{\Phi}(Q\times \Omega
				)}\rightarrow \left\| \varrho (u)\right\| _{L^{\Phi}(Q\times \Omega ; \mathcal{X}^{\Phi}_{A})}$.
