{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.302750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dca8d2f5e0450b162af8f5a160fd266713473467d596a84282fadcb9c0b579a7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:H-1_kernel_young of arXiv:2505.10256, 'Stochastic Oscillators out of equilibrium:\\ scaling limits and correlation estimates'] We have the following properties: 
\begin{itemize}
\item[a)]
For any two real functions $f,g\in \ell^2(\mathbb{T}_N)$, and for all $A>0$, we have that 
\begin{equation}

|\langle f,K_N*g\rangle_{\ell^2(\mathbb T_N)}|\leq \frac{A}{2}\|f\|^2_{-1,N}+\frac{1}{2A}\|g\|^2_{-1,N}.
\end{equation}
\item [b)] We have that 
\begin{equation}

N^2 \big(K_N(0) - K_N(1) \big) \le 1/2. 
\end{equation}

\item[c)]
For any $x>0$, we have that 
\begin{equation}

K_N(x)-K_N(x+1)=\frac{1}{N^2}\Big\{\frac{1-K_N(0)}{2}-\sum_{j=1}^{x}K_N(j)\Big\}.
\end{equation}
Note that the case $x<0$ can be covered using the fact that the kernel $K_N$ is even real.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

