{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.339303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dcc2d0c3b6bfbd8b4d2e059c39559b50f5de3efadd25eb6816e83889e26e7cda","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Let $V\in\mathcal{V}^\mathbb{B}$, and $a,b\in \mathbf{R}$. Suppose that $H\in \mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}_s(A)\cap\mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}_s(V)$ and $K\in \mathcal{L}^\mathbb{B}_s(A)$.
