{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.694001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dcc948444e23c2ff1768e0cb0788773879cc3824db0d819806239a953aea9baa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp prpObsExpMomentBound_corr of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] Let $T>0$ and $a\in \mathbb{R}$. For any $0\leq s< t\leq T$ we have
\begin{equation}
