{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.740788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dccc0d4c34f0e6e72e74e75af2085e6481fa7fde54cf1cd470101542adb31a20","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:stopping_times of arXiv:2603.24803, 'Critical Spectral Invariants in Random Walks with Geometric Resetting'] Define the following random times:

\begin{align*}
&\tau_0 := \inf\{\, n \ge 1 :X_n = 0 \,\}, \text{(first passage to $0$),} \\[4pt]\\
&\tau_a:= \inf\{\, n \ge 1 :X_n = a \,\}, \text{(first passage to $a$),} \\[4pt]\\
&\tau := \min\{\tau_0, \tau_a\}, \text{(first exit from $(0,a)$).}
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.041405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dcd10962968ee9c33d6d6fc5442b3319055363f2d31b4debd1acf225809ef9af","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 (All good) of arXiv:2606.27035, 'R\'emy's diffusion on Brownian trees'] The following events occur with a probability tending to $1$ as $n \to \infty$:
