{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.835995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd5f014ee9eb51aedf1dfa177e45c22870cf65706bbced803cb8f1a43fae5b7b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 (Explicit Poisson domination) of arXiv:2607.16833, 'Dynamical Equations for Poisson Galton--Watson Trees and Component Densities of Sparse Inh'] If $\lambda=uD<1$, then $T_u$ is stochastically dominated, uniformly in the root
