{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.089790+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd63f4da98b0025493b414fd274bb7af583f7f85174748d6b69f1006604029ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def.relstab of arXiv:2504.19553, 'Extremal Ising Gibbs States on Lobachevsky lattices'] A configuration $\sigma^0 \in \Omega$ is $c$-stable if there exists a strictly positive constant $c>0$ such that the following inequality holds {\color{purple} [Matteo: Est-ce qu'on utilise cette definition après?]}
