{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.793349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd73180d6a2ece68c99150a7c9344d3074a7f7fcbcfa489f2c53314f998307f2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 57 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $(\XX,\metr)$ be a non-empty quasi-metric space
 with modulus of concavity $K\ge 1$, let $x\in \XX$, and let $r>0$.
 Then, for every $y \in \ball(x,r)$ we have
