{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.084234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd86bb8fc0b1e6a2707ce1c3bb1949e0615f995def812da58850f7d8bcd70fbe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:varconv of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For each $t>0$, $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3$,  $\delta>0$, we have \begin{align*}
