{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.033369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dda273f622aeedcd11d3874f5e01a998ef7cc742a4c6b6de9099e16c95f041b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ef of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Under the assumption of Theorem (d32 of the paper),
there exists an almost sure event $\bar{\Omega}^\prime$ such that
for every  $\omega \in \bar{\Omega}^\prime$ and every   $ t \in [0,\infty)$,
the mapping

\[ \mathbb R^d \ni x \mapsto \phi_{0,t}(x)(\omega)\in \mathbb R^d\]

 is a surjective homeomorphism.

Moreover,  on $\bar{\Omega}^\prime$, for every $T\ge 0$,   we have:
\begin{equation}
 \phi_{0,t}^{-1}(x) =  \phi_{0,T}^{-1} ( \phi_{t,T}(x)),\;\;   \, x \in \mathbb R^d,\ t\in[0,T].
