Here and in  the remainder of this paper, we denote by $\phi_{0,t}^{-1}$  the inverse of $\phi_{0,t}$. Finally, on $\bar{\Omega}^\prime$, for every $x \in \mathbb R^d$, the process
\begin{equation} 
 [0,\infty) \ni  t  \mapsto \phi_{0,t}^{-1}(x) \in \mathbb R^d
