{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.687491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddb734d93d3f30191f701999b6faf8e258d69e2ab244138d7cecb83ad39952cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Classification of the $2n$-sum range of arXiv:2609.01926, 'On Sum Ranges for $3n$-convergence'] Let $\sum A = \lim_{k \to \infty} \sum_{n=1}^{2k} a_n$ be a series of real numbers that $2n$-converges to $x$. Then $\textnormal{SR}_2(A)$ is one of the following:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(1)] The whole of $\mathbb{R}$;
        \item[(2)] The singleton $\{x\}$;
        \item[(3)] A shifted additive subgroup of the form $r + \Gamma$, where $r \in \mathbb{R}$ and $\Gamma \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ is any countable additive subgroup. Note that case (2) is a special case where $r = x$ and $\Gamma = \{0\}$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.309064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddb76804885b9473445e61b9972f7ddc136de4a1b09c8fd986955730cffe32f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Girsanov of arXiv:2603.14302, 'On Partition Functions for Time-Inhomogeneous Branching Random Walks'] (Cameron-Martin-Girsanov formula)
     Let $X = (X_1,...,X_n)$ be a Gaussian vector under the law $\mathbb{P}$, with mean $\mu$ and covariance matrix $V$. Let $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}^n$ be a vector and we define a new probability measure by:\begin{equation*}
         \frac{d\tilde{\mathbb{P}}}{d\mathbb{P}}=\frac{e^{\langle \alpha,X\rangle}}{\mathbb{E}[e^{\langle \alpha,X\rangle}]}
     \end{equation*}
     (here $\langle \alpha,X\rangle$ is the scalar product of two vectors $\alpha$ and $X$) Then under $\tilde{\mathbb{P}}$, $X$ is still a Gaussian vector, with covariance matrix $V$ and mean $\mu+V\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.317335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddb834ed4c58ca3ad67154a2404e77f3226007d877d5a36380743c87e126324e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2506.20470, 'Pivot probabilities and norm effects in Gaussian elimination for $\beta$-ensembles'] Let $A$ be a $2 \times 2$ GUE matrix and GEPP pivot comparisons use the $L^1$ norm (as in LAPACK). Then the pivot probability is
