\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.825131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddbbe5df63ff909a147251a16429d2ddee5a52fb3c2279c7a47012f11a2960e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2609.02104, 'Conformal Ricci Curvature and Spectral Estimates'] Let $\Omega\Subset M^4$ be smooth, bounded, and connected. Assume that $R_g>0$ and $\frac{Q_g}{R_g}\geq-\kappa$ on $\Omega$ for some $\kappa\in\mathbb R$. Then
