{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.899067+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddbd6636c1b5f1fb28c43482e2e707b480ebb5e5213b563f4bff323d3d2e818f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:limitingF_SSK of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] When no external field is present ($h=0$), the free energy of SSK exhibits the following convergence in distribution as $N\to\infty$.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item In the high temperature regime, $\beta<1$,
 \begin{equation} 
N(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to\mathcal{N}(-\frac12 \sigma^2,\sigma^2)
 \end{equation} 
where
$\sigma^2=-\frac12\log(1-\beta^2)$.  

\item In the low temperature regime, $\beta>1$,
 \begin{equation} 
\frac{2N^{2/3}}{\beta-1}(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to TW_1.
 \end{equation} 
\end{enumerate} 
The limiting free energy $F(\beta)$ in this setting is given by the formula
 \begin{equation} 
F(\beta)=\begin{cases}
\frac14\beta^2& \text{for }\beta\leq1,\\
\beta-\frac12\log\beta-\frac34 & \text{for }\beta\geq1.
\end{cases}
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.075880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddc1544fa56ef26e22ac20b2f4c6140622d9580569d11520d5469a5890fd0e84","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 7. cor: GW tree satisfies the sub-aging assumption of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Define a probability measure $\tilde{p} = (\tilde{p}_{k})_{k \geq 1}$ on $\mathbb{N}$ 
