       I_{\psi_0}(\psi):=\inf\bigg\{\frac{1}{2}\|f\|_{L^2(0,T;\mathcal{H}_{0,1})}^2+&\frac{1}{2}\|g\|^2_{L^2(0,T;\mathcal{H}_{0,2})}:\notag\\ &\hspace{-1cm} f\in L^2(0,T;\mathcal{H}_{0,1}),\ g\in L^2(0,T;\mathcal{H}_{0,2}),\ \psi=\psi^{\psi_0,f,g} \bigg\}.
   \end{align}
In particular, $\Psi^{\tau,\psi_0}$ also satisfies a large-deviation principle on $\mathcal{E}$ uniformly on compact subsets of $\mathcal E_0$, with speed $1/\tau$ and the same rate function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

