{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.257972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de4fdd829860a83309fe373fa82abe65c5fb509cc35300f9ab2f8b7f1dbca853","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:3 of arXiv:2410.23250, 'Strict inequalities for arm exponents in planar percolation'] Fix $t\in [0,1/2]$.   Let $A,B,S,T\subset[n]$ pairwise disjoint. Let $F,G:\{0,1\}^n\times\{0,1\}^n\to \mathbb R$ such that
  \begin{itemize}
  \item $F(\omega,\omega_t)$ is  measurable w.r.t.\@ $\{(\omega(x),\omega_t(x))\:: \: x\in A\cup S\cup T\}$, 
  \item  $G(\omega,\omega_t)$ is measurable w.r.t.\@ $\{(\omega(x),\omega_t(x))\:: \: x\in B\cup S\cup T\}$,
  \item $F,G$ are both $S$-increasing and $T$-decreasing.
  \end{itemize}
  Then for every $t\in [0,1/2]$
  \begin{equation}
        \mathbb E[F(\omega,\omega_t)G(\omega,\omega_t)]\ge\mathbb E[F(\omega,\omega_t)]\mathbb E[G(\omega,\omega_t)]
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.239755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de521d58127cf677d0f98823998045b68459765375bac724d3c83ee6adb6438d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 2 of arXiv:2603.05174, 'Regularization of the superposition principle: Potential theory meets Fokker-Planck equati'] Let $0\leq s<T<\infty$. 
    A probability $\eta\in \mathcal{P}\left(C([s,T];\mathbb{R}^d))\right)$ is called a solution to the canonical martingale problem (canonical MP) associated to $\left({\sf L}_t\right)_{t\in [s,T]}$, with initial distribution $\nu_s\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ if
    \begin{equation*}
        \int_s^T\int_{B(0,R)} \|b(t,x)\|+\|a(t,x)\| \; \eta_t(dx) dt <\infty, \quad R>0,
    \end{equation*}
    and for all $f\in C_c^{1,2}((s,T)\times \mathbb{R}^d)$ the process $(M(t))_{t\in [s,T]}$ given by
    \begin{equation*}
        M(t):=f(t,\Pi_s(t))-f(s,\Pi_s(s))-\int_s^t\overline{{\sf L}}f(r,\Pi_s(r))\;dr, \quad t\in [s,T]
    \end{equation*}
    is an $\left(\mathcal{F}_s(t)\right)$-martingale with respect to $\eta$, where $\mathcal{F}_s(t):=\sigma\left(\Pi_s(r),s\leq r\leq t\right), t\in [s,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.342417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de532c1e473f175c5fb74f80b4fea0488a7c0378fb87ccb13d7a96e62b0f2fcf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem sec2-thm.2 of arXiv:2602.04303, '\Large\textbf{Strong solutions to SDEs with singular drifts driven by fractional Brownian '] Assume $C>0$ and that the sequence of $\mathcal{F}_T$-measurable random variables $\{F_n\}_{n=1}^\infty\subset L^2(\Omega)$ satisfies the following three conditions:
		\begin{align*}
