		Then, the sequence $\{F_n\}_{n=1}^\infty$ is relatively compact in $L^2(\Omega)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.184892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de54a22625a8087184cbbe500070893a6e168ea9092d730ee59a1dc0cca19560","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RelaxationTimeInduced of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] We can bound the relaxation time $t_{\textup{rel}}^{\textup{ind},+}$ of the additive reversibilisation $\mathbf{X}^{\textup{ind},+}$ of the induced chain $\mathbf{X}^{\textup{ind}}$ by
