{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.604835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de927d23b288ee3a46d3417e0dc740e56fce22974b57baae86cf85350a67664f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3.01 of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] There is  $c$ so that for all $\epsilon>0$
