    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.397540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_deb09a8b6ad9ab6d5b8710d08f153b2df534bc144024748111e13a5a0be145c8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Block graph event the for the one-arm event of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[proposition]{prop:block_one_arm}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel.  

    Then

    \begin{multline}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            o 
            \leftrightarrow 
            B(r)^c, 
            \# K
            \leq 
            k(r)
        \right) 
        \\
        \leq 
        \sum_{\substack{
            b \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)
            \\
            \mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}(b,\mathbf{m},r)
            \\
            \mathbf{A} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})
        }}
        \sum_{\substack{
            \ell \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}'(\ell,\mathbf{A})
        }}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \mathcal{B}(K)
            =
            \mathbf{A} \cup \mathbf{B},
            P(\mathbf{A}, \mathbf{r}) 
            \subseteq 
            \mathcal{H}^*(\mathbf{A}),
            \mathbf{A} 
            \text{ is } 
            \mathcal{B}(K) 
            \text{-isolated}
        \right).
    \end{multline}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.439196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_deb18ab781d8ef37b02ca8fa78576a87446c2bcd333ef6f029f6ca9c550f4145","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:PI of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Fix $p \geq 1$ and let $\mathcal{F}_p$ and $\Gamma_p$ be as in (1)-(2) of Definition (def:SSS of the paper).
    For a given scale function $\Psi$, we say that the pair  $(\mathcal{F}_p,\Gamma_p)$ satisfies the \emph{Poincar\'e inequality} (eq:PI of the paper) if there are constants $C,\sigma \geq 1$ satisfying the following condition.
    For all $x \in X$, $r > 0$ and $f \in \mathcal{F}_p$,
    \begin{equation}
        \tag{$\textup{PI}_p(\Psi)$}
        \int_{B(x,r)} \abs{f - f_{B(x,r)}}^p \, d\mu \leq C \Psi(x,r) \int_{B(x,\sigma r)} \, d\Gamma_p\Span{f}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

