{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.441866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debb1639ec89c020a2faf3aeaf96f2250f2f461b8e514276b857f69b8984f88a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition arf_prop of arXiv:2608.25513, 'Adaptive Regularization for Random Features: A Neighboring Early-Stopping Rule with Oracle'] Suppose Assumptions (ass1 of the paper)--(ass5 of the paper) hold. Let $0<\widetilde\lambda\leq\lambda\leq1$ satisfy
\begin{align}
\tilde{\lambda} \geq 4\kappa^2/|D| \ \text{and} \ \max\{{\cal U}_{D,\lambda,\delta},{\cal U}_{D,\tilde{\lambda},\delta} \}\leq 1/2,
\end{align} 
If the number of random features $M$ satisfies
\begin{align}
M\gtrsim 
\begin{cases}
c_{\mathrm{RF}}\widetilde\lambda^{-\alpha}\log\frac{384\kappa^3|D|}{\delta}, & 0<r<\frac12,\\
c_{\mathrm{RF}} \widetilde\lambda^{-[(2r-1)(1+\gamma-\alpha)+\alpha]}\log\frac{384\kappa^3|D|}{\delta}, & \frac12\leq r\leq1,
\end{cases}
\end{align}
then with probability at least $1-\delta$, there holds that
\begin{align}
\|(C_{M,D}+\lambda I)^{1/2}({\boldsymbol{u}}_{M,D,\lambda}-{\boldsymbol{u}}_{M,D,\widetilde\lambda})\|_2
\leq C_2\frac{\lambda-\widetilde\lambda}{\widetilde\lambda}
\left({\cal W}_{M,D,\lambda}+\widetilde\lambda^r\right)\log^2\frac{16}{\delta},
\end{align}
where $c_{\mathrm{RF}}, C_2$ are some positive constants independent of $M$, $\lambda$, $\tilde{\lambda}$, $|D|$ and $\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.283123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debbed20e4a7bc281566566c493a27a78779aac5b675c16c0d3d05da277138cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:pureweak-nonstrong2 of arXiv:2507.14676, 'On the critical parameters of branching random walks'] {cf:BZ17}}]  
Let $(X,K)$ and $(X,K^*)$ two irreducible continuous-time BRWs such that $k_{xy}=k^*_{xy}$ for all $x \in X \setminus A$
where $A$ is a finite nonempty set.  Suppose that $\lambda^*_w<\lambda_w < \lambda_s$, and let $B\subseteq X$ be nonempty.

Then, for the BRW $(X,K^*)$
\begin{enumerate} 
\item if $\lambda \le \lambda_w^*$ there is a.s.~extinction in $B$;

\item if $\lambda \in (\lambda_w^*, \lambda_w)$ there is strong survival in $B$; 

\item if $\lambda =\lambda_w$ and $(X,K)$ dies out globally, then there is strong survival in $B$;

conversely, if $(X,K)$ survives globally and $B$ is finite; there is non-strong survival in $B$;

\item if $\lambda \in (\lambda_w, \lambda_s]$ and $B$ is finite, then

there is non-strong survival in $B$;

\item if $\lambda > \lambda_s$ and $B$ is finite, then survival is strong (resp.~non-strong) in $B$

if and only if 
the same holds for $(X,K)$.  
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.203043+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debe0cfe1fea31281c3cda97a380c160611b56070262b5598e2f18ad7b2d6832","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:HRmixing of arXiv:2412.07643, 'Ballistic Convergence in Hit-and-Run Monte Carlo and a Coordinate-free Randomized Kaczmarz'] Let $\varepsilon>0$, $\nu\in\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ and $\rho$ as defined in (equation eq:rate of the paper).
Then, there exist absolute constants $C,C'>0$ such that the mixing time of Hit-and-Run with respect to the Gaussian measure $\gamma^\mathcal{C}$ starting from $\nu$ to accuracy $\varepsilon$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    \tau_{\operatorname{mix}}(\varepsilon,\nu)\ &=\ \inf\bigr\{ n \in \mathbb{N}\,:\,\mathcal \mathsf{TV}\bigr(\nu\pi_{\mathrm{H\&R}}^n,\,\gamma^\mathcal{C}\bigr)\leq \varepsilon \bigr\} \\
    &\leq\  C\,\rho^{-1}\,\log\Bigr(C'\max(\kappa,M,m^{-1})\,d\,\varepsilon^{-1}\,\boldsymbol{\mathcal{W}}^2_{\mathcal{C}^{-1/2}}(\gamma^{\mathcal{C}}, \nu)\Bigr)
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $\kappa,M,m$ denote condition number, largest and smallest eigenvalue of $\mathcal{C}^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.771776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debf4f779e213b76555e9eb1e7c624d489eed841fb6301509523556e8ead12d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $\XX$ be a quasi-normed space and let $\emptyset\ne\SC\subset \XX$.
