{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.473752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debf56f0e7aac0cd6b4f1a17ca72ba921f71c07ecfdfb7db98ea7116423ff062","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 55 (Low-endpoint all-cut recovery) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $m\ge1$, $1\le r\le2$, and $1\le p<\infty$.  There are constants
