{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dec6b9d36984b65ddc956945c0d10b481f8a6468b533bbf1ae2d718a3e2f0b41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma B4LagPoly of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] For any $n,~a\in\mathbb{N}$ and $x\ge0$, the Laguerre polynomials are bounded as
