{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.135052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ded627e3dd4251875c3b61b5e454e9042a4b91d98c6b3d1a2c7039e16fa8ea9a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2608.10515, 'Limiting Law of Local Fields for the Mean Field Ghatak-Sherrington Model'] Under the same conditions as in Proposition~\ref{prop:ratio}, we have
\begin{equation}
  \E\left[\langle U(l)\rangle-\frac{\E_\xi[U(\xi+\gamma)W(\beta(\xi+\gamma)+h)]}{\Wtil(\beta\gamma+h)}\right]^{2k}\le \frac{K}{N^k},
\end{equation}
where now $\xi\sim N(0,v)$ and $v=p-q$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\E_\xi[U(\xi+\gamma)W(\beta(\xi+\gamma)+h)]}{\Wtil(\beta\gamma+h)}
  =\int U(x)d\nu_N(x),
\end{equation}
where $d\nu_N$ is the mixture of $2S+1$ Gaussian measures defined in \eqref{eq:nu-def}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.323978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ded6e04308ec1160b56dc5d5bb5200d73bef021c7050504740742688ea952652","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2607.05219, 'Random free semigroups of affine groups'] Let $r$ be the free   rank of $A$. Then 
