{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.269477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df0520eb2620b3f1dc4591cfd101d42f45dc66417a111087c7856e6147e4abc7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: technical estimate on slow varying functions of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
	Let $L$ be a strictly positive slowly-varying function and let $\xi > 0$.
	For every $\varepsilon > 0$, there exist a constant $C = C_{\varepsilon}$ such that for every $k,N \in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} ^*$,
