\end{equation}
Then $\{Z_n\}$ is irreducible, in the sense of Definition (def:irreducibility of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.528235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df339cec12beb066d7f13f1cb5798378455d14f5c6aaff876ef17b08bbf18957","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.18557, 'Randomly Permuted Orthogonal Products and Fast Dimension Reduction'] Let \(X\) be a random variable and let \(\sigma,M>0\). Suppose that
	\[
	\log \E e^{\lambda X}
	\le
	\lambda^2\sigma^2
	\qquad
	\text{for }|\lambda|\le\frac1M.
	\]
	Then, for every \(t\ge0\),
	\[
	\Pp\{|X|\ge t\}
	\le
	2\exp\left[
	-\min\left\{
	\frac{t^2}{4\sigma^2},
	\frac{t}{2M}
	\right\}
	\right].
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.253691+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3406349685278eb441cba7c9ef71b63539d3c6fb9f41fc5403584c2d3f509b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: construction of the continuous noise of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
	$\boldsymbol\zeta^{(a)}$ converges almost surely in $H_{\rm loc}^{-s}(\Omega)$ for every $s >  \frac{D}{2}$. Its limit is denoted $\boldsymbol\zeta$ and its law is characterized by 
	\[ 
	\mathds{E}\Big[ \mathrm{e}^{i \langle \boldsymbol\zeta, \ensuremath{\mathbf{f}} \rangle} \Big] = \exp\bigg( \int_{\Omega \times {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} } \Big( \mathrm{e}^{i \ensuremath{\mathbf{f}}(x) z} -1 -i \ensuremath{\mathbf{f}}(x) z) \mathrm{d} x \lambda(\mathrm{d} z) \bigg) \,,
	\]
	for every function $\ensuremath{\mathbf{f}} \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal D}} _0(\Omega)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3857f993be4c3fed94826e3be21eae14cc2af5e28b5fb50c9b6aa3027feacc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For all~$\lambda>0$, $\sigma\in(0,1/10)$ and~$\delta\in(0,1)$ there exist~$c>0$ and~$a_2\ge0$ such that for all $s\ge 1$, all~$u$ satisfying $s\ge u\ge s-\lambda$ and all~$n$ with~$s\le n^{1-\delta}$,
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
Q_{n,s,u}\Biggl(\biggl(\,\bigcap_{k=1}^n\Bigl\{h(x_k)\le&\frac {n-k}n\wt m_n+s+\gamma_{n,a}(k)\Bigr\}\biggr)^\cc\,\Biggr)
\\
&\le
c\frac{(1+s-u)s}n\sum_{1\le k\le n/2}\bigl[k+\gamma_{n,a}(k)^2\bigr]\texte^{-\frac18 c_2\gamma_{n,a}(k)}
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
holds for all~$a\ge a_2$ with
\begin{equation}

\gamma_{n,a}(k):=a+\bigl(\min\{k,n-k\}\bigr)^\sigma.
\end{equation}
Here~$c_2$ is as in \eqref{E:4.73}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.283533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3c37e9ae2b9dfd584c24cd591a0ed84067f1ced7215ad94a3bbdf1303eb15f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2606.22044, 'Degenerate Stochastic Delay Modified Equation: Approximation of Stochastic Variance Reduce'] Let $Y_{t}$ be defined by (\ref{sfde-0-0}) and for any $g\in\mathcal{G}_{1}^{2},$ denote $P_{t}g(y)=\mathbb{E}[g(Y_{t}^{y})]$. Then, for arbitrary $y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$, whenever $\eta\in(0,1]$ and $t\in[0,m\eta]$, the following holds:
