|\nabla P_{t}g(y)|\leq e^{Cm\eta},
\end{align}
\begin{align}
\|\nabla^{2}P_{t}g(y)\|_{{\rm HS}}\leq C_{1}e^{C_{2}m\eta},
\end{align}
where $C,C_{1},C_{2}$ are positive constants, and are independent of $m$ and $\eta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.305941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3cdb42c510ef47af560f4570416d49ac3f15d3d21de684e64c7b7095d1d581","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 8 ($L^p$ decay) of arXiv:2606.24167, '\bf On the stability of rarefaction for stochastic viscous conservation law'] Let $\phi\in X_1(T) $ be the solution of \eqref{perturbation}. Then for any $4< p< \infty$ 
