{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.777631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3eeb8efb00ddfc6571e4d745a432e0f0023ef32ee3e07343f54bbf3e4db2f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2609.02225, '\textbf{The direct moving plane method for weak solutions of the fractional $p$-Laplacian}'] There exists \(c_H=c_H(n,s,p)>0\) such that, for every \(\lambda\in\mathbb R\) and \(x\in\Sigma_\lambda^-\),
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\Sigma_\lambda}
 \frac{
 \bigl(
  |u(x)-u(y)|+|u_\lambda(x)-u(y)|
 \bigr)^{p-2}}
 {|x-y^\lambda|^{n+sp}}\,dy
 \ge c_H(\lambda-x_1)^{-sp}u(x)^{p-2}.
\end{equation}
If \(\lambda\le0\), then
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\Sigma_\lambda}
 \frac{
 \bigl(
  |u(x)-u(y)|+|u_\lambda(x)-u(y)|
 \bigr)^{p-2}}
 {|x-y^\lambda|^{n+sp}}\,dy
 \ge c_H|x|^{-sp}u(x)^{p-2},
 \qquad\text{for }x\in\Sigma_\lambda^-.
\end{equation}
Let \(I\subset\mathbb R\) be a bounded interval and set $L_I:=\max\left\{1,\sup_{\mu\in I}|\mu|\right\}$. Then, for every \(\lambda\in I\) and every \(x\in\Sigma_\lambda^-\) with \(|x|\ge L_I\), there exists \(c_H'=c_H'(n,s,p)>0\) such that
\begin{equation}
   \int_{\Sigma_\lambda}
 \frac{
 \bigl(
 |u(x)-u(y)|+|u_\lambda(x)-u(y)|
 \bigr)^{p-2}}
 {|x-y^\lambda|^{n+sp}}\,dy
 \ge c_H'|x|^{-sp}u(x)^{p-2}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.423836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df4157655c520924fdabb6f25d93959ad90c15afe275d872a883d60fb2f07276","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 104 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] Let $E \subset \R^m \times [0,\epsilon_0]$ be compact and globally subanalytic. Put $E_0 = E \cap (\R^m \times \{0\})$. Suppose $F: E \to \R$ is continuous, constructible, and vanishes on $E_0$. Then there exist constants $C>0$, $\alpha>0$, and $\epsilon \in (0,\epsilon_0]$ such that
$$
|F(z,t)| \le C t^{\alpha}
$$
for every $(z,t)\in E$ with $0<t<\epsilon$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.057156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df425a7616b0361b707e0b3db514589fc3e648dfb192467c330efabae9f9870d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:R<p/q of arXiv:2607.14062, 'Gilbert's disc model conditioned on the square lattice'] Let $a,b\in \mathbb{Z}_{>0} = \{1,2,\dots\}$, let $R \in (0, a/b)$, and let $u_0,\ldots,u_n\in\mathbb{Z}^2$. If there exists $P\in\mathcal P$ such that $u=(u_0,\ldots,u_n)$ is a path of $\Gamma_{p,R}^{\texttt{CN}}(P)$ (resp.\ of $\Gamma^{\texttt{NN}}_{p,R}(P)$), then 
