	for all \( i \in \mathbb{N} \) and \( t > 0 \). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.577520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df4946fb3139b0d1aa4ff3707e825c56419248654c504f6dd8f85b2b3821c7b7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:moderate of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] There exist constants \(\kappa=\kappa(E)\in(0,1)\) and \(c=c(E)>0\) such that
for every \(a\in(1/2,1)\) and all sufficiently large \(n\),
	\begin{align}
