{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.982100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df6d5127be35a6000226b11c9494ab156f860b810e11dd04892e0b84a353eba3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tau-decay of arXiv:2607.26169, 'Scaling and partial universality of the height zero probability in the 2D Abelian sandpile'] There exists a constant $c > 0$ only depending on $\mathcal{G}$ and the fixed vectors $h_1, h_2$ such 
