{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.647705+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df7382093229528cc45af0a08f2b9da13b33a0f8b568b4bc4d49f03136dc771b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm wired disconnection of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta>\beta_c$. There exists $c_1>0$ such that for every $L \geq 1$,
