{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.240289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df9dd8986a252e149a593493ac695758319b15233b636b02807fbedb94bbae90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] For all $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and all $\delta\in[0,\frac{\alpha}{2}]$, there exists $C_{\alpha,\delta}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$, all $t>0$ and all $u\in H^{\alpha-2\delta}$ one has
