{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.199885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df9e9de5f278e3ef1a01765ec1bb802d529333d9024d77845bd3ce08a09cb27f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] Let us fix $T>0$, $p\in [2, \infty)$ and $u_0\in \Vp\cap \bM$. If $u_m$ denotes the unique solution of the SDE \eqref{eqn-Faedo-Galerkin}, then, for each fixed $m\in \N$, the following estimate holds true:
