\mathbb{P}_{-1,B}|_{\mathscr{X}_{-\sigma}^{\mathrm{Dir}}(B;{\mathbb R}^d)} : \mathscr{X}_{-\sigma}^{\mathrm{Dir}}(B;{\mathbb R}^d)\to \mathscr{X}_{-\sigma}^{\mathrm{Sto}}(B) 
$$
boundedly for all $ \sigma \in [0,1]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.795849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dfd27225d9f756218a346c0301a13094ffb7aee7eb1ee72d1fc31c019519183b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lhs of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Let $(X_1,d_1)$ and $(X_2,d_2)$ be two complete and locally compact metric spaces, and consider $f:(X_1,d_1)\to(X_2,d_2)$ a surjective map for which there exists $C>0$ and $\alpha>0$  such that for all $x,y \in X_1$, we have that
