        d_2(f(x),f(y)) \leq Cd_1(x,y)^{\alpha}.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, we have that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \dim_H(X_2)\leq \frac{1}{\alpha} \dim_H(X_1).
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.604693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dfd53a8038ed4aae27114bfa57b5d5b14c98211f2220fa22e820c8d51d329410","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Coefficient asymptotics at an exponential singularity) of arXiv:2607.07712, 'Parameter-Space Heat Flow, Gaussian Density Ratios, and Sharp Hermite Truncation Rates'] Let \(\beta>0\) and \(\lambda>0\). Then, as \(m\to\infty\),
