O_{n}>2N\right) =0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.708251+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dff9d78c45a4e9084ab827ec05666b88a41072095a65138d11a69f54d3affb8b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop main term being probability of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $O_n$ be the event defined in (equation definition of O_n of the paper) and $S_n$ be the random walk defined in (equation def of S_n and S_n hat of the paper). Then, 
    \begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_2\left[ \frac{1}{|S_n(X_0-X_2)|^4} \mathbbm{1}_{O_n} \right]= \mathbb{P}_2[O_n]. 
        \end{align}
    In particular, 
    \begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left[ \frac{1}{|S_n(X_0-X_2)|^4} \mathbbm{1}_{O_n} \right]= \mathbb{P}[O_n]. 
        \end{align}
Furthermore, for any integer $k\in \mathbb{Z}$, 
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_2&\left[ \frac{1}{|S_n(X_0-X_2)|^4} \mathbbm{1}_{O_n} \mathbbm{1}_{\left \{ \frac{|X_0-X_2|}{|X_0-X_3|} \in [2^k, 2^{k+1})\right\}}\right] \nonumber
           \\ &\qquad \qquad\qquad\qquad = \mathbb{P}_2\left[O_n \cap \left\{ \frac{1}{|S_n||X_0-X_3|}\in [2^k, 2^{k+1})\right\}\right].
            \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.327825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dffcd9bd2784134cca70fd9c74c34d7f436d05d04a9f62c85b54718914815e89","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 3 of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $p \in (0, \infty)$. A collection $\{X^n_s : s\in S_n, n \ge 1\}$ of $\cX$-valued random elements is  \textit{$(\nu_n)$-compactly uniformly $p$-th order integrable} (or $(\nu_n)$-$\CUI(p)$, for short) if:
	\begin{enumerate}[\rm (a)]
		\item the map $(\omega, s) \mapsto X^n_s(\omega)$ is $\cF \otimes \cS_n/\cB(\cX)$-measurable for every $n \ge 1$,

		\item for any $\ep >0$, there exists $K_\ep \in \cK(\cX)$ such that
		\begin{align*}
			 \sup_{n \ge 1} \bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p \1_{\{X^n_s \notin K_\ep\}} \nu_n(\od s)  \le \ep.
		\end{align*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.347682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0011270692d129961d2678c8ec674bbab972fcf1e9873b6555c723dd9b14f22","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gordon of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $E$ be a Euclidean space of finite dimension, let $T \subseteq E$ be a nonempty compact subset of the unit sphere of $E$, let $\Gamma_1, \dots, \Gamma_N$ be independent standard Gaussian vectors in $E$, and let $g_N \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I_N)$.  Then for every $t > 0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left\{
\inf_{\|z\|_2 = 1}\, \sup_{R \in T}\,
\sum_{i=1}^N z_i \ip{\Gamma_i}{R} \; \le\;  w(T) - \mathbb{E}\|g_N\|_2 - t
\right\} \le 2\, e^{-t^2/4} .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.748842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0032b600b19bc73cdd69ed513e8a620737774d18f58092dcd6098eeb6929fc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cme-f of arXiv:2507.20324, 'Non-existence of several random fractals in Brownian motion and Brownian loop soup'] For a fixed $n$-box $S$, recall that $\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}(\cdot):=\mathbb{P}(\cdot|S\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}(\delta+2^{-\sqrt{n}}))$, and assume that
\[\mathrm{dist}(S,T),\mathrm{dist}(S,U)\geq 2^{-n+jL}.\]
Then there exist $c,c_{1},c_{2}>0$, such that
\begin{equation}
c_{1}\mathrm{dist}(S,T)^{-2}2^{-2n}\leq\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}_{n}(T\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}|\mathscr{F}_{j-1})\leq c_{2}\mathrm{dist}(S,T)^{-2}2^{-2n},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}_{n}(T,U\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}|\mathscr{F}_{j-1})\leq cD_{1}^{-2}D_{2}^{-2}2^{-4n},
\end{equation}
where
\[D_{1}=\min\{\mathrm{dist}(S,T),\mathrm{dist}(T,U),\mathrm{dist}(U,S)\},\]
and
