{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.977169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e02c557cc2e4a82abf5805629eb7de5bf1bdbaf0ad5b5e592170d54ae1ff1c0a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] Let $m \in \{1,\dots,n-1\}$, $T \in\cT_m$, $r_0,\dots,r_m \in \N$. Then
