{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.851504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e031d63662d6be43326eeac46a240b0931de0ec1fe9e401439956701db0043b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop main2_2 of arXiv:2607.10105, 'The four-dimensional Anderson model: a case study for critical SPDEs'] Let $(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n,m_\mathfrak l)$ be a fixed marked Hepp tree with multiplicities $m_\mathfrak l\geq 2$, and with both simple and compound leaves (Definition (def.mul of the paper)). Let $(y_1,\cdots,y_m)$ be a fixed vector (where $m=\sum_\mathfrak l m_\mathfrak l$), such that the multiset $\{y_1,\cdots,y_m\}=\cup_\mathfrak l \{\textrm{$m_\mathfrak l$ copies of $z_\mathfrak l$}\}$, where $(z_\mathfrak l)$ satisfies Definition (def.hepp_3 of the paper) (a); moreover, instead of Definition (def.hepp_3 of the paper) (b), we assume that for each $\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B$ and two leaves $\mathfrak l,\mathfrak l'\in\mathcal L_\mathfrak n$, we have \begin{equation}|z_{\mathfrak l}-z_{\mathfrak l'}|\leq\sum_{\mathfrak m\leq\mathfrak n}\gamma_\mathfrak m^\infty\cdot N_\mathfrak m.
\end{equation}

Fix absolute constants $C_0>1000$ and $D=\exp(C_0^{10})$. Then, for any $(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n,m_\mathfrak l)$, and under all the above assumptions, we have
\begin{multline}\sum_{\pi}^{(*)}\prod_{j=1}^{m-1}\frac{1}{\langle y_{\pi(j)}-y_{\pi(j+1)}\rangle^2}\leq C_0^mD^{|\mathcal B|}\sum_{W\subseteq\mathcal B\backslash\{\mathfrak r\}}((m-2|W|)!)^{1/2}\\\times\prod_{\mathfrak l\in\mathcal L^S}(m_\mathfrak l!)^{1/2}\prod_{\mathfrak l\in\mathcal L^C}(m_\mathfrak l!)^{3/4}\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B} N_\mathfrak n^{-2(\gamma_\mathfrak n^2-1)}\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B\backslash\{\mathfrak r\}}\bigg(\frac{N_\mathfrak n}{N_{\mathfrak n^+}}\bigg)^2\prod_{\mathfrak n\not\in W}\frac{N_\mathfrak n}{N_{\mathfrak n^+}}.
\end{multline} Here $\pi\in S_m$ in ((eq.vol_3_2 of the paper)) (which is identified with a permutation of $m_\mathfrak l$ distinct copies of each leaf $\mathfrak l$) and satisfies the primitivity condition in Proposition (prop.main_3 of the paper). In addition, we restrict that there is no $j$ such that $\pi(j)$ and $\pi(j+1)$ are two copies of \emph{the same leaf}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.501562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0327be9e5ff72cdba98a450be4566ae9e20fa0e529df65c8a8cd03b9cbdb4f4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem : FdTmon/Intrinsic/Pgrad of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Assume that $\FdTmon(D)<\infty$. Then for $\hd$-almost all $z\inX \setminus\bigcup_{k\ge 1}\sigma_k$,
