{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.835369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0357a6ad79a941c81d933870d7c100f4092e7af56423cb3bd994ae95d4d5d11","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2506.12834, 'Space-time fractional stochastic partial differential equations driven by L\'evy white noi'] Let $p\in[1,2]$. For any $\cF_t$-adapted function $\phi:[0,\infty)\times\R^d\times E\times \Omega\to\R$ satisfying
  \begin{equation*}
    \int_{0}^{t}\int_{\R^d}\int_E \E\left[\left|\phi(s,x,\xi)\right|^p\right]\ud s\ud x \mu(\ud\xi)<\infty,
  \end{equation*}
  the stochastic integral
  \begin{equation*}
