{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.054535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e04c60bcd8da0c0bc6fd3bdc18b56eec399976bbc17a660ee9fc1f07753076e2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 (Exponential-tail anisotropic estimates imply a subspace law) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $K\Subset\C\setminus[-b,b]$.  Suppose that, conditionally on $P_n$ when the signal is random, there are deterministic $a_n(K)\downarrow0$ and constants $C_K,c_K>0$ such that, for every deterministic unit $x,y\in\F^{2r_n}$ and every $t\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left(
   \sup_{\zeta\in K}
   \left|\ip{x}{\bigl(\calG_n(\zeta)-\calM(\zeta)\bigr)y}\right|
   >a_n(K)+t
   \ \middle|\ P_n
 \right)
 \le C_K e^{-c_Knt^2}+e^{-c_Kn}.
\end{equation}
Then \cref{ass:holo-SLL} holds with
\begin{equation}
  \eps_n(K)\le C_K'
  \left(a_n(K)+\sqrt{\frac{r_n}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\right).
\end{equation}
In particular, the error vanishes for every $r_n=o(n)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.907001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e04f1326ad8d1b216f8d14dfbc251a7421bc906881225d02fe54ffa391564334","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bd-Delta of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] Let $ A\subseteq \mathbb R^d$  {convex}, $ B\subseteq \mathbb R^{ d},r = 1 + d(A,B).$
