{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.502044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e05a774b1fa73ebbb851b41eea14212ce7779f0f3a59e81fea44cfbc5468969a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem : LDP/ContinuousMetric of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] The process $(\TightSPT)_{n\ge 1}$ takes values in $\RegPD[b \normeUn\cdot]$ and for all $x,y \in \frac1n\intint0n^d$,
