		The complex square root is chosen with non-negative real part.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.813380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0609103b8531990f216b5187b18348daefa4791099e6af5b1e172759b0d5799","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:compact_embedding of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] For every $r, m\in \mathbb{R}$ with $r\ge m$, $T>0$, $\gamma>0$ and $\varepsilon>0$, the following embedding is compact
