{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.863806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0798196b81e1d544c967133d387a606cd702e993c95b47c6653000a40c198ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 29 of arXiv:2511.22156, ''] There exist constants $\alpha_1, C>0$ independent of $m$ such that if $f$ is bounded harmonic in $B(z,r)\cap \tilde{F}_n$, then 
\begin{equation}
|f(x)-f(y)|\leq Cr^{-\alpha_1}|x-y|^{\alpha_1} \|f\|_{\infty}, \qquad \forall x,y\in B(z,\frac{r}{2}).
\end{equation}
\begin{proof}
Let $x,y\in B(z,\frac{r}{2})$, set $\bar{r}=|x-y|$. Take $m\in N$ such that $ \frac{1}{2}C_H^{-m-1}r<\overline{r}\leq \frac{1}{2}C_H^{-m}r$ .By Lemma \ref{lemma6.6}, 
\begin{equation*}
