{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.467262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0922426df8bd596975c46d725ef4f34bea54decc086fce37ace76a19f508d4e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Intrinsic oriented coefficient scale) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] For $m\ge1$ and $1\le r<\infty$, let $\CutCoeff_{m,r}$ be the completion
of $\mathcal K_{\mathrm{alg}}$ in the norm
\begin{equation}

 \|K\|_{\CutCoeff_{m,r}}
 :=
 \begin{cases}
  \|K\|_{\mathrm{cut},m,r}^{\Sigma},&1\le r<2,\\
  \|K\|_{\mathscr K_m},&r=2,\\
  \|K\|_{\mathrm{cut},m,r}^{\cap},&2<r<\infty.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
Put $\CutCoeff_{0,r}:=\Sch_r$.

In the same-field setting, let $\cH$ be the complexification of a real
Hilbert space, let $\cH^{(1)},\ldots,\cH^{(m)}$ be labelled copies, and let
$J_\nu:\cH\to\cH^{(\nu)}$ be the canonical unitary identifications.  Define
the deterministic labelling map
\begin{equation}

 \Dec_m
 :=J_1\otimes\cdots\otimes J_m
   \otimes\Id_{\conj{\cC}}\otimes\Id_{\cE}.
\end{equation}
Let $\Coeff_{m,r}$ be the completion of symmetric algebraic kernels in the
norm
\begin{equation}

 \|K\|_{\Coeff_{m,r}}
 :=\|\Dec_mK\|_{\CutCoeff_{m,r}},
 \qquad \Coeff_{0,r}:=\Sch_r.
\end{equation}
The definition is independent of the chosen labelled copies by unitary
functoriality.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.332563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0967e66764ceebce0b2fb8dc3bf74f3ea06b851b520b1cca3a11843c4b0cc63","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{a2-2} holds. Then, for every $d' > d$ there exists a constant $C_{12}>0$ such that for every $R \geq R_1$ (here $R_{1}$ is the same constant in Assumption~\ref{a2-2} associated with $d'$) and $f, g\colon B(R) \to \R$ with $(g)_{B(R)} = 1$,

  \begin{align}
    &\norm{f - (fg)_{B(R)}}{\rho_{*}}{B(R)}
    \nonumber\\%[.5ex]
    &\mspace{36mu}\leq\;
    C_{12}\, R^{1-d/d'}\,
    \Bigl(
      1 + \Norm{g}{\rho_{*}/(\rho_{*}-1), B(R)}
    \Bigr)\,
    \Biggl(
      \sum_{\substack{y, z \in B(\delta_{\mathrm{S}} R) \\ y \sim z}}
      \mspace{-12mu}\bigl|f(y) - f(z)\bigr|^{\rho}
