{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.325544+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0d5023532d936aec7b6b724cdcbfb3d4e3ec4176d0c00902ff8ebb876828cc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:formula-for-nu of arXiv:2411.09075, 'Weak Poincar{\'e} Inequalities, Simulated Annealing, and Sampling from Spherical Spin Glas'] Let $\eps$ be as in Lemma~(lem:band-models-eps-strictly-rs of the paper). 
    On an event with probability $1-e^{-cN^{1/5}}$, the following holds.
