{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.006753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0eb058292f94913573ab5e397d675af97519fe3acc55f6569e5afce570c5098","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.14802, 'Dynamical Gibbs-non-Gibbs transitions for finite-alphabet models on trees'] A configuration $\eta \in \Omega$ is \underline{good} for $\mu^l_t$ if for all $x\in V$, all local
functions $\varphi$, and each sequence of finite volumes $\Lambda_n\uparrow V$,
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}\sup_{\substack{\xi^1,\xi^2\in \Omega\\ \Delta:~\Lambda_n\subset \Delta \Subset V}}\Big|\mu^l_t(\varphi|\eta_{\Lambda_n\setminus \{x\}}\xi^1_{\Delta \setminus \Lambda_n})-\mu^l_t(\varphi|\eta_{\Lambda_n\setminus \{x\}}\xi^2_{\Delta \setminus \Lambda_n})\Big|=0.
\end{equation}
A configuration which is not good is called \underline{bad}. If all configurations are good for $\mu^l_t$, the measure $\mu^l_t$ is called \underline{quasilocally Gibbs}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.667302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0eb56c7d81c5fa64c829786531994c01ccdd85ea5749baa55e9d936f354ec74","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Krawtchouk transform functional equation) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For every radial vector $u$,
