{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.934925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0ed01b92b5d8df688a17f05eb5710fa353a9d47055418b4415726b027f7aa2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question 19 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Suppose that $\beta \neq \beta'$. Is it true that for any finite set of edges $F \subset E^d$, with $|F| \geq 2$, one has
