{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.184866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e15fe0b1d1cbca04d97302fb41d3b4afd59eb9bd4cf0534348a1709bbf102032","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:level_line_hits_right_side_with_positive_prob of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Fix $j \in \{1,\ldots,N\}$,  $k \in \{0,1,\ldots,\lfloor R \rfloor - 1\}$ and $m \in \{0,1,\ldots,23\}$.  There exists a constant $p \in (0,1)$ depending only on $\mu$ and the constants $a,R_0$ of (lem:rectangles_are_not_wide of the paper) such that the following holds.  Conditional on $U_1,\ldots,U_N$ and $\eta_{j,\widetilde{k}}^{\widetilde{m}}$ for $(\widetilde{k},\widetilde{m}) \neq (k,m)$,  and on the event that the boundary conditions of $\Psi|_{U_j}$ are given by the zero function,  and that $I_j^3 \cap \partial B_{2^{-2 R /3}}(0) = \emptyset,  I_j^4 \cap \partial B_{2^{-R /3}}(0) = \emptyset$,  we have that the curve $\eta_{j,k}^m$ first intersects the right boundary of the rectangle 
