{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.125657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e178e5903d13fdc5ff7df3753394775c041c7b546a92cd4759f671b00946443f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] There exists $\eta_2\in(0,\eta_0)$ and $\vt_2\in(0,\vt_1)$, and for each
