{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.615444+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e189ebe36dfcc159de1cd9f1e238db30fa2e210c4fb225ebc4f0e6e9546882dc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exists $\delta_0>0$ and constants $C',c'$ such that for any $\delta<\delta_0$, we have
    \begin{equation}

