{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.348859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1970ef833954e5709c37522cf147e22b0db4b80763d2b30babebca1b8cb1ea4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn:sub-stop of arXiv:2601.07045, 'From Continuous to Discrete: \\ a No-U-Turn Sampler for Permutations'] Let $\mathcal{O}$ be an orbit of length $2^j$, and let
$\{\mathcal{O}_{s,t}\}$ denote its dyadic sub-orbits
(Definition~(def:dyadic-suborbit of the paper)). We say that $\mathcal{O}$ satisfies the \emph{sub-stopping condition}
(\textsc{SubStop}) if at least one dyadic sub-orbit satisfies the
\textsc{Stop} condition:
\[
\textsc{SubStop}(\mathcal{O},\varepsilon,w)
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
\exists\, s\in\{0,\dots,j\},\; t\in\{1,\dots,2^s\}
\text{ such that }
\textsc{Stop}\bigl(\mathcal{O}_{s,t},\varepsilon,w\bigr).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:17.908623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1a06341bac7b2488ef27d3239fb58c8ece50ba03bda3e118305ef75eef32048","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Local Fourier semi-norms of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Let $\alpha\in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2})$. 
Let $\square_1\subsetneq \square_2\subset \mathbf{Cyl}$ a strict inclusion of rectangles in our cylinder $\mathbf{Cyl}$ and $\chi\in C^\infty_c(\square_2)$ such that $\chi=1$ on $\square_1$. Then for any $T\in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha,\alpha-1}$   
