{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.436100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1ad9d38cf39c96d71f0ea88371d1a479ca3a9d6f8dd772192a7ae9199f32ef7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ApprxSplit of arXiv:2609.02180, 'Helly-Type Theorems for Splitting Point Sets \thanks{A preliminary version of this article'] Let $P\subset {\mathbb R}^d$ be an $m$-point set, $1\leq k \leq d-1$, and let $\epsilon >0$. There exists a set $A\subseteq P$ of size at most $O\br{\frac{d}{\epsilon^2}\ln(\frac{d}{\epsilon})}$ with the following property:
  \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item if $\tau$ is a $k$-flat that $\alpha$-splits $P$ then it $(\alpha-\epsilon)$-splits $A$;
    \item if $\tau$ is a $k$-flat that $\alpha$-splits $A$ then it $(\alpha-\epsilon)$-splits $P$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1ae54d4ba16b3476d1ed13e19b0b782f655b79dc61395cccde1cd19f9ab4b1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nmlsi of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] For any $p\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\O)$, let $h=h(m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p))$ denote the unique $h\in\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ such that $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\mu_{J,h})=m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p)$, and let \(p_t\) denote the solution of (equation non-linear rqs of the paper) with initial datum $p$. If the system satisfies the Nonlinear MLSI with rate function $\ensuremath{\mathcal I}$, then 
\begin{equation}
    H(p_t|\mu_{J,h}) \le e^{-\ensuremath{\mathcal I}(h) t} H(p|\mu_{J,h})\,,\qquad t\ge 0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:58:44.381264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1b06ea43fc180655244d4cdd058fe53d8daef35b203ed0d1b6a70c02a629687","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2609.02819, 'Adelic Points and Unramified Brauer Approximation for Classifying Stacks'] Let $S\subset\Omega_k$ be finite.  The following are equivalent:
