{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.220850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2380715b03fcc8aaa8abde5361d8e4beac97748e221d97c4c7b3a6009d94011","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (The small-parameter boundary) of arXiv:2607.17630, 'Higher-Order Hankel Obstructions to Free Infinite Divisibility\ for Beta Distributions'] Fix $p>0$ and let $Y_{p,q}=1-X_{p,q}\sim\beta_{q,p}$.  For every fixed
