Moreover, the unique fixed point $\mathcal{P}(y(t))=y(t) \in \mathcal F$ is the unique solution of the initial value problem \eqref{eq:Yode} in \( [0,t_0] \), where $u^\flat(t, x)$, $ u^\sharp (t, x)$ solve the Cauchy problems \eqref{eq:sys_ub}-\eqref{eq:sys_ud} with $\bar u(0+)=u^*$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

