{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.783034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2d1d3897802ab63813d2c11fefd8cd5299d11d29a778bc2cdc109328dd20988","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the:pk of arXiv:2608.04303, 'The rank and layer distributions in random recursive trees'] The cumulative layer distribution is given by
\begin{equation}

    \bar{\ell}_k = \displaystyle\int_0^\infty  s_k(y) \, e^{-y} dy,
\end{equation}

with functions $s_i(y)$ defined recursively via 

\begin{equation}

    s_0(y) = 1,
    \quad s_i(y) = 1 - \exp\!\left[ -\int_0^y s_{i-1}(y^\prime) \, dy^\prime \right] \quad \forall i \geq 1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.397395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2d36a0b0a8b0c6e91d868840a2cfa02abbe4466e20e7dcdd85759069be852d3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 47 ({\cite[Theorem~6.4) of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] {zhan2019two}}]

Let $v_-, w_-, w_+, v_+ \in \BR$ with $v_- < w_- < w_+ < v_+$ be such that $0 \in [v_-, v_+]$. Let $(\eta_w,\eta_v)$ be a bichordal SLE$_4$ in $\BH$ with link pattern $\{\{w_+, w_-\}, \{v_+, v_-\}\}$. Then, there exists a universal constant $C \in (0,\infty)$ such that
