for all $L > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.609436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2d52f37f65f3caefdbde82d2dec8903dc1590c94811dc17ec3c627f9703fef9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] Let $f:\T^d\to\T^d$ be a $C^1$ diffeomorphism and $\mu\in L^1(\T^d)\cap\mathcal{P}(\T^d)$ be an absolutely continuous Borel probability measure on $\T^d$. Then we have the formula
