{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.363475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2ed5121bd69958b26dccb1f2286c252e3dcb54d18c4b72cf680ebee6cc461c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem2.4 of arXiv:2411.13266, '\bf A new maximal regularity for parabolic equations and an application'] ([Krylov02]) Given a (nonlinear) operator
${\mathcal A}: L^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})\rightarrow L^\infty(\mathbb{R})$, and suppose that

(i) ${\mathcal A}$ is subadditive and bounded, that is for a constant $C>0$ and every $k=1,2,\ldots$ and $f,f_m\in L^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})$, $m=1,2,\ldots,k$, we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
\Big|{\mathcal A}\Big(\sum_{m=1}^kf_m(t)\Big)\Big|\leqslant \sum_{m=1}^k |{\mathcal A} f_m(t)|, \ a.e.,
\end{eqnarray*}
and
\begin{eqnarray}
\|{\mathcal A} f\|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{R})}\leqslant C\|f\|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})}.
\end{eqnarray}

(ii) For each $g\in {\mathcal C}_0^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})$ and for almost all $t$ outside of the closed support of $g$ we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
|{\mathcal A} g(t)|\leqslant \Bigg\|\int\limits_{\mathbb{R}}{\mathcal K}(t,r)g(r)dr\Bigg\|_{\widetilde{{\mathcal H}}},
\end{eqnarray*}
where ${\mathcal K}(t,r)$ is an $L({\mathcal H};\widetilde{{\mathcal H}})$-valued Calder\'{o}n--Zygmund kernel relative to a filtration of partitions.

(iii) If $f,f_1,f_2,\ldots\in L^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})$, $f$ and all $f_k$ vanish outside of the same ball, the norms $\|f_k\|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})}$ are bounded with respect to $k$, and $\|f(t)-f_k(t)\|_{{\mathcal H}}\rightarrow 0$ at almost each $t\in \mathbb{R}$, then there is a subsequence $k(i)$ such that $k(i)\rightarrow +\infty$ as $i\rightarrow +\infty$ and
\begin{eqnarray}
|{\mathcal A} f(t)|\leqslant  \liminf_{i\rightarrow +\infty}|{\mathcal A} f_{k(i)}(t)|, \ \ a.e..
\end{eqnarray}
Then the operator ${\mathcal A}$ is of weak-type $(1,1)$ on smooth functions with compact support, that is there exists a positive constant $C_1$ such that, for any $f\in {\mathcal C}_0^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})$ and $\gamma>0$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\gamma\left|\{t: |{\mathcal A} f(t)|>\gamma\}\right|\leqslant C_1\int\limits_{\mathbb{R}}|f(t)|_{{\mathcal H}}dx,
\end{eqnarray}
where $|\cdot|$ in the left hand side of ((2.7 of the paper)) denotes the Lebesgue measure of the set $\{t: |{\mathcal A} f(t)|>\gamma\}$. Furthermore, ${\mathcal A}$ is of strong-type $(p,p)$ for every  $p\in (1,+\infty)$, that is there is another positive constant $C_2$ such that for all  $f\in {\mathcal C}_0^\infty(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\|{\mathcal A} f\|_{L^p(\mathbb{R})}\leqslant C_2\|f\|_{L^p(\mathbb{R};{\mathcal H})}.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.606866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2f01a73c10a5c1f9e7e69878d3382e8ed65296a8edf86c245b046bfd7cad038","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2607.08129, '2607.08129'] Let $X_1,\ldots,X_N$ be independent centered random variables satisfying $|X_i|\le b$ almost surely, and put $V:=\sum_{i=1}^N\Var(X_i)$.  Then, for every $x>0$,
