{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.889485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2f04617e50999bcebd510959178be274dbfea5f77b286396de369d30001d90f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:type2constant_TCS of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Given $r\geq 2$ an integer and $2 \leq p < \infty$, we define the type-2 constant  of the $\ell_p$ injective norm of order $r$ tensors  to be the smallest number $\mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)$  such that for all positive integers $n$ and tensors $T_1, \ldots, T_n \in (\mathbb R^d)^{\otimes r}$, we have\footnote{The sum of squared norms on the right-hand side of (equation eq:type2def_TCS of the paper) have also appeared in [Tom74,AW02] in the context of random matrices as a variance parameter, which is not as precise as the one given in~(equation eq:NCK_TCS of the paper) that gained attention after it appeared in matrix concentration inequalities~[Oli10,Tro10].}
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb E \Big\|\sum_{k=1}^n \varepsilon_k T_k\Big\|_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2 \leq \mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)^2 \cdot \sum_{k=1}^n \left\lVertT_k\right\rVert_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2 ,
\end{equation}
where $\varepsilon_1, \ldots, \varepsilon_n$ are i.i.d. Rademacher variables, i.e., $ \varepsilon_k = \pm 1$ with probability $\frac12$ each.","status":"unverified"}

