{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.006402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e30db7d1894f9d7f610609052d1ecfb20860754c082b7d83c1d23ebb97d99554","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma bundi of arXiv:2412.04013, 'Rate estimates for total variation distance with applications\thanks{The author gratefully'] If (equation smoothie of the paper) holds then
for each integer $l\geq 1$, there are $N(l),H_{l}>0$ such that
