\]
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.344874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e346632976e123b59dcfc8b391e53c22fb6949a3ba39d0821fc26a033845f2ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] Given $\widetilde{M}\in (\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{loc}})^{i,\mathbb{B}}$ and $a,b\in\mathbf{R}$, let $H\in \mathcal{L}_m^\mathbb{B}(M)\cap\mathcal{L}_m^\mathbb{B}(\widetilde{M})$ and $K\in \mathcal{L}_m^\mathbb{B}(M)$.
