{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.698880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3572f632dd946ccb9a904910406c14f01f2179adeac723e1c4e553c88aaa812","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def 24 (Normal sub-local group) of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] We say that a sub-local group $H$ is  \emph{normal} if it admits an associated neighborhood $V$ such that  
