{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.288638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e357d142078fd7ca219d2d4d27638cb60b2ff2132b48a3235bd812cb7d3af441","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem $X^pq^21$ of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $p>0$,  there exists a positive constant $C_p$, which does not depend on $\Delta$, such that for any $s>0$, it holds that 
