{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.331613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e358e5d59e93765af692579b1276a6ed33a1901b2df829a3151c820950cbc458","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Anchored Nash inequality) of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{a2-2} holds and suppose there exist $p, q \in (1, \infty]$ satisfying

