{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.807824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3c96833fcc9f5dedf568b21dba089d8a9137c2ae7540f1195931b0d3d592e9d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition th:main2 of arXiv:2609.01488, 'Stabilization by a background magnetic field: global well-posedness of the full compressib'] Assume $\mathbf n$ satisfies the Diophantine condition (equation Diophantine0 of the paper) and the initial data \\ $(\rho_0,\mathbf u_0,p_0,\mathbf h_0)\in H^{N}(\mathbb T^3)$ satisfying (equation xiajie-1 of the paper)-(equation chuzhixiaoyu0 of the paper). Let $M,N$ be two integers satisfying $M\geq r+1$ and $N> M+2(r+1)$. Suppose that $(\rho,\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)$ is a smooth solution to   the system (equation no-heat-mhd3 of the paper) on $\mathbb T^3\times[0,T_1)$ for some $T_1>0$. Then there is a positive constant $\epsilon$, depending only on $\|\rho_0\|_M$, $\|\rho_0\|_N$, $\mathbb T^3$, $|\mathbf n|$, $M$, $N$, $\mu$, $\lambda$, $\gamma$, $\bar P$, $\underline{\rho}^{-1}$, $\bar\rho$, $M_0$, $r$ and $c$, such that
