{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.299830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3d09a1e71de54a8eabcdcbef911a505d83516b3902f606581cb0f77e4009324","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.23433, 'Emergence of Common Noise: Quantitative Conditional Propagation of Chaos'] Suppose that $\mathbf{A(\beta })$ holds for $\mathcal{X}$ and let $T>0.$ Let 
