converges in the total variation sense as $n\to\infty $ to the law of $\mathcal Z^{\operatorname{b}}|_{[-N,N]}$, where $\mathcal Z^{\operatorname{b}}$ is the encoding walk for the UIBHBOT, as defined at the beginning of Section~(sec-busemann-sym of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.277575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e42f8198a90618f788b81211b50d7c0f40ed146c3c7f0c47009ad4a560f0cb34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.22526, 'The conditional expectation of the product of the first $n-1$ Hermite polynomials in a mul'] Let $n-$dimensional random vector be normal with $N\left(
