{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.673855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4573ed7e823d97692a86960eb32fa28983ba8ba131ab77e1a04bb8cb7a61ee3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem8 of arXiv:2412.05521, 'Random attractors for the stochastic Nernst-Planck-Navier-Stokes system with multiplicativ'] There exist a positive number $R_0$ and a random variable $R_1(\omega)$ depending on the initial data, $\varepsilon_0$, $\nu$, $f$ and universal constants, such that: For every $E >0 $, there exists $t(\omega,E) \leq -1$, such that for all $x_0=(u_0,\rho_0,\sigma_0) \in {H^1}$ with $|x_0| < E$, and for any $t_0 < t(\omega,E)$, we have
		\begin{align}
			\|\sigma(t,\omega,t_0,\sigma_0)\|_{L^2} \leq R_0,~for~all~t \in [-1,0],
		\end{align}
