{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:35:59.919489+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e47475aabce749a7d3fd5c5c6f3818db6f962f75a123f3128ca148768f5ddc4e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2608.26084, 'Localic Esakia Duality\\via Conic Frames'] We say a partially ordered space~$(X,\leq)$ is:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item a \emph{Priestley space} if~$X$ is Stone and \emph{Priestley separation} holds: for all $x\not\leq y$ there exists a clopen $U=\up U$ such that~$x\in U$ and~$y\notin U$;
		\item an \emph{Esakia space} if it is a Priestley space and~$\down$~preserves open subsets.
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.689323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4750e755f99cfe486aabd8a77b888acc020051d70b5bb2ddb362ed062aa35e7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 (Weighted local tempered norm) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] For $f\in\mathcal S'(\R^3)$ set
