{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.115366+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e475c11cd2533f32ab9cbb338ead0e0177bcced12faa494fd31998939f82af6d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:moments_of_nu of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Given $k \in \mathbb{N}$, let us denote the $k$'th moment of the cardinality of a random subset with law $\nu$ by
