{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.047483+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e487fb164d7f2c8584223d6bfdfd1ff73fd6d9640e70bd296d486f50602ed25d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Vanishing-mesh cutoff) of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Assume $0<A<A_c(N)$. Then, for every fixed $a\in\R$,
