{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.311193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e48a1398ee26c9ff50c6ddc6512c23a00ed22640798dbef8675662ab5d98d078","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] Suppose $p \ge 2$ and $d(p-1) < 2p$. The distributions $t^{-p} \widetilde{\ell}_t^{\otimes p}$ satisfies an LDP in $(\widetilde{\mathcal{X}}(\mathbb{R}^d), \mathbf{D})$ defined in \eqref{eq:MV-set}, \eqref{eq:MV-metric} with good rate function
