{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.856012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e48be79c3e4dd32dee5dce8127098f8c69d305a326d6be825273d50c23d42a55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 95 of arXiv:2511.20322, 'Dissertation'] Assume \assref{assum:H} and \assref{assum:barHandSi}. Further, assume we are given $\cR\in \dC \infty(\R^d)$, such that $\bar f = -\nabla \cR$ and $\nabla X_t^0$ is a symmetric matrix for all $t\geq 0$ and initial values. Let $x \in \R^d$, $D\in \set{0, \Si(X_\infty^0), \Si}$ and\footnote{In the case $D = \Si(X_\infty^0)$ we implicitly assume that the limit $X_\infty^0$ exists.} consider the solution $X$ to the family of \tSDE s 
	\[dX_t^h = - \nabla \cR(X_t^h)\,dt + \sqrt{h D(X_t^h)}\,dW_t, \quad X_0^h = x,\quad  t\in [0,T], h\in (0,1).\]
	Then we have
	\begin{align}

		\LE(X) = &\frac 12 \innp{\nabla^2 \cR(X_T^0)}{\al_T^D - T\nabla \cR(X_T^0)^{\otimes 2}} + \frac 12 \innp{\nabla \cR(X_T^0)}{\be_T^D},
	\end{align}
	where 
	\begin{align*}
		\al_T^D = & \int_0^T \nabla X_T^{0,t}(X_t^0) (\Si(X_t^0) - D(X_t^0))  \nabla X_T^{0,t}(X_t^0)\,dt \in \R^{d\times d}, \\
		\be_T^D = &\int_0^T \innp{\nabla^2 X_T^{0,t}(X_t^0)}{\nabla\cR(X_t^0)^{\otimes 2} + \Si(X_t^0) - D(X_t^0)}\,dt \in \R^d.
	\end{align*}
	Moreover,
	\begin{align}

		2|\LE(X)| \leq &d T M_T^2 |\nabla \cR(x)|^2 (|\nabla^2 \cR(X_T^0)| + d^{3/2}|\nabla \cR(x)| \zeta_T) \nonumber\\
		& + d\xi_T^D (|\nabla^2 \cR(X_T^0)| + \sqrt d |\nabla \cR(x)| \zeta_T),
	\end{align}
	where 
	\begin{align*}
		M_t =  \exp\left(-\int_0^t \la_{\min}(\nabla^2 \cR(X_s^0))\,ds\right), & \quad \zeta_t =  \int_0^t M_s |\nabla^3 \cR(X_s^0)|\,ds, \\
		\xi_t^D =  M_t^2 \int_0^t \frac{|\Si(X_s^0) - D(X_s^0)|}{M_s^2}\,ds&, \quad t\in [0,T].
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.531936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e48d79b9157d48da5a482a8128b537fab99f06ff8d0c78ce48991866b4ff6d88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 (the fiber-collapsing case) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Suppose $(\widehat{M}, g(t))$ encounters the finite-time singularity at $T = T_F' < \min_{k \geq 2} \{T_k^0, T_k^\ell\}$. Take $K_j := \big[ 2 ( m + 2 ) ( T - t_j ) \big]^{-1}$, and fix any base point $x_j \equiv \bar{x} \in \widehat{M}$. Define $g_j(t) = K_jg(t_j + K_j^{-1}t)$, where $t \in [-K_jt_j, K_j(T-t_j))$. Then, along a subsequence,

\begin{equation}
\big( \widehat{M}, \; g_j (t), \; \bar{x} \big) \;\longrightarrow\; \Big( \mathbb{CP}^{m+1} \times \mathbb{C}^{n'} \,, \;\; g_{\mathrm{FS}} (t) \oplus g_{\mathbb{C}^{n'}} \Big) \,, \qquad t \in \Big( - \infty, \tfrac{1}{2 ( m + 2 )} \Big) \,,
\end{equation}
in $C^\infty$-Cheeger-Gromov sense, where $g_{\mathbb{C}^{n'}}$ is the flat metric on $\mathbb{C}^{n'}$ with $n' = \dim_{\mathbb{C}}\widehat{M} - (m+1)$, and $g_{\mathrm{FS}} (t)$ is the shrinking Fubini--Study metric.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.251214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e491baf1d0fdc96f05e9cd8412d07ffdfd876623944589f58daf5f3a2e3d5520","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Integrated Davies trick) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] For any $q\in[1,\infty]$, denote by $q'$ its H\"older conjugate and let $0\leq V,W\in\ell^\infty(X),$ $I\subset \RR$. Then, for any $q$-norm with respect to any measure on $X$, we have 
\begin{multline*}
\left(
\fint_I \|VP_{2\tau}W\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^\frac{2}{q}
=
\left(
\fint_I \|WP_\tau V\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^{\frac{2}{q}}
\\
\leq 
\inf_{\omega\in\ell^\infty(X)}
\sup_{\supp V}\euler^{-\omega}
\sup_{\supp W}\euler^{\omega}
\left(
\fint_I
\|V P_\tau^\omega\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}
\left(
\fint_I
\|W P_\tau^{-\omega}\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}.
\end{multline*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.941750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e49366e27e803930dcac3733b5215aed7387cda6048d1b80de422d1c09febb40","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 47 (Fixed-rank Laurent integrality) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every zero-framed knot $K$, every fixed $n\ge2$, and every $k\ge0$,
