{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.874040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e52f6d4a60c04915194e204feacab9bf441648c211ef694be40620c79c41e9c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:core of invariant lower probabilities of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be a capacity preserving system, where $V$ is an upper probability. Then
	\begin{longlist}
		\item	for any $P\in \operatorname{core}(V)$, there exists a unique $\hat{P}\in \mathcal{M}(T)\cap\operatorname{core}(V)$ such that $P(A)=\hat{P}(A)$ for any $A\in\mathcal{I}$;
		\medskip
		\item given $A\in\mathcal{F}$, if for any $P\in\operatorname{core}(V)$, $\hat{P}(A)=0$, then $V(A)=0$.
	\end{longlist}","status":"unverified"}

