{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.344390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e53cb16425066bb4a03261713e407566762eda972c4a222ad414da0150e87931","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem chessboard-seminorm-bound of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] Suppose $4$ divides $L$. Fix any $\vec{f} = (f_1,...,f_k) \in E_1(\mathcal P)$, any $\vec{\Delta}$, and any $\vec{\mathcal W}$ compatible with those. If $\mathbf{V}$ satisfies~(equation eq:potential assumption of the paper) and $V_1(1)\ge \beta_0$, then 
