0 & (\text{if } i=j) \\
\left. -\frac{d}{dt}f_{i j}(b;t) \right|_{t=1} & ( \text{if } i\neq j)
\end{cases}
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.675593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e581dc71888a3709c50790c549067ff10e95b01ed91412e6ff070607eb02960e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2609.02699, '\vspace{-0.5 cm}Gauge theory and symplectic structures'] The equations on an almost Hermitian manifold $(M,g,J)$ for 
