    for $C,c>0$ constants independent of $N$ and $T$, depending only on $\beta$ and $\theta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.125272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5be7126406786abc51ac02a32de06b4af421867bf5e68c08f258d836024cc47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] There exist positive constants $\vt_1$ and $\eta_1$ and positive constants $c_1,c_2$, and $c_*0$, independent of $\eta_1$ and $\vt_1$, such that for every $\al>0$, 
