{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.331283+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5d5a13ba77e25dfc653a7d54dc15b7141dd0c3d9d2aaab4f8bbdec744b0f90c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop of arXiv:2505.12127, 'Generalised principal eigenvalues and global survival of branching Markov processes'] For any $\sigma>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \limsup_{\sigma{\rightarrow} 0}\lambda_1'(L_0^\sigma)\leq -\frac{1}{2}.
\end{equation}
