{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.193781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e61dbdc457de23f49947f4568799ece918988e68ca14890965727abf70dca0da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:MCMC of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] Consider a generator of the form 
((def:Glauber of the paper)) and suppose that for each $x\in\mathbb{X}$ and $i\in[n]$, the quantity
\begin{eqnarray*}
\delta_i(x) & := & c_i(x)-\sum_{j\in[n]\setminus\{i\}}\left(c_j(x^i)-c_j(x)\right)_+,
