{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.729017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e65fe58ad100746dbc07eeb74b0f325884eff2809f99e1cf3df3a4755f14d8e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 of arXiv:2608.29761, '2608.29761'] Let $\mathcal P$ be a finite collection of points in $\M$, and $\delta>0$. We say that $\mathcal P$ is a $\delta$-net  if
