{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.805303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e660bfea2875af6525bb42627c8ce2793f5413d5396dbaf04407ed373aa1d001","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:K6-7 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let $\mathsf{K}_6(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ and $\mathsf{K}_7(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ be defined in equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W2W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
