{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.388909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e662b563325e57fd7d41734af93786976832792d7d057fe58dbb7d3ceb0e9d32","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 72 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] Let \(k > 1\), \(I = \{1,\ldots ,k\}\), \(I_{1} = \{1\} ,\ldots ,I_{k - 1} = \{1,\ldots ,k - 1\}\). We have the isomorphism
