{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.502697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6a6cb8717055ca40d1eda10b8f88aabbfd2463713329112fca32e2e0e35e9fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (affine decay at the bolts) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Let $Q$ be one of the two bolts and let $\varepsilon_Q = +1$ at $Q_0$, $\varepsilon_Q = -1$ at $Q_\ell$, so that in the inward arclength coordinate at $Q$ the Kähler condition reads $( f_i^2 )' = \varepsilon_Q\, q_i\, h$. Then each restriction $f_i^2 |_Q$ is an \textbf{affine linear function of} $t$:

	\begin{equation}
		f_i^2 \big|_Q (t) \;=\; f_i^2 \big|_Q (0) \;+\; 2 \big( \varepsilon_Q\, q_i - p_i \big)\, t \,.
	\end{equation}

	Moreover, since $h > 0$ on $M^0$, \eqref{eq:kahler-condition} makes $f_i^2$ strictly monotone in $s$, so $\inf_{\widehat{M}} f_i^2$ is attained along the bolt at which $\varepsilon_Q\, q_i = | q_i |$, and

	\begin{equation}
		\inf_{\widehat{M}} f_i^2 (\cdot, t) \;=\; \inf_{\widehat{M}} f_i^2 (\cdot, 0) \;+\; 2 \big( | q_i | - p_i \big)\, t \,.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.751866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6a6d75990c9defba6da621696f74672ead7abebf7f651ae2bf6de2e0abadd55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Let $\cS_{T,h,g}$ be the following SFS operator:
\begin{equation}

\cS_{T,h,g} B=\e^{2\pi i g}\begin{pmatrix}
DT(T^{-1}) & 0\\
h(T^{-1}) & 1
\end{pmatrix}B(T^{-1}),
\end{equation}
where $h: \TT^2 \to \CC^2$ is a mean-free, smooth, vector, $g :\TT^2 \to \CC$ is a smooth function, and $T:\TT^2 \to \TT^2$ is a volume-preserving diffeomorphism isotopic to the identity. Then, there exists $C_r, C_{r,\delta}>0$ independent of $T,h$, so that there holds the following Lasota--Yorke inequality
\begin{align}
\|\cS_{T,h,g} B\|_{\mathcal X} \leq C_{LY,S}(T,h,g)\|B\|_{\mathcal X}+C_{LY,W}(T,h,g)\|B\|_{\mathcal Y}
\end{align}
where 
\begin{equation}

C_{LY,S}(T,h,g)=C_{r,\delta}\|\e^{2\pi i g}\|_{L^\infty}\bigl (\|DT \|_{L^\infty}^{1-r}+\|DT \|_{L^\infty}^{r+\delta} \bigr) ,
\end{equation}
\begin{align}

C_{LY,W}(T,h,g)& =C_{r,\delta}(\|\e^{2\pi i g}\|_{L^\infty}\bigl (\|DT\|_{L^\infty}+\|DT\|_{L^\infty}^{r+\delta}\| h\|_{C^1} \bigr )\\
&\quad +\|\nabla (\e^{2\pi i g})\|_{L^\infty} \bigl(\|DT\|_{L^\infty}^{1-r+\delta}+\|DT\|_{L^\infty}+\|DT\|_{L^\infty}^{r+2\delta}(1+\|h\|_{C^1}) \bigr )) \notag.
\end{align}
Finally, there holds the weak-to-weak bound 
$$
\|\cS_{T,h,g} B\|_{\mathcal Y} \leq C_{LY,WW}(T,h,g)\|B\|_{\mathcal Y},
$$
where 
\begin{align}

&C_{LY,WW}(T,h,g)=C_{r,\delta}\|\e^{2\pi i g}\|_{C^1}\bigl(\|DT\|_{L^\infty}^{1-r+\delta}+\|DT\|_{L^\infty}+\|DT\|_{L^\infty}^{r+2\delta}(1+\|h\|_{C^1}) \bigr ).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.066656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6a73f27894a75ca067fc9db484387ee0a5966d84b17ba4506a62a039af83948","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2606.27520, 'Critical curve of loop percolation on the $d$-regular tree'] Let $\alpha>0$ and $\kappa\geq\kappa_c$. Let $u,v,w$ be vertices such that $v$ lies on the geodesic between $u$ and $w$. Then 
