{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.559749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6de8b4bf380dfca57b4f7c5d7b77a1c3c317fc31a57381d4ad94dd21bd36499","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:Nachmias_diam of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Fix $\varepsilon > 0$ and $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}$. There exists $A = A(\varepsilon, \lambda) < \infty$ and $n_0=n_0(\varepsilon,\lambda)\in \mathbb{N}$ such that
