{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.355247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6df2a452b60b9d86acabdd034a07cc6ec7b68a2669c3c6d29f57fe0f9f728fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: main theorem in simple continuous time form of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] For every continuous time scaling triplet $((t_n), (w_n),p)$, there exists a sequence of continuous time Markov chains $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+})_{n\geq 1}$ such that for every $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $, we have 
