\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.705080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e712b68dff38c72e07d4089fc509bbbe54357abbb2f930d44c4e62d381a49057","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2608.06038, 'Efron type identities\\ for stopping sets and Poisson hulls'] Let $B\in\cX_0$, $k\in\N$ and $l\in\N_0$. Then
