{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.554208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7203122fd3b3487a75a7795703f342630407177ae3dc17d942fe261b94a2618","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cint of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] For all $x,y\in[n]$ with $x\neq y$  and uniformly over $u\in [0,1]$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb E\bigl[u^{d(x)+d(y)}\mathbf{1}_{x,y\in\mathcal{Q}_n\cap \mathcal{T}_n}  \mathbf{1}_{B_{\omega}(x)\cap B_{\omega}(y)\neq  \varnothing}\bigr]  = \frac{c_{\textrm{int}}(w,u)}{n}+ O\Bigl(\frac{1}{n^2}\Bigr),
\end{align}
where 
\begin{equation}
c_{\textrm{int}}(w,u) :=  2\sum_{(i,j)\in \mathcal{M}} \mathbb E^{i,j,\ell_{i,j}}_{\mathbf{Y},\mathbf{Y}'} \bigl[u^{Y_k+Y_k'}\mathbf{1}_{Y_{2k}=Y_{2k}'=0}\bigr].
\end{equation}
where $\mathbb E^{i,j,\ell_{i,j}}_{\mathbf{Y},\mathbf{Y}'} \bigl[u^{Y_k+Y_k'}\mathbf{1}_{Y_{2k}=Y_{2k}'=0}\bigr]$ is explicitly given by Proposition~(prop:cross_monster of the paper), 
	and where $\mathcal{M}=\mathcal{M}(w^2)$, $\ell_{i,j}=\ell_{i,j}(w^2)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.230949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e722b4584494eaac84d8095e7e1ef3fb24f7619b2b6c390067db7df5c47bfae5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 46 (Consistent collection of flows) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $M \subset M_0$, its open covering $V=\{S_i \subset M\  |\  i \in I \}$, and locally defined flows 
\begin{equation*}
CF=\{{\Psi}_i \in FLOW(S_i) \ |\ i \in I\}.
\end{equation*}
$CF$ is called \textit{consistent} if
\begin{equation*}
{\Psi_i}|_{S_i \cap S_j}={\Psi_j}|_{S_i \cap S_j} \quad  (i, j \in I).
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.677777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e725787f5e47dbffba9bf1f00c4d8e04711451b5f1ad75cd764e20aec24a4754","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lmm:poly-highsnr of arXiv:2602.14998, 'Random geometric graphs with smooth kernels: sharp detection threshold and a spectral conj'] Suppose the kernel $K(t)$ satisfies the conditions in~\prettyref{thm:highsnr}. 
There exists a degree-$L$ polynomial $\widetilde K(t) = \sum_{\ell\geq 0}^L a_\ell t^\ell$ 
that satisfies
