{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.204718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e72b9d61461e92162096576932f04d2ae4c0fea5e9db3f6d8888685e5995b786","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Let $(\eta_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a multi-class stochastic six-vertex process on the line with parameters $0<b_1<b_2<1$ and with the following initial conditions:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item There are some first-class particles (finitely or infinitely many).
        \item There are infinitely many second-class particles, all to the right of $0$.
        \item There are infinitely many third-class particles, all at or to the left of $0$.
        \item All other positions are empty, i.e., have class $\infty$.
    \end{itemize}
    Let $\cdots < {Z}_t(-1) <  {Z}_t(0)<{Z}_t(1)<\cdots$ be the ordered positions of the second- and third-class particles at time $t$, where $Z_t(0)$ is chosen such that the number of third-class particles among $(Z_t(k))_{k>0}$ equals the number of second-class particles among $(Z_t(k))_{k\leq0}$.
    Let $\xi_t$ denote the configuration obtained by considering the labeling process of the second and third-class particles at time $t$ where a second-class particle receives label $1$ and a third-class particle receives label $0$. In other words, let 
    \begin{equation}
    \xi_t(k) = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if ${Z}_t(k)$ contains a second-class particle} \\ 0 & \text{if ${Z}_t(k)$ contains a third-class particle, } \end{cases}
    \end{equation}
    for $k\in\mathbb Z$.
    Then for any $t$, the law of $\xi_t$ conditioned on both $\bm{Z} = (Z_s(k))_{ s \leq t,k \in \mathbb Z}$ and the space-time history of the first-class particles, is stochastically dominated by the blocking measure $\pi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.240692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e72c53700c93d88c87920062487106ecc0fe8852100eaa794f131aa05a6d1480","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 62 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix $M\in \N$ and consider a family of $(\delta,N)$-patched ASEPs $\big(\eta^{\textup{patch},N,i}_t\big)_{t \geq 0}$ for $i\in \lbr M \rbr$. Let $\big(\bar{\eta}^{N,i}_t\big)_{t \geq 0}$ be a family of unwrapped $N$-periodic ASEPs such that for all $i\in \lbr M \rbr$ and $N\in \N$
\begin{equation}
    \eta^{\textup{patch},N,i}_0 =  \bar{\eta}^{N,i}_0  
\end{equation} almost surely. Fix some $T>0$. Assume that \eqref{eq:DominationAssumptionPatch} holds for the processes in the definition of $\big(\bar{\eta}^{N,i}_t\big)_{t \geq 0}$. Then there exists a coupling $\mathbf{P}_{\ast}$ and  $c_1,C_1>0$ such that for all $\delta>0$
\begin{align}
\liminf_{N \rightarrow \infty}\mathbf{P}_{\ast}\left( \bar{\eta}^{N,i}_t = \eta^{\textup{patch},N,i}_t  \ \forall t \in [0,T N^{3/2}] , \,  i \in \lbr M \rbr\right) \geq 1- C_1\exp(-c_1\delta^{-1}) . 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e72f0dbc58b76f97ca3246cebb9c0765d6475b8a957f4070ecab4a482d763243","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:two_sided_current of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:conc_current of the paper), for all $t>0$ and $a>0$,
