{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.474822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7332321826c608e6d676b9dd384644678a78699ca4bcd2ca1ff64b8c88e4baa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def : Topology/GMT/Gradient of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $D \in \RegPD[\mu]$ and $z\in X$. The \emph{gradient by paths} of $D$ at $z$ is defined as the function
