{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.826402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e73ac31dd19fe77fbc261e4833516cdd204c8836094be0b8012769a88b2eb43b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def: chi-square distance of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Given two distributions $P, Q$ whose supports are the subset of the countable set $\cS$ and $P$ is absolutely continuous w.r.t $Q$ 

