{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.865164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7442938630ce9357680087daf10aa445f32d1b37b7c3be6d51ea5ad456b35a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 2 of arXiv:2609.02427, 'Ampleness in the Farey graph'] \cite{PillayGeomFork, AmpleDividing}
Let $T$ be a stable theory and $n\geq1$. Then $T$ is $n$-ample if (after possibly adding some parameters) there are 
$a_0,a_1,\ldots,a_n$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $a_0$ forks with $a_n$ over $\emptyset$;
\item $a_{i+1}$ does not fork with $a_0,\ldots,a_{i-1}$ over $a_i$, for $1\leq i<n$;
\item $\acl^{eq}(a_0)\cap \acl^{eq}(a_1)=\acl^{eq}(\emptyset)$;
\item $\acl^{eq}(a_0,\ldots,a_{i-1},a_i)\cap acl^{eq}(a_0,\ldots,a_{i-1},a_{i+1})=\acl^{eq}(a_0,\ldots,a_{i-1})$, for $1\leq i<n$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.473808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e748d30a842be05754a0cdd8dc305ba29a49280ed165e22753049f597a39fb3a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:dI-budget of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:aggregate-jet-budget}
Uniformly in \(O\in\mathcal O_{N,L}\),
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{I\in[N]^p}\mathfrak d_I\le C N,
 \qquad
 \max_{I\in[N]^p}\mathfrak d_I\le Cq_N^2.
\end{equation}
Writing \(\alpha_I(J)=\partial_I\Psi_O(J)\), one also has
\begin{equation}
 \max_I\left\lvert\alpha_I(J)\right\rvert\le Cq_N,
 \qquad
 \sum_I\left\lvert\alpha_I(J)\right\rvert^2\le CN,
\end{equation}
and, for \(2\le k\le m+1\),
\begin{equation}
 \left\lvert\partial_I^k\Psi_O(J)\right\rvert
 \le C_k\mathfrak d_Iq_N^{k-2}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for \(2\le k\le m+1\),
\begin{align}
 \left\lvert\partial_I^kF_O(J)\right\rvert
 &\le C_kF_O(J)
 \left(\left\lvert\alpha_I(J)\right\rvert^k+
       \mathfrak d_Iq_N^{k-2}\right),
 \\
 \sum_I\left\lvert\partial_I^kF_O(J)\right\rvert
 &\le C_kNq_N^{k-2}F_O(J).

\end{align}
All constants are uniform in \(J,N,O\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.433009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7499bd48b6e4ae49c74e5e575cca7979e2ed3443eb7ad7d0d7d0151f317a5ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma10.444 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Under the assumption of Theorem (Theorem1.2 of the paper), for any $\delta_1,\delta_2\geq e^{-cn^{\sigma}}$, any $u\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$, and any $p>1$, we have the following estimate:
