{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.679849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e75dc0a40ef70a679d89d4916f2a6a96d10bea87f51aad1db32436e583e6df33","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 35 (Lossless decoding of the step-two It\^o signature) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Under an accessible operational type, the modelwise solution of
\eqref{eq:primitive-triangular-system} is
\[
 U_{s,t}^{P,s}=X_{s,t},
 \qquad
 V_{s,t}^{P,s}=\mathbb X^{I,P}_{s,t}
 =A^P_{s,t}+\frac12
   \bigl(X_{s,t}^{\otimes2}-\qv{M^P}_{s,t}\bigr).
\]
It obeys the lossless identities
\begin{equation}

 A^P_{s,t}=\Anti V_{s,t}^{P,s},
 \qquad
 \qv{M^P}_{s,t}
 =(U_{s,t}^{P,s})^{\otimes2}
  -V_{s,t}^{P,s}-(V_{s,t}^{P,s})^*.
\end{equation}
Hence the standard step-two It\^o signature determines both central channels
of the canonical state.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.197376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7639f6484dddbe8c4edcc1d00aef616f6ab64a63af392677de8819c5ac4138b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Fu_derivative of arXiv:2608.13452, 'Wasserstein stability of the zero cell of a Poisson hyperplane tessellation under directio'] Let $x\geq 0$ and $u\in S^{d-1}$.
