{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.420723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e767fcb2401a335562b03681af490cf8feec9ee7b47fcd73a6315e9cbf06220d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 53 of arXiv:2608.20252, '2608.20252'] Let $f\in L^2(Q)$ and define $\hat f \in L^2(Q)$ to be the projection onto the subspace $H_0$.  In other words, $\hat f$ is the conditional expectation $\hat f = E[f| \mathcal T]$ with respect to the time-shift invariant sets $\mathcal T$.

