{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.387653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e78531ddbdae6e7c23e8e5b7656ce9147cb3900d57f4c9d0a2f95805a6850556","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:J-opt of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mu,\nu\in \Lambda_2(\mathbb R^d)$ and set $\mathcal{A}=\Lambda_{\text{glob}}(0,0,\mu)$, $\mathcal{B}=\Lambda_{\text{glob}}(0,0,\nu)$. 
