{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.783178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7bf913359838ea8a7f1e7737d7167311c8beb673c9b3929043f22c921ff1b4b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 18 of arXiv:2604.00190, '2604.00190'] For $\bfb \in \Xi^\nu$, there exists a measurable function $p_\bfb$ from $E$ to $[0, 1]$ such that for $y\in E$, 
