{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.329479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7c20e4b2a54389981ca79a74edb8c4b4da339d77fd1329e09188ec14a1e73ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor diag-preserve of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The functor $\textup{diag}\colon{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-lvl}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-gl}$ inverts $G$-global weak equivalences.
    \begin{proof}
        By cocontinuity (Lemma~(lemma:delta*-cc of the paper)), it suffices to show that $\textup{diag}$ inverts the maps in the set $S$ from Construction~(constr:S of the paper). By definition of the latter together with the previous lemma, it then suffices (after possibly changing the compact Lie group $G$) to show that all maps of the form $\smash{\textup{const}\,\kappa_{V,W}^{G,G}}$ for $G$-representations $V,W$ are inverted. As $\textup{diag}\circ\textup{const}=\textup{id}_{\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}}$, this is an instance of Proposition~(prop:kappa-gl of the paper).
