{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.250943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7ca826f6684b1a584cbed70a5f952f04415496e4da360b23e55b3609d87568d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 57 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let $(H_s)_{s \ge 0}$ denote the height function at time $s$ for the Glauber dynamic on $\mX$, with floor constraint $\cH_{-q_0}$ and ceiling constraint $\cH_{q_0}$ (as in \Cref{def:constrained}), started from the maximal configuration compatible with these constraints (recall \Cref{def:partorder}). Then, for each $j \in [0, \mathfrak{j}]$ and $w \in \mathfrak{X}$, let 
