{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.619645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7cb63789cd66096811a96d9d42686549712749df43f7d00944654a86de9a85a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop_decrease_of_phi of arXiv:2606.23648, '\textsc{Optimal Stopping for a Diffusion with Unobserved Bernoulli Drift}'] Fix \(x\ge0\), and suppose that \(k_x'(y)>0\) for all \(y\in I_x^\circ\). Assume that \(\Theta_x\) is convex on \(I_x^-\), and that $\Theta_x(y) \ge 0$ holds for every $y \in I_x^+$.
