{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.695220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7d9788618a59152b4287c5e8052eba251959cba37173d1ece1a347f05bb0733","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp prpAppExpEst_LDP of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] There exists $C>0$ such that for any $\sigma>0$, any $s, t\in \mathbb{T}$ such that $t\neq s\in \mathbb{T}$,
