{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.902661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7e66c4bb98d146a4eb4ad236388549fea242e8217c343b0d55955db1b2fa45b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:controlledRP of arXiv:2607.19037, 'Semiclassical analysis for Yang--Mills \\ random connections on compact surfaces'] Given a rough path \(\mathbf{W}\in \mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,1],\mathfrak{g})\), we say that a path \(Y\) is controlled by \(\mathbf{W}\) if there exists \(Y' \in \mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,1],\mathrm{End}(\mathfrak{g}))\) such that
