{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.761442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7eda1a40f22dfff1dcc098212dbc840db97546bfd89eca5d09b466a7f46c8a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition increment-moments of arXiv:2604.27682, 'Multifractional Stable Motion with Random Hurst Exponent'] Under condition (equation eq: continuity assumption on H of the paper), for any $\delta>0$, there are constants $C > 0$ and $\epsilon > 0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \left\|\frac{X(t)-X(s)}{|t-s|^{\min_{r\in[s \wedge t,s \vee t]} H(r) - \frac{1}{\alpha} - \delta}}\right\|_{\Lambda^\alpha(\Omega)}^\alpha \leq C |t-s|, \quad \text{whenever } |t-s|\leq \epsilon.
    \end{align*}
    Hence, for any $\delta > 0$ and $\frac{\alpha}{1+\alpha\delta/2}<p<\alpha$, there are constants $C > 0$ and $\epsilon > 0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \left\|\frac{X(t)-X(s)}{|t-s|^{\min_{r\in[s \wedge t,s \vee t]} H(r) - \frac{1}{\alpha}-\delta}}\right\|_{\mathbb{L}^p(\Omega)}^p \leq C |t-s|,\quad \text{whenever } |t-s|\leq \epsilon.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.574572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7f032ac2fbeec6ceb69bf18305e594a8523a787686252d8fecbc4df9b02db55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem C theorem of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] Let $\mathbf{C}_{p\times n}$ be a sequence of non-symmetric rectangular random circulant matrices defined in (equation definition of C of the paper) and satisfying assumptions (equation Lyapunov of the paper) and (equation new asymptotic regime of the paper). Then, as $n \to \infty$, the spectral norm satisfies
