If, in addition, (equation stronger asymptotic regime of the paper) holds, then the convergence in probability in (equation main convergence C of the paper) strengthens to convergence in $L^\gamma$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.653904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7f0d6e6918df5c0e455768127ed96cf5da8be5fb13c0e1d90223006c736e6f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:cluster-expansion of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] There is a $\beta^* = \beta^*(d)>0$ such that 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item For any loop $\ell \in \Lambda$, $\langle W_{\ell} \rangle_{\beta,\Lambda}$ is an analytic function of $\beta$ in $\mbb{D}(0,\beta^*)$ and for real $\beta$ in this disk, there is a unique infinite volume limit of the Yang--Mills measure such that,
    \begin{equs}
        \langle W_{\ell} \rangle_{\beta,\Lambda_L} \to \langle W_{\ell} \rangle_{\beta,\Lambda_{\infty}}
    \end{equs}
    uniformly on $\mbb{D}(0,\beta^*)$ as $L \to \infty$.
    \item For any $L <\infty$, $Z_{\beta,\Lambda_L} \neq 0$ for all $\beta \in \mathbb{D}(0,\beta^*)$, and thus,
