{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.714201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e816a15cdc3160adad635d4a934ca8095ceb85a09b488c3a383df909fd97941d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:TLC_Holder of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] Let $\alpha\in\left(0,1/2\right)$ and define $p\left(\alpha\right):=\left(1/2-\alpha\right)^{-1}$. 
