Moreover, $\eta^x_{t}$ is twice differentiable in mean square with respect to $x$, and the first derivative $\partial _x\eta^x_{t}$ and the second derivative $\partial^2_x\eta^x_{t}$ satisfy that for all $t\ge s$, $x\in \mathbb{R}^n$ and $y\in \mathbb{R}^m$
