{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.186684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8886b50e0cbffdbe671aac1d17da31102fae5115f7a75047e92c7ec952eae57","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:types-short of arXiv:2608.05123, 'A central limit theorem for the random assignment problem'] Under \(\mathbb P_n^{\mathrm{ref}}\), the empirical law of \((A_i,U_i)\) converges
weakly in probability to
