{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.220551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e88a1572cacf9b74fe2d53f3d3df7cb4bee931e963c5319fdb31b5512b0af837","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] Suppose assumption (A4) holds for some $R_0>0$. For each  $x_0\in \sX$ and $R\in (0, R_0/8),$   there exists $C=C(x_0, R)>0$ such that
