{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.600235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8ac5de7b821769ffae56c0a8054ab58b26c05ce6c058e899705c1d9a69954af","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn:nvali of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For ${\mathfrak d},C_*>0$, a Nevanlinna function $Y$ is \emph{$({\mathfrak d}, C_*)$-Airy-like}, or simply \emph{Airy-like}, if 
