{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.981352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8c941a240fb023ffbb121cb0275cf1eebb712f9c2c91d1f2d52ebd807765d37","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:truncated_expectation_bound_at_doubling_scales of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] If $\alpha<d$ then there exist positive constants $c$ and $C$ such that
