        $ (\mathbb{g}^{\bullet\circ}, \mathbb{g}^{\circ\bullet}) \in  \mathcal{C}^{\beta+\gamma}_2([0,1]^2;  (V\otimes E) \times (E\otimes V) )$, and that the Chen's relations
        \begin{equs}                
            \mathbb{g}^{\bullet\circ}_{s, t}-\mathbb{g}^{\bullet\circ}_{s, u}- \mathbb{g}^{\bullet\circ}_{u, t}= g^\bullet_{s, u} \otimes g^\circ_{u, t}, \qquad \mathbb{g}^{\circ\bullet}_{s, t}-\mathbb{g}^{\circ\bullet}_{s, u}- \mathbb{g}^{\circ\bullet}_{u, t}= g^\circ_{s, u} \otimes g^\bullet_{u,t}       
        \end{equs}
        hold for all $(s,u,t)\in[0,1]^3_\leq$.
        Moreover, we set 
        \begin{equ}
         \,    [{\color{purp}g}]_{\mathcal{R}^{\gamma, \beta}}= [g^{\bullet}]_{\mathcal{C}^\gamma}+ [g^{\circ}]_{\mathcal{C}^\beta}+[\mathbb{g}^{\bullet \bullet}]_{\mathcal{C}^{2\gamma}_2}+[\mathbb{g}^{\circ  \bullet}]_{\mathcal{C}^{\gamma+ \beta}_2}+[\mathbb{g}^{\bullet \circ}]_{\mathcal{C}^{\gamma+ \beta}_2}.
