{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.485610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9650223afb6fcf4d6f09c7f965950824d163b68d519ac298cd02d0abee19d06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2605.28377, 'Geometric functionals of Brownian motion on Hermitian symmetric spaces of non-compact type'] We have for every $t>0$, $\alpha >0$ and $\tau \in \bar{\mathcal{C}}$
    \begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left( e^{i\alpha S(t)} \mid \tau(t)= \tau \right) & =\mathbb{E}\left( e^{-\frac{\alpha^2}{2}  \gamma \sum_{i=1}^r \int_0^t \tanh(\tau_i(s))^2\,ds } \mid \tau(t)= \tau \right) \\
 &=e^{n\alpha \sqrt{\gamma}t} \frac{p^{a,1+2\alpha \sqrt{\gamma},2 b-2\alpha \sqrt{\gamma}}_t(\tau(0),\tau)}{p^{a,1,2 b}_t(\tau(0),\tau)}\prod_{i=1}^r \left( 4 \cosh (\tau_i(0)) \cosh (\tau_i)  \right)^{\alpha \sqrt{\gamma}},   
    \end{align*}
    where $p^{k_1,k_2,k_3}_t$ is the heat kernel of the Heckman-Opdam Laplacian $\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{L}_{k_1,k_2,k_3}$ about which details are collected in Appendix \ref{sec:Heckman-Opdam_Laplacians}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.471831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9658ed807079e310011f1595fd4e187371c250300c93f7064d8cf7fb1b61263","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Exp1overDeg of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] Let $\psi_1(z):=\frac{d^2}{dz^2}\log(\Gamma(z))$ be the trigamma function. Then 
