{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.218988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e96e993a8148c9e7b7acc05ddcd572fc5bbd33c81e59b0584a2dbfa955b5f7a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (Properties of uniform spacings) of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] Recall for each $i=2,\dots,n$ the variables $|E^{(i)}_j|=U^{(j-1)}_{i-1}-U^{(j)}_{i-1}$, where $U^{(1)}_{i-1}<\dots<U^{(i-1)}_{i-1}$ are the order statistics of $U_1,\dots,U_{i-1}$.
 \begin{itemize}
     \item [(i)] The variables $|E^{(i)}_1|,\dots |E^{(i)}_i|$ are identically distributed and satisfy $$\Prob{|E^{(i)}_1|>x}=(1-x)^{i-1},x\in [0,1].$$
     \item [(ii)] $|E^{(i)}_1|\stackrel{d}{=}1-U^{1/(i-1)},$ where $U$ is uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$.
     \item [(iii)]  $|E^{(1)}_1|=1$, and for $i\geq 2$, $|E^{(i)}_1|\prec E/(i-1)$, where $E\stackrel{d}{=} \mathrm{Exp}(1)$ is exponentially distributed.      
 \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.015302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e96ed9d3d67361a0a85e33d142ee3d7f7e8f0d10edecaba53033f0b710fcb1b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 of arXiv:2605.05430, 'Dirichlet problems and exit distributions for the telegraph process and its planar extensi'] For $x\in[a,b]$, it holds that
