{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.822094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e974d6c547e3352f71db91e289ea21e040100c0af77ac9d0220e3496b80d4777","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thmmin of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Assume that the minimal $\mathrm{CBDI}$ processes $X^{\mathrm{m}}$ and $Y^{\mathrm{m}}$ with mechanisms respectively $(\Psi,\hat{\Psi})$ and $(\hat{\Psi},\Psi)$ do not explode. Then, under the convention $0^+\cdot \infty,\ \infty\cdot 0^+,$
		\begin{equation}\mathbb{E}_{x}[e^{-X^{\mathrm{m}}_ty}]=\mathbb{E}^{y}[e^{-xY^{\mathrm{m}}_t}], \ \forall (x,y)\in [0,\infty]^2,\ t \in [0,\infty).\end{equation}
		Moreover, $X^{\mathrm{m}}$, whose boundary $0$ is absorbing, is Feller at $0$:
		\[\mathbb{E}_{0}[e^{-X^{\mathrm{m}}_ty}]=\mathbb{E}_{0+}[e^{-X^{\mathrm{m}}_ty}]=\mathbb{P}^{y}(Y^{\mathrm{m}}_t<\infty)=1, \ \forall y\in [0,\infty],\ t \in [0,\infty),\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.664866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e974eaf6e1cff2f9d4cbf92b061461d628e7d663827320950a02a389cd69c9bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:LPS6.1 of arXiv:2411.00748, '\bfseries Central limit theorems for the nearest neighbour embracing graph in Euclidean an'] Let $F$ be an integrable Poisson functional such that $\mathbb{E} \int (D_x F)^2 \lambda (dx) < \infty$ and $\operatorname{Var} F > 0$, and let $N$ be a standard Gaussian random variable. Assume there are constants $c_1, c_2 > 0$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{E}|D_x F|^5 &\le c_1\qquad \text{for $\lambda$-a.e. $x \in \mathbb{Y}$},\\
        \mathbb{E}|D_{x,y} F|^5 &\le c_2\qquad \text{for $\lambda^2$-a.e. $(x,y) \in \mathbb{Y}^2$}.
    \end{align}
    Writing $\bar{c} = \max\{1,c_1,c_2\}$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        d_W \Big( \frac{F - \mathbb{E} F}{\sqrt{\operatorname{Var} F}}, N \Big) \le \, &\frac{3 \bar{c}}{\operatorname{Var} F} \Big[\int \Big( \int \mathbb{P}(D_{x,y}F \ne 0)^{1/20} \lambda(dy) \Big)^2 \lambda(dx)\Big]^{1/2}\\
        &+ \frac{\bar{c}}{(\operatorname{Var} F)^{3/2}} \int \mathbb{P}(D_x F \ne 0)^{2/5} \lambda (dx)
    \end{align*}
    as well as
    \begin{align*}
        d_K \Big( \frac{F - \mathbb{E} F}{\sqrt{\operatorname{Var} F}}, N \Big) \le \,
        &\frac{3\bar{c}}{\operatorname{Var} F} \Big[\int \Big( \int \mathbb{P}(D_{x,y}F \ne 0)^{1/20} \lambda(dy) \Big)^2 \lambda(dx)\Big]^{1/2}\\
        &+ \frac{2\bar{c}}{\operatorname{Var} F} \left(\int \mathbb{P}(D_x F \ne 0)^{1/5} \lambda(dx)\right)^{1/2}\\
        &+\frac{13\bar{c}}{\operatorname{Var} F} \Big(\int \int \mathbb{P}(D_{x,y}F \ne 0)^{1/20} \lambda(dy) \lambda(dx)\Big)^{1/2}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.330832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9767ce995efad0bb77d5d6026fe750d4300bc54c0dec106cde3eb7e47dfc1d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Theorem~2 in \cite{HebischSikora1990} of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\mathbb G$ be any homogeneous Carnot group equipped with the  dilations $(\delta_\lambda)_{\lambda>0}$. Then there exists $\varepsilon_0>0$ such that for every $0<\kappa<\varepsilon_0$, 
