{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.509015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9a539c459d5f41a38350edb35060cdcd203a2eeca44653319af3946ac89dd56","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 of arXiv:2609.02581, '\bfseries Interior Curvature Estimates for the Graphical Scalar Curvature Equation in All '] Under the assumptions of Proposition~\ref{prop:jacobi}, with
\(I\) defined by
\eqref{def:good-bad-directions}, we have
\begin{equation}
 \sum_i\Theta_iT_u^{ii}b_i^2
 \geq
 \frac12\sum_{i\in I}T_u^{ii}b_i^2
 -\frac{n-4}{n}
  \sum_{i\notin I}T_u^{ii}b_i^2.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 T_u^{ij}h_i^kh_{kj}\geq\frac{H^2}{64}
 \sum_{i\notin I}T_u^{ii}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, \eqref{eq:jacobi} implies
