{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.302307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9bdfa76d41939bda9635af602b5f0ae215a30ab9144d28482fd34a0401ccef7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition3.3 of arXiv:2604.22130, 'Reflected Stochastic Differential Equations Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Nonlinear C'] Suppose $g^i,h^i$ satisfy Assumption (ass of the paper), $i=1,2$ with $h^1\geq h^2$ and $g^1\leq g^2$. For any given $s\in D[0,\infty)$, let $(x^i,k^i)$ be the solution to the Skorokhod problem $\mathbb{SP}_{g^i}^{h^i}(s)$ with $k^i=k^{i,h}-k^{i,g}$. Then, for any $t\geq 0$, we have
