{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.184014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9dc820053f8371ac03e5aa0fa3090f63cdd6c5dcbf2ffe3de81a599c463c094","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:MNGridDimTheory of arXiv:2508.08150, 'Recent Progress on Fractal Percolation'] Let $F$ be fractal percolation on the $M\times N$ grid with retention probability $p$. If $p\leq
1/(MN)$ then $F=\varnothing$ almost surely, otherwise, there is a positive probability that $F\neq
