    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.551311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea177e70b55c20b630506f3cbedf42f5d6b5da3523d1385b43c2d859e0c4b53d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Uniform sub-Gaussian moments of the nonlinear law) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:concentration}, together with either kernel assumption, there are $a>0$ and $C<\infty$ such that
