{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.569462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea2616f50cf3a5e3a4b89e50424300eb561c69db447cdec6610d4f0c8cd1040f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor.uniform-renewal of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Let $\theta\in(0,1/4)$ and $\varepsilon>0$. There exist a $\mathbb{Q}$-full-probability event $\Omega_{\theta,\varepsilon}$ and a deterministic constant $C=C(\theta,\varepsilon,d,\Lambda,r_0)<\infty$ such that, for every $\omega\in\Omega_{\theta,\varepsilon}$, there exists a finite random scale $\lambda_0(\omega)>0$ with the property that for every $0<\lambda\le\lambda_0(\omega)$ and every $t\ge\lambda^{-2-\varepsilon}$,
		\begin{equation}
			E_0^{\lambda,\omega}|X^\lambda(t)-\ell(\lambda)t|\le C\sqrt t (\lambda^2 t)^\theta\, ,
		\end{equation}
		and
		\begin{equation}
			\widehat E_0^{\lambda,\omega}|A^\lambda(t)-\eta(\lambda)t|\le C\lambda^{-1}\sqrt t (\lambda^2 t)^\theta\, .
		\end{equation}
		Moreover, $\lambda_0$ has polynomial tails of every order: for each $p>0$ there is $C_p=C_p(p,\theta,\varepsilon,d,\Lambda,r_0)<\infty$ such that
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{Q}\bigl(\lambda_0\le 2^{-k}\bigr)\le C_p 2^{-pk}\qquad\text{for every integer }k\ge 0\, .
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.539285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea262a586673a24c4892322891781cafc7d0bb286f967382e04b91be2cf19beb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: Bounds A-loc. states of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Consider a nearest-neighbor $\mathbb{Z}_q$-valued clock model with Gibbsian specification defined via the transfer operator $Q(i)=e^{-\beta \overline{u}(i)}$ where the function $\overline{u}$ satisfies the $u,U,d$-condition (equation eq: u,U-bounds of the paper). Then, we have 
   \begin{equation}
    (q-1)^{\frac{2}{d+1}}e^{-\beta U}\leq\epsilon \leq (q-1)^{\frac{2}{d+1}}e^{-\beta u}.
\end{equation}
   Furthermore, let $ A \subset \mathbb{Z}_q$ with $n=|A|\geq 1$ and $\beta$ be large enough, then there exists a spatially homogeneous tree-indexed Markov chain Gibbs measure $\mu_A$ which is localized on the subset $A$. The transition matrix $P_A$ is strictly positive and the following bounds hold:  
   \begin{align*}
       (i) ~\|&\Delta|_{A^c}\|_{\frac{d+1}{d-1}}\leq C_1 e^{-(d-1)\beta u},~~~~(ii)~\min_{i\in A} \Delta(i)>1-C_2e^{-\beta u},\\
        (iii) ~\sum_{i\in A^c} \pi_A(i) \leq C_1&  e^{-(d+1)\beta u},~~~~(iv)~ \Big(1-(C_1+C_2)  e^{-\beta u} \Big) \frac{1}{|A|}\leq \pi_A|_A  \leq \left(1-C_2e^{-\beta u}\right)^{-1} \frac{1}{|A|}
   \end{align*}
   where $C_1:=2^{d+1}d^3(n+1)^{d}(q-1)^{2}$ and $C_2:=3d(d^{\frac{1}{d-1}}-1)(n+1)(q-1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.243066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea26b2ef2f15798cf200caaf1e4ac38da57e8850a989d5ca0b956a9c98f85343","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 28 of arXiv:2603.05174, 'Regularization of the superposition principle: Potential theory meets Fokker-Planck equati'] If \eqref{eq:b da in L2 loc duplicate}, \eqref{eq:ellipticity_duplicate}, and \eqref{eq:hu in H-1} hold, then for every $\gamma\in(0,1)$ we have 
