{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.697517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea27c57fcb7f183770749f903e8a21ef74b0c1f7ed0790a1928882d394d07e7c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: double-connection-trunc of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Let $\epsilon > 0$ be fixed. There exists a $C = C(\epsilon) > 0$ such that, for all $1 \leq M \leq K \leq \epsilon n / 2$ and edges $f \in B(M)$, vertices $x_1, x_2 \in F(\epsilon, n)$, we have
