{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.586708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea5143324918bd43ea0483bd788640f4da5c77422f3bcd4e088f2f1b61558b8f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop-2-1 of arXiv:2608.30518, 'Grow-up rates of inhomogeneous semilinear heat equations in the critical dimension'] Assume that (equation katei-f of the paper). Then, (equation eq-intro-1 of the paper) admits the unique singular radial stationary solution $(\lambda_{*}, U_{*})$. Moreover, $U_{*}\in C^2_{\mathrm{loc}}(0,1]\cap H^{1}_{0}(B_1)$ and $U_{*}$ is
