{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.905983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eade91507e43b4e09fe567e72f5441dfcc0b4760d2c7f311227343104232ff51","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:deterministic-cell of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Fix $A,B,R<\infty$. Let $a>0$, $0<r\le A$, and define $\log_+(x) = \max\{0, \log x\}$. Assume $w\le B\bigl(1+\log_+(A/r)\bigr)$. Set $\lambda=ar$ and define $x_k=(k-1)_+/a$, $Z(k)=kw|\mathsf C_R(x_k)-\mathsf C_R(r)|^2$, and $D(k)=I_\lambda(k)$. There exist constants $C<\infty$, $r_0\in(0,1)$ and $c>0$ ensuring:
\begin{itemize}
 \item $Z(k)\le C(D(k)+1)$ for all $k$.
 \item If $r\le r_0$ and $x_k\le\sqrt r$, then $Z(k)\le Cwr(D(k)+1)$.
 \item If $r\le r_0$ and $x_k>\sqrt r$, then $D(k)\ge c\bigl(1+\log(A/r)\bigr)$ and $Z(k)\le CD(k)$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.336243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eae2e9211d6f39e724bc29c475afbd79be0da75bb53f82d0a707493256c1fe6c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] The process $(Z_u^+)_{u\ge0}$ is a Feller process on $E\times[0,\infty)$ with the generator $\mathfrak{A}^+$ such that
		\begin{align*}
			\mathfrak{A}^+ h(x,t)&=-a\,h(x,t)+b(G-\partial_t^{(0,\infty)})h(x,t)\\
			&\hspace{4em}+\int_0^\infty \left(P_sh\big(\cdot,(t-s)\vee0\big)(x)-h(x,t)\right)\nu(ds),
		\end{align*}
		for all $h\in \mathrm{span} \{(x,t)\mapsto f(x)g(t): f\in \DD(G),g\in C_{00}^1([0,\infty))\}$.\footnote{Here $C_{00}^1([0,\infty))\coloneqq \{f\in C_0([0,\infty)):f\in C^1(0,\infty),\, \lim\limits_{t\searrow0}f'(t)=\lim\limits_{t\to\infty}f'(t)=0\}=\{f\in C_0([0,\infty)):f\in C^1(0,\infty),\, \lim\limits_{t\searrow0}(f(t)-f(0))/t=\lim\limits_{t\to\infty}f'(t)=0\}$, and $\partial_t^{(0,\infty)}f(t)=f'(t)\1_{t>0}$, $f\in C_{00}^1([0,\infty))$.}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.996448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eae67a8fcb6a61d558133a98fff50a44f7163d4e308f3ac8f87586087ade2541","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] $(a)$    $\mathcal{HP}_{T,t}$
