{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb02856c08a965d5ea63d769e574910ea4104edac38bd8fa3804915580d9dbb5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm restate of pnkt and nu of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $c\in\mathbb{R}$ be an absolute constant. Let $(n_N)_{N\ge 1},(m_N)_{N\ge 1}$ and $(l_N)_{N\ge 1}$ be sequences of positive integers, such that 
\begin{enumerate}
\item $m_N,l_N\ge 2$ for all $N\ge 1$.
\item $n_N=m_Nl_N$ for all $N\ge 1$, and $\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}n_N=\infty$.
\end{enumerate}
For all $N\ge 1$, let $t_N=\frac{n_N}{2}(\log n_N-\frac 12\log l_N+c)$. Let $P_{n_N}^{*t_N}$ be defined as in (defi: Pnk and its convolution of the paper), and $\nu_{n_N}^{t_N}$ be defined as in (defi: construction of nu of the paper). Let $\sim_{l_N}\backslash P_{n_N}^{*t_N},\sim_{l_N}\backslash \nu_{n_N}^{t_N}$ be their induced probability measures over $\sim_{l_N}\backslash\mathfrak{S}_{n_N}$. Then, we have
$$\limsup_{N\rightarrow\infty}\log n_N(d_{TV}(\sim_{l_N}\backslash P_{n_N}^{*t_N},\sim_{l_N}\backslash\nu_{n_N}^{t_N}))\le -1.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.318118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb047d98db83506a94b85261785d114852dcf8060a09f9d00b38d00f200da223","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition of arXiv:2606.01664, 'Brown measure convergence for the spectrum of polynomials in Ginibre matrices'] There exist some $B_Z>0$ depending only on $\dim Z$ (where $Z$ is an irreducible factor), and a constant $N_0(R)\in\mathbb{N}_+$ depending on the nontrivial $R_1,\cdots,R_n$ action, such that whenever $N\geq N_0$, with probability at least $1-\exp(-\Omega(N))$ over the non-exposed columns in $\mathcal{T}_{-a}$, 
we have
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N\sum_{\ell=1}^n |\langle A_i,R_\ell\rangle|^2\geq N^{-B_Z},
\end{equation}
for any unit vector $A:Z\to W_a$. Here, the coefficient in $\Omega(N)$ does not depend on $R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb06545466dcd1f1fe686014e19c62f6f1c9975592a0e2cfd8ebd67f70dc3f2a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:En-fg of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] For $f\in L$, we denote $\mathrm{diam}(f):=\inf\left\{n\in\mathbb{N}:\\supp(f)\subset\llbracket -n,n\rrbracket\right\}$, and $\mathrm{diam}(e_{L})=0.$ For $n\geq0$, we define $\mathcal E_{n}:=\operatorname{span}\left\{U_{f,g}:\\mathrm{diam}(f)\leq n,\ |g|\leq n\right\}.$ We then have
