\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.980278+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb18fc9225830477257624258e5bae685cd22716e6ec4ba5e13735406398d638","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor jointap of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Fix $d\geq 3$. Suppose  the elements of a set $A_n \subseteq [n]$, with $|A_n| \rightarrow \infty$, are colored independently and uniformly at random with $c_n$ colors such that the following holds: For all $3 \leq r \leq d$, there exists a constant $\lambda_r \geq 0$ with  
