{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.288517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb1ba621a29af16ac61081cf4e39d5c95fef01a135255b58152d4fe4bdbdd372","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:cPI of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The (classical) \emph{Poincar\'e inequality (PI)} is satisfied if there exists a constant $\alpha>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \forall f\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}: \ \ \operatorname{var}_\pi(f)\leq \frac{1}{\alpha}\mathscr{E}_\pi(f).
\end{equation}
The supremum over all possible choices of  $\alpha$ is called the \emph{Poincar\'e constant}. We denote it by
\begin{equation}
    \alpha_{\PI}(M) \coloneqq \inf_{\substack{f\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|} \\ f\notin \langle\1\rangle}} \frac{\mathscr{E}_\pi(f,M)}{\operatorname{var}_\pi(f)}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.345582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb1d1108daf95205df290d79b379760d7a23c02dfb2db56a870ba1d74970c2e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma sec4-lm.1 of arXiv:2602.04303, '\Large\textbf{Strong solutions to SDEs with singular drifts driven by fractional Brownian '] Assume (equation cond1 of the paper), $p,q\geq2$ and $H<1/2$. Then, for $b_1(t,\cdot),b_2(t,\cdot)\in L^p_xL^q_t$ and an arbitrarily small $\varepsilon>0$, there exists a constant $C=C(H,d,p,q,\varepsilon,\Vert b_1\Vert_{L^p_xL^q_t},\Vert b_2\Vert_{L^p_xL^q_t})$ such that
			\begin{align}
				J&:=\int_{\Delta_{\theta,t}^2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2d}}b_1(s_1,x_1)b_2(s_2,x_2)\nonumber\\
				&\qquad\times\frac{1}{s_1^{H(1+d)}}e^{-\frac{|x_1|^2}{4s_1^{2H}}}\frac{1}{(s_2-s_1)^{H(1+d)}}e^{-\frac{|x_2-x_1|^2}{4(s_2-s_1)^{2H}}}(t-s_2)^\alpha\mathrm{d} x\mathrm{d} s\nonumber\\
