{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.915232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb268a2c31e2522f41a4231db95b08092e4e3683e219f3521666ba05b4b6ea60","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:biInf of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] A \textbf{leftmost mixed $\xi$-Busemann bi-infinite interface} is a continuous function $\tau:\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that, for every $s \in \mathbb{R}$, 
\[
\tau|_{[s,\infty)} = \tau_{(\tau(s),s)}^{\xi,-}.
\]
A \textbf{rightmost mixed $\xi$-Busemann bi-infinite interface}  is defined similarly, except that we have $\tau|_{[s,\infty)} = \tau_{(\tau(s),s)}^{\xi,+}$. We let $\mathcal{T}^{\xi,-}$ denote the set of leftmost mixed $\xi$-Busemann bi-infinite interfaces, and let $\mathcal{T}^{\xi,+}$ denote the set of  rightmost mixed $\xi$-Busemann bi-infinite interfaces.

 Furthermore, we define the sets
\begin{equation} 
\overline \mathcal{T}^{\xi,-} := \mathcal{T}^{\xi,-} \cup\{\nu_{-\infty},\nu_{+\infty}\},\quad\text{and}\quad \overline \mathcal{T}^{\xi,+} := \mathcal{T}^{\xi,+} \cup\{\nu_{-\infty},\nu_{+\infty}\},
\end{equation}
where $\nu_{-\infty}:\mathbb{R} \to \{-\infty\}$ is the trivial path $\nu_{-\infty}(t) \equiv -\infty$, and $\nu_{+\infty}:\mathbb{R} \to \{+\infty\}$ is the trivial path $\nu_{+\infty}(t) \equiv +\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.417938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb27c72de0eb779c2fb822f4e786a916098ddb34a09fd1d864540c6be907990e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (\bf Anticipative approximation with KW-projection) of arXiv:2606.08776, 'Approximation of certain stochastic integrals with anticipating integrands'] Assume $Z$ has the admissible representation \eqref{eqn:definition:admissible_representation_Z}
