The constants in the remainders depend only on $\underline\lambda,\overline\lambda$ and, in the second statement, on the implicit constant in $\|m_{0,p}-m_{1,p}\|^2=O(p)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.439273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb46b15858c72a5a36ddd08ea4c555b4278386cea63aa60928ec3e9076818d5b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm mainGeneral of arXiv:2509.26254, '$K$-Branching Random Walk with Noisy Selection: \\ \Large Large Population Limits and Phas'] Assume that $(M_N^0)_{N \in \mathbb{N}}$ has limiting log-profile $g^0\in{\mathcal D}$ and let  $(g^t)_{t\geq0}$ be the dynamics as defined in Theorem (thm:main of the paper). 
