{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.302268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb82fc4df266bc577dfbe9d39dae53a5a81248ec85895e3dbbb72126ff9f95e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[The thm:moregeneral of arXiv:2605.26869, 'Law of Large Numbers for a random walk on dynamic environments with drift'] Let $\eta$ be an environment satisfying~(pe:markov of the paper)-(pe:density of the paper) and  (pe:densitychange of the paper)-(pe:nacelle of the paper). Then for all $\rho \in (0,\infty)$ except at most countably many, there exists $v(\rho)$ such that 
