{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.499220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb83a3c70575dd99e69ede1acf773df0b870c11aed56db503d9b23ed680b3a1a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo lgp of arXiv:2411.07158, 'Markov chains on trees: almost lower and upper directed cases'] Let $\pi^{T{(k)}}$ be  the ${\sf h}$-invariant measure of $\;{\sf U}^{T{(k)}}$ on the finite tree $T{(k)}$, normalized by $\pi_{\varnothing}^{T{(k)}}=1$.
	\begin{itemize} \topsep0pt   \itemsep=0pt   \partopsep=0pt   \parsep=0pt \setcounter{c}{0}
	\addtocounter{c}{1}\item[($\roman{c}$)] 	$(a)$ the measures  $\pi^{T{(k)}}$ and $\pi^{T{(k-1)}}$ coincide on $T{(k-1)}$,\\
	$(b)$ to compute the value $\pi^{T{(k)}}_{u_k}$ (on the additional node) using $\pi^{T{(k-1)}}$,
	\begin{eqnarray} 
	\pi^{T{(k)}}_{u_k}    ={\displaystyle\sum_{v\in \cro{\varnothing,p(u_k)}} \pi^{T{(k-1)}}_{v} {\sf U}_{v,T_{u_k}}}/ {{\sf U}_{u_k,p(u_k)}} .\end{eqnarray}
	\addtocounter{c}{1}\item[($\roman{c}$)] The measures $(\pi^{T{(k)}},k\geq 0)$ are consistent (that is $\pi^{T{(k+1)}}$ and  $\pi^{T{(k)}}$ coincide on $T{(k)}$, for all $k$), so that there exists a measure $\rho$ on $T$, such that $\rho\big|_{T{(k)}}=\pi^{T{(k)}}$. This measure $\rho$ is the \textsf{h}-invariant measure $\pi$ of ${\sf U}$.
	\end{itemize}\vspace{-2em}~ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb85357c821ce48d6e63bc96f943b8a1c6b06f7738413965c68927ae8a1ba328","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Spectral zero pattern) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] The directional scales satisfy
