{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.319262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec25e626ae9f306c2db413b2fdd1c6f4447bd14de92d269925524cd47a238c28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma oftheorem3.1 of arXiv:2606.01664, 'Brown measure convergence for the spectrum of polynomials in Ginibre matrices'] Let $\mu$ be a complex random variable and fix an integer $d>0$. Suppose that 
    $$
\mathbb{E}|\mu|^{2d}<\infty,
    $$and the following Gram matrix 
    $$
M^\mu_{(d)}=(\mathbb{E}[\mu^a\bar{\mu}^b])_{0\leq a,b\leq d}
    $$is positive definite. Let $\xi_1,\cdots,\xi_s$ be i.i.d. copies of $\mu$, and let $g_1,\cdots,g_s$ be i.i.d. standard complex Gaussians. Then for any holomorphic polynomial $$Q(z_1,\cdots,z_s)$$
    with total degree at most $d$, we have the comparison
    \begin{equation}
C_{d,\mu}^{-1}(1+s)^{-d}\mathbb{E}|Q(g_1,\cdots,g_s)|^2\leq\mathbb{E}|Q(\xi_1,\cdots,\xi_s)|^2\leq C_{d,\mu}(1+s)^d\mathbb{E}|Q(g_1,\cdots,g_s)|^2       .
    \end{equation}
    Here the constant $C_{d,\mu}$ depends only on $d$ and the law of $\mu$, but does not depend on $s$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.206007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec271e38b30069e0a6628c4a52bb26d4280345fa5faef0dd4027fc5c359fb17f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corol 16 of arXiv:2604.27205, 'An Analysis of the Diaconis-Holmes-Neal Markov Chain Sampler Under Generalized Unimodal Un'] The mean length of an intermediate return in the general unimodal case is
