{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.469300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec4d9f9ac1d8fdfac266306408284f8ab4c6327bbcacd9221d61eb30d0d775a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Self-adjoint Gaussian Khintchine inequality) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $W$ be a finite-dimensional Hilbert space, let
$B_1,\ldots,B_N\in\cL(W)$ be self-adjoint, and let
$\gamma_1,\ldots,\gamma_N$ be independent standard real Gaussians.  For
$p\ge2$ and $2\le r<\infty$,
\begin{equation}

  \biggl\|\sum_k\gamma_kB_k\biggr\|_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r(W))}
  \le C\sqrt{p+r}
  \biggl\|\biggl(\sum_k B_k^2\biggr)^{1/2}\biggr\|_{\Sch_r(W)}.
\end{equation}
More precisely, if
\begin{equation*}
  \sigma_r(B):=
  \biggl\|\biggl(\sum_k B_k^2\biggr)^{1/2}\biggr\|_{\Sch_r(W)},
\end{equation*}
then
\begin{equation}

  \E\biggl\|\sum_k\gamma_kB_k\biggr\|_{\Sch_r}
  \le C\sqrt r\,\sigma_r(B).
\end{equation}
Moreover, the function
\[
  f_B(x):=\biggl\|\sum_kx_kB_k\biggr\|_{\Sch_r},
  \qquad x\in\R^N,
\]
satisfies
\begin{equation*}
  |f_B(x)-f_B(y)|\le\sigma_r(B)\,\|x-y\|_{\ell_2^N}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

