{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.872209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec7d04874da8d998d5697663a2cfb1e19e4ef6e4aa903eac9af9d7dcd991aede","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] Suppose Assumption~\ref{ass:metric-entropy} holds.
For any $\delta\in(0,1)$, define the statistical error terms 
\begin{equation}
 q_{\nu,n}(\delta) := \frac{C_{\mathrm D}}{\sqrt n} \left[ \Gamma_{\nu,\eps} + B_\eps\sqrt{\log\frac4\delta} \right], \qquad
 q_{\mu,n}(\delta) := \frac{C_{\mathrm D}}{\sqrt n} \left[ \Gamma_{\mu,\eps} + B_\eps\sqrt{\log\frac4\delta} \right].
