{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.473057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec7ed8f470ace9243e4888470023f5b246e878ffe1b4c19e295f5ee57e8eb26d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma pointwise-crit-cocomplete of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\textbf{\textup{U}}\subset\ul\Spc_T\subset\ul\CAT_T$ be any full subcategory. Then a $T$-$\infty$-category ${\mathcal{C}}$ is $\textbf{\textup{U}}$-cocomplete if and only if the following conditions are satisfied:
