{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.694237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8aaa11dd54d51e6065fbdb98f3eb125b2f58c911eac4f95bbe4aca27f3c3d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:existence_Volterra_V of arXiv:2605.29073, 'Volterra clocks and their pure-jump limits: \\hitting times of curved boundaries'] Let $\lambda \,, \nu\geq 0\,$, $f$ satisfying Assumption (assumption:f of the paper), $K \in L^2_{loc}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}_+\,, \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}_+)$ a completely monotone kernel, and $g_0 \in \mathcal G_K\,$. Then, there exists a continuous, nonnegative weak solution $V$ to 
    \begin{equation}

    Y_t = g_0(t) + \int_0^t\,K(t-s)\,\left(-\lambda\,Y_s\,ds + \nu\,\sqrt{f'(X_s)\,Y_s}\,dB_s \right)\,, \quad t \leq T\,,
    \end{equation}
    where $X_t := \int_0^t\,Y_s\,ds\,$. Additionally, $\sup_{t \leq T} \,\mathbb E \left[Y_t^p \right]$ is finite for all $p \geq 2\,$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.726329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8f2ebeb8822374178f4f8112ba4962d4276eba908429fd76b8215ea4edf43c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Let $L:C^{0,1}(\Omega_T)\to\mathbb{R}$ be any linear functional and recall 
    \begin{equation*}
    \mathfrak{M}(H):=\int_0^T\int_0^1\sigma(\rho_t)|\nabla H_t|^2\;dx\;dt+\int_0^T\Psi(t,H_t(0),H_t(1))\;dt.
\end{equation*}
Then 
\begin{equation*}
    \sup_{C^{0,1}(\Omega_T)}\{L_0(H)-\mathfrak{M}(H)\}=S_1+S_2,
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
    S_1=\sup_{C^{0,1}_0(\Omega_T)}\{L_0(G)-\int_0^T\int_0^1\sigma(\rho_t)|\nabla G_t|^2\;dx\;dt\}
\end{equation*}
and 
\begin{equation*}
    S_2=\sup_{h,g\in C([0,T])}\{L(g_t[1-\Xi_t])+L(h_t\Xi_t)-\int_0^T\zeta_t[h_t-g_t]^2\;dt-\int_0^T\Psi(t,g_t,h_t)\;dt\}.
\end{equation*}
In the above formula, $\zeta_t=1/\langle 1/\sigma(\rho_t) \rangle$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.073625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8f3b50dc8e238c426be03ec77c700b6335692414842eb76c3f4cd0a90eee60","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.formula_cts_incre of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Under~(i.setting of the paper), fix $X_0=0$. 
