{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.277539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecde0178e1285e18f1a7b5304e04c134ccbe5784d2a25118c358e5bec791d322","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2604.24677, 'Local Limit of Random Regular Bipartite Planar Maps'] Let $\rt\in\T$. Then, for any $v\in\rV(\rt)$:
\begin{itemize}
	\item If $v\in\rV_{\!\circ}(\rt)$, then $\c(v)=d-1$. Moreover, its ordered offspring consists of $d-1$ elements, each of which is either a closing stem or a black vertex.
	\item If $v\in\rV_{\!\bullet}(\rt)$, then $\c(v)=0$ if $v$ is the root vertex and $\c(v)=1$ otherwise. Moreover, its ordered offspring  consists of a single white vertex together with opening stems, exactly $d-1$ if $v$ is the root vertex and $d-2$ otherwise.
\end{itemize}
Moreover, all the possibilities can occur. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.656481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ece2a17050bda4d94b42e8fac92d7c1d0d7854f7e16932ce1125cc3633b21bad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:Haar-zero-integral of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] Fix a nonnegative integer $k$ and suppose $Q_1,\dots,Q_k \sim \mrm{Haar}(\mrm{SO}(3))$ are all independent of each other. Then for any indices $i,j \in [3]$, subset of pairs $P \subset [k]^2$, and collection on nonnegative integers $\{\ell_{(a,b)}\}_{(a,b) \in P}$, we have,
