 \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.730713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed067be64baa9044f892aca9b7b74e9796da88fc0c3639a5344c7c4c46fb458c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem joint_degree_distribution of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m\in\mathbb{N}$, $c\in(0,m+1)$ and $k,\ell\in\mathbb{N}_0$ such that $k+\ell\geq 1$. Fix a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$ is satisfied  for some $\varepsilon<1-c/(m+1)$ in  Part~(item:hI of the paper) and some $\eta<1-c/(m+1)$ in Part~(item:Jn of the paper). Let $V_1,\ldots,V_k\in\mathbb A_n$ be distinct active vertices and $W_1,\ldots,W_\ell\in\mathbb F_n$ be distinct frozen vertices selected uniformly at random from $G^{(n)}$. Then, there exists $\alpha\in(0,1)$ such that uniformly over all natural numbers $d_{a_1},\ldots,d_{a_k} < ch_n^+$ and $d_{f_1},\ldots,d_{f_\ell} < c\log F_n$,
