{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.611457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed92f9a4b1ecd6a847789a4982203cc81b8c219208a08122e842aa2570b6d65a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm t:converge_Airy_details of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $\{\lambda^{(n)}_i(t)\}_{i=1}^n$ be either the stationary DBM (equation e:DBMV of the paper) with fixed general potential $V$ satisfying (a:Vasump of the paper), Laguerre process (equation e:stationary_Laguerre of the paper), or Jacobi process (equation e:Jacobi of the paper).
Take $n\to\infty$, with
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\limsup m/n<\infty$ and $\liminf m/n >1$ in the Laguerre case;
    \item $\limsup p/n, \limsup q/n <\infty$, $\liminf p/n>1$, $\liminf q/n>0$ in the Jacobi case.
\end{itemize}
Then we have that
$\{(\lambda^{(n)}_i(\zeta t) - E)/\chi \}_{i=1}^\infty$
converges to ALE$_\beta$, under the uniform in compact topology. Here we take the convention of $\lambda^{(n)}_i=-\infty$ for $i>n$, and $E, \zeta, \chi$ are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[DBM:] 
    \begin{equation}   
        E=Bn^{1/2}, \zeta=R^{-4/3}n^{-1/3}, \chi=R^{-2/3}n^{-1/6},
    \end{equation}
    where $B$, $R$, and $\varrho_V$ from (a:Vasump of the paper);
    \item[Laguerre:]
    \begin{equation}   
        E=(\sqrt{m}+\sqrt{n})^2, \zeta=2^{-1}(\sqrt{m}+\sqrt{n})^{2/3}(mn)^{-1/3}, \chi=(\sqrt{m}+\sqrt{n})^{4/3}(mn)^{-1/6};
    \end{equation}
    \item[Jacobi:] 
    \begin{equation}   
        E=\left(\frac{\sqrt{p(m-n)}+\sqrt{qn}}{m}\right)^2, \zeta=\frac{(E(1-E))^{1/3}}{2(pq(m-n))^{1/3}}n^{-1/3}, \chi=\frac{(E(1-E))^{2/3}}{(pq(m-n))^{1/6}}n^{-1/6}.
    \end{equation}
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.939003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed9572f28d1ad2e7b0c0b2f41e59d72cf52c663132475ba7d01d348241920b42","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm1stResult of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Suppose that Assumption (Assumptions of the paper) holds, let $\mathbf{X}_0$ be an initial random variable independent of $\mathbf{W}$, and let $\mathbf{X} = (\mathbf{X}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the corresponding solution to (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) with $d$-th component $X = (X_t)_{t \geq 0}$. Then the probability distribution of the length of the first monotone run of the sampled process $(X_{n\delta})_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ converges to the geometric distribution with parameter $1/2$ as $\delta \rightarrow 0$ , i.e., for all $\ell \in \mathbb{N} \cup \lbrace \infty \rbrace$ it holds that
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{\delta \rightarrow 0} P( T_{1,\delta}(X) = \ell) = \frac{1}{2^\ell},
