	\item[(ii)] \textbf{Resonant product estimate.} Let $s_1,s_2 \in \mathbb R$ such that $s=s_1 + s_2 > 0$. Let $p,p_1,p_2,q \in [1,\infty]$ satisfy $\frac 1p = \frac 1{p_1} + \frac 1{p_2}$. There exists $C>0$ such that
