{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.143501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_edc3712e427717239231ab5e80d446145f55535eee23202c7b8ca5c3402b78cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm informal of arXiv:2607.05097, 'Asymptotics of Lyapunov Exponents and Phase Transitions for Fluids with Degenerate Forcing'] Let $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$, $x \in \mathbb{R}^n \setminus \{0\}$, $A, B_i \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$,
    \begin{equation}
           \begin{aligned}
                dz^\epsilon(t) &= -\epsilon z^\epsilon(t)\,dt + \sqrt{\epsilon}\,dW_t \\
                dx^\epsilon(t) &= \Big(A + \sum_{i=1}^d B_i z_i^\epsilon(t)\Bigr)x^\epsilon(t)\,dt \eqqcolon A(z^\epsilon(t))x^\epsilon(t)\,dt \,,
            \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    and $\lambda^\epsilon \coloneqq \lim_{t \to \infty} t^{-1}\ln \|x^\epsilon(t)\|$. Let $Z$ be distributed 
