{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.857192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ede5eda779ce971b2fd261a7e549e579da21217db9078de0343c7bc84b7de2eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Sequential mixed coincidence identity) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] Let the one-step likelihood ratios $R_1,\dots,R_T$ be strictly positive, and let $\alpha \in \R^T$ satisfy $0 < Z_T(\alpha) < \infty$ for $Z_T$ of~\eqref{eq:seqZ}.
