{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.570219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_edf3277412850c10620ff2025aad224682a79698e658d246425fc117c3db6ee5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 39 (Local Regularization) of arXiv:2608.26516, '2608.26516'] Let $\psi: \CH \times \CX \to \R_{\geq 0}$ be a local regularizer. A learner $A$ is \defn{induced} by $\psi$ if for all samples $S$ and points $x \in \CX$, 
