{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.942512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee347d0cb7a4fee1c461f927fd06ed452288bdd31ebc37e07abc3e8e7b973d9b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:conv_yh of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $T_0 > 0$ be such that (equation eq:est_lem65 of the paper) in Lemma~(lem:exponential_moment of the paper) holds for $\gamma = 2a$ and $K= \nu((0,\infty])$. Furthermore, let $(X_{t})_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with initial condition $X_0$ satisfying (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper). Furthermore, let $(g_n)_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of measurable bounded functions on $\mathbb{R}$, that converge boundedly pointwise to a bounded, measurable function $g$ on $\mathbb{R}$.
