{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.578116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee598a401b74f86c21aeef3d9bc68bfa9aa747a2ffa44d72549e8720da742ff7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, $p\in [1,2]$ and $q\in [1,2)$,
