{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.321359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee6029933bcb88f7183476ac91527a2b2a16c10da39314ad6f9f7ea5cd4441fc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma P5.1 of arXiv:2412.09850, 'Averaging principles for time-inhomogeneous multi-scale SDEs via nonautonomous Poisson equ'] Let $h$ be a  bounded and $\tau$-periodic function on $\mathbb{R}$. Then, for any $T>0$,
