{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.747600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee639a63cb41a0032706a109018ccb39fc48840ccf638c9c0771b780caef0d2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz 2 of arXiv:2511.20322, 'Dissertation'] Let $\be \in (0,1)$, $c > 0$, $L, \la > 0$ and $\cR : \R^d\to \R \in \dC 2$ be $\la$-strongly convex and $L$-smooth such that $\nabla^2 \cR$ is Hölder continuous.
