{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.636785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee71ba786b6164763a7c1fdff89049d04dda807032c3c79c68c46a6677e0a2e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma1 of arXiv:2609.01835, 'On Exposed (Symmetric) Tensors'] Let $Y = (c_0, \|\cdot\|_Y)$ as defined above. For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, consider the coordinate functionals $e_n^* \in Y^*$. Let us set $f_1 := e_1^*$, $f_2 := e_2^*$ and $f_3:= -e_1^* - e_2^*$. Then, $\|f_j\|_{Y^*} = 1$ for every $j=1,2,3$ and 
