{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.600945+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee7be88a9f18199ccf61c7e01a2245e316c17e0e05310eac04d28c1d8b337e06","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:perimeter of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] Let $0<a<b<\infty$. There exist constants $C_{a,b}<\infty$ and $T_{a,b}<\infty$ such that, for all $T\ge T_{a,b}$ and all $r\in[a,b]$,
