{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.504568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee9a9143cc3345c2232c6ff4ef7bf1620455e833d2c9b2a0db4b1f99f00ac550","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2607.28578, 'On two differing geometric descriptions of the passage from microscopy to macroscopy in Ma'] If $X_t$ follows the deterministic equation $\dot X_t=u_t+B_t(X_t-\mu_t)$ and $\Law(X_t)=\mathcal N(\mu_t,\Sigma_t)$, then
	\begin{equation}
		\dot\mu_t=u_t
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
