{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.414318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee9afbc7d1de21922f3161767b179195f42aea0cc9eac4cc19a04d9a8d9b14bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:MD of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] There is a constant $N \in \mathbb{N}$ depending only on the doubling constant $D$ of $\mu$ in (equation eq:muDoubling of the paper) such that the following holds. For all $x \in X$ and $r > 0$ there are points $x_1,\dots,x_N \in X$ satisfying
