{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.096570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee9b4197aa3b7999401c67a4f50ac6a449dd9b0f5181b3e1666dbc9f2fb3a98b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 5lem22 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Suppose that $\Phi$ is an $L^{\infty}\text{-Lipschitz}$ functional satisfying condition (equation Lips1 of the paper)\footnote{A similar approximation procedure in the case where $\Phi$ is an $L^{1}\text{-Lipschitz}$ can be found in [MaZhang01]}. Let $\Pi = \{\pi\}$ be a family of partitions of $[0,T]$. Then there is a family of discrete functionals $\{ \varphi^{\pi}: \pi \in \Pi \}$ such that 
				\begin{itemize}
					\item[(i)] for each $\pi \in \Pi$, assuming $\pi:0=t_0<\cdots < t_n=T$ we have that $\varphi^{\pi} \in C_b^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d(n+1)})$ and satisfies 
					\begin{equation}
						\sum_{i=0}^n |\nabla_{x_i}\varphi^{\pi}(x)| \leq S({\varphi}), \quad \forall x=(x_0,\cdots,x_n) \in \mathbb{R}^{d(n+1)},
