{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.272315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eec1ac647172fb4810c884f6de9993688278d928a2515cb7e0659681dcc9ce3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Arizmendi--P\'erez-Abreu squaring identity) of arXiv:2604.22114, 'Free compressions of R-diagonal random variables and the semigroup of Brown measures'] Let $\mu$ be a symmetric probability measure on $\R$, and let $S_\mu$ denote the $S$-transform of $\mu$
\emph{in the sense of} \cite{arizmendi_perez-abreu2009}.
Then there exist $\varepsilon>0$ and an open set $U\subset i\C^{+}$ with $(-\varepsilon,0)\subset U$ such that
$S_\mu$ and $S_{\mu_{sq}}$ are well-defined on $U$, and for every $z\in U$,
\begin{equation}

S_{\mu_{sq}}(z) \;=\; \frac{z}{1+z}\,\big[S_\mu(z)\big]^2,
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{sq}$ is the push-forward of $\mu$ under the map $t\mapsto t^2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.840287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eec86513853ba9f57f98005784be21efc1e0ad850c7e76810dba24f682b22f6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_reachability of arXiv:2606.09488, 'The temporal stochastic block model'] Under assumptions $(ass1 of the paper)$ and (ass2 of the paper), for any $v\in V$,
