{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.278618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eec8b7a5c46c2a4da8a1d9f51cc3301f1023cab01eb3b8a0dd62bfc60ea65390","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cauchy of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $V \subseteq \mathcal{U}$ be finite and $((\xi^{u}_{0})_{u \in V},R_{0}) \in (\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{|V|} \times [0,R_{\max}]$. Then, there exists a neighborhood $O \subseteq (\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{|V|} \times [0,R_{\max}]$ of $((\xi^{u}_{0})_{u \in V},R_{0})$, and a neighborhood $J \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{+}$ of 0, such that
\begin{itemize}
\item[1.] For every $((\xi^{u})_{u \in V},R) \in O$, there exists a unique local solution with values in $(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{|V|} \times [0,R_{\max}]$ to the system of coupled equations (equation eq:regroupindiv of the paper)-(equation regeoupee of the paper), starting from $((\xi^{u})_{u \in V},R)$ at time 0. This solution is at least defined on $J$, and denoted as $\left((X^{u}_{t}(\Xi,R))_{u \in V},X^{\Re}_{t}(\Xi,R)\right)$, with $\Xi := (\xi^{u})_{u \in V}$. 
\item[2.] The function $(t,(\xi^{u})_{u \in V},R) \in J \times O \mapsto \left((X^{u}_{t}(\Xi,R))_{u \in V},X^{\Re}_{t}(\Xi,R)\right)$ is $\mathcal{C}^{1,1}(J \times O)$, and $\mathcal{C}^{2}$ in the variable $t$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.334481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eecaadfc14bdbce13917293034cd757c92001ae1371316bdee7228113ef6aa80","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma number of clockwise loops of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] We have the following convergence
