{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.316047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eecedd188acbb924775eef3fd6825c5543e0e5892ec34f0a4596505d1987ac6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-cell-ldp-upper of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] For each $n\in\mathbbm N$ and $A >1$, 
\begin{equation}  
\mathbbm P\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \max\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ \operatorname{LDP}_{M_{0,n}}(x,y)  : x,y\in\mathcal V(M_{0,n}) \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} \leq A n^{3/4} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] \geq 1 - A^{-2/3 + o(1)}
\end{equation} 
where the $o(1)$ goes to zero as $A\to\infty$, uniformly in $n$, and we set $\operatorname{LDP}_{M_{0,n}}(x,y) = -\infty$ if there is no directed path in $M_{0,n}$ from $x$ to $y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.867197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eecf5b3177453d481136d52ccb3fa26cee1af40689696c851d6603ec11a5eb5c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] Let $X\sim\NN(\mu,\sigma^2)$. The moment generating function of $X^2$ is given by
