{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.749039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eecfba96d160fcf0a1a247a735a3949a4e75bef14b7ff032cfcb39305478d06c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-sol of arXiv:2512.17736, 'Pathwise uniqueness by noise for singular stochastic PDEs'] Assume (H0 of the paper)--(H4 of the paper).
A weak mild solution to (equation SDE of the paper) is a pair 
$(X,W)$ where $W$ is a $H$-cylindrical Wiener process defined on a filtered probability space 
$(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\{\mathcal{F}_t\}_{t\geq0},\mathbb{P})$ and 
$X$ is a $H$-valued progressively measurable process such that 
\begin{alignat*}{2}
X &\in C^0(\mathbb R_+; H)\cap C^0((0,+\infty); D(A^\alpha))
\quad {\mathbb{P}}\text{-a.s.} \qquad&&\text{if } x\in H\,,\\
X &\in C^0(\mathbb R_+; D(A^\alpha))
\quad {\mathbb{P}}\text{-a.s.} \qquad&&\text{if } x\in D(A^\alpha)\,,
\end{alignat*}
for every $t>0$ it holds $s\mapsto e^{-(t-s)A}B(X(s)) \in L^1(0,t;H)$, ${\mathbb{P}}\text{-a.s.}$, and
\begin{align}
X(t)=e^{-tA}x+\int_0^te^{-(t-s)A}B(X(s))\,{\mathrm d} s+W_A(t)
\quad\forall\,t\geq0\,, \quad \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.},   
\end{align}
where $W_A$ is the stochastic convolution process given by 
\begin{equation*}
W_A(t):=\int^t_0e^{-(t-s)A}A^{-\delta}\,{\mathrm d} W(s)\,, \quad t\geq0\,.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.567570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eed07a3276dbeedae2c34eae8dab4019e42941fb746750aac2b3023773922611","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:irreg3 of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] One has 
