{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.318613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eed375dd98fa4e35d004e5bdb963500e1c7cc6bbd5b06d72cf2ffd6a47a33458","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Exact occupancy mixture) of arXiv:2604.09933, 'Explicit cutoff profiles for colored top-\texorpdfstring{$m$}{m}-to-random shuffles'] For every \(k\ge0\),
\begin{equation}
Q^{*k}
=\sum_{a=0}^{n}\mu_k(a)\,\widetilde Q_{a,p}
=\sum_{u=0}^{n}P_k(u)\,\widetilde Q_{n-u,p},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\mu_k(a):=\frac{1}{n^k}\binom{n}{a}\left\{\!\!\begin{matrix}k\\ a\end{matrix}\!\!\right\}a!,
\end{equation}
and \(P_k(u)=\Prob(E=u)\) for the usual balls-into-boxes model with \(k\) i.i.d.\ uniform balls in \(n\) boxes, where \(E\) is the number of empty boxes. Equivalently,
\[
P_k(u)=\mu_k(n-u).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.685259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eed454382ac64bc15dd515a339f6bbb6cb895c04688363e6c4c8e236d9e61c6c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Weighted-ratio expansion) of arXiv:2608.30916, 'Selection-Aware Stress Testing for Interactive Agents'] Let $a_g=P s_g>0$, $P^g h=P(s_gh)/a_g$, and $P_n^g h=P_n(s_gh)/P_ns_g$. Whenever $P_ns_g>0$,
\begin{equation}
 P_n^g h-P^g h
 =\frac{a_g}{P_ns_g}(P_n-P)
 \left\{\omega_g(h-P^gh)\right\},
 \qquad \omega_g=s_g/a_g.

\end{equation}
If $P\{\omega_g^2(h-P^gh)^2\}<\infty$ and $P_ns_g\to_p a_g$, then
\begin{equation}
 \sqrt n(P_n^g h-P^g h)
 =\frac{1}{\sqrt n}\sum_{i=1}^n
 \omega_g(W_i)\{h(W_i)-P^gh\}+o_p(1).

\end{equation}
The same statement holds coordinatewise for a fixed-dimensional vector $h$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.151020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eed82080d495ec751dd3c8eda637108b925311fc49f178a62800beb2363eee53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-covering of arXiv:2510.13733, 'Internal Diffusion Limited Aggregation \\ with Critical Branching Random Walks'] For any $d>2$  there exists a constant  $\alpha $ large enough such that for any integer $n$ and any particle configuration $\eta$ supported in $B_{n/2}$ with $|\eta| \geq  \alpha  |B_n|$, it holds that 
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{P}\big(B_n\not\subseteq \mathscr{S}(\eta ) \big)\le
 \exp\Big(-C \frac{\alpha\cdot n}{\log n\cdot \1_{d=3}+\1_{d>3}}\Big)
\end{equation}
for some positive and finite constants  $C$,  depending only on the dimension. 

Moreover, for any $d \geq 2$ there exists a constant  $\alpha $ large enough such that for any integer $n$ and any particle configuration $\eta$ supported in $B_{n/2}$ with $|\eta| \leq  \alpha \cdot |B_n|$, it holds that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\big(B_n\not\subseteq \mathscr{S}(\eta ) \big)\geq 
\exp\Big( - c \cdot \alpha\cdot n^{d-2}\Big)
\end{equation}
for some positive and finite constants  $c$,  depending only on the dimension. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.228426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eedb2d6f2e5eba83fa1526793c8614f998da62a92fa721a4e6ec990678d76b08","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 38 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [The defining system of equations for a rational molecule (3)]
