{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.047489+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef0c480737321adc6d81a457ce0367254af5625a4ef0f2f8bfa28a9183203c93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition uniform_bound_derivative_and_A of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_g \underset{g \to +\infty}{\rightarrow}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c - \mu_g = o(g^{-2})$ and any $n\ge 0$, we have for $g$ large enough
