{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.313085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef63266aa558fcb315a77d034683060a81807149889cbeb2f114c65f2be258cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.23305, 'On extremes of a random walk with positive drift\\ over an intermediate regularly varying '] Assume that $a:=\E\xi>0$.
Let the distribution of $\tau$ be intermediate regularly varying at infinity and such that
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{|\xi|>x\} &=& o\biggl(\frac{\P\{\tau>x\}}{\E(\tau\wedge x)}\biggr)\quad\mbox{as }x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray}
If $\tau$ does not depend on the future, then
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{M_\tau>x\}\ \sim\ \P\{S_\tau>x\} &\sim& \P\{\tau>x/a\}\quad\mbox{as  } x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.052686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef657d91ecb511e0e9be68802981ac4577f0a029bdb0343f520424dd52903449","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (Weighted square-root perturbation) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $G$ and $M$ be positive definite $2r\times2r$ matrices whose spectra lie in a fixed compact subset of $(0,\infty)$.  Suppose that $M=\diag(a\Id_r,b\Id_r)$ with $a,b>0$, and let
