{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.384932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef8a077d4c9c72fc82ea3d8f697401faa30d8b28ade836a94ea1619790755729","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma FTOLOT3to1lemma of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Suppose $\gamma \in \Gamma^{\Lambda}(\mu, \nu)$ and let $f:\mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}$ be measurable such that $f^+ \in L^1(\mathbb R^d,d\mu)$. Then $f^+ \otimes 1 \in L^1(\mathbb R^{2d},d\gamma)$ and
