{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.351856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef95a0914ade98c49dd3baac6b8c9e2d4f7035e419a744e38ebb28b04b9e04cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:PsiBd of arXiv:2506.06559, 'Bi-infinite incipient cluster in high dimensions'] If (equation eq:tauAsy of the paper), (equation eq:DtauBd of the paper) and (equation eq:Aass of the paper) are satisfied, then for any $F\in\mathfrak F_{00}$ there exits $C>0$ such that for all $x,x'\in\mathbb{Z}^d$ and $p\le p_c$, 
