{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.787976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef980341ac07cfdff93991eae36cbeac5f8104b38800aa591c5d85399aa8014f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm general-local-thm of arXiv:2509.07729, 'Permuton and local limits for the Luce model'] Set $f_n(y):=\theta_{\lfloor yn \rfloor}$ for all $y\in[0,1]$ and assume that $f_n\to f$ almost everywhere for some positive, finite, measurable function $f$ on $[0,1]$. 
Then, for all $k\geq 1$ and every permutation $\pi\in\mathcal{S}_k$,
\begin{equation}
    \Lambda(\pi)=\lim_{n\to +\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=0}^{n-k}p\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\theta_{i+\pi^{-1}(1)},\dots, \theta_{i+\pi^{-1}(k)}\aftergroup\egroup\originalright)=\frac{1}{k!},
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{(\nu_n(\pi))^2}{n}=\nu_\infty(\pi),
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}
\nu_\infty(\pi)
=\frac{1}{k!}+\frac{1-2k}{(k!)^2}+2 \sum_{h=1}^{k-1}\zeta_{\pi}(h,k),
\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}
    \zeta_{\pi}(h,k):=\mathbb P\!\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(
E_{\pi^{-1}(1)}<\dots<E_{\pi^{-1}(k)},
\;\; E_{h+\pi^{-1}(1)}<\dots<E_{h+\pi^{-1}(k)}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright),\quad\text{$1\le h\le k-1$,}
\end{equation}
where $(E_{j})_{j}$ are i.i.d.\ exponential random variables with parameter 1. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.716971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef9938ef6cd09696e580f905f3581dc11de7b21892d492b2f3d83f5623d21127","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:fs-frame-condition of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] An f-frame $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ is said to be an \emph{FS2}\footnote{Also known by backward confluence [balbiani_constructive_2021], F2 [simpson_proof_1994], back-up confluence [aguilera_gocalculus_2022], and $\textsf{I}_{\Diamond \Box}$-weak [groot_semantical_2025].} frame
  if $(\sqsubset \cdot \leq) \subseteq (\leq \cdot \sqsubset)$,
  that is, $\forall x,y,y'\, (x \sqsubset y \leq y' \mathrel{\Rightarrow} \exists x'\,(x \leq x' \sqsubset y'))$.
  Let us denote by $\mathscr{F}_{FS2}$ the class of all FS2 frames.","status":"unverified"}

