                    \,\Big|\, \cF_t\Bigr],
\end{equation}
where $h_t$ is the forward factor. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.739858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efa643787a7a55a5fbe4b9f0737b586978b6fa9bc99ed4eab9dfc742b3b767a3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cortau of arXiv:2605.01878, '\Large Random trade timing and power-law tails in realized prices'] Let $X$ be a real-valued random variable whose Laplace transform $\varphi_X$ satisfy the conditions (lemxpluda of the paper)--(lemxpludc of the paper) of Lemma (lemxplus of the paper). Then there exist finite constants $C_1$ and $C_2$, depending only on
$\alpha$, $\ell$, and $\delta$, such that
\begin{align}
A_\ell C_1
&\le \liminf_{x\to\infty} x^{-\ell+1} e^{\alpha x} \mathbb{P}(X>x) \notag\\
&\le \limsup_{x\to\infty} x^{-\ell+1} e^{\alpha x} \mathbb{P}(X>x)
\le A_\ell C_2. 
\end{align}
If, in addition, $\ell=1$ and $-\alpha$ is the unique singularity of $\varphi_X$ on the
axis $\mathrm{Re} (s)=-\alpha$, then
\begin{align}
\lim_{x\to\infty} e^{\alpha x}\mathbb{P}(X>x) = A_1/\alpha. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.337776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efa79627386d7b30c4093a0a68ad39c1c352c2b7a856a33910c3af46e06fd1c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $K$ be a graph over $V$. We define the self-overlap of $K$:

