{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.700922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03c49dbcf039b322af094e794299b2a0f0d75816f916dbb127e9539d407cd6b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition discover_balls of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] For any $r \ge 0$ and any $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists $k > 0$ such that, for $n$ large enough, 
