{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.287404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03cabc9462dd5d646e5762377f47ac646a9f3f5e177ea47db7d7e380185f16d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:liftedPoincare of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] Let $(\mathcal{E},\dom(\mathcal{E}))$ be a densely defined, closed, non-negative definite symmetric bilinear form on $L_0^2(\mu)$, and let $({\mathcal{C}},\dom({\mathcal{C}}))$ be the non-positive self-adjoint linear operator on $\mathbb{H}^l$ that is the generator of $\mathcal{E}$ restricted to $\mathbb{H}^l$.
