{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.184732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f04157af0b43ab9ab9b742ee362f9bbe54802e2971cf61f3965ec58d88f3784d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] Let $B\subset \mathbf N(\mathbbm{X})$ be measurable, and let $X_0,\dots,X_m$ be $\mathbf N(\mathbbm{X})$-valued random variables defined on a common probability space. Then
\begin{align*}
\Pb\big[\{X_0\in B\}\Delta\{X_m\in B\}\big]
\le
\sum_{i=1}^m \Pb \big[\{X_{i-1}\in B\}\Delta\{X_i\in B\}\big].
\end{align*}
Equivalently,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_B[X_0,X_m]
\le
\sum_{i=1}^m \mathcal E_B[X_{i-1},X_i].
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.125870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f047772d31aaf341b9af0eb5c05bc6647c9b552634c8da291b427f251c416c1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2507.03552, 'On one-dimensional Cluster cluster model'] Let $d=1,\alpha\ge 0,p\in(0,1)$. $\exists T>0$ s.t for all $\varepsilon>0$ there exists $c>0$ s.t for all $t>T$,
