{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.850397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f04e85a2c4b19e313bb97e915c731b1f2e9401d76acf51132ee6994e205c49b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 15 of arXiv:2609.03869, '\bf Sharp asymptotics for a transport model with a nonlocal condition of the Fisher-KPP ty'] Let $u$ be the bounded and continuous solution of the linear transport problem
	\eqref{moving frame-u} associated with an absolutely continuous, bounded and compactly supported  initial datum
	$u_0$ in $[0,i^\dagger)\times\mathbb R$. 
	Then, for every $T>0$ and $\boldsymbol{a}>0$,
