\end{equation}
where the sum converges absolutely and uniformly. Moreover, $\norm{v}\le2\tmix b.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.405500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f07375b394d5a5c765b08550f5d30f94df39a98f68742b3ee3cb64d3102442ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 11 of arXiv:2609.03268, 'Poincare Polynomials of Heavy-Light Hassett Spaces'] Let $p_n(x)$ be as defined in \cref{thm:LM-ppoly-deg2-recursion}. Then for $n\ge 1$, 
