{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.132855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f07b4125577d635547aacbb2c3ef684e8e951f2bc802bd777d6411b5e47e5e04","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2608.26693, '2608.26693'] Fix $p$ and $\Sigma\in\mathbb S_{++}^p$.  If $X,Y,K_0,K_1$ range over operator-norm-bounded subsets of the symmetric matrices, then, uniformly as $\varepsilon\to0$,
\begin{align}
