{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.352583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f089ad7906be7edde9ed2f39e48419e1ebe5a8bf9d2f320a986505c576b129a8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_gammaapplication_momentbound of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Assume the setup of Theorem (theorem_superconvergencetogamma of the paper). Let $q$ be any positive number satisfying $q<\alpha$. Then we have the moment bounds 
