{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.708949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0e045545d2b78958bba907a6da8d707bd027ae3cd8827fd35065a2ffd870c92","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 26 of arXiv:2609.00254, 'On the geometry and cohomology of almost abelian solvmanifolds'] Let $\rho$ be a non-degenerate integrable pure spinor and let
$X+\xi\in\left(\mathfrak g\oplus\mathfrak g^*\right)\otimes_{\mathbb R}\mathbb C$ be such that
$\d\rho=(X+\xi)\cdot\rho$. Then the character of Lemma \ref{lem:bicomplex}(d) is
\begin{equation}
\chi(v)=2\left\langle X+\xi,\,v\right\rangle,\qquad v\in \mathfrak L .
\end{equation}
In particular, $\chi=0$ if and only if $\rho$ is closed, that is, if and only if the structure is
generalized Calabi--Yau, in which case
$GH^{\,n-\bullet}_{\overline\partial}(\mathfrak g)\cong H^\bullet\left(\mathfrak L,\mathbb C\right)$.","status":"unverified"}

