{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.996692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0eac586711597ba09782bc056906ccced2545d1cf379134de76c217e192e68c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $K(z,w)$ be a $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function positive definite on $\Omega$.
  In the above notation there is  a uniquely defined Hilbert space, denoted by $\mathcal H(K)$ and called the reproducing kernel Hilbert space associated to
  $K(z,w)$ with the following properties:\\
  $(1)$ The elements of $\mathcal H(K)$ are functions defined on $\Omega$.\\
  $(2)$  For every $z\in\Omega$ and $f\in\mathcal H(K)$
  \begin{equation}

f(z)=\langle f,K_z\rangle_{\mathcal H(K)}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, given any orthonormal basis $(f_a)_{a\in A}$ (where $A$ is an index set with the dimension of $\mathcal H(K)$) it holds that
\begin{equation}
  K(z,w)=\sum_{a\in A}f(z)f(w)^*.

  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.165701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0edf017ed6f90c38e743ec18d6a1251d9ce22abfa83fb1679f119dccaf0912c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_ThickenedSpaceOfZ2ZEigenSpinors_Submanifold+Submersion of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] For every $({\mathbf{p}}_0,[{\mathfrak l}_0];\Phi_0,\lambda_0) \in \mathbf{Eig}^*$
