{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.892750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f116df90d425afc566dabfb9eb119f222d2748c153a3471d0161ebdb6cea40a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Concentration of the predictable quadratic variation) of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] There exist constants $C,c>0$ such that, for every $n\ge2$ and $u>0$,
