{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.760161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f118b1db0d26097313922a96e66a57d2c8234d3f82eb5712633a4b356be2d650","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Galerkin of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] For all $U_0=(u_0,\eta_0)\in\mathcal{H}^0_\mu$ and $t\ge 0$, there exists a unique strong solution pair $(V_N,\eta_N)\in C([0,t];H\timesM^0_\mu)$. Furthermore, there exists a positive constant $c(U_0,t)$ independent of $N$ such that the following holds
