{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.185275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f14a07d76c0fcb08e0fa4bb3567da71efc915543584c8021f7f12345e387b1b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:mixing of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] There is a unique probability law $\pi\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{X})$ satisfying the \red[stationarity equation] $\pi T=\pi$. Moreover, $\pi$ has full support, and it is a global attractor:
