\end{eqnarray*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.763786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f14c48ebcac942f0ece75298c021c008e067aee3d26913933a2fb44a59e270db","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_u_s of arXiv:2605.00657, 'Spectral Duality and Reset-Neutral Distributions\\ in Random Walks with Multi-Site Geometr'] For any $z\in\{1,\dots,a-1\}$ and $gamma\in(0,1)$:
\begin{align}
u(z) &= \sum_{nu=1}^{a-1} A_nu(z)\,f_nu(gamma),
\\
s(z) &= \sum_{nu=1}^{a-1} \bigl[A_nu(z)+B_nu(z)\bigr]\,f_nu(gamma),

\end{align}
where the spectral coefficients are
\begin{align}
A_nu(z) &= \frac{2}{a}\left(\frac{q}{p}\right)^{z/2}
\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu z}{a}\right)\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu}{a}\right),
\\
B_nu(z) &= \frac{2}{a}\left(\frac{p}{q}\right)^{(a-z)/2}
\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu(a-z)}{a}\right)\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu}{a}\right),

\end{align}
and the spectral transfer function is
\begin{equation}
f_nu(gamma) := \frac{\lambda_nu(1-gamma)}{1-\lambda_nu(1-gamma)}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

