{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.950774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f165acd53c902c92c4421a0b0e4a1fb1bbeefe6e46f1cb9f398eac42ae8b0b00","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor.conv.nb.zeros of arXiv:2609.01007, 'Global universality of the expected number \\of zeros of non-analytic random signals'] Suppose that the base function $f$ is of class $\mathcal{C}^2([0,2\pi])$ and satisfies the condition $\mathbf{(H1)}$, then we have
