{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.752537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1d3f2af74bdddd268a72b60acdd59283bd98b1391369255a7972acffda6e11e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{distribution of outliers}, set $z=\theta_i^a+\ii n^{-2}$ for some $1\le i \le r$. Then, for $\mathcal{P}_i^a\equiv \mathcal{P}_i^a(z)$ and any fixed $\ell\geq 2$, we have 
