{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.460674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1d7b79171a7aa30c0bcc90d44f2249400d1e3c471e22fdf174a166f851c3a94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-GG1 of arXiv:2505.00198, '\ttl'] For any $q\in (0,1)$, the equation (equation eqGG1:mainequation of the paper) has a unique bounded solution. Since both $F_{W^{\texttt{R}}}$ and the CDF defined by the series (equation eqGG1:solutionseries of the paper) satisfy (equation eqGG1:mainequation of the paper), they must coincide. That is, 
