{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.642131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1d8349efb779b9ccf69b1816da5094e066a0c6dabba1c3ba1db215c2899ff94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2607.28992, 'Minimal inversion of a permuton sample'] Let $\mu$ be a $(\alpha,\phi)$-standard permuton as defined in Section~\ref{sec:ass}.
    Let $\minv_n^\mu$ be the minimal inversion of $n$ points distributed according to $\mu$, as defined in~\eqref{eq:main}.
