{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.050372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1d89b21d7872f32f83e6418e1d1a1bd522145c9da70da1d5e072b950f556d43","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sharpmain of arXiv:2607.12564, 'Power-law and log-periodic degree tails for a family of probability generating function eq'] For every integer $j\ge1$ there is a continuous, strictly positive, $1$-periodic function $\Psi_j$,
