{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.836764+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2102553f303e69c469bf5c678c95ce886a473b3da8e51f0f54d68ffbe0707d7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2607.20646, 'The Independence-Preserving Property and Planar Web Geometry'] Fix $\alpha\not=\beta\in\mathbb{CP}^1$.
    Define $\HIp$, $\HIIp$ and $\HIIIA$ by
    \begin{alignat}{3}

        \HIp(x, y)
        &=                                                                      
        \Big\lparen
            \frac{y}{\alpha}\,\frac{\beta+\alpha x+\beta y+\alpha \beta x y}{1+x+y+\beta x y}
            &,\quad& \frac{x}{\beta}\,\frac{\alpha+\alpha x+\beta y+\alpha \beta x y}{1+x+y+\alpha x y}
        &&\Big\rparen,
        \\

        \HIIp(x, y)
        &=
        \Big\lparen
            \frac{y}{\alpha}\,\frac{\beta+ \alpha x+\beta y}{1+x+y}
            &,\quad& \frac{x}{\beta}\,\frac{\alpha+ \alpha x+\beta y}{1+x+y}
        &&\Big\rparen,
        \\

        \HIIIA(x, y)
        &=
        \Big\lparen
            \frac{y}{\alpha}\,\frac{\alpha x+\beta y}{x+y}
            &,\quad& \frac{x}{\beta}\,\frac{\alpha x+\beta y}{x+y}
        &&\Big\rparen.
    \end{alignat}","status":"unverified"}

