{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.279634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2329c573e7c45570f73f11e9d7b7134b711273dd2a032b2f8cc1be62b8b7eb0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop martingalerenormalisee of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Under the \hyperlink{ren}{renormalized setting}, let $\varphi \in \mathcal{C}^{1,1}_{\omega}(\mathbb{R}^{+} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$ and $K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}$. Then the process $(\langle \mu^{K}_{t}, \varphi_{t} \rangle)_{t \geq 0}$ is a semi-martingale, with for all $t \geq 0$, a finite variation part given by
\begin{align*}
V^{K}_{\varphi,t} := & \hspace{0.1 cm} \langle \mu^{K}_{0}, \varphi_{0} \rangle + \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}} \langle \mu^{K}_{s}, \Phi_{s}(R^{K}_{s},.) \rangle \mathrm{d}s - \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} }} d(x)\varphi_{s}(x) \mu^{K}_{s}(\mathrm{d}x) \mathrm{d}s \\
    &  + \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} } b(x)\bigg( \varphi_{s}(x_{0})+\varphi_{s}(x-x_{0})-\varphi_{s}(x)\bigg) \mu^{K}_{s}(\mathrm{d}x) \mathrm{d}s,
\end{align*}
with $\Phi$ associated to $\varphi$ as in (equation eq:Phidef of the paper), and a square-integrable martingale part $\heartsuit^{K}_{\varphi,t} := \langle \mu^{K}_{t}, \varphi_{t} \rangle -V^{K}_{\varphi,t} $ whose predictable quadratic variation is given by
\begin{align*}
\langle \heartsuit^{K}_{\varphi} \rangle_{t} & = \dfrac{1}{K} \Bigg( \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}}}b(x)\bigg[ \varphi_{s}(x_{0})+\varphi_{s}(x-x_{0})-\varphi_{s}(x) \bigg]^{2} \mu^{K}_{s}(\mathrm{d}x) \mathrm{d}s \\
& \hspace{8cm} + \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}}}d(x)\varphi_{s}^{2}(x) \mu^{K}_{s}(\mathrm{d}x) \mathrm{d}s\Bigg).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.302436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2337e91fbd03bc8b624df459d4e7c0f4da2bb583d6740dcb01edd810eeae009","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop loiderho2 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] For the Skorokhod $J_1$-topology, when $i \rightarrow +\infty$
