{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.968784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f28f2129afda0829b5f63d3525e119a297715a74bdae76267e9c895afb3cdd3d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma anewlemma of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] Under the same conditions as in Proposition (procha3 of the paper), there exists a constant $n \in \mathbb{N}$, such that for any $k \geq n$, any SE operators $\hat{T},\ \check{T} \in \mathcal{M}$,
