{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.576684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2a56e53b4d440653cb2c95c70980549df4977b04f417cfb8f57daf457cd12d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: grid of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] For any $\tau\in(0,3/4)$, there exist positive integers $T=T(\tau), k=k(\tau)$, and vectors $\mathbf{u}^{(1)},\dots,\mathbf{u}^{(T)}$ from the interior of the unit ball in $\mathbb{C}^k$ such that, for any $t\in\{1,\dots,T\}$ and all $p/n\in\left(\tau_{t-1},\tau_t\right]$,
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\|\Pi_{p/N}^{[k]}\operatorname{diag}\{\mathbf{u}^{(t)}\}\Pi_{n/N}^{[k]}\|}{\sqrt{p/N}}>K_{1,n/p}-\tau/2.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, for all $p/n\in\left[\log^{-\alpha} n,\tau\right]$ and all sufficiently large $n$, we have:
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\|\Pi_{p/N}^{[2L_n+1]}\operatorname{diag}\{\mathbf{u}^{(0)}\}\Pi_{n/N}^{[2L_n+1]}\|}{\sqrt{p/N}}>K_{1,n/p}-3\tau/4,
    \end{equation}
    where  $L_n:=\lceil \log n\rceil$ and $\mathbf{u}^{(0)}=(0,\dots,0,1-\tau/15,0,\dots,0)^\top$ with $L_n$ zeros on both sides of the term $1-\tau/15$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.383349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2a7a0372596eae92ff82e32a4a052af3a7cbd07d3afa737e5f2464964718a20","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let $\alpha>-1$, $\theta>0$ and $\mu$ be a positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$. Then
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{B}_n}\left|V_{\mu}^{\xi}(z)\right|^{\theta}{\rm d}v_{\alpha}(z)\simeq \int_{\mathbb{D}}\left|V_{\mu}(u)\right|^{\theta}(1-|u|^2)^{n+\alpha-1}{\rm d}A(u),
