{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.266057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2c31955dec797de8bd78e0616b9e80b050dbd10a355e8ec2a48293e03a4d953","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2604.20323, '2604.20323'] For $u\ge 1$, $\theta\in\{0,1\}$ and $k\in\N$, there exists $C<\infty$ such that 
  \begin{align}
    \forall t\in(0,T],\;\|\partial_t^\theta\nabla^kp_\alpha(t,\cdot)\|_{L^u}+\|\partial_t^\theta\nabla^k\bar p_\alpha(t,\cdot)\|_{L^u}\le Ct^{-(\theta+\frac k\alpha +\frac d{\alpha u'})}.\end{align}For $k\in\N$, there exists $C<\infty$ such that
  \begin{equation}
