{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.020114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2cde778ed0cfd2756ccc18608bcc9b76c495650f36e9d1befbe0fe18bb07409","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:ProjectionLemma of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] For any positive definite matrix $P$, the unique BW projection onto the geodesically convex set $[\alpha I, \beta I]$ (for $0<\alpha \leq \beta < \infty$) is given by eigenvalue-clipping:
