{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.575796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2ceb5e4d74e166de6d53c0a32ca34366dc9d13f2402f46131a1687de3911744","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2606.14564, 'Upper tails for irregular graphs \\ beyond the mean-field regime'] There exist positive constants $\eta$ and $\sigma$ such that the following holds for all $p_H \le p \le p_H \cdot n^\eta$.
