with high probability.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.057340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2e1506196d2cb490b45d0904ca13456b8cdcd8348892876b62f41f113aecd05","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 (Net bounds) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] A $1/4$-net $\mathcal N$ of the unit sphere in $\F^r$ may be chosen with $|\mathcal N|\le9^{2r}$.  For Hermitian $A$ and arbitrary $B$,
