for every $ \varphi \in c_{ 00}( \mathbb N^M)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.594515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f343c7e5d9f96545d3246b84ba0d4ed54d5909b85bea03250bd4d3d327b1dd15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-1.4 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Let~$\beta>0$ and  let $v_\star$ be a $1$-periodic continuous function such that  (equation Eq:3.33 of the paper) holds.  Let~$\nu_\star$ be the Borel measure  on~$[0,1)$  defined by
\begin{equation}

\nu_\star(\text{\rm d}\mkern0.5mu z):=\Bigl[\int_{[0,1]}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-(b+1)v_\star(z')}\text{\rm d}\mkern0.5mu z'\Bigr]^{-1}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-(b+1)v_\star(z)}1_{[0,1)}(z)\text{\rm d}\mkern0.5mu z.
\end{equation}
For~$k=1,\dots,n$, abbreviate
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
A_{n,k}:=(b+1)&\sup_{z\in\mathbb R}\bigl|v_\star(z)\bigr|+\sup_{z,z'\in\mathbb R}\bigl|v_k(z)-b v_{k-1}(z')\bigr|
\\&+\frac\beta2\max\{\sigma_k^{-2},1\} 
+ \frac12\log(2\pi/\beta)+\log\max\{\sigma_k,1\}
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\delta_k:=\sup_{z,z'\in\mathbb R}\Bigl| \bigl[v_k(z)-bv_{k-1}(z')\bigr] - \bigl[v_\star(z)-bv_\star(z')\bigr]\Bigr|+\log\max\{\sigma_k,\sigma_k^{-1}\}.
\end{equation}
Then for all $k=1,\dots,n$,
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
\bigl\Vert P(\phi_k\text{\rm\ mod }1\in\cdot) - \nu_\star\bigr\Vert_{\text{\rm TV}}
\le \prod_{i=k}^n (1-\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-A_{n,i}}) +\sum_{j=k+1}^n (1-\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\delta_{j-1}})\prod_{i=k}^{j-2}(1-\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-A_{n,i}}),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
 where the last product is interpreted as~$1$ when~$j=k+1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.498437+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f343e4d93309868c71dff177c2fddb864053ced7e1da9f08025069e60a16b01c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] Fix $T,\beta,\varepsilon>0$ and $\delta>0$. There exist constants
