{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.157980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f350bf1ba78013b29130f52cee7ef3f4fa0e8bf50a85a379778a5bd6a7669bab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.15874, 'On Continuous Data Assimilation for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids o'] In this lemma, we collect some inequalities that will be used later on:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item  We can find a positive constant $C_{S,d}$ (\cite[Subsection 2.4]{Kesavan_1989}) such that 
		\begin{align}
			\|\w\|_{\infty} \leq C_{S,d} \|\nabla\w\|_{4}, \quad \text{	for all } \;	\w\in	\mathbb{W}_0^{1,4}(\Ocal).
		\end{align}

		\item  We can find a positive constant $C_{K,d}$ (see \cite[Theorem 2 (ii)]{DiFratta+Solombrino_Arxiv}, a Korn-type inequality) such that 
		\begin{align}
			\Vert	\nabla \w \Vert_{4}	\leq	C_{K,d}\Vert	\Arm(\w)	\Vert_4,\quad \text{	for all } \;	\w\in	\mathbb{W}_0^{1,4}(\Ocal).
		\end{align}		
		\item In view of \eqref{Sobolev-embedding3} and \eqref{Korn-ineq}, we can find a positive constant $\mathrm{N}_d$ such that
		\begin{align}
			\|\w\|_{\infty} \leq \mathrm{N}_d \|\Arm(\w)\|_{4}, \quad \text{	for all } \;	\w\in	\mathbb{W}_0^{1,4}(\Ocal).
		\end{align}
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.015827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f35288ef21203ef5b08f858a157d5575726eee43b4cbb739f267d3d48d9bc544","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:general-spectral-link} holds.
