{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.171028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3924dea5e942b890f001a8e08e1e2c7922edf5e68181076d6a02a8e3b17b981","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 45 (Mild Variation of Constants) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumption \ref{ass:regular_obstacles} hold. For any penalization parameter $\varepsilon > 0$ and any initial state $(t, x) \in [0, T] \times H$, the continuous obstacle $\Phi$ satisfies the following identity:
