{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.412601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f393a1da9013c40a3a466801fa28226a407b4093ed020be5b4ab032bd77096ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:global_nonasymptotic of arXiv:2608.27313, 'A Finite Sample Analysis for Quantile Temporal Difference Learning in Distributional Reinf'] Suppose $\bm\theta^{(0)}\in[0,(1-\gamma)^{-1}]^{{\mathcal{S}}\times[m]}$ and $cC_0\le1$. For every $\delta\in(0,1)$ and $T\ge T_0(\delta)$, where the explicit threshold $T_0(\delta)$ is given in Equation~(equation eq:T0_conditions of the paper), with probability at least $1-\delta$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    \norm{\bm\theta^{(T)}-\bm\theta_m}_\infty
    \lesssim{}&
    r_{\mathrm{out}}
    \exp\left\{-\frac{c\lambda_mT^{1-a}}{C}\right\}
