with $\sum_k\frac{h^k}{k!}C_{k,t} < \infty$ almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.632960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3ce447031872b3068030b485b959820c0fde9bd9197bb5ef957f0ab59c5bdc3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2506.17061, 'Non-uniform bounds for non-normal approximation via Stein's method with applications to th'] Let $p\ge 1$, $0<s\le 2p$ and let $|c|\le 100$. Then
