{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.392123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3d1bf679f341393b95e87b77807e42d85c7b9d62b8c21d7e3560ce1ab998e26","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] For each $p \in (0, 1)$, we may choose a sufficiently small $\delta = \delta(p) > 0$ and a sufficiently large $r_\ast = r_\ast(p) > 0$ such that
