{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.116807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3d9e40dc64cd1d5798e6685181baa8663c6d3d8d3d4c417c41c31b1ffd59f6e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Lyapunov drift for a perturbed potential) of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Make the Assumptions~\ref{a:criticalpts}--\ref{a: nondegeneracy} on~$U$.
There exist constants~$\hat\epsilon, \eta, \lambda, \gamma, a, b, C_P > 0$ such that for any~$\epsilon \le \hat\epsilon$, we have a perturbed potential $\hat U\colon \T^d \to [0,\infty)$, depending on~$\epsilon$, with the following properties.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For all~$x\in B(m_1, a \sqrt{\epsilon})$,
    \begin{equation}
        \hat U(x) = U(x)\,.
    \end{equation}
    \item Perturbed potential~$\hat U$ is close to~$U$ in~$L^\infty$ in the sense that
    \begin{equation}
        \norm{\hat U - U}_{L^\infty(\T^d)} \leq C_P\epsilon\,.
    \end{equation}
    \item Define $W \colon \T^d \to [1/10,\infty)$ as
\begin{equation}
W(x) = \exp(\gamma\hat U(x))\,.
\end{equation}
Then, for all $h$ satisfying $h/\epsilon^2 \le \eta$, 
\begin{equation}
\hat Q_{h,\epsilon} W(x)
\le
(1-\lambda \gamma h^2) W(x)
+ b \one_{\Omega_1 \setminus B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})}\,,
\qquad
\forall x \in \Omega_1 .
\end{equation}

Here $\hat Q_{h,\epsilon} = \hat P_{h,\epsilon}\vert_{\Omega_1}$ denotes the restriction of the chain $\hat P_{h,\epsilon}$ to $\Omega_1$, where $\hat P_{h,\epsilon}$ is the Metropolis random walk with step size $h$ and the stationary density $\hat\pi_\epsilon \propto \exp(-\hat U/\epsilon)$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.902557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3dd1312830bc725c28049b2c69cdc0e262ae224e854f9fe469d27073d6d78ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Greydis of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] We keep the previous notation. We assume $\mathbf{A1}$--$\mathbf{A4}$. For all $z\! \in \!  [0, a_p]$, we set $\psi_p (z) \! :=\! b_p \big( \varphi_{\xi_p} \big(1\! -\! \frac{1}{a_p}z \big) \! -\! 1 + \frac{1}{a_p}z\big)$, where we set $b_p\!:=a_pc_p$. Then $b_p\rightarrow\infty$, and the laws of $(\mathtt{Ht}_{ p})_{p\in \mathbb{N}}$ are tight on $\mathbb{R}_+$ iff the following condition is satisfied: \vspace{-0.1cm}
\begin{equation}

\lim_{z\to \infty} \limsup_{p\to \infty} \int_{z}^{a_p}\!\!  \frac{du}{\psi_p(u)}= 0 \; .
\end{equation} 
In that case, the Grey condition ((Grey of the paper)) is satisfied, $\mathtt{Ext}$ is a.s.~finite and $\mathtt{Ht}_{ p} \! \to \! \mathtt{Ext}$ in law on $\mathbb{R}_+$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.043696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3dd44784c3aa0e8c1785d179fe9f7712f1a22acd3980f26306e67ae40c7659e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 75 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] There exist  $d_{0}\in(1,d)$ and a constant    $N $, depending only
on $d,\delta$, 
 such that for any ($\lambda\geq\varkappa_{0}^{2}\rho_{b}^{-2}$)  ball  $B$ of radius $\rho\leq \varkappa_{0}/(2\sqrt\lambda)$ 
