{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.241412+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3f9e392e2754ac3ce71f7c9be1165b046f81af5c3f4759f725ff62ad6eb6c43","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] For all $T\in(0,\infty)$, $\alpha\in[0,\beta)$, and any mapping $\varphi\colon H\to\R$ of class $\mathcal{C}^4$, with bounded derivatives up to order $4$, there exists $C_{\alpha}(T,\varphi)\in(0,\infty)$ such that for all $t\in[0,T]$ one has
