{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.829243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3fbb4146a5d87b31ca2be0c866f1991daa34706c8832c487b85b68eb9a901a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2604.10705, '#1'] Let $F \in \mathfrak{C}^2([0, T],\mathbb{R}^d)$, let $x \in C([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)$, let $\pi = \{\pi_n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of partitions such that $\lim_{n \to \infty} |\pi_n| = 0$, and let $x$ be of bounded quadratic covariation along the partition $\pi$. Then,
