{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.826671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4393a3a5af55a674f80dbc15a2c03c441729899da20d2843e38cd93b17d5735","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary mgf-bound of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Given two distributions $P, Q$ with countable supports and $\theta \in \R^+$ such that $\E_Q[e^{2\theta X}] < \infty$, then 

