{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.850566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f48a12729db404a74806cce9361704b93792740b2b197a0653e6deba9253f6e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop renorm_3 of arXiv:2607.10105, 'The four-dimensional Anderson model: a case study for critical SPDEs'] Given $\sigma$ as in ((eq.setup_8 of the paper)). Consider the process in Definition (def.renormterm of the paper) and the set of fully paired \emph{proper} subintervals obtained (i.e. not including $[1,2q]$ itself), with left and right endpoints $\ell_i$ and $r_i$ for $1\leq i\leq s$. Then for the $\mathcal J_{2q,\sigma}$ in ((eq.setup_8 of the paper)), we have
