{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.855688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4995da3042c7c6b13b1929eea2d8bde81ecae4f47fb28c8cd4ee6eefd7a95e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2607.16145, 'The Memoryless Best-Choice Problem'] For arbitrary stopping rule $\tau$, the $\delta$-extensions 
