then $\lambda(t)$ is called an $\mathcal{F}_t-$\emph{stochastic intensity} of $\Phi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.744728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f49c6d8b02fccb2af60764bcc9226d8ae8de44b6dc076c392942ba9300d42645","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2605.02499, '2605.02499'] Let $Z^{(N)}=(Z^{(N)}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the continuous-time Markov chain on $[N]_{0}^\Delta$ with transitions
\begin{equation*}
    n\in[N]_{0} \to \begin{cases}
        n + j & \text{at rate } n \sum_{m=j}^{\infty} s_m \,p_{mj}^n
        \text{ for }  j\geq 2,\\[5pt]
        n+1 & \text{at rate } \frac{\kappa}{N} \binom{n}{2} \frac{N-n}{N} + n \sum_{m=1}^{\infty}  s_m \, p^n_{m1}, \\[5pt]
        n-1 & \text{at rate } \frac{1}{N} \binom{n}{2} \big( r + \kappa \, \frac{N-(n-1)}{N}\big)  + u\nu_1 n ,\\[5pt]
        \Delta & \text{at rate } u\nu_0 n,
    \end{cases}
\end{equation*}
with $p_{mj}^n$ of \eqref{eq.pnmj}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.577309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f49fd936f24ad968ea443b1ed5b604308d1fa64daca0f4fbdb19512c08edc69d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] In addition to Assumption \ref{assumption}, suppose that 
