{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.047960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4a07d838248b62a010f754e0bc150d3391f40ac99409ba2669db1e8a3f19ad8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition number_of_cusps_mean_and_concentration of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_g \underset{g \to +\infty}{\rightarrow}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c - \mu_g = o(g^{-2})$ and any $r \ge 0$, we have 
