{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.826467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4bb904fa7dcd2d44c79321c5f5e3e5544367380a97cd0b5e6c0c1a950a07fc2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2604.10266, 'A singular SDE driven by additive fractional Brownian motion with Hurst parameter $H<\frac'] Let $(\alpha_i,\beta_i)$, $i\geq 1$, be an interval in the presentation of \eqref{interval}. Then,
