{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.495993+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4bd35c4be90c0c568117056640f8a621ecc402af3eb162610fc3819fbbba17f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2607.04193, 'Onsager--Machlup Functionals for Generalized Newtonian Equations of Motion with Time-Varyi'] Let $f \in I_{a^+}^\alpha(L^p)$ and $g \in I_{b^-}^\alpha(L^p)$ with $p \ge 1$. The left-sided and right-sided Riemann--Liouville fractional derivatives of order $\alpha > 0$ are defined respectively by
    \begin{align*}
        (D_{a^+}^\alpha f)(x) &:= \left( \frac{d}{dx} \right)^{[\alpha] + 1} I_{a^+}^{1 + [\alpha] - \alpha} f(x), \\
        (D_{b^-}^\alpha g)(x) &:= \left( -\frac{d}{dx} \right)^{[\alpha] + 1} I_{b^-}^{1 + [\alpha] - \alpha} g(x),
    \end{align*}
    where $[\alpha]$ denotes the integer part of $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.203249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4bd936a9e015c5fffa93aa9b3a6629c44abba0ec29562391d87ea9ccafa2caa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Let $\delta_{\bm{1}_{x>0}}$ be the Dirac delta on the configuration $\eta(x)=\bm{1}_{x>0}$.
    For any sequence $k_1,\dots,k_n$, the measure
    \[
    \prod_{i=1}^nP_{k_i}\delta_{\bm{1}_{x>0}}
    \]
    is stochastically dominated by the blocking measure $\pi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.354161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4bfe063c839e71752077a55b69378efe73d59d6c9ad73459315698e13de9b33","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp unified_inversion of arXiv:2608.10215, 'The variance of the Pitman--Yor process: a Cifarelli--Regazzini identity and inversion for'] The density function $q_{\alpha,\theta}(y)$ of $\mathfrak{L}$ exists for all $\theta > 0$ and admits the unified Riemann--Liouville representation:
\begin{equation} 
q_{\alpha,\theta}(y) = \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} y} \int_0^y (y - t)^{\theta-1} \Delta_{\alpha,\theta}(t) \, \mathrm{d} t
\end{equation}
where the spectral jump function $\Delta_{\alpha,\theta}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\Delta_{\alpha,\theta}(y) = \frac{1}{\pi [R_\alpha(y)]^{\theta/\alpha}} \sin\left( \frac{\theta}{\alpha} \phi_\alpha(y) \right)\ .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.048255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4c2340a9f5074cad0be902aa4bcafeb4d3d232af946c297dc9b6d61a48a16eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mytheo 1 of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] For every $p \in (0,1/2]$ and $\varepsilon > 0$, there are $n_{\ref{Theorem A}}$ and $c_{\ref{Theorem A}} >0$ depending only on $p$ and $\varepsilon$ with the following property. Let $n \ge n_{\ref{Theorem A}}$, $1 \le k \le c_{\ref{Theorem A}}\sqrt{\log{n}}$, and let $B_{n}(p)$ be $n \times n$ random matrix with independent entries $b_{ij}$ such that $\mathbb{P}(b_{ij}=0)=1-p$ and $\mathbb{P}(b_{ij}=1)=p$. Then we have 
   \begin{align*}
       \mathbb{P}\left(  \mathrm{rank}\left(B_{n}(p) \right) \le n-k   \right) \le \left( 1-p+\varepsilon \right)^{kn}.
   \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.240401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4c2ace431f839d5ae330bca73b27ccaefed72656fdbd8062317f9baef7e32f7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem res:RM:quant:fast of arXiv:2607.07309, 'Quantitative limit theorems for generalized P\'olya urns with applications to random tree '] Let $(X_n)$ and $(\Delta M_n)$ be  sequences of random variables, adapted to a filtration $(\mathcal{F}_n)$, taking values in $\mathbb{R}^n$, let $(\gamma_n)$ be a sequence of nonnegative real numbers, and let $F: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n$ be a measurable function on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and $P$ be a symmetric, positive-semi-definite $n \times n$ matrix. Suppose (i)-(iv) and (vi) of Theorem (thrm:RM of the paper) hold, and 
\begin{itemize}
    \item [(v'')] $K\gamma_n^2\leq q/(n+r)^2$ and $c/(n+r)\leq 2A\gamma_n$, for all $n\in\mathbb{N}$ where $c>1$, $q\geq 0$ and $r\ge1$.
\end{itemize}
 Then
\[
\mathbb{E}[\left\lVertX_n-z\right\rVert_P^2]\leq\frac{t}{n+r} \text{ and }\mathbb{P}\left(\exists m\geq n(\left\lVertX_n-z\right\rVert_P\geq \varepsilon)\right)\leq \frac{t+2q}{\varepsilon^2(n+r)}
\]
for all $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $\varepsilon>0$, where $t\geq \max\left\{q/(c-1),rL\right\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.409703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4c302f7655b1419bad23e45a316c9d2857502614ecd709bcec92c167574648e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.07207, 'Mixing times of step-reinforced random walks'] Under Assumption \ref{mainassum}, if $\mu$ is symmetric, then for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$,
