{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.835458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4df5f9843e4c7bbfeb7ec469da51ba584134d8547adb3338672a430fe3b91f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2607.20373, 'Embedding martingale diffusions as binary posteriors in sequential inference'] Suppose $\delta\not=0$ on $J$. Then, for each $t\geq0$, the map
