{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.057389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4ed1785e86e912031f97fe5737c59741dfb0b33f118e2688f94d2c7f0bd3881","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 (\cite{chen2022hamilton}) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Let $\psi:\mcl Q_2^\D\to\R$ be $\Ll(\mcl Q_2^\D\Rr)^*$-increasing and satisfy
\begin{align}
    \Ll|\psi(q)-\psi(q')\Rr|\leq \Ll|q-q'\Rr|_{L^1},\qquad\forall q,q'\in\mcl Q_2^\D.
\end{align}
With initial condition $f(0,\cdot)=\psi$, there exists a viscosity solution $f$ of~\eqref{e.hj}, unique in the class of Lipschitz functions on $\R_+\times\mcl Q_2^\D$. Moreover, if $\psi$ is convex on $\mcl Q_2^\D$, then $f$ admits the Hopf representation
\begin{align}
        f(t,q) = \sup_{p \in \mcl Q_\infty^\D}\inf_{q' \in \mcl Q_\infty^\D}\left\{ \psi(q') + \la q - q', p\ra_\cH +t\int_0^1\xi(p(s))\d s\right\},\quad\forall(t,q)\in\R_+\times\mcl Q_2^\D.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.478358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4ed5f015379813ca8e611fac3ea0e3acb8877a9702f8781c3ee76ba74be6822","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Variational reduction for a high-centered wedge) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] For $0<p<q<1$,
\begin{align*}
 &\inf\left\{
 \KL(x_1\|p)+\KL(x_2\|p)+\KL(y\|q):
 (x_1,x_2,y)\in[0,1]^3,\ x_1\ge y,\ x_2\ge y
 \right\}
 \\
