{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.895326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f51024da977cd194ccfb5b54433ff26406690a35a91b9a7de3133fe5c8bd3da3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] A point~$(\xi,\eta)\in (-1,1)^2$ is in
