{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.750125+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f521f3bce598806cd3a2809f1f706f07c0ac45e32bd4dbe64e7c874087fcaa9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Assume that 
\begin{equation}
\big[(t,x)\mapsto b(t,x,y)\big], \ \big[(t,x)\mapsto \sigma\sigma^\top (t,x,y)\big] \in L^{\infty}_{\text{loc}}([0,\infty)\times\mathbb{R}^d),
\end{equation}
uniformly w.r.t. $y\in \mathbb{R}$.
Then, D-MKV$(b,\sigma)$ is weakly well-posed if and only if D-NL-MP$(b,\sigma;\nu)$ admits a unique solution for any $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

