{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.629940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5380b0ec13413e4e6258da8184606b7eef965188f74d26239726b21d5911e8a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: second moment of arXiv:2603.10738, 'Pairwise Negative Correlation for Uniform Spanning\\ Subgraphs of the Complete Graph'] Let $\mathrm{Aut}(K_n)$ denote the automorphism group of the complete graph $K_n$, and recall that ${\ensuremath{\mathscr F}} ^{(k)}(K_n)$ denotes the set of $k$-forests of $K_n$. Suppose ${\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} $ is an $\mathrm{Aut}(K_n)$-invariant probability measure such that that ${\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} \big[(V,\eta(\omega))\in {\ensuremath{\mathscr F}} ^{(k)}(K_n)\big]=1$, where $\omega$ is a random element of $\{0,1\}^{E(K_n)}$ with law ${\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} $. For $n\;\geqslant\;3$ define $p_1\coloneq {\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} \big[\omega(e)=\omega(f)=1\big]$, where $e$ and $f$ are a pair of adjacent edges in $K_n$. For $n\;\geqslant\; 4$, define $p_2\coloneq {\ensuremath{\mathbf P}} \big[ \omega(e)=\omega(e')=1\big]$, where $e$ and $e'$ are a pair of non-adjacent edges in $K_n$. Let $\deg(x;\omega)$ denote the degree of the vertex $x$ in the random subgraph $(V,\eta(\omega))$. Then we have
	\begin{equation}
	p_1=\frac{{\ensuremath{\mathbf E}} \Big[\sum_{x\in V(K_n)}{\deg(x;\omega)^2}\Big]-2(n-k)}{n(n-1)(n-2)}\quad \mbox{ for }n\;\geqslant\;3\,,
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
	p_2=\frac{4\bigg((n-k)(n-k+1)-{\ensuremath{\mathbf E}} \Big[\sum_{x\in V(K_n)}{\deg(x;\omega)^2}\Big]\bigg)}{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}\quad \mbox{ for }n\;\geqslant\;4\,.
	\end{equation}
	In particular, for $n\;\geqslant\;4$,
	\begin{equation}
	p_2=\frac{4\big[(n-k)(n-k-1)-n(n-1)(n-2)p_1\big]}{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}\,.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.727983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f53cf9170ce2add32c37f8a1cb4fe745d66637628253ed028c992d79d0e1169d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollary7.3 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] Lemma (lemmas7.1 of the paper) and (lemmas7.2 of the paper) imply that, for every fixed \(t>0\),

