{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.032319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5613dca5d0cc3f30573e1566c6dca19cd543f5d60caf3c0df4e697727531d26","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2605.02771, 'Universality in Deep Neural Networks:\\ An approach via the Lindeberg exchange principle'] Let \(z^{(L+1)}\) be the output of a DNN with \(L\) hidden layers with Gaussian bias as in \eqref{eq:Gaussian_biases} and with activation function \(\sigma\in C_b^3(\R)\). Then
