{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.289602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f565c4454db13acd9a53c7f6daf034c3e5eaf160598f38ae1217ecf41b17a17b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop gPI-char of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The gPI constant $\alpha_{\gPI}$ defined in~(equation def:PI-LSI-con of the paper) is continuous on $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$. Moreover, we have the following alternative characterisations for any $\zeta \in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$
    \begin{align}
        \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta) 
        = \inf_{\substack{f\in \langle \1 \rangle^{\perp_\zeta} \\ \|f\|_\zeta=1}}\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f)
        = \inf_{\substack{f\in \langle \1 \rangle^\perp \\ \|f\|=1}} 
        \frac{\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f)}{\operatorname{var}_\zeta(f)}  
        .
     \end{align}
    In addition, for any $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}) \ni \zeta_\varepsilon \to \zeta$ and any $0 < \delta_\varepsilon \to 0$ as $\varepsilon \to 0$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta) 
        = 
        \frac12 \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \inf_{\substack{\varphi \in \mathcal D_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}) \\ 0 < \| \varphi - \1 \|_{\zeta_\varepsilon} < \delta_\varepsilon }}
\frac{\mathscr{R}_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\varphi)}{\mathscr{H}_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\varphi)}.
     \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

