{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.783717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f569d40adf1175c53ccad8798c509b8b80b76b164647080399612bc3bbffe6ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the:Rnk_expectation of arXiv:2608.04303, 'The rank and layer distributions in random recursive trees'] The differences between the expected fractions of nodes of rank~$k$ or at layer~${k}$ in RRTs of size~$n$, and their respective values in the infinite RRTs, obey the following asymptotic inequalities for any fixed~$k$:

