{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.679032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f56edc466b4668db860387cceeb97bc7427db032356ef4bcfce05900c201bd76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:CE-law-without-area of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] {ChenLubetzky25}}]
		Let $V\subset \mathbb Z^2$ be a connected domain, and consider the \ensuremath{\mathbb Z\textsc{gff}}\xspace model ${\widehat\pi}_V^\xi$ with boundary conditions $\xi$ that are $1$ on a $*$-connected path in $\partial_{\mathtt v} V$ and $0$ elsewhere so that they induce a unique disagreement polymer $(\gamma,\{D_i\},\{h_i\})$ in $V\cup \partial_{\mathtt v} V$ that contains boundary disagreements. Then for $\beta\geq \beta_0$, the law of this unique disagreement polymer is given by 
