{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f583451e69473d8a0d3e42c8b3606bdf7b1d80795b692a465b9637c651fc0b6b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Absence of positive-time multiple collisions) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $x_0\in\Cc$.  Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, and \ref{ass:k:positive}.  Then the weak solution $X$ constructed in Theorem~\ref{thm:existence} has no multiple collisions at positive times.  More precisely, for every two different roots $\alpha,\beta \in R_+$ such that $\sum_{i=1}^\no \alpha_i^2\beta_i^2>0$ we have 
