{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.272413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f597ac35134cfefb51a7d7333723e0c7650f2bfddc9e615203753af2fa1a3353","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo1 theo1 of arXiv:2507.07923, 'Optimal Sets and Quantization Errors under Geometric Constraints for Discrete Distribution'] For any positive integer $n$, if $1\leq n\leq 5$, then the sets
\[\Big\{U_2(Av[n, \infty)), U_2(\frac 1 {n-1}),  \cdots, U_2(\frac 13), U_2(\frac 12), U_1(1)\Big\},\] where $1\leq n\leq 5$, form  constrained optimal sets of $n$-points;  on the other hand, if $6\leq n\leq 2000$, then the sets $\set{U_2(Av[n+1, \infty)), U_2(Av[n-1, n]), U_2(\frac 1 {n-2}), \cdots, U_2(\frac 13), U_2(\frac 12), U_1(1)}$ form constrained optimal sets of $n$-points for the probability measure $\mu$. The corresponding $n$th constrained quantization errors are given by
\begin{align*}
 Q_n^{(c)}(\mu)=\left\{\begin{array}{cc}
 Er[n, \infty]+\frac 34 \mathop{\sum}\limits_{j=2}^{n-1}\frac 1 {2^j} (\frac 1 j)^2+\frac 34 \mathop{\sum}\limits_{j=n}^\infty \frac 1{2^j} (Av[n, \infty])^2 & \text{ if } 1\leq n\leq 5, \\
\Big(Er[n+1, \infty]+Er[n-1, n]+\frac 34 \mathop{\sum}\limits_{j=2}^{n-2}\frac 1 {2^j} (\frac 1 j)^2+\frac 34\frac 1{2^{n-1}} (Av[n-1, n])^2 \\
+\frac 34 \mathop{\sum}\limits_{j=n}^\infty \frac 1{2^j} (Av[n, \infty])^2\Big)  & \text{ if } 6\leq n\leq 2000.
\end{array}
\right.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.335334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5984ed62f55f07b07354332dc08ae6ceb4ccd6acd2e204f8b359f40edc6c61a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a locally finite weighted graph and let $\psi\in C^{1}(0,+\infty)$ be a concave function with $\psi^\prime \left(1\right)>0$ and $H_{\psi}<\infty$.  Assume that $u:V\times[T_{1},T_{2}]\rightarrow(0,+\infty)$ satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
        \left(1-\alpha\right)\Gamma^{\psi}\left(u\right)-\psi^{\prime}\left(1\right)\frac{\partial_t u}{u}\leq\frac{c_1}{t}+c_2,
    \end{equation*}
    where $\alpha\in[0,1), c_{1}>0$ and $c_{2}\ge0$. Then for any $x,y\in V$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        u\left(x,T_1\right)\leq u\left(y,T_2\right)\left(\frac{T_2}{T_1}\right)^{\frac{c_1}{\psi^{\prime}\left(1\right)}}\exp\left(\frac{c_2}{\psi^{\prime}\left(1\right)}\left(T_2-T_1\right)+\frac{\psi^{\prime}\left(1\right)H_{\psi}\mu_{\max}d^2\left(x,y\right)}{\left(1-\alpha\right)w_{\min}\left(T_2-T_1\right)} \right).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

