{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.713173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5be35bdff4c525e0c98b948d5c0494d684963c1330f9bdb97d4e75933f90952","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Invertibility via distance of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $M$ be any random matrix. Let $R_1, \ldots, R_n$ denote the row vectors of $M$, and let $H_k$ denote the span of all row vectors except the $k$-th. Then for every $\delta, \rho \in(0,1)$ and every $\varepsilon \geq 0$, one has
\begin{align*}
\textbf{P}\left(\inf _{x \in \operatorname{Incomp}(\delta, \rho)}\left\|x^{\top}M\right\|_2 \leq \varepsilon \frac{\rho}{\sqrt{n}}\right) \leq \frac{1}{\delta n} \sum_{k=1}^n \textbf{P}\left(\operatorname{dist}\left(R_k, H_k\right) \leq \varepsilon\right) .
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.165871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5be8249531d11c8f486217fd1241ea94de237d3b327e860fa7c39f73232eb56","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2607.02777, 'Hypocoercivity for Hamiltonian Diffusions \\ with Singular Drift'] Let $f\in\ccinfty(\Omega_1)$ and $\varepsilon>0$, then
