{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.578380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5eb16fedfac231f10dd05f144f9676cddb4f0b718f65901d54c503e8ccb22da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: lemma 12 of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] Fix $\eta>0$, let $k_n=o(\log n/\log \log n)$ be positive integers. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for all $0<j_1<j_2<\dots<j_{k_n}<N/2$ and all sufficiently large $n$, we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
    &&\mathbb{P}\left\{|d_{j_1}|>\beta_1\sqrt{\log n},\dots,|d_{j_{k_n}}|>\beta_{k_n}\sqrt{\log n}\right.
    \\
    &&\quad \left.\text{ for some }\beta_1,\dots,\beta_{k_n}>0 \text{ s.t. } \beta_1^2+\dots+\beta_{k_n}^2\geq 1+\eta\right\}\leq Cn^{-1-\eta/3}.
\end{eqnarray*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.379306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5eb74fe66b248fdb9fc6353263533064b315cd0489cf45a8072b9918314d869","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 19 (Safe subdivision) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\phi: K \rightarrow M$ be a purely $d$-dimensional $C^2$ triangulation of a compact set $M \subset \RR^D$. Let $\eta: K \rightarrow L$ be a subdivision of simplicial complexes and let $\psi = \phi \circ \eta^{-1} : L \rightarrow M$ be an induced triangulation. Assume that $\Theta_{\phi} > 0$, and denote $c_\phi = 2/\sin(\Theta_\phi/4)$. Then there exists $r_0 > 0$ such that the following holds for all $r \in [0, r_0]$:
    \begin{align*}
        \bigcup_{\substack{\tau_i \neq \tau_j \in L \\ \dim \tau_i = \dim \tau_j = d}}\ball(\tilde\tau_i, r) \cap \tilde \tau_j \subseteq \ball(\partial_{\psi} M, c_{\phi} r)
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.741922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ec3a03bb01475a9197377a1fd886cd2398005a5bebb0a0370ce8374fbead58","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lower_bound_tail_vertex_degrees of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$, recall $\theta$ from~(equation eq:theta of the paper), and suppose the choice sequence $\mathbf x$ satisfies Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper) and $A_i\geq m+1$ for $i\in\{I,\ldots,n\}$ with $I\in[n]$. For any $d_{a_1},\ldots,d_{a_k},d_{f_1},\ldots,d_{f_\ell} \in [n-1]$,
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
&\P{\deg_n(a_v)\geq d_{a_v}\text{ for all }v\in[k],\, \deg_n(f_w)\geq d_{f_w}\text{ for all }w\in[\ell]} \\
&\geq \theta^{-\sum_{v=1}^k d_{a_v}-\sum_{w=1}^\ell d_{f_w}}\mathbb P(|\mathcal{S}_n(v)\cap [I,n]|\geq d_{v}\text{ for all }v\in\{a_1,\ldots, a_k,f_1,\ldots, f_\ell\},\tau_{k,\ell}<I).
\end{aligned}\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.060071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ed2aec5e936c75d1b9b00aa94009821acb32458f06e6776d7d0e132c2aa8da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:simplified-left-kernel of arXiv:2606.19507, 'The $t$-Split Two-Periodic Aztec Diamond Model'] For $m,\,m' < tN$, the correlation kernel of the $t$-split model can be written as
    \begin{multline} 
        \left[\mathbb{K}_N(4m',2\xi'+j;4m,2\xi+i)\right]_{i,j=0,1} = \frac{\1_{m\leq m'}}{2\pi \mathrm{i}} \oint_{\gamma_{0,1}}\frac{\mathrm{d}z}{z} z^{\xi'-\xi}\Phi_{\alpha}(z)^{m-m'} \\
        -\frac{1}{(2\pi\mathrm{i})^2}\oint_{\gamma_1}\mathrm{d}w\oint_{\gamma_{0,1}} \frac{\mathrm{d}z}{z(z-w)}\frac{w^{\xi'+N}(z-1)^N}{z^{\xi+N}(w-1)^N}r_{\alpha,2}(w)^{tN-m'}r_{\beta,2}(w)^{(1/2-t)N} \\
        \times c(w) F_{\alpha,2}(w) F_{\beta,2}(w) \Phi_{\beta}(z)^{(t-1/2)N} \Phi_{\alpha}(z)^{m-tN}.
    \end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.219060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5edc3dd58b9f7bc4090fd4d4aa3ea8e93cc29a5fb3a353a3469305d5bda91b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:asymptotic-at-1 of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Let $\sigma_n$ be the top eigenvalue of $H$, and let
    $\nu_n\in\RR^{nL}$ be a corresponding unit eigenvector.
    Split $\nu_n$ into $L$ segments written as $\nu_n^{(1)},\ldots,\nu_n^{(L)}\in\RR^n$. Recall the sign flipping $s(\nu_n)$ in~(equation eq:sign breaking of the paper) and denote
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        w &:= \sqrt{\lambda} \odot \rbr{\mathbf{1}_L -\diag\sbr{M(1)}} \in \RR^L, \\
        c^{\ast} &:= \sum_{l=1}^L \lambda_lM_{ll}(1)\sbr{1-M_{ll}(1)}>0, \\
        \Sigma_1 &:= \frac{1}{\sqrt{c^{\ast}}} \cbr{ V^{-1} \sbr{B - M(1)} } \in \RR^{L \times L}, \\
        \Sigma_2 &:= \frac{1}{c^{\ast}}\cbr{ I - V^{-1} M(1) V^{-1}} \in\mathsf{Sym}_L^+(\RR).
    \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, $c^\ast=w^\top\cQ'(1)w$.
    Then $\abr{\sigma_n-1} = \cO_{\prec}(n^{-1/10})$, and
    \begin{align}
        \nbr{ \frac{s(\nu_n)}{\sqrt{n}} \matop(\nu_n)^\top X - \Sigma_1 } = \cO_{\prec}(n^{-1/10}), \\
        \nbr{ \matop(\nu_n)^\top \matop(\nu_n) - \Sigma_2 } = \cO_{\prec}(n^{-1/20}). 
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.834724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5eecca74016bdfc8ccabc5aedef2b0e66f015608db33d334dc7f01bca0483a6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.13359, 'Fractional moments of the Stochastic Heat Flow and\\2D Directed Polymers'] Let \(Z\geq0\) satisfy \(\EE[Z]=1\).
