{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.438515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ef3a669d9934ab44fe0aacd4831f4a028156789e11d6eef643553f58970b29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Patching of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$ and $\sigma \geq 1$. Fix any collection $\{x_i\}_{i \in I} \subseteq X$ such that $d(x_i,x_j) \geq \varepsilon$ for all distinct $i,j \in I$, and let
    \[
        G := \bigcup_{i \in I} B(x_i,\sigma \varepsilon).
    \]
    Then $I$ is at most countably infinite and there is a constant $C \geq 1$ depending only on $N$ in (equation eq:MD of the paper) and $\sigma$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \sum_{i \in I} \mathds{1}_{B(x_i,\sigma 2^{-m})} \leq C \mathds{1}_G.
    \end{equation*}
    Here $\mathds{1}_A$ denotes the characteristic function of a Borel set $A \subseteq X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.224090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5f9f91a2a326039b8e86aa6d84ff09da2eeb60064bed41a94407829e0771deb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (KKS average of the Euler-Arnold derivative vanishes) of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] For any $z$ in the interior of $\mathcal{A}_{\text{regular}}$ and any smooth observable $Q: \su(N)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, we have
