{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.047339+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6220b059ea1318bffb382124e7b5c65b46939b49dcbf0449879141969fa91c2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition split_sum of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] There exists a function $r(g,\mu)$ such that for every $g\geq 2$, $\mu\in[0,\mu_c)$ and $p_1,\cdots,p_k \ge 1$ such that $|\mathbf{p}| \le 3g-3$, we have
