{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.591288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f646b94d1587917f830c9ded0ecf9321231b64690a2f65a0a1bbbb59714fa562","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm stochconv-(sub)crit of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] Let $t\delta_t^d \rightarrow 0$ and $(k,\alpha_1), (k,\alpha_2)$ be an admissible sequence with $4\alpha_i >-d+k-1$ for $i\in \{1,2\}$. Then 
\begin{equation*}
\tilde{ \mathcal{V}}_k^{(\alpha_2)} = \frac{\mu_k^{(\alpha_1+\alpha_2)}}{\mu_k^{(2\alpha_1)}}\tilde{ \mathcal{V}}_k^{(\alpha_1)}
+ \frac{\sqrt{\mu_k^{(2\alpha_1)}\mu_k^{(2\alpha_2)}-(\mu_k^{(\alpha_1+\alpha_2)})^2}}{\sqrt{(k+1)!\mu_k^{(2\alpha_1)}}} Z 
+ D_t^{(\alpha_1, \alpha_2)} 
\end{equation*}
as $t \to \infty$, with $Z\sim \mathcal N(0,1)$ independent of $\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_k^{(\alpha_1)}$ and 
$D_t^{(\alpha_1, \alpha_2)}$ satisfies ((eq:order-Dt of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.826078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f647701731debf201e3d731dc96739d4dc4c2946fa9577406e5f930b198ce31c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_cluster_healing of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] Consider a zero-range process on $\mathbb{Z}$ starting from an initial configuration $\eta_0$ with $k \le m$ particles. Assume all particles are infected at time 0. Then there exists a constant $c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:single_cluster of the paper)}}>0$, depending only on $m$, $\Gamma_\pm$, and the healing rate $\delta > 0$, such that, for all $T \geq 1$,
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}^{\eta_0}\big( \text{infection survives up to time $T$} \big) \le e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:single_cluster of the paper)}} T}.
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.702949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6493c447111232a02c73af46ce6f3be491ed6c05cc7a22a5dece9c14a00caa0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2609.00973, 'The Vlasov-Maxwell point charge system : study of the spherically symmetric case'] The map $(\Theta,\mathcal{A}):\R^*_+\times\R\rightarrow\R\times\R^*_+$ defines a $C^1$ diffeomorphism with inverse $(R,U)$. Moreover, it preserves the volume form, i.e.
