{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6548acc27fcd466ae7571406470574a090239b10a3d4b2748a609658a974f25","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Coupling of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Let $(\mathcal{X},\mu)$ and $(\mathcal{Y},\nu)$ be two probability spaces. A coupling of $(\mu,\nu)$ is a pair of random variables $(X,Y)$ living in a common probability space $(\mathcal{X}\times \mathcal{Y}, \mathbb{P})$, such that $\mathrm{Law}(X)=\mu$ and $\mathrm{Law}(Y)=\nu$. The collection of all the couplings is then denoted by
		\begin{align*}
			\varPi (\mu,\nu):=\{\operatorname{Law}(X,Y):\operatorname{Law}(X)=\mu, \operatorname{Law}(Y)=\nu\}.
		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.490311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f65585ee3c84bad0988b4cc2326e51f0124d0a88fd9155d4534a4146e360bf9f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 220 (Functions of the second kind, type II and III) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] For each $g \in [H]$, let $\gamma(\alpha_g)$ (respectively $\gamma(\beta_g)$) be a small positively oriented circular loop around $\alpha_g$ (respectively $\beta_g$). If $f_g(z)$ is a meromorphic function in a complex neighborhood $\amsmathbb{M}_g$ of $[\alpha_g,\beta_g]$ with possible poles only at $\alpha_g,\beta_g$, then we define for any $h \in [H]$
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\mathfrak{F}_h^{\textnormal{II}}[\boldsymbol{f}](z) & = \sum_{g = 1}^H \left[\oint_{\gamma(\alpha_g)} + \oint_{\gamma(\beta_g)}\right] \frac{\dd \zeta}{2\ii\pi}\left(\frac{\delta_{g,h}}{2(z - \zeta)^2} + \big \langle \bth_g \cdot \mathcal{F}_{h,\bullet}(z,\zeta)\big \rangle\right) \sigma_g(\zeta) f_g(\zeta), \\
\mathfrak{F}_h^{\textnormal{III}}[\boldsymbol{f}](z) & = \sum_{g = 1}^H \left[\oint_{\gamma(\alpha_g)} + \oint_{\gamma(\beta_g)}\right] \frac{\dd\zeta}{2\ii\pi} \left(\frac{1}{2(z - \zeta)^2} + \sum_{g' \neq g} \theta_{g,g'} \mathcal{F}_{h,g'}(z,\zeta) \right)\frac{f_g(\zeta)}{\theta_{g,g}},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where $z$ is outside the contours of integration.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.056021+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f655a59c8c92304a495debccb743e46dff7a5e4cfeb3b731bc26c65167345776","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma E_sup_sum_W of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let the metric $d^{(2)}_{N,j}$ be defined via (equation eq:d_Nj of the paper). Then
