{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.798666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f65630878a875fcf80f7f3e4c86fb0aed20846cc7dfd1f01e0ddb5e819c2df59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 60 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$ be compactly supported and such that

\begin{align}

1 + \frac{2}{\ell} \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln|x-y| \, \mathrm{d}\mu(y) \geq \kappa > 0 \qquad \dd \mu(x)\;\;  \e{a.e.} \; x \in \mathbb{R} \;.

