{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.800020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6565af1d05c3aa78b37e80943f58a08b3f8c6766840d7f58a8da8b2589b0868","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:n-pt-gf of arXiv:2510.05850, 'Three-point connectivity constant for $q$-state Potts spin clusters'] For any $n\in\mathbb{N}$, the $n$-point Green's function $G_n^\mathrm{Potts}(z_1,\ldots,z_n)$ for the event that $z_1,\ldots,z_n$ are all in the same red cluster is given by
