{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.701798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f66a3fb9b83d84b14c24dfb195f49b25f07ddc03258b0eacfa085fb401c16817","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP:con of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Let $D>0$. Then, we have the free energy limit
\begin{align*}
\lim_{L\to\infty } \frac{\log Z_L}{L^3}=-\inf_{\substack{ \|\phi \|_{L^2(\mathbb{R})}^2 \le D  } } H(\phi),
