{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.279037+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f690ffa0fc51595673ca74c14e9d3996561b8e6e371d7c49f4e8f4e47a5a6b9f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] An $\mathcal{F}_t$ progressively measurable process $\mathcal{Y}^{\epsilon}: \R \times \Omega \rightarrow H$ is said to be a stationary solution for the crude cocycle $(U^{\epsilon}, \theta)$ if for any fixed $s \in \R$, $\P$-a.s.
