{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.035138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6a82adda6b31ed724ccfc615f8be103d38e1df22949f1c167539b3309a9d50e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6t2.1 of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] {wom}}}]
	If $ f(z)= \prod_{\delta \mid N} \eta(\delta z)^{r_\delta}$ is an eta-quotient with
	$k= \frac{1}{2} \sum_{\delta \mid N}{r_\delta} \in \mathbb{Z}$, and satisfies the following additional properties:
	\begin{align}
		\sum_{\delta\mid N} \delta {r_\delta} \equiv 0 \pmod {24},
	\end{align}
	\begin{align}
		\sum_{\delta \mid N} \frac{N}{\delta}  {r_\delta} \equiv 0 \pmod {24},
	\end{align}
	then $f(z)$ satisfies 
