{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.768243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6d8348643f29db5ed32868008be30e3be0b2adea3290ad5a66c5e5a833af875","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2411.02898, '\vspace{-1.5cm}The connectivity and phase transition in inhomogeneous random graphs of fin'] Consider $\ensuremath{\mathbb{G}} := \ensuremath{\mathbb{G}}_{n,c/n}$ where $c>0$ is a constant.
