{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.224833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6f3a6459a3d77caeadcc14ed48b3cb3fe6e154d36c04c4c3975ac08c3223090","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 65 of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] Let $\alpha<1-\frac{1}{2\log 2}$ be fixed. The following hold with high probability:
