{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.420563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6f60127a1ee32e2cbe339ac8d3671c5cd0620e6651e3f75c0042fe542dc571a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:rev-mean-var of arXiv:2605.17513, 'Nonconcentration of hitting times for random walks on graphs'] Let \(P\) be a finite irreducible reversible Markov chain with state space $\Omega$, and let $x$, $y \in \Omega$. Then,
