{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.240381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6fd8e747144a42a173db44dd8a9ed0c9f29563cc05bd2fb0d7642b2dd82a0ef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 of arXiv:2512.10761, 'Special times for the point set process of the Brownian Net'] For any interval $I\in\mathcal{C}$, we associate a Bernoulli random variable $Z(I)$ to $I$, and let $A(k)=\cup_{I\in \mathcal{C}_k,Z(I)=1}I$. We define $A$ to be the limsup fractal associated with the family $\{Z(I):I\in\mathcal{C}\}$ by
