{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.668418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f71d2d00ddf06097742e8d9d19690686cf168d9aa91471767370b0da876479b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_lower_bound of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] For all $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(\overline{\mathbb{Z}})$, 
