holds for all~$n\ge1$, all $t>0$ and all $u\in(0,n]$.  Here $s\vee t:=\max\{s,t\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.088655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f729368494751f8c4bf0f6be90cf99497c845747832351284286aa66b3a8ec75","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2609.03821, 'Condensation and Metastability in the Supercritical Two-Species Zero-Range Process via Res'] The following statements hold for any $\ell_{N}$
that satisfies \eqref{eq:ellN-def}.
