{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.025318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f72b6ed48554b61c162c39eecaa2e2454ffb73c2eefaf207e55cef0197c71eee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] Let $\xi\in \C_{\theta}$, $\alpha\in\mathcal A$, and $K\in\K$.
We define:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{array}{ccc}
\displaystyle 
\displaystyle \underline{J}(K,\alpha)\coloneqq \liminf_{\rho\downarrow 0} J^{K_\rho}(\xi,\alpha)  & \text{and}
& \displaystyle \overline{J}(K,\alpha)\coloneqq \limsup_{\rho\downarrow 0} J^{K_\rho}(\xi,\alpha) \, , 
