\]
Finally, if $(Y,Z,\Lambda)$ is a solution of the ergodic backward SDE, we define $\hat{\mathcal{A}}$ as the subset of $\mathcal{A}$ such that for all $\alpha \in \hat{\mathcal{A}}$, there exists $\xi \in \C_{\theta}$ and a nonnegative function $\varepsilon\in L^1_{loc}(\R_+)$ satisfying:
\begin{equation*}
    \begin{array}{ccc}
         \displaystyle f (t, \mathcal{X}^{\xi}_t , \, \alpha_t \big) + \alpha_t \cdot Z^{\xi}_t - H (t, \X^\xi_t , Z^{\xi}_t ) \leq \varepsilon(t) \,, \; d\mathbb{P} \otimes dt-\text{a.e.} & \text{and} & \displaystyle \frac1T\int_0^T\varepsilon(t)dt
