{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.389233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f77e0e5773238906bfbe0654b6f74b55acd28f61cf31616c37f2988fec30b738","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 76 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] For integers $b,c\ge 0$, we have 
\ali{
\lim_{\epsilon\to 0}\int_{|z|=\epsilon} z^a \bar z^b |z|^c \frac{dz}{z} 
&=\lim_{\epsilon\to 0} r^{a+b+c} \int_0^{2\pi} e^{(a-b)i\theta} id\theta
=2\pi i \delta_{a,0}\delta_{b,0}\delta_{c,0}, \\
\lim_{\epsilon\to 0}\int_{|z|=\epsilon} z^a \bar z^b |z|^c \frac{d\bar z}{\bar z} 
