{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.899984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f78e5c0a0fe1c1229d81e069000121f47c64b99061243272d4d4f1eb7be12335","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition qgamma of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] For $0<q<1$ and $z\in\mathbb{C}\setminus\{0,-1,-2,\ldots\}$, the $q$-Gamma function is
