{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.122697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7b9b35630562fd7d305970f4622efda14c2402faa8e12e54310eabb95280712","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition equivalent_characterisations of arXiv:2608.13716, 'Graph Causal Optimal Transport \\ and Wasserstein Distances'] Suppose $G$ is a sorted DAG, $\mu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{X}}$, $\nu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{Y}}$, and $\pi \in \couplings{\mu}{\nu}$. Then $\mu \otimes \nu \in \Gbicouplings{\mu}{\nu} \subseteq \Gcouplings{\mu}{\nu}$.
    Moreover, the following are equivalent:

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[1)] $\pi \in \Gbicouplings{\mu}{\nu}$;
        \item[2)] When $(X,Y) \sim \pi$ the following conditional independence relations hold for $2 \leq i \leq n$:
        $$\condindep{(X_i, Y_i)}{X_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}, Y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}{(X_{1:i-1}, Y_{1:i-1})}, \quad \condindep{X_i}{X_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}{Y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}, \quad \condindep{Y_i}{Y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}{X_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}};$$

        \item[3)] $\pi$ may be disintegrated as $\pi(dx, dy) = \bigotimes_{i=1}^n \pi_{i}\brackets{dx_i, dy_i \mid x_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}, y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}},$
        with $$\pi_{i}\brackets{dx_i, dy_i \mid x_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}, y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}} \in \couplings{\mu_{i}\brackets{dx_i \mid  x_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}}{\nu_{i}\brackets{dy_i \mid  y_{\mathrm{pa}_{i}}}}$$ $\pi$-a.s. for all $1 \leq i \leq n$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7bbb05a0cd93f1b380ab19bf2ab261078c6a3b9897834150dbb71b78f5ae12a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ftpbds of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Let $T_n\sim\mathrm{UA}(n)$ and fix constants  $0<s<\beta\leq 1$. Then for all $k=0,1,\ldots, n$, we have
