{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.083833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7c5a19fb95797ccd6ff7619b19e434f617d71d20d6c69cf97e49e40fddf2aee","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:limitT1 of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For any $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3$ ($x\not=0$), we have $T_1^{\varepsilon,x}\Rightarrow \sigma^x$ as $\varepsilon\to 0$, where $\sigma^x$ is a $(0,\infty)$-valued random variable whose law has the density \begin{align*}
