{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.562021+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7c9005fcbb8ac4e051c39684797d8b0b991f7623eb51e414a51d90995c7631c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2603.29571, 'Randomstrasse101: Open Problems of 2025'] Given a degree $d$ pseudo-expectation $\tilde{\mathbb{E}}$, its associated moment matrix $\Lambda$ has rows and columns indexed by monomials $p$ and $q$ of degree at most $d/2$, and its entries are given by
