{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.887807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f82da418fe4a308a0b2153bd2974da880f0d3f21637a267f52e6fec3dddb841a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.29554, 'Limiting Behavior of a Class of Hermitian Yang--Mills Metrics, II: Exponential Approximati'] For any nonnegative integer $k$, there exist constants $C_k,c_k>0$, independent of $\epsilon$, such that for all sufficiently small $\epsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
