{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.347163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8508c8dc0023b03d7b6e649224d4f94aebb5abb53a22e3067a8a0aa76834587","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] There exists $R'_e>0$, depending on the potential $V$ and the constants $M$, $L_\sigma$, and $C_{\sigma}$, such that for any full solution $u$ of \eqref{main-eq} bounded in $H^{1}(\R^{N})$, the following estimate holds
