{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.790947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f858421097d1213d344db0d9c2551a287529d35af3348875b5e872014696bbb2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_variance_estimates_v1 of arXiv:2412.04328, 'The critical Karp--Sipser core of Erdős--Rényi random graphs'] Let $C>0$. If $V_k Z_k \geqslant \log^3 n$ and $Z_k\leqslant C$ and $X_k>0$, then we have
