{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.675636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f86cb577bdae3379196aeefe3cd86f99fcb97f337b4c859a674a04510dbb9824","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma1 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] For all $k\in \{2,...,\lfloor \beta \rfloor +1\}$, $t\in [0,1)$ and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, we have
    \begin{align*}
    \|\nabla^{k} V(t,x)\|\leq &  C \sum_{l=1}^{k-1} \Biggl( \|\int f^{l}(y)\nabla^2_x p^{t,x}(y)d\lambda^d(y)\| \prod_{j=1}^{k-2}\left(\|\int f^{j}(y) dp^{t,x}(y)\|\vee 1\right)^{k-2}\\
    &+ \|\int f^{l}(y) \nabla_x p^{t,x}(y)d\lambda^d(y)\|\sum_{j=1}^{k-2}\|\int f^{j}(y) \nabla_x p^{t,x}(y)d\lambda^d(y)\|\prod_{i=1}^{k-3}\left(\|\int f^{i}(y)  dp^{t,x}(y)\|\vee 1\right)^{k-3}\Biggl).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f86cddbe15188bafc4041801dce73f48a3909b89c9b96b7e875520b587736b4d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a finite graph with at least one cycle and distinct edge weights $\{\exp(-\beta \omega_e)\}_{e\in E}$. Then the quantity 
