{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.241152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f86dfd97fce61817de7e994ca2a3c1e266553b3b76caa0c7cc9fb07c53450055","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lipG of arXiv:2607.00753, 'Threatening excursions in large population\\ quasi-stationary birth and death systems.\\ O'] Let $A$ and $G$ be open subsets of $\mathds R_{+}^{d}$ satisfying  Assumption {\bf (HS)}  and such that $A \Subset G$.   Then there exists a positive constant $K(A,G)$ such that for any $K\ge K(A,G)$,

(i) there exists a positive constant $ C(A,G)$ with
\begin{align*}
\sup_{{\underline n ;\,  d(\frac{\underline n}{K},A)\le  {1\over 2}  d(\partial A, \partial G)} }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{\underline n} \big(T^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{G}\le 1 \big) &\le e^{-C(A,G)\,K}\,; \\
\sup_{\underline n \in K*A }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{\underline n}\big( {\underline N^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}}(1)\in K*A^{c}\big)& \le e^{-C(A,G)\,K} \,;
\end{align*}
(ii) there exist positive constants  $C_{1}(A,G),   C_{2}(A,G),  \zeta(A,G)$ such that  for any $0<\zeta\le \zeta(A,G)$,
$$
\sup_{\underline z;\, d(\underline z,A)\le {1\over 2}d(\partial A, \partial G) }{{\mathds P}}^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}_{[\underline z K]} \Big(\sup_{0\le t \le 1} \left\| \frac{{\underline N^{({\scriptscriptstyle K})}}(t)}{K}-\varphi_{t}(\underline z)\right\| >\zeta\Big) \le C_{1}(A,G)\,e^{-C_{2}(A,G) \,K\,\zeta}.
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.063077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8734ab24bb42bf91ed6cf7ce0fd1f61b940aa43f2e8cf3f0af94b3b0a0136ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma BoltzB of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Suppose that (equation VL4 of the paper)--(equation VL5' of the paper) are in force. Moreover, suppose that Assumption~(ass:Boltz of the paper) holds and, for the even integer $p$ therein, set 
		$
		\kappa_{p}=2^{{p}-3}(p-1)(2Q_2+2^{p-1}Q_{p}).
		$	
		Let $X$ be $\mathcal{F}_s$-measurable with $\mathcal{L}(X)=\mu\in\mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R}^d)$. Then for $t-s\leq 1$ and even integer $p$ one has
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{array}{rl}
				{\mathbb E}[ |\mathcal{X}_{s,t}(X,\mu)|^p]
				\leq &
				\displaystyle \Big(1-p\Big(\bar b_{p,\delta}-C(t-s)\Big)(t-s)\Big)\|\mu\|_p^p\\
				&+C(1+\|\mu\|_{p-2}^{p})(t-s),
			\end{array}
		\end{equation}

		where,  for $\delta>0$,  $ 
		\bar b_{p,\delta}:=	\bar{b}-\delta-\kappa_{p}$, 
		$C$ is a positive constant depending only on $p,b,\delta$ and $\|\mu\|_0:=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.992583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8753164bd6fd908e40a83ba4653dcf6e1d593daceb265cb88c3e3344f4c04b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 119 (Lemma \ref{L:TVgap}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Assume $\omega$ is such that $\cC_1(p_0) \subseteq \cC_1(p_1)$. Denote by $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ the laws of $\ClCp{1}{p_0}$ and $\cT_{p_1 \mid p_0}$, respectively. Then
    \begin{equation} 
        \Vert \nu_1 - \nu_2\Vert_{\mathrm{TV}} \leq n^4 e^{-\beta(p_1 - p_0)}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.942641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f876b27efef40f960a1f69ab9f690f5abae4548390222417b884ac0fd64ed4ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm strong inequality of arXiv:2412.02913, 'On the boundedness of Gross' solution when the underlying distribution is bounded'] [butzer1971hilbert] If $f$ is in $L_{2\pi}^{p}$, then $H\{f\}$
