{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.469939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f890ad573cd485125de759fb150757f0f02d062f3101289c7d798ccb4550264b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 26 (Real isonormal Gaussian process) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $\cH$ be a real Hilbert space.  A \emph{real isonormal Gaussian process}
over $\cH$ is a real-linear map
\[
  W:\cH\longrightarrow L^2(\Omega;\R)
\]
such that $W(h)$ is centered Gaussian for every $h\in\cH$ and
\begin{equation*}
  \E[W(h)W(k)]=\ip{h}{k}_{\cH},
  \qquad h,k\in\cH.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.859970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f891c9ba9c64b9e3091e6474f10e71337a87b70b9b4e912173ec2cc159a4ceef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.02423, '2609.02423'] Let $H$ be a Hilbert space.  If $f:\R\to H$ has Fourier support in $|\xi|\le C\lambda$, then
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{x_0\in\R}\norm{f(x_0)}_H^2
 \lesssim_R
 \lambda\sup_{x_0\in\R}
 \int_\R a'\left(\frac{\lambda(x-x_0)}R\right)
 \norm{f(x)}_H^2\dd x.
\end{equation}
The analogous statement holds in the $y$ variable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.114241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f891ca5e7721f79eaeb2edcd868330e884cf9800000b1f780b70bf12f80b5e6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem LM24 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Let $x\in E$ and $B\in \mathscr{B}^n(E)$. Then the following statements hold:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(1)] If $B$ is finely open (in particular, if $B$ is open), then $d(x,B)=\widetilde{d}(x,B)$. 
    \item[(2)] If $B\subset \overline{\mathrm{int}^f(B)}$, then $d(x,B)=\widetilde{d}(x,B)$. In particular, if $B$ is the closure of an open subset of $E$, then $d(x,B)=\widetilde{d}(x,B)$. 
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.622936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8937b5e61b9de5c6b70450c9dcf6d09f66d1d7c42bbde141d7cea19e763fd77","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2608.16256, 'Error Distribution of the Local Linearization Method for Stochastic Differential Equations'] \label[proposition]{prop:ll_R123_ucp_zero}
