{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.768416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8b0136d1f6676e908b35a4bc07cd873abbf3e7c019f2117346665af3a476ca9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thm:norm-lemma of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta \in\mathds{R}$, $p\in (0,\infty)$, and $q\in (0,\infty]$.
Let further $(\xi_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in\mathds{N}_0\times\left\{F,M\right\}^d\times\mathds{Z}^d}$ by a family of of random variables.
Set $a=(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}$ where
\begin{equation*}
a_{j,t,m}\mathrel{\mathop:}= 2^{j\alpha} \lr{1+\frac{\left\lVertm\right\rVert_\infty}{2^j}}^{\beta + (\gamma-\beta)\mathds{1}_{j=0}}\lambda_{j,t,m}\xi_{j,t,m}
\end{equation*}
for $(j,t,m)\in J$.
If Property A is satisfied, then for $\Xi$ as in 
  \hyperref[{eq:master-quantity}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:master-quantity}}}}
, we have $\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}\lesssim\Xi^{\frac{1}{p}}$, where the implied constant only depends on $d$, $p$, $q$, and $\beta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.190946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8b043868285235ad8eb5dd6cec533636e2259f899f9c54f6b9ade2989bb7df5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:0_1_law of arXiv:2608.06263, 'Almost sure path localisation for the derivative martingale of branching Brownian motion'] Almost surely, the limiting mass satisfies
