\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.471740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8b27663da55f5ef615a8f25e1bbb9dd8b1f3da93214ad374a2b0a882c8e13eb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: asymptotic uncorrelated of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] For any $k \in \{1,2\}$, any $\omega \in \{0,1,\ldots,m_k\}$ and any $d \in \{m_k,m_k+1,\ldots\}$,
as $n \to \infty$, the sequence of random variables 
\begin{equation}
\left(\mathbb{P}(d_{\phi_n}=d,d_{\phi_n}^{+,\mathrm{mino},(n)}=\omega,X_{\phi_n}=k \mid G_n)\right)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}     
