{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.627190+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8c101fd87f83dbff984beb06bee123b3293677c72aca305666d05a82c231d39","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:P_t-bounded of arXiv:2511.22162, 'Landau Hamiltonian with Gaussian white noise potential and the asymptotics of its bottom o'] For $\bA \in \ccA$ and $q = (h, \zeta) \in \ccM$, $(P_t^B(\bA, q))_{t \ge 0}$ defines a strongly continuous semigroup satisfying the bound
	\begin{equ}
		\left\| P_t \right\|_{\cL(L^2(B))} \leq M_h^B e^{\omega^B(\bA, q) t},
	\end{equ}
	for all $t \ge 0$, where $M_h^B$ is given by (equation eq:C-and-M of the paper) and $\omega^B(\bA, q)$ is some positive constant bounded by
