{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.999366+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e80a1f4d8ad69e1c5b875405b328a844bbbe3b1c371cf3ed8e585521b5838f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma vanishing of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] Let \(N\sim\varepsilon^{-\frac1\nu+\mu_1}\) be defined by (equation eq:N of the paper), and let \(\delta\) be as in (cor:polynomial_decay of the paper). Then, for every \(\omega\notin\Omega_\delta\),
