{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e901258be90e6112facb17adaeb69188e62fb223eeefb0ba5ed0327bdcc80c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:8.3 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let ${\rm A} \subseteq{\rm D}_n^\circ$ be an $(r_n,n-r_n)$-clustered set and ${\mathbf A}$ a minimal $r_n$-cover of it in the sense of~(equation e:2.10t of the paper) such that $|{\mathbf A}|\leq n^{1/2+\eta_0/4}$, where $\eta_0$ is as in~(equation e:2.3 of the paper). Then, as $n \to \infty$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}_\partial \Big(\tau_{\partial {\rm B}(x;r_n)} < \overline{\tau}_\partial \wedge \min_{y \in {\mathbf A} \setminus \{x\}}
		\tau_{\partial {\rm B}(y;r_n)} \Big)
		= \frac{2\pi}{\deg(\partial) n}\Big(1+o(n^{-\eta/4})\Big) \,,
	\end{equation}
	uniformly over all such sets ${\rm A}$ and $x \in {\mathbf A}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.434560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e9ab0db4a64cce5f24dfd8b2ae62bff513a24e2789652ee558d09d465fab25","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj: WithoutSymmetry of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] Let $\bM$ be uniformly distributed on $\{0,1 \}^{n\times n}$ and consider an independent uniform random vector $\zeta\in \{0,1 \}^{n\times n}$. 
    Then, $\bW = [\zeta, \bM \zeta, \ldots, \bM^{n-1}\zeta]$ satisfies that for every prime $p$,
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{n\to \infty} \bbP\Bigl(p^2 \nmid \det(\bW) \Bigr) &= \Bigl(1 + \frac{1}{p} \Bigr) \prod_{i=1}^\infty \Bigl(1 -  \frac{1}{p^{i}}\Bigr)
    \end{align} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.693788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8f1db2e63490e7d916491232dca03fc420cf68f97b40935eed232c930d26ced","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thr_old thrMainCorrelations_corr of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] For $N\geq 0$ let $\big\{\obs{\phi}{s_{j}}{t_j}\big\}_{j=1}^{N}$ be a set of non-interlaced observables, and $\{l_j\}_{j=1}^N$ be a set of positive integers. 
Let also $\{k_m\}_{m=1}^{N+1}$ and $\{\tau_m\}_{m=1}^{N+1}$ be as above.
Then 
\begin{multline}
\int\limits_{{\mathrm{Diff}^1(\mathbb{T})/\mathrm{PSL}(2, \mathbb{R})}} \prod_{j=1}^N \obs{\phi}{s_j}{t_j}^{l_j}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathscr{M}_{\sigma^2}(\phi)
=
\int_{\mathbb{R}_+^{N+1}} 
\prod_{j=1}^N \frac{\Gamma\left(\dfrac{l_j}{2}\pm i w_1(j) \pm i w_2(j)\right)}{2\pi^2 \, \Gamma(l_j)}
\cdot\left(\frac{\sigma^2}{2}\right)^{l_j}\\
\times
\prod_{m=1}^{N+1}\exp\left(-\frac{\tau_m \sigma^2}{2}\cdot k_m^2\right)  \sinh(2\pi k_m) \, 2 k_m \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} k_m,
\end{multline}
where the integral on the right-hand side converges absolutely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.171706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8f3f3de2374efc7e3ce8103563479022c47d5fc6ef707d9bb7d8648b7bce6ff","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_TransversalityOfTheObstructionMap_Eigen of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] In the situation of (Prop_ThickenedSpaceOfZ2ZEigenSpinors_Submanifold+Submersion of the paper)
