R\left(\sum_{i=1}^{m}\delta_{X_i},\sum_{j=\ell+1}^{n}\delta_{X_j}\right)=\frac{m-\ell}{\sqrt{m(n-\ell)}},
\end{equation}
where $\delta_{x}$ is the Dirac measure at $x$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.832253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8fc9e24157b9ca0636284b39ac44dbacc9a82022802b7ed1b8a83719fe382e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 3 of arXiv:2506.12443, 'Error Rates for Large Deviations in the domain of an $\alpha=1$ stable law'] Assume the set up of Theorem~\ref{t:LD}.
