{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.720494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9309a10cff065d635479e54ba10ea6a84beefb2fcc45389a01e5068b2b7b122","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition energy-inequality of arXiv:2609.02769, 'Divergence-Free Approximation in Sobolev and Lebesgue Spaces on general unbounded domains '] We say that $\boldsymbol{u}$ is a \emph{Leray-Hopf weak solution} of the CBF equations (equation abstract-CBF of the paper), with initial data $\boldsymbol{u}_0\in\mathbb{H}$, if it is a weak solution in the sense of Definition (weakd of the paper) that additionally satisfies the following properties:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item  \emph{strong energy inequality}:
