{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.295690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f944224a1be9c9f00fb0f9b5a92f2e3a151503ee654a3f7d6060992750be8fec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:capbounds of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] For every $\gamma >  \gamma' > 0 $ there exist $c_d > 0$ and $T_0= T_0(d,\gamma, \gamma') > 0$ such that, for all $T \ge T_0$,
