{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.718971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f947553ed344450e8f5f17cd4895c70a2de728f38bdc01884f2da1e451b41dbe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F} = \{ f \in C(\X) : |f(x)| \le 1 + \rho(x_0, x)^p \}$ with any given $x_0 \in \X$ be a family of test functions satisfying Hypothesis $\mathbf{(H_1)}$. Then the following statements are equivalent:
