{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.250433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f962d9522e5b2e33024f19ad40d81db0134200aaca41a481ec755fe7c9ce1f20","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.09532, 'Percolation on the stationary distributions of the voter model with stirring'] $\mathcal T: T_N \to \mathbb{Z}^d$ is a \textit{proper embedding} of $T_N$ if 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\mathcal T(\{ \varnothing \}) = 0$;
        \item for all $0 \leq k \leq N$ and $m \in T_{(k)}$ we have $\mathcal T(m) \in \mathcal L_{N-k}$;
        \item for all $0 \leq k \leq N$ and $m \in T_{(k)}$ we have 
        $$|\mathcal T(m_1)- \mathcal T(m)| =  L_{N-k}, \qquad |\mathcal T(m_2)- \mathcal T(m)| = 2L_{N-k}.$$
    \end{enumerate}
    We denote by $\mathcal P_N$ the set of proper embeddings of $T_N$ into $\mathbb{Z}^d$.","status":"unverified"}

