{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.335056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9887d2a398e62ecb647950b192a37bc641f339f13a03147b3bc4f0632d10deb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cumulant_expansion_formula of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] Let $h$ be a random variable with finite moments. The $k$-th cumulant of $h$, denoted by $c^{(k)}$, is defined as \begin{equation*}
		c^{(k)} := (-\ii)^k \left. \left(\frac{\mathop{}\!{d}^k}{\mathop{}\!{d} t^k} \log \EX[\mathrm{e}^{\ii t h}]\right) \right|_{t=0}.
	\end{equation*}
	Let $f : {\mathbb R} \to {\mathbb C}$ be a smooth function. Then for any fixed $l \in \mathbb{N}$ we have \begin{equation}
		\EX [h f(h)] = \sum_{k=1}^l \frac{1}{k!} c^{(k+1)} \EX [f^{(k)}(h)] + R_{l+1},

	\end{equation} provided that all the expectations in (equation cumulant_expansion_formula of the paper) exist. The error term satisfies \begin{equation}
		\abs{R_{l+1}} \leq C_l \EX [\left\lverth\right\rvert^{l+1}] \sup_{\left\lvertx\right\rvert \leq M} \abs{f^{(l)}(x)} + C_l \EX \left[ \left\lverth\right\rvert^{l+1} \indicator_{\{\left\lverth\right\rvert > M\}} \right] \norm{f^{(l)}}_{\infty},

	\end{equation} where $M > 0$ is an arbitrary fixed cutoff and $C_l$ is a constant depending only on $l$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.492770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f98e0fe5224accce990c5d17a9d5e5c1e75ca349146d8483237ca7f1cebe2b31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $\gamma<2$  and $\mu_\ph$ be as above. Then there exists $C = C(\omega) < \infty$ and $q >0$ nonrandom such that 
