{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.164344+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f98f9a425472096dac7865015769ad38124a774e66c4ba7a83f1dd1c151fc5b1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] For each $\theta\geq0$, we define the $\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R})$-valued operator $P_{\theta}$, defined over the domain $\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R})$ by
