{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.796414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa0716cf66f29c43640e70776fcb900121e2c965ba21e8f1bf64005ac8048fe7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Let $(\vec{x},t,\Psi)$ be sampled from $\mathbb{Q}_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma,N}$. The conditional law of  $(\vec{x},t)$ given $\Psi$ is 
    \begin{equation*}
        \nu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma,N}(d\vec{x}dt):=\frac{\exp\left(\gamma\sum_{i=1}^N\Psi_{\varepsilon}(x_i,t)
        -\frac{\gamma^2}{2}\mathbb E[(\sum_{i=1}^N\Psi_{\varepsilon}(x_i,t))^2]\right)
        }{\mu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma,N}(D^N_T)}d\vec{x}dt.
    \end{equation*}
    And on the other hand, the law of $\Psi$ conditionally on $(\vec{x},t)$, is equal to 
    \begin{equation*}
        \hat{\Psi} + \gamma\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{cov}(\cdot, \Psi_{\varepsilon}(x_i,t)),
