{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.660625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa5e3a67b3c58f20df81a0b3cb87c5008fb0973a60d9b1fa24df62afa50c90bf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2604.23462, 'Invariant measures for the open KPZ equation: the Gaussian case'] Given $T > 0$, there is a finite positive constant $C = C(T,\kappa)$ such that, for all $t \in (0,T]$ and $\bm{x} \in \R^4$, we have that
