Then SFDEwJ \eqref{EQ:0603:01}  has a unique invariant measure $\pi$. Further, $P_t(\xi,\cdot)$, $t\ge \tau$, converges to $\pi$ in the Wasserstein metric $W_{d \wedge 1}$ and the rate of convergence is given by \eqref{EQ:0603:05}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.271802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fac515e18c1503638f77605904e92e32a7a3716015e5bc63e9d3290cd53834ce","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] For $\beta>0$, the $\mathsf{Sine}_\beta$ point process is characterised as
