{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.837567+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fae7d36c1667d19b5c14b4a4e55bf9976beda98fe7b2d77e7e577f0f29645d8f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2609.02169, '2609.02169'] Put \(\Lambda=\NS(A)\), let \(e_1,\dots,e_r\) be an integral basis,
