{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.077079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb00c8a33fba7f21ab163576dcbdeca337a71f7d21cea3859ca556dcf7c02c9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 22 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] Suppose the assumptions in Theorem~\ref{thm} holds. Fix $N\in\NN^+$, \(t_1, \ldots, t_N \in [0,1]\) and \(b_1, \ldots, b_N \in \mathbb{R}\). We have 
        \begin{equation}
            \widetilde{Y}_n:=\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} \sum_{j=1}^N b_j \sum_{u=0}^{[nt_j]-1} \mathcal{T}^{\ge d} \phi\left(X_u\right)
        \end{equation}
    converges to $\mu\sum_{j=1}^N b_j B_{t_j}$ in law, where $\mu$ is given in \eqref{e:sigma} and $(B_t)_{t \in [0,1]}$ is a standard Brownian motion. Then the finite-dimensional distributions of $\mathcal{T}^{\ge d} Y_n$ converge to those of $\mu B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.020531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb053a21e41412fac1f667da4adefa471359f3e2aed05ec32e90eef8cbf53ff1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:MixedSC of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] {bhatia2018strong}}] 
        The barycenter functional $f_1$ is $\mu'$-SC on $\{S \in \mathrm{PD}(d) : S \leq \beta' I\}$, where
