{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.618156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb112ceb8edf92eed512083428997cd639b9f1d634f98e6a4c03ca50cb7c4a4b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 73 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c,C',c'$ such that for all $\delta>0$, all $n$ and for all $m\in [\![0,n]\!]$, we have
