{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.681347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb1fea8086eec6101676c0cf04b65f2b779d0c37931fa983d38059ffaada3186","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 47 (Equivalence of the principal lossless response presentations) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Let \(\tau_0=(\eta;\mathcal S_2,\mathcal S_1)\) be accessible and let
\(L=(L_A,L_Q)\) be norming.  For every \(\cP\)-causal state \(S\),
\begin{equation}
