{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb2e0c93680b1628212b678d6724d2db1d1de8dc40c040c54002ee7475575217","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Holder prop for int ell of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a constant $c>0 $ such that, for any $x, x' \in \bb R$ with $|x-x'|\leqslant 1$, 
