{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.765544+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb54857d74148d8bee0ffa68ff26486dd7c3d166292992862f65471f7ca94a13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 (\cites{Rei77, ESI92}) of arXiv:2608.26723, 'Extrinsic upper bounds for the harmonic mean of eigenvalues in curved manifolds'] Let $M$ be an $m(\ge 2)$-dimensional closed orientable submanifolds in a space form $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$. Then the first nonzero eigenvalue $\lambda_1$  of the Laplacian on $M$ satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\lambda_1\leq\frac{m}{\vol(M)}\int_M(c+|\mathbf{H}|^2),
	\end{equation}
	where $\mathbf{H}$ is the mean curvature vector of $M$ in $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$.

	Equality holds if and only if $M$ is either minimally immersed in $\mathbb{S}^n$ by a subspace of the first eigenspace, or minimally immersed in a geodesic sphere of $\mathbb{R}^{n}(c)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.797301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb5525a860d0d5d68584219b955fb9e80493afd24187a8b5de27965b62e7a57f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two_edge_1_gamma_minus_1_le_delta_le_1_gamma of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Suppose $\frac 1 \gamma-1<\delta<\frac 1 \gamma$. The two-edge crossing probabilities are given~by 
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{(u),R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{(u),R}+ u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})}\wedge 1\\
        &\asymp \begin{cases}
                    u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})} & \text{ on } \{u  \geq R^{-d\frac {\delta+1-1/\gamma}{\gamma \delta}} \},\\
                    u^{-\gamma \delta} R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)}  \leq u  \leq R^{-d(\frac {\delta+1-1/\gamma}{\gamma \delta})} \},\\
                    1 & \text{ on } \{u \leq R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)} \}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    \begin{align*}
       \pi_{r,R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{r,R}+ r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})}
        \asymp \begin{cases}
                    r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1+\frac 1{\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma-\frac 1 {\delta})} & \text{ on } 
                    \{  r \leq R^{1+\delta-\frac 1 \gamma}\},\\
                    r^d R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{  R^{1+\delta-\frac 1 \gamma} \leq r \leq R/2\}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.928057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb587d6030afe97c2991717cd36022c09450e6488510629c36657edb618c4ee1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th nombre de faces of arXiv:2412.02666, 'Scaling limit of first passage percolation geodesics on planar maps'] For all $n \ge 0$, let $\Gamma_n$ be the shortest path for $d^\dagger_{\mathrm{fpp}}$ from $f_r$ to some face of $\overline{\mathfrak{e}}_n$ adjacent to the boundary which is chosen arbitrarily. Then we have the following convergences:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item If $a \in (2,5/2]$, then for the topology of uniform convergence on compact subsets,
		$$
		\text{Under } \mathbb{P}^{(1)}_\infty, \qquad
		\left(
		n^{-\frac{a-2}{a-1}}\# \mathrm{Faces}(\Gamma_{\lfloor nt \rfloor}) 
		\right)_{t\ge 0}
		\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n \to \infty}^{(\mathrm{d})}
		\left(
		\frac{e_{\bf q}}{2}
		\int_0^t \frac{ds}{\Upsilon_a^\uparrow(p_{\bf q} s)}
		\right)_{t\ge 0};
		$$
		\item If $a =2$, then 
		$$
		\text{Under } \mathbb{P}^{(1)}_\infty, \qquad
		(\log n)^{-2} \# \mathrm{Faces}(\Gamma_{ n }) 
		\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n \to \infty}^{(\mathrm{L}^1)}
		\frac{1}{\pi^2};
		$$
		\item If $a \in (3/2,2)$, then 
		$$
		\text{Under } \mathbb{P}^{(1)}_\infty, \qquad
		(\log n)^{-1} \# \mathrm{Faces}(\Gamma_{ n }) 
		\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n \to \infty}^{(\mathrm{L}^1)}
		\frac{2}{\pi \tan((2-a) \pi)}.
		$$
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.901399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb5ff238bf70532d857344b2f2ff7f9f17b091587f6d88d8ed9bc7c2b7c11a96","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] Consider the product introduced in Definition~\ref{def:pdt-increments-1d}.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item If $g,h\in\cac_{1}$, then $gh\in\cac_{1}$ and
    \begin{equation}
      \delta(gh)=\delta g\,h+g\,\delta h.
    \end{equation}
  \item If $g\in\cac_{1}$ and $h\in\cac_{2}$, then $gh\in\cac_{2}$ and
    \begin{equation}
      \delta(gh)=-\delta g\,h+g\,\delta h.
    \end{equation}
  \item If $g\in\cac_{2}$ and $h\in\cac_{1}$, then $gh\in\cac_{2}$ and
    \begin{equation}
      \delta(gh)=\delta g\,h+g\,\delta h.
    \end{equation}
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.728106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb6021b2d973087b1d81c20ef9a2dc0d6b431b7840662858de88b2bdf183b153","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2 of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] For a smooth function $f$ of $N$ variables we have
