{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.954382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb6cca1de4fa00cbdf8cf18c0bf40700c653b4afb9980f3b3d8153200100e00c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.25494, 'A functional central limit theorem for kernel gradient flow and infinitesimal gradient boo'] Let $d \ge 1$, $K \ge 1$, $\beta > 0$, and $\alpha > 0$ be fixed
