{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.697598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb71d738488b8862ddcd16e50adebc01a8451ddb19a6718ef8932345c28f3343","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:iicnew2 of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Fix an integer $k \geq 1$ and a tree $T \in \mathfrak{T}_k$.
    For each $n \geq 1$, suppose we have 
    a sequence $( \{ x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}\})_{n=1}^\infty$ where for each $n$,
    $(x_0^{(n)}, x_1^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}) \in G(\epsilon, n)$, and  where $x_i^{(n)} = 0$ for all $n$ for some arbitrary $0 \leq i \leq k$. Suppose also that there exists a $c > 0$ such that
    \begin{equation}\liminf_{n \to \infty} n^{(d-4)k + 2}\tau_T\left(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_{k}^{(n)} \right) \geq  c \ .

    \end{equation}

    Then, for each cylinder event $E$,
    we have for each $i$:
    \begin{equation}  \lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P}( E \mid  \Gamma(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}), \, \mathcal{T}(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}) = T) = \nu(E)\ . \end{equation}

    In particular, with the same $i$ and $(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)})$, for each fixed finite $\mathcal{D} \subseteq \mathbb{Z}^d$, we have
    \begin{equation} 
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\mathbb{P}(\Gamma_{T,i}(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}; \mathcal{D}))}{\tau_T(x_0^{(n)}, \dots, x_k^{(n)}) \nu(\Xi(\mathcal{D}))} = 1\ . 
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.025613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb780ad6b5d510a779e8f3c08418e3c5672f230a88bffba01e7200ebf1326237","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm:mf-spec of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] The multifractal spectrum of $W$ on  the space $ \Omega^\mathrm{crit}$  endowed with the uniform norm is fully described by 
    \[ f_\mathrm{crit} ( \xi)  =
    \begin{dcases}
    1 + \frac{\xi}{2}  &  \text{ if } \xi \ge 2  \\
    - \infty   &  \text{ if }  0 < \xi < 2 \;. 
    \end{dcases}
    \]
   Consequently, on the whole space $ \Omega$ it holds
    \[  f ( \xi) \ge   1 + \frac{\xi}{2}
    \qquad \text{ if } \xi \ge 2 \;. \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.332286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb78f19a0036bc3b7d23856a3bac06c3a5fe11bdc30bb18eda6b3d6ec67cbcc5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:ap1:wellPosed of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Fix $\kappa, d \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$ and $T \in (0, \infty)$. Suppose $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ and $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:lyapunov of the paper). Suppose that $(\mu, \gamma)$ is a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda$. Then the following properties hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The time-marginals of $\mu$ have uniformly bounded second moments, that is
\begin{equation*}
    \sup_{t \in [0, T]} \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}} |\mathbf{x}|^2 \mu_t(d\mathbf{x}) < \infty;
\end{equation*}
        \item There exists a positive locally H\"older continuous function $\mu:[0, T] \times (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa} \rightarrow (0, \infty)$ such that $\mu_t(d\mathbf{x}) = \mu_t(\mathbf{x}) d\mathbf{x}$. Moreover, the H\"older coefficient and exponent of $\mu$ depends only on $(\kappa, d, T)$, the linear growth constant of $(\gamma, \nabla U, \nabla W)$, and the initial condition $\lambda$.
    \item  We have $\mu_t \in W^{1, 1}((\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ for almost every $t \in (0, T)$. Moreover the following estimate holds:
\begin{equation*}
    \int_0^T \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}} \frac{|\nabla_{\mathbf{x}} \mu_t(\mathbf{x})|^2}{\mu_t(\mathbf{x})} d\mathbf{x} dt < \infty.
\end{equation*}
\item For all $t \in [0, T]$, we have
\begin{equation*}
    \int \mu_t(\mathbf{x}) |\log \mu_t(\mathbf{x})| d\mathbf{x} < \infty.
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}
In particular, if $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ and $(\mu, \gamma)$ is a linear growth solution of the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, T]$ with initial condition $\lambda$, then $\mu_t \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ for all $t \in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

