{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.675269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb87fa09aaa1b950acbfc6a58983ad8a44164855e85b453880c7f7373adf0203","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition NS-def sol of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Given a filtered probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},(\mathcal{F}_t),\mathbb{P})$ and a sequence of independent $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-Brownian motion $\{W^k\}$, we say an $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-progressively measurable process $u$ is a strong solution to (equation NS-u of the paper) if the following holds:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[(1).] $u\in C([0,T]; H^{2b+a})\cap L^2(0,T; H^{2b+a+1}),\:\mathbb{P}$-a.s.
			\item[(2).] For every divergence-free vector field $\varphi\in C^\infty (\mathbb{T}^3;\mathbb{R}^3)$, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. the following identity holds:
			\begin{equation*}
				\begin{split}
					\<u(t),\varphi\> &=\<u_0,\varphi\>-\int_{0}^t\<u\cdot\nabla u, \varphi\>\,{\,\rm d} s + \<u,\Delta \varphi\>\,{\,\rm d} t\\
					&\quad- \sum_k\int_{0}^t\big\<u, (-\Delta)^{2b+a}\mathcal{L}_k (-\Delta)^{-2b-a}\varphi\big\> \circ {\,\rm d} W_s^k,\quad \text{ for all } t\in [0,T].
				\end{split}
			\end{equation*}
		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

