{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.669640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fbc8449b49ebd25115e7051a1306f1697ccaaf4107b13cdadae12aba98373bfc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_overline_alpha_sigma_long_enough of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Fix $\sigma \in \{-,0,+\}$ and $w \in \Omega_n^{(0)}(\mu,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$. If $\#J^{\sigma} \neq 0$, then
