{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.027363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc0314d5318acf15cbafa7f166ac28cdc3603d9505cb6c71f7addf68f2535714","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question conj:spec-fBm of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] Is the following conjecture true ?  \medskip
        For every $ H^* \in ( 0,1) $, the local order of the fractional Brownian measure $W^{H^*} $  in the uniform norm evaluated at $B^H$ for $ H \in (0,1) $ is $ W^H$-a.s.
