{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.494528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc35b1b14500435f027150ee6aaa3c96beb91a905b33a6f1a1b986b2e844ddca","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Convex ordering of point processes) of arXiv:2605.28766, 'Convex order and faster transmission in first contact percolation'] Given two simple point processes $\X,\X'$ on $\R$, we say that $\X$ is more {\em reliable} than $\X'$ if for every finite collection of Borel sets $B_1,\dots,B_k\in\mathcal{B}(\R)$ and every decreasing convex function $\varphi\colon\R^k\to\R$, we have
