{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.867956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc777e580956c003b451c6eb732efe7ca4f332a7406739aa7052d032e0723a0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop suffcondrho=0 of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] We work under the assumptions of Lemma~(lem:boundsrho of the paper). Let the tail of the L\'evy measure of $\Sigma$ be denoted by $\bar{\eta}: (0,\infty)\ni u \mapsto \eta([u,\infty))$.
