{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.775435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc8d9a2428941a8e93b1d829cb4db19d4f05d7ffa026c7420c1855556aeaadd5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:gener_h_beta of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] For $x>0$, $\alpha\in (0,2)$, and $\beta\in (-1,\alpha)$, we have
