{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.356614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcd0ddbcfc6a646bd732c3d5c5d61db538815a218c5762d4e4d94e33cdd907c0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: probability to reach the fruit at a given time of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho}) \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal P}} $. There exist $C_1>0$ and $\varepsilon_1>0$ such that the following holds. Let $\varepsilon\in (0,\varepsilon_1)$. Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0} = (X_t^{(\varepsilon)})_{t\geq 0} $ be the FIT Markov chain with parameters $(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho}, \varepsilon)$. Denote its stationary distribution by $\pi_\varepsilon$. 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Let $1\leq i\leq k$ and $\ell_0+1 \leq j \leq \ell_0 + \ell_i-1$. We have
\begin{equation}
    {\ensuremath{\mathbb P}} _{y_j^i} (T_z = \ell_0 + \ell_i - j) \geq 1- C_1\varepsilon.
\end{equation}
In particular, ${\ensuremath{\mathbb P}} _{y_j^i} (T_z \geq \ell_0) \leq C_1\varepsilon$.
        \item Let $1\leq i\leq k$ and $0\leq j \leq \ell_0$. We have
\begin{equation}
    \rho_i(1-C_1\varepsilon) \leq {\ensuremath{\mathbb P}} _{x_j} (T_z = \ell_0 - j +\ell_i) \leq \rho_i(1+C_1\varepsilon).
\end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.608558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcd232892ce5a0ac9aed12e8b402e34606e2c741334c45922e5e7abb4b5abf84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2607.08314, 'Berry-Heisenberg random waves'] \cite[Theorem 4]{Yaglom60}
    Let $\xi = \{ \xi(g), \; g\in G\}$ be a random field on a separable locally compact group $G$ of type I. Then $\xi$ is left-homogeneous if and only if 
    \begin{equation}
        \xi(g) = \operatorname{Tr} \left( \pi(g)Z(\widehat{G}) \right) ,
    \end{equation}
    where $\widehat{G}$ denotes the unitary dual of $G$, $\pi$ is a unitary representation of $G$ acting on a Hilbert space $H_{\pi}$, and $Z$ is a random linear operator over $\widehat{G}$ such that 
    \begin{align}
        \E \left[ \langle Z(A) u_{1} , u_{2} \rangle_{H_{\pi}} \overline{\langle Z(B) v_{1} , v_{2} \rangle}_{H_{\pi}}  \right]= \langle F(A \cap B) u_{1} , v_{1} \rangle_{H_{\pi}}  \langle u_{2} , v_{2} \rangle_{H_{\pi}} ,
    \end{align}
for any measurable subsets $A, B$ of $\widehat{G}$ and any vectors $u_{1}, u_{2}, v_{1}, v_{2} \in H_{\pi}$, where $F$ is an operator-valued measure on $\widehat{G}$, whose values are Hermitian non-negative definite operators on $H_{\pi}$ satisfying \eqref{e.condition.pos.def}. Moreover, the covariance function of $\xi$ is given by \eqref{eqn.pos.def.fun}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.028275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcd58cb8b5ac412f6b189244e6fe8c20652747e6d71f74afa0819a21b43c0426","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.15616, '\textbf{Compact Support Property of Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift}'] Let $n\geq 2$ and $t \geq 0$. 
