{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.892671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcf8b3c7e6d9e55138fcf7b612fd8d8e69d55d555c3785e22cdfdae47aabf121","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 (First hitting time) of arXiv:2608.26834, 'Small-time annealed large deviations principle for one-dimensional diffusions in a random '] For every $\theta\in(0,1)$, there exist positive constants
		$C=C(\theta)$ and $N=N(\theta)$ such that, for every $R>0$,
