{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.304674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd00a71b425d83291861d29775671ff02a3a69557a21c0591db9d3cc531526cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition jtpdf of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] For any $t>0,$ the joint probability density function of $A_t^{(\eta)}$ and $\left(\eta t+B^{(e)}_t\right)$ is given by
\begin{eqnarray*}
\!\!\!&\!\!\!&\mathbb P\left(A_t^{(\eta)} \in \mathrm{d} y, \eta t+B^{(e)}_t \in \mathrm{d} x\right) =\mathrm{e}^{\eta x-\frac{1}{2} \eta^2t} \frac{1}{y} \exp \left(-\frac{1+\mathrm{e}^{2 x}}{2 y}\right) \theta\left(\frac{\mathrm{e}^x}{y}, t\right) \mathrm{d} y \mathrm{d} x,
\end{eqnarray*}
where $$\theta(r, t)=\frac{r}{\sqrt{2 \pi^3 t}} \int_0^{\infty} \mathrm{e}^{\frac{\pi^2-u^2}{2 t}} \mathrm{e}^{-r \cosh u}\sinh (u) \sin \left(\frac{\pi u}{t}\right) \mathrm{d} u,\quad r>0,\,t>0.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.774128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd01dfa78abd4993665fe82637d9300b09b152c53524caa211bf481c1b95d9e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma random_walk_expected_hitting_size_main_text of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Consider a random walk on $\mathbb Z^d$ driven by $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ starting from $x \in \mathbb Z^d$.
    Then, there exists a constant $c' = c'(K, \alpha, d)$ such that for any integer $r > 0$ and any $D \subseteq B_x(4r)$ with $|D| \ge r^d/4$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \sum_{y \in D} \mathbf P_y \left( \tau_x \le \ell(r) \right) \ge c' f(r),
    \end{align}
    where $ \ell(r) $ is defined in (equation def: s(r) of the paper) and $f(r)$ is defined as in Lemma~(lemma: range_estimates_main_text of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd01ff6003a4900e4c82a9a7539c9458938555660f1e69ec7e027ac93d2f1e2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $h,T$ be such that $\frac Th\in \mathbb{N}$, $\sigma$ and $\xi$ satisfy Assumption \ref{Aspt_new} and $f$ be $3$-times weakly differentiable with derivatives of polynomial growth. Assume that $\left(\hE\bigl[\xi_{jh}|\,\hX_{jh}\bigr]\right)_{0\le j\le T/h-1}$ is uniformly bounded from above and below by positive constants not depending on $h$. Then for all $p>1$
    \begin{align*}
        \Bigl|\E\bigl[ f(Y_T)\bigr]-\E\bigl[f(\hX_T^h)\bigr]\Bigr|\lesssim h+\sup_{j\in\{0,\dots,\frac Th-1\}} \bigl\| {\hE\bigl[\xi_{jh}^2\big|\hX_{jh}^h\bigr]}
        -{\E\bigl[\xi_{jh}^2\big|\hX_{jh}^h\bigr]}\bigr\|_{L^p}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.438548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd0213924d6f8fd7c591c4985ac3a8104b13064271e9eb62822a832608c256b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:reverse_linearized_check_score_representation of arXiv:2608.23938, 'Generalization, memorization, and overfitting \\for diffusion models trained in the lazy h'] For every \(t\in [t_0,T]\), \(\widetilde{\mathcal{K}}_t\) maps \(\widetilde{{\mathcal V}}\) to itself, and the linearized score function \(\widetilde{\boldsymbol S}_t\) admits the representation
    \[
        \widetilde{\boldsymbol S}_t({\boldsymbol x})
        =\frac{1}{\sigma_t}\widetilde{\boldsymbol \Psi}_t{\boldsymbol x}
    \]
    where
    \[
