{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.756988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd122b16d9671cf2fad4618ea5c8d8a638c895eea87012d5e6eb1bd91e883eec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (=Theorem \ref{thm:ax-nondeg}) of arXiv:2608.30174, 'Exact counting of spherical metrics with one conical singularity on rectangular tori'] Let $n\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}$, $\rho\in (8\pi(n-1), 8\pi n)$ and $u(z)$ be a solution of \eqref{eq:mfe}, which is axisymmetric. Then 
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
