{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.579887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd48b053cf82d10056ec4a8a5e00e8cac267c8111325619a81cacde89da684cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:frostman of arXiv:2509.06730, 'Hyperbolic branching Brownian motion: \\ the empirical limit measure'] Let $A$ be a compact subset of Euclidean space. Assume that there exists a probability measure $\nu$ on $A$ such that
