{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.378931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde44b7f2a8b9e2fc850a2af5280de46ace42131bd1acfa5eae92a1cbedb9101","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2609.03993, 'The Endpoint Fractional Riesz Estimate on the Hamming Cube'] A semigroup $(T_t)_{t\ge0}$ on $(\cN,\tau)$ admits a Markov
		dilation if there exist
		\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
			\item a larger semifinite von Neumann algebra $(\cM,\widetilde\tau)$;
			\item an increasing filtration $(\cM_s)_{s\ge0}$ of von Neumann
			subalgebras and the trace-preserving conditional expectation
			$E_s:\cM\to\cM_s$;
			\item trace-preserving $*$-homomorphisms
			$\pi_s:\cN\to\cM_s$;
		\end{enumerate}
		such that, for every $0\le s<t$ and $x\in\cN$,
		\begin{equation*}
			E_s(\pi_t(x))=\pi_s(T_{t-s}x).
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.531212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde92a9c810bb2e1d31a09114562924a8ac9ac1808276c793c408396aa22bfc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 (entropy rigidity of invariant Type I blow-up limits) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Let $g ( t )$, $t \in [ 0, T )$, be a Ricci flow of ansatz form \eqref{eq:ansatz-metric} on the compact manifold $\widehat{M}$, of Type I at $T$, and assume:

	\begin{itemize}
		\item \emph{(i) Localized singularity.} The flow closes at a bolt $Q$, with fiber potential $f_{i_0}$, such that for every $\delta > 0$ the geometry of $g ( t )$ is uniformly bounded up to $T$ on $\{ f_{i_0}^2 \geq \delta \}$, while $| \mathrm{Rm} | ( \bar{x}, t ) \asymp ( T - t )^{-1}$ at points $\bar{x} \in Q$.
		\item \emph{(ii) Convergence with the symmetry.} For $t_j \to T$ and $K_j \to \infty$ with $c_0 := K_j ( T - t_j )$ constant, the rescaled flows $g_j ( t ) := K_j\, g ( t_j + K_j^{-1} t )$ converge in the pointed Cheeger--Gromov sense, along comparison maps respecting the ansatz structure --- such as the bundle maps $\Phi_j$ of Step 2 of the proof of Theorem \ref{thm:contracting_Q0} --- to a complete ancient flow $( M_\infty, g_\infty ( t ) )$, $t \in ( - \infty, c_0 )$, again of ansatz form.
	\end{itemize}

	Then $g_\infty$ is a \textbf{gradient shrinking Ricci soliton in canonical form}: there is a smooth potential $\varphi_\infty = \varphi_\infty ( \hat{s}, t )$, depending only on the limit arc-length coordinate and time, with

	\begin{equation}
		\operatorname{Ric} \big( g_\infty ( t ) \big) \;+\; \operatorname{Hess}\, \varphi_\infty ( t ) \;=\; \frac{g_\infty ( t )}{2 \, ( c_0 - t )} \,, \qquad t \in ( - \infty, c_0 ) \,.
	\end{equation}

	In particular each time slice satisfies the ODE system of Proposition \ref{prop:soliton-ode} with $\lambda = \tfrac{1}{2 ( c_0 - t )}$ --- in the Kähler case, the two-ODE reduction of Corollary \ref{cor:potential-prop-H} --- and the flow moves by diffeomorphisms and homotheties. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.204253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde94651adcb350887d79ed98d53f9ad87e4703c5dfae4ba465dc5a6d47ed957","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] There exists a constant $C>0$, depending only on $\omega$, such that for any $N\in\N^+$ and $f\in H^1(\omega;\R^2)$,
