{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.706929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdf8b2e5896c4fbb4f3d4d996dcf1b1800410ed5bb3eb950ec59923dc6c0ad10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.17494, 'Generalized intersection exponents and local cut points for three-dimensional Brownian loo'] Let $\alpha_*\in I_0$, $k \in \mathbb{N}$, and $0<\lambda_0<\lambda_1$. Then there exist
