\end{align*}
Moreover, the same statement holds for $\tilde F_N^x$ and $\bar F^x_{N+1}$ in place of $\bar F_N$, uniformly in $x\in[0,3]^{\N^4}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.901331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe0b9ef168731917f0370dc73315769b5c66d3d9228d6f764de1c8eca48b0341","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] For $g\in\cac_{n}$ and $h\in\cac_{m}$, denote by $gh$ the element of
