{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.562286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe4bbe0fb4e25c66cd1eb61f862212e0dcc181923f56416069b106e5a3724c28","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2603.29571, 'Randomstrasse101: Open Problems of 2025'] The boundary measure of a set $S \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ with respect to the probability measure $\mu$ and Euclidean distance $d$ is given by
    \begin{align*}
        \mu^+(S):= \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0}\frac{\mu(S+\varepsilon B_n)-\mu(S)}{\varepsilon}. 
    \end{align*}
    where $B_n$ denotes the Euclidean Ball in $n$ dimensions.
    The isoperimetric  constant $\psi_\mu$ is the minimal boundary measure among sets $S$ with $\mu(S)\geq \frac{1}{2}$:
    \begin{align*}
        \psi_\mu := \inf_{S \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n} \frac{\mu^+(S)}{\min\{\mu(S), \mu(\mathbb{R}^n\backslash S)\}}. 
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.727845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe4c0f2fb3feaaee3aa812f4abf93a2e0e19525a236c29b4b16cd7c2dc42d266","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop-variational-characterization-rate-function of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] Let the rate functions $\mathcal{I}_{0},\mathcal{I}_{dyna},\mathcal{I}$ be defined by (equation rate-stationary of the paper), (equation rate-dynamic of the paper), and (equation rate-function of the paper), respectively.  Then for any $\theta\in\mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\beta}$ with $\mathcal{I}(\theta)<\infty$, we have 
