{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.466066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe59751ee104c0a905400f00eb1d07a74c6ef7494030d1ba0e93284434a4fa93","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Let $\phi_1^\e:\R^d \times\T^d\to \R$ be the solution to \eqref{e2-3aa}, and define $\Psi^\e:\R^d \to \R$ by
$\Psi^\e(x):=\phi_1^\e\left(x,\e^{-1} x \right)$. Then,
\begin{equation}
\varphi(\e)^{-1}\sL_\e \Psi^\e(x)=-F_1^\e\left(x,\e^{-1} x \right)+\bar F_1^\e(x)+G_1^\e\left(x,\e^{-1} x \right)
+\lambda \varphi(\e)^{-1}\phi_1^\e\left(x,\e^{-1} x \right),\quad x\in \R^d,
\end{equation}
where $G_1^\e:\R^d\times \T^d\to \R$ is defined by \eqref{l2-2-2}.
Moreover, for every $k\ge 0$, there exist positive constants $C_1(k)$ and $C_2(k)$ such that for all $\e\in (0,1)$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
|\nabla_x^k  G_1^\e(x,y)|&\le C_1(k)\xi_{2,\beta_0}(\e)\sum_{i=k}^{k+2}\left(\sup_{y\in \T^d}\|\phi_1^\e(\cdot,y)\|_{\M_{\beta_0},i}
+\sup_{y\in \T^d}\|\nabla_y\phi_1^\e(\cdot,y)\|_{\M_{\beta_0},i}\right)
(1+|x|)^{-d-\beta_0}\\
 &\le C_2(k)\xi_{2,\beta_0}(\e)(1+|x|)^{-d-\beta_0},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where $\xi_{2,\beta_0}(\e)$ is defined by \eqref{e1-8a}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.646872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe5c6659f1f65fd5f1c2c6d1ce03a48f1cf3d25207025824b63d6d0ba48d1187","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 104 (Auxiliary fixed-sample critical boundary) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] Assume $T>0$ and $C\ne0$.  Let $G_C\sim N(0,C)$ and
