{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.650992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe6fdf44f03a5e8b95bc08752c9219f271a261eae40778700eedfcc019917d2f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] For every $\omega\in \Gamma(x_0,\ldots,x_k)$, the connectivity tree $T(\omega)$ is a directed tree with leaves in the set $\{x_0,\ldots,x_k\}$. $T$ is also a tree when viewed as an undirected graph.
    \begin{proof}
    By construction, every vertex in $T$ except $x_0$ has a unique parent, so $\# E(T)=\#V(T)-1$ which implies that $T$ is a tree. Starting at any vertex of $v$ and applying the parent operation repeatedly, we obtain a path in $T$ ending at $x_0$. Since $m_{ij}$ appears on any path from $x_i$, only the vertices $x_j$, $0\le j\le k$ can have 0 children.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.018978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe7072091a8dccd6a0be4cb1da06b50a4a33c20cd17626249254853955808656","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:R3_integral-2 of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 1$, $\varepsilon \in (0,1) $, and denote
$\zeta_0 = \zeta \wedge \frac {d \wedge 2}2$.
Let $x\in{\mathbb Z^d}$ be a nonzero vector in the same direction as $\eta$,
i.e., $\eta = \abs \eta \hat x$.
If $d \le 2$, we further assume $\abs x \abs \eta \ge s_0$.
Then when $T \ge \varepsilon^{-1} \vee \varepsilon^{-(2+\zeta_0)/\zeta_0}$ and
$\abs x \ge 4dM / s_0$, we have
\begin{equation} 
\frac{ 1 }{ B(x; \eta )}
	\int_T^\infty \mathrm{d} t\, \abs{ I_{t}(x)
	- \hat g(0) \rho_t(x; \eta,\Lambda) }
\lesssim  e^{-c_1/\varepsilon}  + \frac 1 { \varepsilon^{d+1+\zeta_0} \abs x^{\zeta_0} }
	+ \frac 1 { \varepsilon^{ (d\vee4) + \zeta_0} \abs x^{\zeta_0 / 2} } ,
\end{equation}
with $c_1 = \frac 1 8 K_{\mathrm{IR}}$ and the implicit constant depending only on $d, \zeta, M, K_{\mathrm{IR}},s_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.620002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe708cbd469f4a4b7a4a7c4c32a5b217d7dac5bd9e482e6c6309fb6d920ec74a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop_birth_sections of arXiv:2606.23648, '\textsc{Optimal Stopping for a Diffusion with Unobserved Bernoulli Drift}'] Under the standing assumptions of this section,
    \(
        x\in\mathcal I
    \)
    if and only if
    \begin{equation}
