{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.041328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe729e715c2ceeb13b0596bc8867a74eaa4073fc1df51b8543d48f57dc4e9713","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition fractionalintegral of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] The fractional integral, also known as the Riemann–Liouville integral, associates with a real function $ f:\mathbb {R} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$  another function $I^{\alpha} f$ of the same kind for each value of the parameter $\alpha>0$
