{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.338199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe7d92d1fc7dbd91799a8370d03fa8f71bb944477f2ccb4884da42d61f95a2f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:hatladder of arXiv:2607.19651, 'Metastability and phase transition in a social network model with multiple opinions'] For any $o \in \mathcal{O}$, we define
\begin{multline*}
    \hat{\mathcal{L}}^{o} = \{ u \in \mathcal{S} : u(a,o) \in \mathbb{Z},\ \forall a \in \mathcal{A}, \\
    0 = u(a_1,o) < u(a_2,o) < \ldots < u(a_N,o),\ \{a_1,\ldots,a_N\} = \mathcal{A}, \\
