{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.334953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe96c2c0d82ecb50360e47779ceaebea478bfafe1bc8ba9c15068ecbec767576","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:GCC of arXiv:2609.03980, 'Decay Rates and Domain Dependence of a Coupled Wave-Heat System with Spatially Dependant H'] Let $(\Omega,\Omega_w,\Omega_h)$ be a Lipschitz interface triple in $\mathbb{R}^n$ with interface $\gamma$. We say that $\Omega_h$ controls $\Omega_w$ in time if there exists a time $\tau>0$ such every wave equation solution $W$ with Dirichlet boundary conditions, i.e., every $$W \in C^0\left(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}, H^\Delta_0(\Omega)\right)\cap C^1\left(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}, H^1_0(\Omega)\right)\cap C^2\left(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}, L^2(\Omega)\right)$$ with
    \begin{align*}
        \partial_t^2 W(t,x) = \Delta W(t,x)~~ &\forall(t,x) \in (0,\infty)\times \Omega,\\
        W(0,\cdot) = w_0 \in H^\Delta_0(\Omega),~~ &\partial_t W(0,\cdot) = w_1 \in H^1_0(\Omega),
    \end{align*}
    satisfies the observability inequality 
    \begin{align}
        \|w_0\|_{H^1(\Omega)}^2 + \|w_1\|_{L^2(\Omega)}^2 \lesssim \int_0^\tau  \|\partial_t W(t,\cdot)\|^2_{L^2(\Omega_h)} \;\mathrm{d} t. 
    \end{align}

    Similarly, for admissible Lipschitz pairs $(\Omega_w,\gamma)$, we say that $\gamma \subset \partial\Omega_w$ controls $\Omega_w$ if there exists a Lipschitz interface triple $(\Omega,\Omega_w,\Omega_h)$ with interface $\gamma$ such that $\Omega_h$ controls $\Omega_w$ in time.","status":"unverified"}

