{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.831555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fea3f2480ea6eab149a2f51cd05ef2344c5db75169928e1aa9199686f44797ee","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.02147, '2609.02147'] Let $N \geq 1$ and assume that \eqref{A1}, \eqref{A3} and \eqref{A5} hold. 
 Then, for every $\mu >0$, there exist $\alpha_0>0$, $w_1, w_2 \in S_\mu$ such that $w_1,w_2\geq 0$ and 
\begin{equation*}
    c_\tau = c_\tau(\mu) \coloneq \inf_{\gamma \in \Gamma} \max_{t \in [0,1]} E_{V,\tau}(\gamma(t)) 
