{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.243608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee33386b6235f8b7c3968e21b6d06b0a10a72da5c99cec69f8cd57c2df944ea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 34 of arXiv:2603.05174, 'Regularization of the superposition principle: Potential theory meets Fokker-Planck equati'] Let $\left(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\left(\mathcal{F}(t)\right)_{t\geq 0},\mathbb{P}\right)$ be a filtered probability space. 
    An $\mathcal{F}(t)$-adapted and $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. path-continuous stochastic process $X=(X(t))_{t\geq 0}$ with values in $\mathbb{R}^d$ is called a {\rm weak solution} to the McKean-Vlasov SDE
\begin{equation}
    dX(t)=b\left(t,x,\mathcal{L}_{X(t)}\right)dt+\sigma\left(t,x,\mathcal{L}_{X(t)}\right)dW(t), \quad X(0)\sim \mu_0\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)
\end{equation}
where $W$ is a $d$-dimensional standard Brownian motion defined on $\left(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\left(\mathcal{F}(t)\right)_{t\geq 0},\mathbb{P}\right)$, whilst $\mathcal{L}_{X(t)}:=\mathbb{P}\circ \left(X(t)\right)^{-1}, \;t\geq 0$,
if
\begin{equation*}
    \int_0^N\int_{B(0,R)} \left(\|b(t,x,\mathcal{L}_{X(s)})\|+\|a(t,x,\mathcal{L}_{X(s)})\|\right) \;\mathcal{L}_{X(s)}(dx) dt <\infty, \quad N>0,R>0,
\end{equation*}

and
\begin{equation*}
    M(t):=f(t,X(t))-f(0,X(0))-\int_0^t\left(\frac{d}{ds}f+{\sf L}_{s,\mathcal{L}_{X(s)}}\right)(s,X(s))\;ds,\quad t\geq 0
\end{equation*}
is an $\mathcal{F}(t)$-martingale for every $f\in C_c^\infty([0,\infty)\times\mathbb{R}^d)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.047324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee3e46bb81909f895c4ee1cb01d2748c77b890caf53442f00f28dc7d000b87d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] For every $\delta>0$ there exists a constant $c_9=c_9(\delta)>0$ such that for $\bbQ$-a.a.\ $\omega \in \Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}$ we can find $N_0(\omega,\delta) \in \bbN$ such that for all $N \geq N_0(\omega,\delta)$
