{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.566432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_feeffc1d4d5268b9bafd5d9116196989b5d5e1f661b9d45ce7d61a5817423fb7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 50 (Type II blow-up limits have nonnegative bisectional curvature) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] We have:

	{(i)} For every $t \in [ 0, T )$, every bisectional curvature of $J$-invariant planes tangent to $\mathcal{V}'$ satisfies

