{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.783819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff1d32f9c5a82f7617b7e3674bc01a5063fc8cf4729306742e35225f99e305db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the:finite_n of arXiv:2608.04303, 'The rank and layer distributions in random recursive trees'] For~${n>2}$, the expected fraction of leaves in an RRT of size~${n}$ is

\begin{equation}

    r_0(n) = \ell_0(n) = \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{n(n-1)}\,.
\end{equation}

The expected fraction of nodes of rank~${1}$ and at layer~$1$ are, respectively,

\begin{align}

    r_1(n) =& \sum_{j=0}^{n-2} \frac{(-1)^j}{j!}  + \frac{1}{n(n-1)} \sum_{j=0}^{n-3} \frac{(-1)^j}{j!} (j+2)\\

    =&~e^{-1} + \frac{e^{-1}}{n(n-1)} + O\!\left(\frac{1}{(n+1)!}\right),\\

    \ell_1(n) =& -\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{n-1}
    + \frac{2}{n!} + \sum_{v=2}^{n-1} \frac{1}{v!} - \frac{1}{n(n-1)} \sum_{v=0}^{n-3} \frac{1}{v!} + \frac{2}{n!} \sum_{j=1}^{n-2} \sum_{v=0}^{j-1} \frac{j!}{v!} \\

    =&~e - \frac{5}{2} + \frac{e-1}{n^2} + O \left( \frac{1}{n^3} \right)\,.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

