{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.585907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff3fda937cff2271fbb9ed693714ae07331d3d1f77df8dc05372d3f12c9f51ee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem YBTH of arXiv:2602.12713, 'GIG random matrices \\ and \\ a Yang-Baxter extension of the Matsumoto-Yor property'] The function $\phi^{(\cdot,\cdot)}=\left(\phi_1^{(\cdot,\cdot)},\,\phi_2^{(\cdot,\cdot)}\right)$ is a parametric Yang-Baxter map, that is
