 $$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.275955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff752971ce82adc7c30c3bfe2a004fbc791582b0e2a7c66bcb311b887802a5ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.21394, 'McKean-Vlasov Equations for Large Networks of Neurons with Adaptive Asymmetric Edges'] There exists a unique symettric positive-definite matrix $V_*^{\alpha\beta} \in \mathbb{R}^{(l+1) \times (l+1)}$ such that
