{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.019988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff829bf133331ff05b7289d4d50a0bb5def3cba1c4a7d3ef0278be0ce1caa6ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Unified Linear Convergence of Projected BW-GD of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] Let $f \in \{f_1, f_2\}$ be the objective function with unique optimum $S_\star \in [\alpha I, \beta I]$ and $\kappa = \beta/\alpha$.
