{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.661357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff83427b9036731d6fd8eb41d6a1afe5f8434cd355473ac986c27ea1400cdf0a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_tau0_tail of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] There exist constants $C_6 \geq 1$ and $L_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that the following holds. For sufficiently small $\zeta > 0$, for any $\delta \in (0,1]$ and $\mathbb{P}_\zeta \in \mathscr{M}_{\gamma,\delta}(\zeta)$, for all $k \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $k \leq \log_2 (1/\zeta) - L_0$, 
