{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.337668+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff85f9fca040168319088e084a0e8201c6962724dd8c3f1cced0cad41b992806","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $K$ be a graph over $V$. An \textbf{allocation} on $K$ is a map $\theta: \vec{E}(K) \to [0, 1]$ such that, for any $(u \to v) \in \vec{E}(K)$, $\theta(u \to v) + \theta(v \to u) = 1$. Any such allocation induces a so-called \textbf{load} map
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{array}{c}
\partial \theta: 
\end{array} \hspace{5pt}
\begin{array}{rcl}
V & \longrightarrow & \R_+ \\
v & \longmapsto & \sum_{\{u, v\} \in E(K)} \theta(u \to v)
\end{array}.
\end{equation}

An allocation $\theta$ is said to be \textbf{balanced} if for any $e = \{u, v\} \in E(K)$, 
\begin{equation}
    \partial \theta(u) < \partial \theta(v) \Longrightarrow \theta(u \to v) = 0.
\end{equation}

Then, balanced allocations over $K$ exist, and they all share the same associated load function $w_K$. We call this map the \textbf{balanced load function} associated to $K$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.354074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff88887d0b6a528b54ee593a9fedf83b49a2fc9dd4f5a9ea79b72ccda8985f64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor eq:CR_variance of arXiv:2608.10215, 'The variance of the Pitman--Yor process: a Cifarelli--Regazzini identity and inversion for'] Let $\theta > 1/2$, and let $\mathsf{G}$ be a probability measure on $[0, +\infty)$ satisfying $\int_0^{+\infty} \log(1 + x^2) \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) < +\infty$. 
Then, for any $t \ge 0$, there holds
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[ \left(\frac{1}{1 + t\mathfrak{V}}\right)^{\theta - 1/2} \right] &= \int_0^1 {\mathcal B eta}(\mathrm{d}\rho; 1/2, \theta - 1/2) \times \nonumber \\
& \times \frac 12 \left\{ \Psi_{+,0}(\sqrt{t \rho (1 - \rho)}, t(1 - \rho)) + \Psi_{-,0}(\sqrt{t \rho (1 -\rho)}, t(1 - \rho)) \right\} \mathrm{d} \rho 
\end{align}
with
\[
\Psi_{\pm, 0}(u, v) := \exp\left\{ -\theta\int_0^{+\infty}  \log(1 \pm 2ux + vx^2) \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) \right\} \ .
\]
Moreover, if $\theta > 3/2$, one has
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\frac{1}{z + \mathfrak{V}}\right] &= \int_0^{+\infty} \frac{f_{\mathfrak{V}}(x)}{z + x} \mathrm{d} x \nonumber \\
&= z^{\theta - 1} \int_{\Delta_2} {\mathcal D ir}(\mathrm{d}\xi \mathrm{d}\eta; 1/2, 1, \theta - 3/2) 
\left[\frac{\Phi_{+,0}(z; \xi, \eta) + \Phi_{-,0}(z; \xi, \eta) }{2} \right]
\end{align*}
with
\begin{displaymath}
\Phi_{\pm, 0}(z; \xi, \eta) := \exp\left\{ -\theta\int_0^{+\infty}  \log(z \pm 2\sqrt{z \xi\eta} x + \eta x^2) \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) \right\}\ . 
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.449091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff894d9b09f9eb9ce84281db17187b1b0d18a786afe4945aff0909cde8d46d28","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:ivgff+diagonal of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, an inverse temperature $\beta > 0$ and a site percolation configuration $r \in \{0,1\}^{\Lambda_L},$ we define
    \begin{multline*}
