{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.164812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff9409429f51d5c166009ae3bdd840a9ab2ef00b9091ad50405e3cb4d549860f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma independence over F_p^n of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] Let $x_1,...,x_g \in \overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$ be linearly independent over $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$, and let $\varepsilon_1,...,\varepsilon_g \in \mathbb{F}_{p^n}$. Let $k \leq g-2$ and consider the $g \times (k+2)$-matrix

\begin{align}
    \begin{pmatrix}
