{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.199334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff9e0332e0550f7420da859dfeacbb8ae8856f73fc0920bc57f57adafe4c81b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 54 (\hspace{-0.05em}{{\cite[Proof of Proposition~2) of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] {lalley2000rate}}}]

    For all shuffle process with pile size $\vec\bn$, suppose that there exists $H(\vec\bn)\subset [N]$ such that (with $E(H)$ the subgraph of the path graph induced by vertex set $H$):
		\begin{equation}

		\begin{aligned}
			|H(\vec\bn)|&\geq N^{1/2} \\
			|\partial H(\vec\bn)|&\leq 2|H|^{1/2}\\
			\mathbb P\left[|E(G)\cap E(H(\vec\bn))|\geq |H(\vec\bn)|^{\frac{1}{2}+\delta}\right]&\to 1.
		\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}
	Then if $\nu \sim \bP(\vec\bn, K)$ and $K\leq (\widetilde C_{\mu}-\eps) \log N$, we have
	\begin{equation}

        \nu\Big(\#\{i\in H: \sigma(i)<\sigma (i+1)\}\leq |H(\vec\bn)|/2+|H(\vec\bn)|^{1/2+{\delta/2}}\Big)
        \to 0,
    \end{equation}  
        where the limit is uniform for all $\vec\bn$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

